window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":301,"title":"Chapter 301 - 217: The Good Show Begins","paragraphs":["Just beyond the courtyard gate, bathed in the glow of bright lanterns, a plain-looking, middle-aged Confucian Scholar in a long black robe was waving at him from a distance.","The man wore a smile, but his eyes were cold and merciless. As he waved, his mouth formed the silent words:","\"If you don’t want her to die, come with me.\"","Chen Yi read the words clearly, and he understood their meaning.","After watching for a moment, his expression grew calm. He offered the man a distant salute and said with a smile, \"Alright.\"","Instead of going back through the gate, he glanced toward Xiao Wan’er and the others, then beckoned to a student standing guard outside and gave his instructions.","\"Please inform Chen Yunfan, the Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office, that something has come up and I must leave early. Ask him to look after the Xiao Family in my stead.\"","\"If he asks what happened, just say that Tiger Girl has gotten into trouble.\"","\"Yes, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","The student at the gate recognized him, offered a bow, then turned and entered the courtyard.","With that taken care of, Chen Yi waved to the middle-aged Confucian Scholar in the distance, gesturing for him to lead the way.","There were few people in the courtyard he could trust.","But his unreliable older brother, Chen Yunfan, was definitely one of them.","Besides, with Chen Yunfan’s concealed Martial Arts Cultivation, he and Cui Qingwu together should be more than enough to protect Xiao Wuge and Xiao Wan’er.","The middle-aged Confucian Scholar heard his voice and saw his gesture. He nodded, pointing in another direction.","Then, he led the way, squeezing into the crowd and heading off.","Chen Yi watched the man’s back and activated his [Qi Observation Skill].","Five plumes of black qi instantly filled his vision.","’An aura of the Middle Three Grades...’","’Upper Fifth Grade, or Lower Fourth Grade!’","Chen Yi’s heart sank. He took a deep breath, then wove through the crowd of guests discussing poetry and followed.","As he walked, his hands moved in secret.","He deftly lifted useful items from the people he passed, stashing them on his person.","Hairpins, earrings, silver needles, and the like, just in case.","But Chen Yi was short on time. In just a few moments, he had passed several tables and followed the middle-aged Confucian Scholar out of the courtyard.","The middle-aged Confucian Scholar was waiting up ahead. With a slight lift of his hand, he pointed forward. \"After you,\" he said with a low chuckle.","Chen Yi gave the man a long, hard look, then walked without a word into a dark thicket of flowers and trees ahead.","He let the darkness swallow the last glimmers of light on his form.","The middle-aged Confucian Scholar watched him go, then glanced back and silently mouthed, \"Let the show begin.\"","Then, he too disappeared into the thicket.","「Meanwhile, in the courtyard of the Mid-Autumn Poetry Contest.」","Having just received the message, Chen Yunfan frowned slightly. He looked at the student with suspicion and asked, \"Did he say what was wrong?\"","\"He said that Tiger Girl has gotten into trouble.\"","Chen Yunfan’s brow relaxed at his words. He thanked the student and didn’t give it another thought.","After the student had left, Cui Qingwu asked in a low voice, \"Chen Yi left?\"","Chen Yunfan grunted in affirmation. He glanced out of the corner of his eye at the oblivious Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge and said:","\"He asked me to look after these two. I’m guessing that Tiger Girl from the Mountain Race got into some serious trouble this time.\"","\"I told him she’s completely unruly and would cause trouble sooner or later, but Brother Yi wouldn’t believe it. Let’s see if he can still be so stubborn now.\"","Cui Qingwu nodded. \"Granny Shan’s granddaughter. I’ve heard of her. They say her aptitude for the Martial Arts isn’t high.\"","\"I suppose so...\"","Despite this, Cui Qingwu couldn’t shake the feeling that something was amiss.","’Why didn’t Chen Yi ask Mr. Yue Ming and the others to look after Xiao Wuge and Xiao Wan’er? Why go to Chen Yunfan instead?’","When she voiced her doubt, Chen Yunfan thought for a moment, then arched a brow. \"Do you think he’s finally realized that his big brother is dependable?\"","\"...I suppose so.\"","\"I knew it! After all these years, he’s changed so much. It was impossible for his attitude toward me, his older brother, to remain unchanged.\"","\"...Perhaps.\"","\"So it seems he still respects me a great deal, doesn’t he?\"","Cui Qingwu replied again, then pointed ahead and said, \"The first poem has been sent to Mr. Yue Ming and the others for judging.\"","Chen Yunfan cleared his throat, straightened his posture, and let his smile fade.","\"Qingwu, the title of ’Poetry Champion’ for this contest belongs to none other than this top scholar.\"","Perhaps his voice was a bit loud, because Xiao Wuge, who was beside him, looked up and asked:","\"Brother Yunfan, what is a ’Poetry Champion’?\"","\"Naturally, it’s the person who writes the best poem of the night.\"","\"Oh. In that case, the Poetry Champion should be my brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yunfan nearly choked on his words and started coughing. \"Your... your brother-in-law, Chen Yi... he learned how to write poetry from me!\"","Xiao Wuge turned his head away. \"I don’t believe you.\"","\"Young Master, how can you not believe me? When I was four and Brother Yi was three, I was the one who taught him how to read and write with my own two hands!\"","\"I don’t believe you...\"","Xiao Wan’er watched the two of them joking. Her gentle gaze swept across the courtyard as she wondered to herself why Chen Yi had yet to return.","Cui Qingwu, sitting nearby, noticed her searching gaze and said with a smile, \"Sister Wan’er, Chen Yi sent a messenger just now. He said he’ll be back later.\"","Xiao Wan’er suspected nothing. She chatted with her for a few moments, then sat quietly at the table, watching over Xiao Wuge.","At that moment, the courtyard grew more boisterous.","Some huddled together, discussing their poetry. Others stared at the full moon in the night sky as they bent over their desks to write. And still others craned their necks toward the high platform, eagerly awaiting the judges’ decision.","Li Huai’gu finally seemed to recall the purpose of the gathering. He patted the hand of Lady Yun beside him and said with a smile, \"Brush and ink.\"","Lady Yun rose dutifully and began to grind the ink for him.","From the next table, Chen Yunfan glanced back and curled his lip. \"Brother Huai’gu, you get a much better feel for it when you grind your own ink.\"","Upon hearing this, Li Huai’gu simply ignored Chen Yunfan. He’d been around the man long enough to know his roguish nature; the more you engaged with him, the more irritating he became."]},{"number":302,"title":"Chapter 302 - 217: The Good Show Begins","paragraphs":["So he kept quiet.","Once Lady Yun finished grinding the ink, Li Huai’gu lifted his brush and wrote the first line of his poem:","\"A jade mirror hangs in the azure sky, a golden wind sweeps the cassia court...\"","Chen Yunfan glanced over, his expression faltering slightly. He looked down at the poem in his own hands:","\"Ten thousand li of clear light reach the celestial palace, the spiritual qi of late autumn gathers in the icy wheel...\"","After a moment, Chen Yunfan rolled up the paper in his hands and sighed softly.","\"So much for being the ’Poetry Champion’.\"","Cui Qingwu covered her mouth and chuckled.","Perhaps her laugh was too loud. Chen Yunfan shot her a glare and huffed, \"Even if I’m not the ’Poetry Champion’, Brother Huai’gu won’t be either.\"","Hearing this, Li Huai’gu surprisingly didn’t argue. He finished his poem, blew on the ink to dry it, and said:","\"Brother Qingzhou’s poetry is heavy with meaning and emotion. I am not even a fraction as skilled as him.\"","\"Good, as long as you know.\"","\"By the way, where did Brother Qingzhou go?\"","\"Out helping someone with their troubles...\"","Quite a few people had the same question, and Chen Yi’s name was mentioned from time to time.","Pei Zhaoye studied the poem in his hand, preparing to seek out a few masters for their appraisal. But when he looked up, he couldn’t see the man he was looking for, and he couldn’t help but frown.","\"Why isn’t Chen Qingzhou here?\"","\"Don’t tell me he got scared off.\"","...","Scared?","Chen Yi was, indeed, scared.","If something happened to Pei Guanli at the Xiao Family estate, never mind how Granny Shan might seek revenge—the Wu Mountain Mutual Market between the Mountain Race and the Xiao Family would be jeopardized.","Such an outcome would be unacceptable to him, to the Xiao Family, and to the Mountain Race.","Moreover, he had spent a fair amount of time with Pei Guanli; how could he not be concerned for her safety?","But while Chen Yi’s heart was heavy, not a trace of it showed on his face.","He silently followed the middle-aged Confucian Scholar on a circuitous route around the academy before boarding a carriage that drove out of the grounds.","Only then did the middle-aged Confucian Scholar finally speak. \"My apologies, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","\"The academy is full of powerful experts. I had no choice but to resort to this crude plan.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him from the side, then ignored him and lifted a window curtain to look outside. He asked:","\"Could you perhaps tell me where that girl is now?\"","As he spoke, his gaze fell upon a shop not far away—There’s a Wonton Shop by the Clouds.","Seeing this, the middle-aged Confucian Scholar didn’t stop him. He smiled and said, \"Of course you can see her, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","\"But tonight’s grand event has just begun. If I let you have your wish so early, wouldn’t that be a waste of all my efforts?\"","Chen Yi lowered the curtain, looked him straight in the eye, and asked in a serious tone, \"What do you want me to do?\"","’Right now, I’ve confirmed two pieces of good news and one piece of bad news.’","’First piece of good news: Tiger Girl isn’t dead yet. At least, not right now.’","’Second piece of good news: the man before me is a brainless idiot.’","’And the bad news is—my good mood for the night ends here.’","As it happened, Chen Yi hated nothing more than these kinds of sudden interruptions.","The middle-aged Confucian Scholar paused, sizing him up for a moment before slowly nodding.","\"To be this calm and composed even now... no wonder she’s so interested in you.\"","\"Her?\"","Before Chen Yi could ask, the middle-aged Confucian Scholar interrupted, \"Patience, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","\"The night is long. We have all the time in the world.\"","Chen Yi gave him a deep look. \"Fine.\"","’The people from the Five Poison Sect... and her, Liu Zhaoxue...’","’Heh.’","A moment of silence.","The carriage drove all the way to the edge of Quchi, where Chen Yi followed the middle-aged Confucian Scholar aboard a painted boat.","He had expected to see Pei Guanli here, but a look around revealed no sign of the girl, and he couldn’t help but frown.","\"I’ve already come with you to this place. May I see Miss Pei now?\"","The middle-aged Confucian Scholar glanced at him, gestured for the boat to set off, and only then said, \"No rush.\"","As if sensing what Chen Yi was thinking, he continued, \"Actually, I’ve invited you here simply to put on a play with you.\"","\"A play?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"A play with Shu State as the stage, the bright moon and endless stars as the props, and the poetry gathering as the first act.\"","Chen Yi was taken aback, and the look he gave the man was rather odd.","’I was wrong.’","’This man isn’t just a brainless idiot. He’s a colossal idiot.’","As if sensing the offense in his gaze, the middle-aged Confucian Scholar narrowed his eyes and stopped wasting words.","He pulled two items from his robes and placed them on the table beside him.","\"Here are two vials of medicine.\"","\"Take one, and your guts will be torn apart within three breaths.\"","\"The other will let you live for three days.\"","The middle-aged Confucian Scholar stared at Chen Yi and grinned. \"Whether or not you’ll be able to perform in the second act, Mr. Qingzhou, will depend on your luck.\"","Chen Yi glanced at the vials on the table and asked, \"It’s death either way. Why make me go through all this trouble?\"","The middle-aged Confucian Scholar smiled and shook his head. \"Not so.\"","\"If you are still alive, I will personally present the antidote to you with both hands within three days.\"","\"So, that’s how it is.\"","\"...How interesting.\"","Chen Yi let out a laugh, then directly picked up one of the vials, opened it, and poured the contents into his mouth.","One breath. Two breaths..."]},{"number":303,"title":"Chapter 303 - 218: When Will the Bright Moon Appear","paragraphs":["...Three breaths.","The night moon hung in the sky.","The waves on the Quchi were calm.","A melodious tune praising the moon drifted through the air.","Carried on the gentle breeze were the faint sounds of catchy poetry recitations and women’s cheerful laughter.","On the Painted Boat.","Chen Yi watched the middle-aged Confucian Scholar, his expression calm as he said, \"It seems my luck is quite good.\"","The middle-aged Confucian Scholar—or rather, Yan Fusha—stared at him blankly, seemingly not expecting him to be so calm, so decisive.","After a moment of silence.","A smile bloomed on Yan Fusha’s simple face, followed by a burst of hearty, unrestrained laughter.","\"You’re not afraid.\"","\"You’re actually not afraid... HAHA...\"","\"Aren’t you afraid of death?\"","His laughter was loud, his tone inscrutable.","It carried far across the Quchi, which was illuminated by the glow of lanterns.","After a good while, the laughter died down.","Yan Fusha looked at Chen Yi and asked with a smile, \"Are you truly not afraid of death?\"","Chen Yi gently set down the medicine vial and replied nonchalantly, \"Everyone is afraid.\"","\"Then why... Is it because of that little bastard from the Pei Family?\"","\"Yes.\"","The smile on Yan Fusha’s face faltered. He sized Chen Yi up for a moment, then shook his head. \"What a pity.\"","He didn’t elaborate on what was a pity.","And Chen Yi, naturally, wouldn’t ask.","’From the moment I was brought to this Painted Boat, everyone here has had only one identity: a mortal enemy!’","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi scanned his surroundings from the corner of his eye and asked:","\"What’s next?\"","Yan Fusha’s expression completely returned to its former state. \"We’ll consider this the first act, and Mr. Qingzhou has passed.\"","\"I will honor our agreement and send you the antidote within three days.\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal nod. \"Thank you.\"","’The potent poison in my body can still be suppressed for some time.’","’Three breaths... Heh.’","Seeing that Chen Yi was still just as calm, Yan Fusha said with a faint, mocking smile:","\"For the second act, I originally planned to throw you into the Quchi and see whether the Painted Boat is faster or you swim faster.\"","Chen Yi froze, looking at him with a hint of surprise.","’This man...’","’He’s seriously sick in the head.’","When Yan Fusha saw his expression, his smile widened slightly.","\"But seeing Mr. Qingzhou’s remarkable composure, I feared an ordinary play would hardly be worthy of your attention.\"","\"Therefore, I had no choice but to present some more... interesting little things for you.\"","As he spoke, Yan Fusha clapped his hands.","Two figures completely clad in black emerged from within the Painted Boat and placed the jars they were holding on the table.","Yan Fusha pointed at the jars and said, \"These are the ’Poison Jars’ my sect uses for practicing the Martial Arts.\"","\"During the refinement process, we place Poisonous Insects like snakes, bugs, centipedes, spiders, and toads inside and let them fight each other to the death.\"","\"Only the one that ultimately survives is deemed worthy of being refined by us.\"","As he spoke, Yan Fusha took one of the jars and slapped open the seal on top.","A pungent, foul stench immediately wafted out.","Chen Yi looked at the two jars. This time, he truly couldn’t guess the man’s intentions.","Before he could think too deeply, Yan Fusha continued, \"The refinement is now in its final stage. There is one Poisonous Insect left in each of the two jars.\"","\"Mr. Qingzhou, why don’t you take a guess as to which Poisonous Insect will be the final survivor?\"","Chen Yi looked at the Poison Jar in his hand. \"Guess?\"","Yan Fusha nodded. \"Guess correctly, and Mr. Qingzhou may proceed to watch the third act.\"","Chen Yi frowned to himself, feigning displeasure as he asked, \"Isn’t this still just a matter of luck?\"","Yan Fusha nodded, then shook his head. \"Yes, and no.\"","\"Heaven and Earth are divided by Yin Yang Five Elements, humans are divided by Yin Yang Five Elements, and so too are Poisonous Insects.\"","\"Their interactions of creation and destruction make it difficult to say for sure.\"","Chen Yi instantly understood the meaning behind his words.","’This coincides perfectly with my own Medical Dao.’","’Yin Yang Five Elements, Six-Meridian Differentiation, Five Elements and Six Qi, Meridian Flow...’","As his thoughts raced, Chen Yi’s expression grew more serious. \"May I take a look?\"","\"Of course.\"","Yan Fusha placed the Poison Jar in his hand on the table, then tore the paper seal off the other one and gestured. \"Please, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, then stepped forward. He turned sideways, his back partially to Yan Fusha, and peered into the two Poison Jars.","HISS!","But before Chen Yi could get a clear look at what was inside one of the Poison Jars, a piercing hiss rang out.","Then, a black shadow shot out from the jar.","—It was a snake, jet-black from head to tail, its fine scales seeming to shimmer with an eerie light!","Chen Yi’s eyes narrowed, but he neither flinched nor dodged.","He stared straight at the black snake, remaining completely still as it lunged at him.","SNAP.","Just as the black snake was less than an inch from his face, a large hand shot out and firmly gripped its head.","\"HSSS—\"","The black snake hissed endlessly, its body twisting as it struggled wildly.","But no matter how much it struggled, its long, forked tongue remained an inch away from Chen Yi.","Chen Yi watched the snake, now just inches away, the foul stench filling his nostrils.","He could even see its two sharp, black fangs and the viscous venom inside its mouth.","At this moment, a faint fluorescent light flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes—the Qi Observation Skill.","A few breaths later.","As if just snapping back to his senses, Chen Yi took a step back, sweat pouring down his forehead like rain.","Yan Fusha sized him up and said with a smile, \"My apologies, Mr. Qingzhou. The Poisonous Insects are ferocious. We wouldn’t want you to get hurt.\"","As he spoke, he pulled a centipede as long and thick as a forearm from the other Poison Jar, holding one creature in each hand.","\"It’s better if I hold them for you.\"","Chen Yi muttered a word of thanks and, in the moment he raised his hand to wipe away his sweat, glanced at the centipede.","’Its aura... there’s something wrong with it!’","Just then, Yan Fusha spoke up. \"Mr. Qingzhou, your performance today has truly earned my admiration.\"","Chen Yi paused but didn’t look up, continuing to pretend he was observing the two Poisonous Insects.","\"Admire what about me?\"","\"Your extraordinary courage.\"","\"Never mind these two treasures in my hands; even an ordinary poisonous insect would be enough to frighten some people to death.\""]},{"number":304,"title":"Chapter 304 - 218: When Will the Bright Moon Appear (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Chen Yi said, \"Oh.\" He straightened up, looked at him, and pointed at the centipede. \"The two poisonous insects look more or less identical. I’ll choose this one.\"","Yan Fusha was taken aback. \"Are you sure?\"","When Chen Yi nodded, he broke into a grin and shook his head.","\"It seems Mr. Qingzhou has only read a great many books but hasn’t truly grasped the principles of Heaven and Earth Yin Yang.\"","\"And what makes you say that?\"","\"Both poisonous insects are imbued with Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism. The black snake is Metal, and the centipede is Wood. Metal overcomes Wood...\"","\"The black snake is guaranteed to survive this fight.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"I choose the centipede.\"","Yan Fusha stated confidently, \"Then I shall have to enjoy the third act of this play alone.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"The outcome isn’t set in stone. Let’s just watch.\"","Seeing his stubbornness, a flicker of displeasure appeared in Yan Fusha’s eyes.","\"You just won’t be convinced until it’s too late. Very well, I’ll make sure you understand exactly why you’ve lost, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","With that, he placed the two poisonous insects into a clay jar and immediately covered it by inverting a second jar on top.","Having done this, Yan Fusha took a few steps back, folded his arms, and said, \"Fifteen minutes.\"","Chen Yi knew he meant they would wait for fifteen minutes, so he simply waited in silence.","Before long, the jars began to shake gently, and faint hissing sounds could be heard from within.","Clearly, a brutal fight was unfolding inside the jar.","Just a moment later, the jar stopped shaking, and the sounds from within gradually faded to silence.","Seeing this, Yan Fusha waved a hand, sending the top jar flying. He looked at Chen Yi and said:","\"Go and see the result for yourself, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","Chen Yi ignored him, his eyes fixed on the remaining jar.","’Truthfully, I had some confidence, but not a great deal.’","’Earlier, when I used the Qi Observation Skill on the centipede, I saw not only the Wood attribute of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, but also the Fire attribute.’","As wisps of black smoke drifted out from the jar, a dark, glossy sheen emerged from within.","CLICK.","The sound was crisp, like the tapping of segmented legs.","Immediately after, the jet-black centipede crawled out, its body still dotted with viscous venom.","Chen Yi relaxed slightly. \"It seems I chose correctly,\" he said.","Yan Fusha froze at his words, turning his head to look at the centipede. His eyes widened slightly.","\"How could this be...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, he flicked out a Silver Needle, pinning the centipede to the jar.","Wisps of white smoke instantly enveloped the centipede, making it let out a series of wretched shrieks.","Chen Yi took a step back, frowning slightly as he watched him. \"Is there a problem?\"","Yan Fusha kept his cold expression and refused to look at him, huffing, \"Mr. Qingzhou, your luck is certainly impressive. You just happened to stumble upon an exceptionally unique poisonous insect.\"","He refused to admit he had made a mistake.","Chen Yi understood this perfectly, but he also knew he couldn’t afford to provoke the man before him right now.","Otherwise, he feared he might never see Pei Guanli, whose whereabouts were still a mystery, ever again.","’If it weren’t for her, why would I have gone to such lengths to hide my abilities?’","With this in mind, Chen Yi lightly pressed a hand to his stomach and said, \"Let the third act begin.\"","At his words, Yan Fusha’s expression darkened, but then he began to laugh.","\"Good, good...\"","\"This act was full of twists and turns. Even I didn’t see that coming. Truly, it was excellent!\"","After his laughter subsided, Yan Fusha stared sinisterly at Chen Yi. \"Mr. Qingzhou, you must hold that little whelp from the Pei Family in high regard, don’t you?\"","Without waiting for a reply, he continued, speaking as if to himself, \"You’ve played along with all my games just for a chance to see her. I imagine you must value her a great deal.\"","\"In that case, I will give you an opportunity!\"","In truth, his original plan had simply been to toy with this live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family, a man whom Liu Zhaoxue held in high esteem.","He hadn’t intended to kill Chen Yi, nor had he ever planned to let him see Pei Guanli.","But now, he had changed his mind.","Yan Fusha clapped his hands and gave a cold command, \"Send a message.\"","\"Yes, sir.\"","A man dressed in black took a bamboo tube from his robes and fired it toward a Painted Boat in the distance.","It burst, scattering sparks of fire.","Chen Yi focused his gaze and saw, on the second floor of the Painted Boat a few hundred yards away, that a light gauze curtain was being slowly drawn aside.","A figure tied to a chair was faintly visible—who else could it be but Pei Guanli?","However, she was clearly in a terrible state.","Not only was she bound with ropes, but her face was also smeared with a black paste.","Two other men in black, holding blades, stood guard at her side.","They stood in a state of high alert.","Seeing this, however, Chen Yi felt a sense of relief.","’Tiger Girl is still alive. That’s the best I could have hoped for in this disaster.’","Just then, Yan Fusha spoke:","\"I have long heard that Mr. Qingzhou has achieved Mastery in Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, as well as in poetry and prose. Your Calligraphy Dao, in particular, is said to possess a profound Mental Realm.\"","\"For this third act, I think we should do something befitting the time and occasion.\"","Chen Yi pulled his gaze away from the boat and looked at him. \"And how do you propose we do that?\"","Yan Fusha raised a hand, gesturing toward the celebrating crowds along the banks of the Quchi.","\"Today is the Mid-Autumn Festival. We have this beautiful night, this fine scenery, the lights of countless homes, and the two of us here on this Painted Boat, watching a play.\"","\"So let’s take this opportunity. I would like to invite you, Mr. Qingzhou, to compose a poem.\"","\"If your Poetry is good enough, I will let you meet with that little Pei whelp!\"","Chen Yi paused. \"That’s...\"","Before he could finish, Yan Fusha raised a hand to cut him off. \"Don’t be so hasty, Mr. Qingzhou. I haven’t finished.\"","\"I know that Mr. Yue Ming had high hopes for you tonight, believing you could win the title of Poetry Champion.\"","\"If I hadn’t interfered, you would be at Guiyun Academy right now, a beauty at your side, surrounded by Poetry.\"","\"Therefore, I will have someone deliver your poem to the academy later.\"","Chen Yi frowned at him. \"And why would you do that?\"","’This time, I truly don’t understand his motive.’","’Composing a poem is one thing...’","’I have no shortage of lines about the moon, the Mid-Autumn Festival, or the fleeting beauty of the night.’","’But what’s the point of sending my poem to the poetry competition?’","Yan Fusha replied with a cold smile, \"Naturally, it’s to allow the masters at the academy to appreciate your Poetry.\"","\"If you can win the title of Poetry Champion... no.\"","\"If the poem Mr. Qingzhou writes can outshine every other poem at the city-wide competition, then I will grant your wish.\"","Chen Yi blinked. \"Outshine the entire city’s competition?\"","Yan Fusha glanced at him. \"Can you not do it, Mr. Qingzhou?\"","Chen Yi’s gaze swept over to the Painted Boat where Pei Guanli was held. He nodded and said, \"I can’t say I’m confident.\"","\"Is that so.\"","Yan Fusha smiled and whispered something to the black-robed man at his side.","The man then jumped directly into the Quchi and began swimming toward Pei Guanli’s Painted Boat.","\"Just a moment, Mr. Qingzhou. For a drama this rare, I feel we can’t let the little Pei whelp miss out.\"","He didn’t need to explain. At such a close distance, Chen Yi had naturally heard his two-part command.","Wake Pei Guanli. Tell her everything.","’Damn it, this lunatic!’","Chen Yi was secretly furious, but his expression remained impassive. \"Very well.\"","A moment later, Chen Yi saw that on the distant Painted Boat, some of the black paste had been wiped from Pei Guanli’s face, revealing half of her soft features.","But after waking, she didn’t struggle in the slightest.","’She must have been given a secret drug, something like Qingfeng Drunk.’","A moment later, the man in black spoke a few words to her.","Pei Guanli seemed to realize something and looked over in their direction.","Chen Yi met her slightly agitated gaze and simply smiled, giving her a small wave.","When Pei Guanli could see him clearly, tears welled in her eyes, and her lips parted.","No sound carried across the water.","But Chen Yi heard it. ’She’s calling me ’Brother-in-law’. ’","’Brother-in-law...’","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, letting her know he understood. He then turned to Yan Fusha.","\"It’s only Poetry. Bring me a brush and paper.\"","While signaling for the men on the Painted Boat to keep a close watch on Pei Guanli, Yan Fusha asked with a smirk:","\"How confident are you, Mr. Qingzhou?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"Even if I told you, I doubt you would understand.\"","\"You...! Fine!\"","Yan Fusha snorted, waved for his men to bring a brush and paper, and then stepped aside. \"Mr. Qingzhou,\" he said coldly,","\"you only have one chance.\"","\"If you waste it, I guarantee you will never see that little Pei whelp again as long as you live!\"","Chen Yi ignored his threat and calmly began his preparations.","He smoothed out the paper, poured water onto the inkstone, and began to grind the ink.","’There have been countless poems written about the moon throughout history, but very few are powerful enough to stun all of Shu State at a time like this.’","’After thinking it over, there’s only one that will do.’","Once the ink was mixed to the right consistency, Chen Yi glanced over at Pei Guanli in the distance.","Seeing the usually fearless, reckless, heaven-defying Pei Guanli crying her eyes out, he couldn’t help but make a goofy face in her direction.","Then, not caring whether Tiger Girl had seen him or not, Chen Yi took a deep breath to suppress the sharp pain in his stomach, lifted the brush, dipped it in ink, and began to write:","\"Bright moon, when did you first appear? With wine in hand, I ask the azure sky...\""]},{"number":305,"title":"Chapter 305 - 219: Sharing the Moon Across a Thousand Miles","paragraphs":["\"When will the bright moon appear? With wine in hand, I ask the blue sky...\"","Chen Yi’s brush danced without pause. The unique strokes of his Cursive Script flowed from his heart, and with them, a Mental Realm drifted out.","A night sky.","A different kind of night sky—deep and sapphire blue, dotted with countless stars.","A bright moon.","One more brilliant and dazzling than the round moon in the real sky, its radiance illuminating all.","This Mental Realm of a moonlit, starry sky, filled with large, golden characters, was like a second night sky appearing this evening.","It stretched out above the Painted Boat, and even...","Over the entirety of Quchi!","Yan Fusha looked up at the Mental Realm and its golden words that had appeared out of thin air, the smile in his eyes slowly fading.","\"You... This...\"","Chen Yi obviously paid him no mind, his brush splashing ink as he completed the work in one fluid motion.","\"I do not know what year it is this evening in the celestial palaces.\"","In the \"night sky\" filled with a sapphire, fluorescent glow, the characters materialized one by one, forming the second line.","It was as if a banished Immortal was writing in the air, creating these large, golden characters.","And within that \"night sky,\" a magnificent palace of jade pavilions with carved beams and painted rafters slowly rose, situated beneath the \"bright moon.\"","Within, celestial maidens danced, silver-armored heavenly soldiers stood guard, and musical notes transformed into talismans that drifted about.","A tall, upright figure in a long, green robe also appeared atop the palace.","His features were blurry, and one could only see him looking up at the moon.","An ethereal voice faintly drifted out.","\"What year... is it this evening?\"","\"The twenty-first year of the Anhe era of Great Wei, the fifteenth day of the eighth month, Shu State...\"","After listening, the figure fell silent for a moment before sighing softly:","\"I wish to ride the wind and return, yet I fear in those jade towers and marble halls, the heights would be too cold for me...\"","\"To dance with my clear shadow—how could that compare to the mortal world...\"","The faint sighs circled above Quchi, scattering along its banks with the bright moonlight.","Rowdy children noticed the splendor, stopping to wave and laugh, shouting that they saw an Immortal.","Courting scholars and beauties, who had been playing coy, froze in a daze when they saw the Immortal Realm.","The lion dancers in the streets stopped.","The gongs and drums were struck without conscious thought.","Strolling pedestrians forgot to take their next step.","Everyone stared blankly at the scene rising over Quchi in the distance.","\"Two... two moons...\"","Time seemed to stand still and all sounds ceased, save for the joyful liveliness of the flowers, birds, fish, and insects.","But the unfolding of the Mental Realm was not yet over.","\"It circles the red pavilion, stoops by the ornate door, shining on the sleepless...\"","\"There should be no hate; why must it always be full when people part?\"","Within the \"night sky\" over Quchi, from amidst the jade towers and marble halls, the figure floated out and flew straight toward the bright moon.","Below his feet was an Immortal Realm; above his head, the bright moon and myriad stars.","The tiny figure, poised in the middle, glanced back for a moment.","It was as if he saw the heavens and the earth, saw Quchi and the mortal world of Shu State, and saw the crowds below the moon, some lonely, some celebrating.","He smiled, free and unrestrained.","\"People have sorrow and joy, separation and reunion; the moon has its waxing and waning—such things have never been perfect since ancient times.\"","\"May we all live long, and though a thousand miles apart, share the beauty of this moon together...\"","The large golden characters shone brilliantly, scattering gold and silver light along with the moonlit Immortal Realm.","Flecks of splendor appeared and vanished in the air.","It left everyone who witnessed this scene utterly enchanted, as if they were truly seeing an Immortal Realm.","Or perhaps, they themselves were within the Immortal Realm.","Meanwhile, some students from Guiyun Academy, murmuring the poetry, naturally also saw the appearance of the figure walking on air.","Upon closer inspection, their eyes suddenly widened.","\"Th-That’s...\"","\"Mr. Qingzhou?!\"","Inside the Painted Boat.","Yan Fusha stared blankly at the Mental Realm that had appeared in the sky.","He had indeed not read many books and couldn’t recite classical canons or elegant poetry.","But it wasn’t that he was illiterate.","Nor was he some sheltered homebody with no worldly experience.","In all his years of wandering the land, Yan Fusha felt that not a single piece of poetry he had ever seen or heard could compare to these \"Words of the Immortal Realm\" before him.","He then retracted his gaze and looked at Chen Yi, who had finished writing the poem. His tone was ice-cold as he questioned him:","\"Mr. Qingzhou, did you do this on purpose?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, placed the Wolf Hair Brush beside the inkstone, and said nonchalantly:","\"I did as you said. I wrote a poem to overwhelm a city. Is there a problem?\"","Yan Fusha’s expression changed abruptly. His robes billowed as an invisible, ferocious pressure surged outwards.","But before it could reach Chen Yi, he instantly retracted his aura, merely pressing his palm onto the table.","CRACK.","A clear handprint appeared on the redwood table, its edges faintly emitting wisps of dim, black qi.","Yet only the tips of Chen Yi’s hair moved slightly; not even the hem of his robe stirred.","He looked at the handprint on the table, then his gaze fell on Yan Fusha, and he offered some faint praise:","\"A very powerful palm strike.\"","Yan Fusha glared at him with a ferocious look in his eyes. A moment later, he abruptly waved his hand, collecting the calligraphy sheet and dispelling the Immortal Realm that filled the sky. He then ordered coldly:","\"Set sail!\"","Chen Yi wasn’t surprised. He just watched him calmly, his eyes sweeping over the busy men in black nearby.","He calculated inwardly.","’Two Painted Boats. Members of the Five Poison Sect. Including Yan Fusha, a total of fourteen people.’","’Also...’","’I saw his previous palm strike clearly—his cultivation has already surpassed the Fifth Grade and reached the Fourth Grade Realm.’","’Lower Fourth Grade, to be precise.’","’At the same time, that palm strike must have contained the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, meaning he’s reached the Great Success Realm of Fist Dao.’","’And it was enhanced by Wood Qi Spiritual Essence.’","’Cultivation, Martial Arts, Poisonous Insects, Poison Skill...’","’A formidable enemy, indeed.’","Not long after.","The Painted Boat sailed north.","The Painted Boat carrying Pei Guanli had set sail even earlier.","It was just that...","After seeing Chen Yi’s \"winks and nudges\" earlier, she finally remembered what she was supposed to be doing.","So, while Chen Yi had been busy writing his poem, Pei Guanli had been muttering to herself incessantly.","’Little Flower, my dear Little Flower, eat faster.’","’Eat up all that poison, swallow it all...’","By the banks of Quchi.","Although the Immortal Realm of the moonlit night sky had dissipated, the crowds who saw it were now swarming toward Quchi."]},{"number":306,"title":"Chapter 306 - 219: Sharing the Moon Across a Thousand Miles","paragraphs":["\"That must have been an Immortal’s Palace!\"","\"Good heavens, it’s an auspicious sign! An Immortal has graced Shu State on this Mid-Autumn day!\"","\"Congratulations! A cause for celebration...\"","Lou Yuxue watched the painted boat recede into the distance, a slight frown on her face.","’The Fledgling should be at the Guiyun Academy’s Mid-Autumn poetry gathering tonight. Why was he on that painted boat?’","’Was it that carriage from before?’","Lou Yuxue was hesitant.","The incident with the Three Towns’ summer grain being burned had just happened, and the turmoil in Shu State City had yet to subside.","At a time like this, a \"remnant\" of the Bright Moon Building like her should not be making any sudden moves.","Besides, the Fledgling, Chen Yi, was part of the Hawk mission. Interfering rashly would inevitably have an impact.","As Lou Yuxue considered this, she made a decision.","\"Someone!\"","\"Go to Guiyun Academy and pass on what happened here to the Simurgh Phoenix!\"","\"And be quick!\"","...","「Guiyun Academy.」","The poetry gathering was in full swing.","The fragrance of fine wine and delicious food filled the air.","Beautiful women sang and played instruments, their melodies hauntingly beautiful.","Amidst the merry chatter and laughter, shouts of approval would occasionally ring out, mingled with words of congratulations and praise.","Through the lively noise, poems were presented one after another on the high platform to be judged by Mr. Yue Ming and the others.","By now, the scene on the high platform had completely changed.","The banquet tables had been cleared away.","Four desks were arranged neatly. Two stacks of paper were piled to the side, while on the two central desks lay only four large sheets of paper, laid out in a row.","The calligraphy on them was still fresh, the works of varying lengths.","At the end of each, four names were clearly written: \"Li Huai’gu of Shu State, Pei Zhaoye of Yan State, Ji Zhiyuan of Jiangnan Prefecture, and... Liu Zhaoxue of Jing State.\"","Mr. Yue Ming sat upright in the Grandmaster’s Chair at the head of the platform, his eyes constantly scanning the area where Chen Yunfan, Xiao Wan’er, and the others were.","He muttered to himself, ’Qingzhou really isn’t coming, he’s really not coming,’ while casually agreeing with the other masters around him.","Mr. Zhuo Ying was just as anxious, but with Chen Yi absent, it was useless to worry, so he could only drink his tea to hide it.","Mr. Lingchuan observed their expressions, then his gaze fell upon Liu Hong, and he said with a smile:","\"Lord Liu, I have long heard that your niece is as brilliant as she is beautiful, with a talent for literature that rivals any man’s. Seeing this today, I can say she truly lives up to her reputation.\"","Liu Hong smiled. \"She has loved reading since she was a child, and she is indeed clever. But as for her talent, I’m afraid in today’s gathering it can only be called ’not weak’.\"","\"Besides, composing poetry depends not only on one’s learning, but also on being in the right time and place.\"","\"Among everyone present, who hasn’t had a moment of sudden inspiration?\"","The people around him naturally understood the meaning behind his words and murmured a few words of agreement.","Yang Ye shot them a glance, his hands tucked into his sleeves, and leaned back in his chair to feign sleep, looking like an old farmer.","He couldn’t stand their fawning and flattery, so he figured what he couldn’t see couldn’t bother him.","Just then, Liu Si saw a gap in the conversation and asked with a smile, \"There have been many fine works today, and from them, four have been chosen as the best of the best.\"","\"I was just wondering, how will the masters and lords choose the ’Poetry Champion’?\"","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying lowered their heads to sip their tea, as if they hadn’t heard a thing.","Mr. Lingchuan glanced at the two of them and asked with a smile:","\"Lord Prefect, you must have an idea already. Why not share it with the rest of us?\"","Seeing this, Liu Si cursed ’Old coot’ inwardly, then began his critique without further ceremony:","\"The two poems by Li Huai’gu and Pei Zhaoye are neck and neck.\"","\"The piece by Ji Zhiyuan of Jiangnan Prefecture is a notch below Liu Zhaoxue’s.\"","The moment the words left his mouth, Liu Si noticed Liu Hong’s calm and steady gaze from not far away, and his heart skipped a beat.","But the words were already spoken, so he had to bite the bullet and continue:","\"If it were up to me, tonight’s ’Poetry Champion’ could be none other than Liu Zhaoxue for her ’Pipa Immortal: Mid-Autumn’.\"","Mr. Lingchuan laughed.","The other masters present also laughed.","Even Mr. Yue Ming, who had just set down his teacup, was the same. He asked with a laugh, \"Does the Lord Prefect truly think so?\"","\"You don’t believe me, Mr. Yue Ming?\"","\"The Lord Prefect misunderstands. This old man simply feels that Liu Zhaoxue’s piece is a bit... overwrought in its wording...\"","Before Mr. Yue Ming could finish, Liu Hong nodded and said, \"Brother Ming is right.\"","\"The little verse Zhaoxue wrote is flashy but without substance, its mental realm crude. It is indeed unworthy of the ’Poetry Champion’ title.\"","After a pause, he looked at Liu Si and asked with a smile, \"Wouldn’t you agree?\"","Liu Si’s expression turned stiff. He gave an awkward laugh and nodded. \"Your Lordship’s instruction is correct. Please forgive my shallow learning.\"","Liu Hong withdrew his gaze and said, \"Brother Ming, it’s getting late. Why don’t we wait another quarter of an hour and then announce the results directly?\"","Mr. Yue Ming glanced at him, sighed inwardly, and nodded. \"Then we shall do as Brother Gong Mo says and wait a quarter of an hour.\"","’Ah, well.’","’Qingzhou never did like these kinds of occasions. I can’t force him.’","At this moment, the outcome of the \"Poetry Champion\" was not only a topic of discussion for the great masters on the high platform, but also of even greater concern to the talented scholars seated at the tables below.","\"Today truly has not been a wasted trip. It’s the Mid-Autumn Festival, and so many talented scholars from the Nine State and Three Prefectures have gathered in Shu State. We are blessed with both fine poetry and a fine scene.\"","\"He’s right.\"","\"Take the poem by Pei Zhaoye of Yuelu Academy: ’Osmanthus seeds fall like golden millet, a fragrant wind crosses the jadeite stairs. Whose flute has begun to play, its melody filling the moonlit air?’\"","\"Even though it was prepared in advance, it is still a fine piece.\"","\"And that line from Brother Huai’gu, ’A jade mirror hangs in the azure sky, a golden wind brushes the osmanthus court.’ That’s just as good.\"","Pei Zhaoye listened to the discussions around him, a hint of pride on his face.","The green-robed scholar next to him saw his expression and said with a smile, \"Brother Pei, the poem you wrote today should be able to take first place, don’t you think?\"","Pei Zhaoye said humbly, \"That will be up to the masters to judge.\"","Despite his words, he already knew that one of the four large sheets of paper spread out on the high platform was his.","’My chances are very good.’","\"This way, Brother Pei, you can make that Mr. Qingzhou who looked down on you see you in a new light.\""]},{"number":307,"title":"Chapter 307 - 219: Sharing the Moon Across a Thousand Miles","paragraphs":["\"Who’s asking for his special treatment?\"","\"Brother Pei is right. In my opinion, that Mr. Qingzhou is indeed talented, but not enough to compose poetry on the spot.\"","\"I heard the few poems he composed before were all written at home.\"","\"Indeed...\"","A scholar looked at the others and shook his head. \"Based on that ’Post-rain Reflections’ alone, I am not his equal.\"","\"It’s a shame he hasn’t put brush to paper today. We’ve missed the chance to witness the elegance of his Calligraphy Dao, and his poetry is a rare sight as well.\"","Pei Zhaoye snorted, his face showing displeasure. \"Even if he were here, his calligraphy is just good. You expect him to compose a poem?\"","\"I wouldn’t be so sure...\"","At a table not far from the high platform.","Chen Yunfan’s face also held a hint of displeasure.","It was just that his thoughts were completely different from Pei Zhaoye’s.","He couldn’t help it.","After listening for so long, Chen Yunfan had only heard two sentences discussing him.","The first was, \"What masterpiece did the Imperial Top Scholar produce today?\" and the second was, \"His writing is poor.\"","Chen Yunfan couldn’t have been more annoyed. He grumbled under his breath about people having no taste and not understanding true literary talent.","Cui Qingwu, beside him, heard him clearly but pretended she hadn’t.","After all, she couldn’t offer words of comfort at a time like this. That would only embarrass a talented scholar even more.","So, she spent most of her time chatting with Xiao Wan’er.","Perhaps because they were of similar age and family background, they had grown quite familiar with each other after spending the better part of an hour together.","In Cui Qingwu’s eyes, this eldest daughter of the Xiao Family had a gentle personality, but she lacked the arrogance common to those from great Noble Families.","In comparison, she herself felt full of the typical faults of a spoiled young lady.","Thus, in their conversation, Cui Qingwu felt a degree of admiration for Xiao Wan’er—she was truly gentle, dignified, and graceful.","As pure and holy as a lotus flower.","In turn, Xiao Wan’er also had a good impression of Cui Qingwu.","At least, she felt more relaxed with her than with Liu Zhaoxue of the Jing State Liu Family.","Just then, Xiao Wuge looked left and right, but still seeing no sign of Chen Yi and Pei Guanli, he couldn’t help but tug on Xiao Wan’er’s sleeve.","\"Sister, isn’t brother-in-law back yet?\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in response. She was even more attentive to the situation in the courtyard than Xiao Wuge, glancing over from time to time.","It had even affected her focus while she was chatting with Cui Qingwu.","\"He might have been held up by something. I’ll take you to find him later.\"","Xiao Wuge said, \"Oh,\" and then watched the surrounding scholars engage in their lofty discussions, bored. He thought to himself:","’A so-called \"scholar\" should be a person of both talent and virtue.’","’The people here don’t seem to match what my brother-in-law said at all...’","Overhearing their conversation, Chen Yunfan gestured to Cui Qingwu, signaling her to keep a close eye on Xiao Wan’er.","Chen Yi had gone to the trouble of asking him for one favor, and he didn’t want anything to go wrong on his watch.","Cui Qingwu nodded, but a question couldn’t help but surface in her mind again.","\"Brother Yunfan, did Chen Yi not say where he was going earlier?\"","\"No, but he probably didn’t go far. After all, with that girl from the Mountain Race’s Cultivation...\"","Before Chen Yunfan could finish, he suddenly turned his head to look at the courtyard gate.","Cui Qingwu did the same.","Faintly, they both heard the sound of hurried footsteps coming from outside the courtyard.","Just as they were wondering, they heard someone shout from outside the gate, \"Sirs, Mr. Qingzhou has written a new poem!\"","\"As the poem was completed, over at Quchi, an Immortal Realm appeared!\"","\"An Immortal Realm?\"","Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu exchanged a look, both of them thinking of Chen Yi’s Perfection Realm of Calligraphy Dao.","Realizing what had happened, Chen Yunfan shrank back, wishing he could become invisible.","’I knew Brother Yi couldn’t possibly keep a low profile today.’","’So instead of showing off at the poetry gathering, he ran off to Quchi and whipped up some \"Immortal Realm.\"’","’Sigh... \"With Yi already born, why was Fan ever created?\" Being his elder brother is just too hard.’","Cui Qingwu knew he didn’t really mean it and said with a smile, \"Aren’t you curious what poetry Chen Yi wrote?\"","\"Nope...\"","Xiao Wan’er’s heart leaped with joy when she heard their voices, but after looking up and seeing no sign of Chen Yi, she couldn’t help but ask:","\"Little Sister Qingwu, has my brother-in-law returned?\"","Cui Qingwu shook her head and said, \"He hasn’t, but his poetry has.\"","\"His poetry?\"","\"Look, they’re asking about it over there.\"","Xiao Wan’er looked in the direction she pointed, her long, slender neck peeking out from her cloak.","She saw two scholars in long robes run up to the high platform, speaking excitedly with Mr. Yue Ming and the others.","The distance was too great; she couldn’t hear clearly.","Cui Qingwu perceived her curiosity and began relaying the conversation from the high platform as she listened:","\"Those two scholars are saying that Mr. Qingzhou composed a poem at Quchi, and it was like a Human World Immortal Realm.\"","\"Mr. Yue Ming is asking, ’Is that true? What poem did he write?’\"","\"The scholar says, ’Bright moon, when did you appear?’\"","\"The other one adds, ’I raise my cup and ask the azure sky...’\"","Hearing this much, a smile graced Xiao Wan’er’s face.","From those two lines alone, she knew the poem Chen Yi had composed was exceptional.","\"What else?\"","Cui Qingwu glanced at Chen Yunfan, who could no longer lift his head, and covered her mouth with her hand as she said with a laugh:","\"’I know not what year it is in the celestial palaces tonight... May we all be blessed with longevity, to share the moonlight though a thousand miles apart.’\"","After listening, Xiao Wan’er subconsciously murmured, \"What a beautiful poem.\" But as she repeated the last line to herself, a complicated feeling welled up in her heart.","’\"May we all be blessed with longevity, to share the moonlight though a thousand miles apart...\"’","’Is my brother-in-law writing about the moon, but also thinking of my second sister?’","Cui Qingwu, unaware of her thoughts, continued on her own, \"Mr. Yue Ming and the others are praising it, saying this poem deserves first place.\"","\"They’re also saying...\"","Chen Yunfan’s head was starting to ache from listening. He lifted his head to look at her and sighed, \"Qingwu, having good hearing isn’t meant to be used like this.\"","It was bad enough that the people on the high platform were praising the poem and Chen Yi.","But having to listen to Cui Qingwu repeat it all down here was simply excruciating."]},{"number":308,"title":"Chapter 308 - 219: Sharing the Moon’s Beauty Across 1000 Li","paragraphs":["Cui Qingwu chuckled, covering her mouth. \"I would have thought Brother Yunfan would be happy for Chen Yi.\"","\"Happy? Oh, I’m thrilled.\"","Beside them, Li Huai’gu could understand Chen Yunfan’s feelings. He shook his head and said,","\"Now that Brother Qingzhou has produced a poem like this, I’m afraid none of us will ever be able to compare.\"","The sentiment resonated deeply with Chen Yunfan.","By now, most of the people, both on the high platform and below it, had heard what had transpired. All of them had complex feelings about it.","Mr. Yue Ming, however, had lost his earlier composure. He stroked the beard on his chin, exclaiming in admiration,","\"A masterpiece, an absolute masterpiece...\"","\"So powerful and majestic, with such a magnificent Mental Realm... Truly, I have never seen its like in all my life.\"","Lord Liu smiled and nodded. \"It’s a pity Qingzhou isn’t here. Otherwise, we could have witnessed his ’Immortal Realm’ for ourselves.\"","Yang Ye, who had been sitting ramrod straight, offered a rare agreement. \"Qingzhou’s poem is exceptionally well-written. If we could but see the original manuscript, this trip would not have been in vain.\"","Seeing these three major figures speak, Mr. Zhuo Ying and the others had to hold back their own praise for Chen Yi’s poem for the time being.","Lord Liu looked at Lord Yang and asked with a gentle smile, \"Lord Yang, you’ve met Qingzhou before. What kind of young man is he?\"","\"Him? He’s just like his older brother, Yunfan. Both of them are a handful.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"To be comparable to the current Imperial Top Scholar... He must be quite remarkable.\"","Lord Yang glanced at him. \"Lord Liu, since when have you taken such an interest in Qingzhou?\"","The words may have been casual, but they struck a chord with the listeners.","Even Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the others turned to look at Lord Liu, their expressions unreadable.","Everyone present knew Lord Liu’s identity. They also knew that the Jing State Liu Family and the Xiao Family had been at odds recently.","Furthermore, they knew that just this afternoon, Lord Liu had been reprimanded by the Holy Emperor over the burning of the summer grain supply in Iron Wall Town.","So, when they heard Lord Yang’s question, their interest was naturally piqued.","Lord Liu calmly swept his gaze across the crowd before it landed on Lord Yang. He replied with a smile,","\"Mr. Qingzhou is so young and so talented. Remaining with the Xiao Family is not a sustainable long-term plan for him.\"","That single sentence was enough for Lord Yang to understand. ’He wants Chen Yi to enter officialdom?’","He thought for a moment before shaking his head. \"To each their own path. Qingzhou is currently at Guiyun Academy with Mr. Yue Ming. His talent will have its chance to shine there.\"","Mr. Yue Ming nodded. \"Unfortunately, he is incorrigibly lazy. Even I cannot persuade him otherwise.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Zhuo Ying said with a smile, \"There’s no need to persuade him, Headmaster. Qingzhou has his own plans. It’s better for him to stay with our academy.\"","\"Haha, Zhuo Ying is right.\"","Han Zhangping, Si Feng, and the others could clearly see the pride in the two men’s expressions, and they couldn’t help but feel a little envious.","After all, who wouldn’t want an instructor at the Perfection Realm of Calligraphy Dao in their own academy?","What’s more, he was capable of writing a timeless masterpiece like \"When will the bright moon appear?\"","Just then, Lord Liu said with a smile, \"The result is already clear. Brother Ming, why don’t you go ahead and announce it?\"","\"With a gem like Qingzhou’s poem presented first, I imagine all the students present will accept the outcome without complaint.\"","Mr. Yue Ming glanced at him, then at the others present, and nodded with a smile.","\"In that case, it would be rude of me to refuse.\"","That’s what he said, anyway. He had already made up his mind to give Chen Yi a piece of his mind later.","’Why couldn’t he have written it earlier? He just had to wait until the last possible moment to produce such a stunning masterpiece.’","’Making me worry for nothing for so long.’","A short while later, Mr. Zhuo Ying rose to announce the results. \"Today’s Poetry Champion is—from Guiyun Academy, Chen Yi, also known as Chen Qingzhou!\"","\"Let us all appreciate the poem he has written!\"","\"*Song of the Water Melody*. When will the bright moon appear...\"","Most people could accept this result. When faced with such superior talent, further argument was pointless.","Even the resentful Pei Zhaoye could only grit his teeth and swallow his pride.","Meanwhile, Liu Zhaoxue, sitting among the attendees, couldn’t stop frowning to herself.","She had known all along that Yan Fusha was going to make a move and test Chen Yi.","’But I can’t fathom under what circumstances Yan Fusha would be stupid enough to have Chen Yi compose a poem.’","’Isn’t he afraid of being discovered?’","But thoughts were just thoughts. There was nothing Liu Zhaoxue could do now but hope that Yan Fusha and the members of the Five Poison Sect wouldn’t be found out.","’At the very least, they can’t implicate me.’","In that moment, some were troubled, while others were overjoyed.","Xiao Wuge was slapping the table and shouting, \"Brother-in-law is the Poetry Champion!\"","Xiao Wan’er was also delighted, but two lines kept replaying in her mind: \"One like you is rare in this world,\" and \"Though a thousand miles apart, we share the same moon’s glow.\"","Her feelings were, to say the least, complicated.","Seeing all this, Chen Yunfan raised his cup with Li Huai’gu, and they both downed the wine in one gulp.","\"From now on, with Brother Yi here, if I write another poem... I’m a dog!\"","\"Brother Yunfan, you shouldn’t take it so hard. With Brother Qingzhou’s talent, we should all just be in awe.\"","\"Be in awe of him? He...\"","Chen Yunfan trailed off, sullenly shutting his mouth.","’I really should be in awe of Chen Yi.’","’Ever since they were children, Chen Yi was always the one everyone praised.’","’From the Chen Family elders and the great masters of Jinling down to the aunts and concubines in the various estates—even the servants doted on Chen Yi.’","’And I, Chen Yunfan, had it truly miserable.’","Cui Qingwu had a good idea of what he was thinking and was about to speak, but just then, she saw Huan’er hurrying over.","\"Miss, please step aside. There’s something...\"","Before Huan’er could finish, Cui Qingwu excused herself to those around them, then got up and followed the maidservant out.","Chen Yunfan watched her leave, a brow raised in curiosity. He discreetly strained to listen.","\"...message... Fledgling suspected to have been... kidnapped...\"","’Fledgling?’","Chen Yunfan sneered inwardly. ’What a stupid code name. And he got himself kidnapped.’","He was just about to reactivate his Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to rein in his Cultivation when he heard Cui Qingwu say,","\"How can that be?\"","\"His poem just arrived, and it even gave rise to an Immortal Realm...\"","’Poem... Immortal Realm...’","Chen Yunfan’s expression changed. ’Are they talking about... Brother Yi?’"]},{"number":309,"title":"Chapter 309 - 219: Sharing the Moon Across a Thousand Miles","paragraphs":["\"Miss, I don’t know the specifics either.\"","\"In that case, we’ll go take a look later.\"","Cui Qingwu was a bit puzzled, unsure of what had happened to Chen Yi, but all the Silver Banner Officers knew the name \"Fledgling.\"","She couldn’t very well just ignore it.","With this in mind, Cui Qingwu returned to the table, preparing to find a suitable excuse to leave.","But before she could speak, she saw Chen Yunfan gently pull her back. \"You stay here.\"","Cui Qingwu was taken aback. \"You...\"","Chen Yunfan explained in a low voice, \"You stay here and watch over the Xiao Family siblings. I’ll go.\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu’s beautiful eyes widened. \"You... Yunfan...\"","Chen Yunfan glanced at her, a serious expression on his handsome face, and said:","\"I’m going to see who’s so bold as to touch one of the Chen family!\"","Without waiting for Cui Qingwu to ask any more questions, Chen Yunfan stood up and walked out.","Huan’er had also overheard their conversation. \"M-Miss, Young Master Chen, he... he...\"","Cui Qingwu stared blankly at his retreating figure.","After a long moment, she suddenly smiled.","’Brother Yunfan, you’ve been hiding yourself so well.’","...","「Just past nine o’clock.」","The Painted Boat traveled north through a narrow channel and sailed onto the Chishui River.","The clamor was instantly cut off, leaving only the faint sounds of laughter from a few other Painted Boats that preferred not to linger in the Prefecture City.","Yan Fusha sat imposingly on the roof of the Painted Boat, his sinister gaze fixed on Chen Yi.","Several men in black stood around them, each watching a different direction, on high alert.","Chen Yi, in contrast, looked out over the Chishui River with a natural expression, as if he were simply admiring the scenery.","What Yan Fusha failed to notice was that Chen Yi’s fingers, hidden in his sleeves, were using a fine needle from an earring to pierce his acupoints.","He was extremely carefully and cautiously clearing the deadly Poison from his body.","In fact, his luck earlier had been terrible.","Of the two bottles of Poison—a fifty-fifty choice—he had, as fate would have it, grabbed the one containing the lethal toxin that killed in three breaths.","If Yan Fusha hadn’t assumed he was just an ordinary scholar with no Martial Arts Cultivation and used a low-grade Poison, he probably wouldn’t have lasted this long.","By then, the Painted Boat had traveled several miles, and their surroundings fell completely silent.","Only then did Yan Fusha speak. \"Mr. Qingzhou, there is something I do not understand. I hope you might enlighten me.\"","Chen Yi turned his head to look at him, waiting for his question.","\"You’ve been with us for so long. Aren’t you curious about our identities?\"","\"Curious? Of course I’m curious.\"","\"But if I ask, will you tell me?\"","Hearing Chen Yi’s words, Yan Fusha started laughing. \"Tell you? Why wouldn’t I?\"","\"I am Yan Fusha. HAHA... If I don’t tell you, how can I let Mr. Qingzhou die an informed man?\"","Chen Yi’s heart stirred. He turned his head to look at him. \"You’re going to kill me here?\"","Yan Fusha’s laughter stopped. He shook his head. \"Mr. Qingzhou, you are mistaken.\"","\"I intend to kill not only you, but that little beast from the Pei Family must not survive the night either.\"","He pointed to another Painted Boat about a hundred and fifty yards away and sneered, \"Perhaps you don’t know, sir.\"","\"My feud with her Mountain Race is a blood feud that cannot be reconciled.\"","Chen Yi said, \"Oh,\" and in the moment he took to glance at the other Painted Boat, he tapped the earring against his body twice more.","Yan Fusha, completely oblivious, continued, \"Mr. Qingzhou, your luck is both good and bad.\"","\"Originally, when I came to Shu State, I didn’t plan to make my move so soon.\"","\"However...\"","Before he could finish, one of the men in black beside him suddenly cried out, \"My lord!\"","\"Hm?\"","\"That Painted Boat!\"","Yan Fusha looked over and saw a small figure peeking out furtively from a second-floor window of the nearby Painted Boat.","Who else could it be but Pei Guanli?","Yan Fusha instantly understood what had happened. \"I seem to have underestimated the Mountain Race’s Gu Insects.\"","\"To think she could neutralize so much potent Poison.\"","With that, Yan Fusha angrily ordered, \"Move in closer! Capture her!\"","However, there was no movement from his men.","Yan Fusha froze for a second, then erupted with his full power, striking out with a palm to his side.","BOOM!","More than half the Painted Boat was instantly blasted apart, sending splinters flying through the air.","Yan Fusha shot a sidelong glance, and when he saw the figure standing in a corner of the boat, his eyes blazed with murderous fury.","\"It was you?!\"","Chen Yi ignored him. He glanced at the sneaky Pei Guanli on the other Painted Boat, tossed aside the medicine vial in his hand, and sighed.","’This girl, she neutralizes the poison and then can’t even stay put. She endured for so long, too.’","Fortunately, Tiger Girl had understood his earlier warning, which gave him some small comfort.","Over on her boat, Pei Guanli wasn’t thinking that far ahead. Seeing Yan Fusha make his move, she dropped the pretense and ran out, shouting:","\"Brother-in-law, I’m here to help!\"","Chen Yi grimaced as if he had a toothache and turned his head to scold her, \"Just stay put over there! Haven’t you caused me enough trouble?\"","Pei Guanli shrank back and leaned over the side of her boat, watching him with wide, pitiful eyes.","\"I was just a little careless...\"","Chen Yi shook his head helplessly and stopped paying her any mind. He looked over at Yan Fusha, sized him up, and said with a smile:","\"As expected of an Elder from the Five Poison Sect. Your poison resistance is indeed high.\"","One bottle of Qingfeng Drunk and one of Immortal Drunk had taken down all the men in black, but Yan Fusha alone was still standing.","He had to admit, the people of the Five Poison Sect were quite capable.","Although Yan Fusha had never heard the two words \"poison resistance,\" he understood the meaning behind them.","He stared daggers at Chen Yi, his voice sinister and vicious as he asked, \"You... you knew about me and the Five Poison Sect all along?!\""]},{"number":310,"title":"Chapter 310 - 220: Chen Wudi","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Chen Yi neither confirmed nor denied it.","\"Elder Yan, your actions tonight have truly given me a headache.\"","It had been a long time since he’d been in such a sorry state.","The only other time he’d been injured was during his encounter with Simurgh Phoenix Cui Qingwu.","At all other times, he was either confined in the Xiao Family’s residence with servants to wait on him, or he was the one plotting and scheming against others.","This was the first time he had ever been schemed against and ended up in such a miserable state.","But compared to Chen Yi’s \"headache,\" Yan Fusha was filled with shock and fury.","He couldn’t understand how Chen Yi knew he was from the Five Poison Sect.","He hadn’t mentioned the \"Five Poison Sect\" at all tonight.","Even when he had brought out the snakes and centipedes, given the common knowledge of Jianghu People today, most would only associate them with some other Evil Demonic Dao.","Yet Chen Yi, an Instructor from Guiyun Academy, had exposed his identity as a Five Poison Sect Elder in a single breath, making it impossible for him not to be suspicious.","After a moment of silence, the aura around Yan Fusha began to churn.","Wisps of dim, black energy floated from his hands, at times forming into coiled snakes, at others into poisonous scorpions.","He stared at Chen Yi with a sinister expression and said menacingly,","\"I never expected that not only is Mr. Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao profound, but your Martial Arts are formidable as well.\"","Chen Yi glanced at his palms. \"I can’t compare to you, Elder Yan.\"","Lower Fourth Grade, and Great Success in Fist Dao.","And that wasn’t even counting the possible Poisonous Insects and Poisons he had.","Yan Fusha was clearly much harder to deal with than any common practitioner of the Evil Demonic Dao.","\"Mr. Qingzhou, there is one thing I don’t understand. I hope you might enlighten me.\"","\"How did you find out about my identity?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"No comment.\"","The information about the Five Poison Sect had all come from Liu Lang’s eavesdropping; there was nothing to discuss.","Besides, he and Pei Guanli had nearly been killed by Yan Fusha tonight. It was already a fight to the death between them.","He wasn’t about to say anything more to a mortal enemy.","With that thought, Chen Yi completely released the restraints of his Black Tortoise Concealment Technique.","He activated the Four Symbols Skill, and the True Essence in his meridians began to surge like liquid mercury, flowing without end.","As his energy circulated, his originally frail-looking frame began to swell and expand.","He looked more upright, more substantial.","Even his face took on a harder, more rugged quality, losing its previous scholarly look.","Yan Fusha gave him a long, hard look and said, \"What a pity.\"","\"A pity for such a promising teacher!\"","Before his voice had even faded,","Yan Fusha stomped forward, his body blurring into a shadow. In the blink of an eye, he was right in front of Chen Yi.","His left hand, shaped like a blade, jabbed straight for Chen Yi’s eyes.","Simultaneously, his Fist Intent stirred the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, unleashing a pressure like a fierce gale scouring a mountain range. It roiled the very air around them in an attempt to slow Chen Yi’s movements.","Furthermore, a wisp of Evil Poisonous energy formed a blade and slashed across.","But in the next instant, his body and his hand-blade froze, as if crushed under the weight of a great mountain.","It was Chen Yi’s Great Success Fist Dao, as imposing as a mountain peak!","Not only that.","As his own Fist Intent erupted, Chen Yi used the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Step Technique. He twisted like a roaming dragon, evading both the hand-blade and the slash of Evil Poisonous energy.","Then, he unleashed his full power—Mountain Shattering Fist: Shaking Mountain!","As he threw the punch, his True Essence exploded into rippling shockwaves. The wooden planks beneath his feet shattered in concentric circles, splinters flying everywhere.","Whether intentionally or not, Yan Fusha made no move to dodge or evade.","BOOM!","Waves of energy rippled out from the fist’s impact. The mountain-like might of his True Essence and Fist Intent combined, as ferocious as a wildfire.","The sheer force of the blow was enough to shred what little remained of the tattered Painted Boat.","Yet, a punch of such incredible power was completely blocked by an extremely faint layer of black energy enveloping Yan Fusha’s body.","\"’Protective True Gang...’\"","Chen Yi’s brow furrowed, and his body shot back like a meteor to the stern of the Painted Boat.","Completely unharmed, Yan Fusha retracted his hand and stood up straight. He turned to face Chen Yi and sneered,","\"Great Success in Fist Dao, a Fist Intent as mighty as a mountain... Mr. Qingzhou, what impressive skill you possess.\"","\"If your Cultivation wasn’t so far beneath mine, I’m afraid I might not have been able to handle you today.\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal flick of his wrist, his eyes remaining fixed on Yan Fusha as his mind raced.","’Not only was that last punch blocked, but the rebound from his Protective True Gang injured my fist.’","’In a head-on fight, I’m no match for him at all.’","’I can’t fight him directly. I’ll have to rely on hit-and-run tactics.’","At this thought, Chen Yi took a deep breath. He circulated the Four Symbols Skill throughout his body, and his feet immediately felt a little lighter.","Great Success Martial Arts·Step could also connect with the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, granting it the blessing of Spiritual Essence.","The Meteor Butterfly Step possessed a relentlessly surging power, allowing for greater stamina.","The Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Step utilized Vortex Power, making one’s movements far more agile within a confined space.","Seeing Chen Yi remain silent, Yan Fusha snorted coldly and pressed his attack once more.","He thrust out a palm.","Having no intention of a direct confrontation, Chen Yi twisted his body and dodged with ghostly speed.","The swiftness of his Body Technique made Yan Fusha’s eyes narrow.","He whipped his head around to follow Chen Yi’s movement. \"A Body Technique at the Great Success Realm?\"","\"You... how can you have achieved Great Success in two different Daos!?\"","’It’s not that no one can cultivate both Fist Dao and Body Technique to the Great Success Realm. But those who do are all famous grandmasters of the Jianghu.’","’Even someone as mighty as Immortal Bai, a peerless talent, was only at the Perfection Realm in Fist Dao and the Great Success Realm in Body Technique when he first made his name!’","’But how old is Chen Yi?’","’On what grounds?’","’Is his talent in Martial Arts truly that peerless?’","Unwilling to accept it, Yan Fusha’s eyes widened as he stared at Chen Yi in disbelief. \"You’re not Chen Yi!\"","\"Who in the world are you?\"","\"Shui Hetong from the Wind and Rain Tower? Or Hua Huixiang from Wudang Mountain?\"","\"No, that’s not right. Their Calligraphy Dao couldn’t possibly have reached Perfection...\"","\"That’s right, there’s also your Calligraphy Dao...\"","\"Two Daos at Great Success, and one at Perfection...\"","\"You... you... you’re even stronger than Immortal Bai was when he first made his name in the Jianghu?\"","\"...\"","Hearing all this, even in the middle of a life-and-death struggle, Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh.","\"Of course I’m not Chen Yi. The people of the Jianghu gave me a nickname: the ’Wave-Riding White Dragon,’ Chen Wudi!\"","At that moment, Pei Guanli, who had been listening to their exchange, grew inexplicably excited. She couldn’t help but leap to her feet, cupping her fair, delicate hands to her face as she cried out:"]},{"number":311,"title":"Chapter 311 - 220: Chen Wudi","paragraphs":["\"That’s right! My brother-in-law is Chen Wudi, known in the Jianghu as the ’Wave-Riding White Dragon’!\"","Chen Yi shot her an irritated glance and waved for her to stay hidden.","’As long as Yan Fusha’s target is me, it’s fine. I can still barely manage.’","’If Yan Fusha switched his target to Pei Guanli, wouldn’t I be thrown into a panic?’","Fortunately, at this moment, Yan Fusha only had eyes for him. He was still staring at him in disbelief, muttering incessantly:","\"A young man, not even twenty, has reached Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao and Great Success in both the Fist Dao and Body Techniques...\"","\"How is that possible? How is that possible...\"","Suddenly, Yan Fusha’s voice stopped.","The eyes looking at Chen Yi instantly turned blood-red, the whites filling with crimson veins.","The True Essence Gang Qi protecting his body turned as dark as ink, with wisps of deep red drifting through it.","\"I must admit, Mr. Qingzhou, your talent for Martial Arts is something I have never seen in my entire life.\"","\"Therefore, I cannot let you live today!\"","Chen Yi immediately felt the power of Yan Fusha’s gale-like Fist Intent increase dramatically.","He hastily retreated another two steps, secretly on guard.","’This man is a complete lunatic.’","Lunatic or not, Yan Fusha clearly didn’t care at this moment.","He only knew that he absolutely could not let Chen Yi leave here alive today.","With such terrifying talent for Martial Arts, if he wasn’t killed today, he would one day become a grave threat to the Five Poison Sect.","The next moment, with a single step, Yan Fusha was at Chen Yi’s side, lashing out repeatedly with his hands formed into claws.","Five-colored Evil Poisonous scattered from his claws, filling a ten-foot area across half of the Painted Boat.","This time, with both Fist Intent and Evil Poisonous unleashed, Yan Fusha was using his full strength.","Just as before, Chen Yi refused to be drawn into a direct fight. His eyes were locked on Yan Fusha’s figure as his feet twisted and turned without pause, dodging the pair of multi-colored claw blades.","But while he could evade, the Painted Boat beneath his feet suffered the consequences.","In less than three breaths, the fifty-foot-long Painted Boat was reduced to a single layer of floorboards.","Even so, Yan Fusha did not stop.","Even though his Body Technique was more than a step slower than Chen Yi’s, he forcefully channeled his True Essence Gang Qi to ride the wind, relentlessly pursuing Chen Yi.","His claws danced relentlessly, every strike packed with immense power.","BOOM, BOOM, BOOM...","Amidst a series of roars, the Painted Boat disintegrated. The turbulent currents of the Chishui River exploded, creating one watery crater after another.","River water splashed everywhere.","In just ten breaths, Yan Fusha had all but demolished the Painted Boat.","Chen Yi, treading on the splintered planks, frowned to himself. ’Body Techniques aren’t true flight; they require a surface to push off from.’","’On the Painted Boat, it was fine, the True Essence consumption wasn’t too high. But switching to the river’s surface will accelerate my True Essence consumption.’","’I can’t keep getting tangled up with him here!’","With this in mind, Chen Yi dodged two more strikes and, in the brief opening as he ducked, suddenly shot away.","Using the Meteor Butterfly Step Body Technique, he tapped lightly and swiftly across the surface of the Chishui River, skimming straight for the bank.","Yan Fusha, of course, gave chase relentlessly.","And when he took a step through the air, his speed was actually a notch faster than Chen Yi’s Body Technique.","In a single breath, he caught up to Chen Yi and threw a palm strike, his eyes filled with vicious malice.","Chen Yi glanced to the side. His True Essence suddenly condensed beneath his feet, and he stomped in mid-air with an explosive sound.","His entire body shifted sideways three feet, narrowly dodging Yan Fusha’s palm.","But the five-colored Evil Poisonous carried in the palm’s wake still brushed against his shoulder.","A searing, needle-like pain instantly flared up on the side of his shoulder.","Without pausing to look, Chen Yi used the momentum to land on the bank, where he ducked and rolled to evade two more palm strikes before finally getting a moment’s respite.","He glanced at it with his Qi Observation Skill—the shoulder tainted by the Evil Poisonous had swollen up in an extremely short time.","The pus and blood within had turned a purplish-blue.","’This Evil Poisonous is terrifyingly potent.’","Realizing this, Chen Yi’s hands moved quickly. He directly plunged a hairpin into the flesh below the swollen pustule.","Using the Controlling Needle with Qi technique, he swiftly began to purge the Evil Poisonous from his shoulder.","Seeing this, Yan Fusha’s blood-red eyes turned even redder, and a faint black glow seemed to surface within them.","He stared at Chen Yi’s actions and roared with a savage expression, \"You... you’re a Medical Saint Hand as well?!\"","Yan Fusha was on the verge of madness. He couldn’t believe anyone could achieve what Chen Yi had.","Medical Dao, Martial Arts, Calligraphy Dao... spanning three Daos, yet you have four great accomplishments!","Even Immortal Bai, who was unrivaled in the Jianghu, had only cultivated three Daos after decades of fame.","\"I cannot let you live!\"","\"I cannot let you live!\"","Yan Fusha roared savagely as his attacks grew even more ferocious.","His body became a blur of afterimages as he chased Chen Yi, striking out with his palms again and again.","\"Stop! Just stand there and let me kill you!\"","\"With talent like yours, if I don’t eliminate you today, you’ll become a disaster in the future!\"","How could Chen Yi possibly stop?","He alternated between Wandering Dragon and Phoenix and Meteor Butterfly Step, continuously evading Yan Fusha’s claws.","To conserve True Essence, he didn’t run far, instead just circling within a hundred-foot radius.","Whenever the Evil Poisonous pervaded the area, he would change position and continue to tangle with Yan Fusha.","「A few moments later.」","Chen Yi gradually grew accustomed to Yan Fusha’s Palm and Claw Techniques. In between dodges, he was now able to find openings to strike back.","However, due to the vast difference in their Cultivation, his Mountain Shattering Fist and Hundred Flowers Palm were completely unable to injure Yan Fusha.","’A Fourth Grade Realm Martial Arts Powerhouse is this terrifying... I wonder how strong Xiao Jinghong is, with a Cultivation in the Upper Three Grades?’","’Compared to Yan Fusha, that Elder Demon Fang was a real idiot.’","’If Elder Demon Fang hadn’t attacked me and Liu Lang right in front of Black Tooth, I’m afraid even the two of us together wouldn’t have come out on top.’","Chen Yi continued to run circles around Yan Fusha while trying to think of a counter-strategy.","He knew this couldn’t go on.","His Cultivation was already weaker than Yan Fusha’s. The longer this dragged on, the worse his situation would become.","He thought and thought, but he couldn’t come up with a good solution.","Unless he chose to expose his Martial Arts and Medical Dao skills and make a desperate run for the Prefecture City."]},{"number":312,"title":"Chapter 312 - 220: Chen Wudi","paragraphs":["Yan Fusha didn’t know what Chen Yi was thinking, his expression turning grim as he stared at him.","After so long, he had regained his composure and had also come to accept the fact that Chen Yi’s talent was peerless.","A man even more terrifying than Immortal Bai... his talent was indeed worthy of being called \"peerless.\"","’Too bad I’ve already offended such a person beyond any hope of reconciliation.’","’What’s even more unfortunate is that he’s not a member of my Five Poison Sect.’","As Yan Fusha mulled this over, he took advantage of a lull in the action to pull out several Silver Needles and shoot them forth.","Chen Yi subconsciously used Wandering Dragon and Phoenix to dodge.","But just as he turned to dart away, a snake’s mouth as large as a bowl suddenly appeared before his eyes.","HISS—","With no time to think, Chen Yi raised his arm to block.","DING!","DING!","DING!","Amidst a series of sharp clangs, Chen Yi was sent flying backward by an immense force. He crashed through a tree before landing gracelessly on the ground.","\"Brother-in-law!?\"","Pei Guanli, seeing this from a distance, couldn’t help but cry out in alarm before unleashing a stream of curses at Yan Fusha.","\"You goddamn Yan Fusha! Are you a complete moron? Did you take the wrong medicine or something?\"","\"What kind of hero ambushes people?\"","\"The Five Poison Sect taught you how to use poison, but did they forget to teach you how to be a decent human being?\"","\"You...\"","Yan Fusha paid Pei Guanli no mind, merely frowning as he stared at Chen Yi.","A black snake, as thick as a baby’s arm, was slowly coiling around his waist. Its triangular head was raised near his neck, its gaze also fixed on Chen Yi.","\"Mr. Qingzhou, you were lucky to survive that attack.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi got to his feet and waved at Pei Guanli to show he was fine, then looked at his right arm.","The sleeve there was torn, revealing a glint of silver.","’The Five-section Spear...’","’It’s a good thing the Five-section Spear was there to block. Otherwise, that black snake’s surprise attack would have left me either dead or severely wounded.’","After confirming he wasn’t seriously injured, Chen Yi let out a long breath. He then unwrapped the Five-section Spear from his arm and assembled it.","Yan Fusha was stunned by his actions. \"A spear?\"","Suddenly, as if realizing something, he stammered, \"You... your spear... your Spear Dao couldn’t also be...\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"Just as you see. Great Success.\"","Today, aside from his Chess Dao and Zither Dao, which weren’t suited for combat, he had played all his cards. Revealing his Spear Dao now wouldn’t make much of a difference.","Yan Fusha was unwilling to believe it. \"Ha, haha... Are you toying with me?\"","\"How could anyone in this world possibly achieve such a feat?\"","Chen Yi twirled the Long Spear with both hands in a flourish before holding it at his side. \"Want to try me?\"","’A blessing in disguise, I suppose.’","’If not for that black snake’s attack, I would have forgotten I still had my Spear Dao to use.’","It wasn’t that his Spear Dao was stronger than his Fist Dao, but that his Dragon-Falling Spear Technique, when enhanced by the Divine Position Gold Spirit, possessed an incredible Sharp Power.","Combined with the Celestial Tier Dragon-Falling Spear Technique, perhaps he could tear through Yan Fusha’s Protective True Gang.","\"Try you?\"","Without another word, Yan Fusha’s figure shot forward.","Man and snake attacked as one.","\"I don’t care if you’ve reached Great Success in the Spear Dao or not, you will die today!\"","Chen Yi stared at the approaching figure, let out a soft breath, and then thrust his spear, sending out a flash of light.","Yan Fusha’s eyes twitched. He actually felt a hint of a threat from that spear’s gleam.","With no time to think, he tapped his feet and shot off at an angle.","The black snake at his waist flew out in the opposite direction, forming a pincer attack.","The five-colored Evil Poisonous aura, along with the venom spat by the black snake, enveloped the thirty-foot area in front of Chen Yi.","Yan Fusha charged straight at Chen Yi, aiming to engage in close combat to prevent him from unleashing the full power of his Spear Technique.","But Chen Yi saw it all.","He took a step back. As he pulled back with his left hand, his right hand flicked the Long Spear from side to side, executing two consecutive thrusts.","The Spear Intent was like gold.","The swift thrusts formed two three-foot-long golden beams of light along the spear’s shaft, stabbing straight for the faces of Yan Fusha and the black snake.","Yan Fusha roared in anger and slapped out with his palm, shattering the spear’s gleam.","However, the Gang Qi in his palm was also torn open in the exchange.","The black snake wasn’t so lucky. It failed to dodge in time and was pierced through the head by Chen Yi’s spear, dying a miserable death on the spot.","Yan Fusha’s eyes looked ready to split open with rage. \"Black Dragon!\"","Having landed a successful blow, Chen Yi pressed his advantage. \"Black Dragon? It’s just a dead snake!\"","He took a single step, man and Long Spear becoming one.","A ball of light, as dazzling as the sun, suddenly erupted from the spear’s tip. Within it, one could faintly see palm-sized golden dragons.","It was none other than the first form of the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique—Dragon Chasing the Sun!","Watching the approaching Chen Yi, Yan Fusha flicked his wrist and threw several Silver Needles.","At the same time, the True Gang within his body erupted completely as he charged recklessly toward Chen Yi.","He formed his hands into claws and tore directly at the golden sphere.","\"I want you dead!\"","BOOM—","A deafening roar erupted as the Evil Poisonous aura collided with the Gold Spirit Spear Intent.","Amidst the churning, multicolored Evil Poisonous aura, countless palm-sized golden dragons could be seen flitting up and down.","They attacked Chen Yi and Yan Fusha respectively.","Chen Yi’s eyes narrowed. He swept his Long Spear, tearing an opening in the Evil Poisonous aura, and used the Meteor Butterfly Step to pursue Yan Fusha.","Yan Fusha, in contrast, was not faring as well.","The countless golden dragons descended upon him like sharp daggers plunging into his body.","Under the spear’s light, his Protective True Gang seemed to have lost its effect, and in the blink of an eye, several wounds appeared on his body.","His clothes were shredded, and blood flowed freely.","As if struck by lightning, Yan Fusha was sent flying backward, dodging Chen Yi’s follow-up Spear Techniques.","\"Your Spear Dao can actually tear through True Essence Gang Qi!?\"","Although such a thing wasn’t unheard of—it could be achieved through a Cultivation Technique, a Secret Technique, or a higher Martial Arts Realm—how could it be so coincidental? Why now, of all times?","Why did Chen Yi have to pull it out right when he was about to kill him?","The situation was now completely reversed—he was actually at a disadvantage!","Seeing this, Chen Yi breathed a sigh of relief. ’The tables have turned. Now I just have to kill Yan Fusha, and all this will be over.’","But just as he was about to press his advantage and finish things in one fell swoop, he saw Yan Fusha take a small bottle from his robes and swallow its entire contents.","\"You forced me to do this!\"","As he roared, several streams of black energy inexplicably appeared on Yan Fusha’s face, snaking downwards in hideous, terrifying lines.","It looked as if they were about to spread across his entire body.","Chen Yi’s brow furrowed slightly, and he immediately used his Qi Observation Skill to look.","He saw that Yan Fusha’s aura had suddenly surged, more than doubling in strength.","’Damn it, a banned substance?’"]},{"number":313,"title":"Chapter 313 - 221: Dragon-Falling Kills the Enemy, Spear Dao Perfection","paragraphs":["Having achieved Great Success in the Medical Dao, Chen Yi naturally knew a few methods for stimulating the body’s potential, whether through striking acupoints or using medicinal drugs.","But most of those were sinister techniques with severe consequences, either causing extreme damage to the meridians or harming one’s physical foundation.","A momentary burst of power could mean stagnating for the rest of one’s life, never to advance another inch.","Even if a normal person knew of such methods, they would not dare to use them.","Unfortunately for him, there was a madman right before his eyes.","Yan Fusha, however, couldn’t be bothered with any of that. Once the drug’s effects took hold, his blood-red eyes saw nothing but Chen Yi.","\"Kill! I’ll kill you!\"","Before the words had even left his lips, he stomped forward, transforming into a streak of black light as he shot straight toward his target.","Chen Yi had no time to think, simply raising his spear to defend himself.","Almost at the exact moment he did, a tremendous force slammed into him.","An overwhelming force!","Chen Yi was sent flying, his eyes widening slightly as he stared at the savage figure charging at him once more.","His True Essence flared, coursing through his limbs as he grounded himself with tremendous force.","His form shifted again, and he used the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Body Technique to evade, by the slimmest of margins, a claw swipe from Yan Fusha aimed right at his face.","If that claw had connected, it would have torn off half his face.","Yan Fusha missed, then dropped into a low sweep. Halfway through the motion, the kick angled sharply upward, aimed straight for Chen Yi’s neck.","\"Die!\"","Chen Yi blocked again with his spear.","THUD.","It was another heavy, powerful blow, and it sent him flying sideways.","But unlike the last time when he was caught off guard, Chen Yi was prepared. He kept his stance low, sliding firmly across the ground.","His Cultivation, Technique, and physical strength were all inferior at the moment; he absolutely had to avoid being knocked into the air.","There, he would be nothing but a target for Yan Fusha.","Chen Yi kept this firmly in mind, putting all his effort into neutralizing Yan Fusha’s ferocious and deadly attacks one by one.","He was especially careful to avoid the five-colored Noxious Miasma erupting from Yan Fusha’s palms.","In the span of just ten breaths, the two had exchanged over a hundred blows.","They moved so fast that they were little more than a blur of green and black, tangling and separating in an instant.","All the trees and rocks within a hundred-zhang radius shattered into pieces.","In particular, every time Yan Fusha unleashed his five-colored Noxious Miasma, it would corrode everything in its path.","Amidst a SIZZLING sound, wisps of acrid, poisonous smoke began to spread, shrouding the dense woods.","Seeing this from the distant Painted Boat, Pei Guanli forgot all about cursing at Yan Fusha and began to pace back and forth anxiously.","\"Brother-in-law, you have to be okay!\"","\"It’s all my fault. If I hadn’t fallen into those bastards’ trap, my brother-in-law wouldn’t have had to come here.\"","Pei Guanli was filled with worry and self-blame, but she knew there was nothing she could do. All she could do was pray that Chen Yi could kill Yan Fusha, or that someone would come to rescue them.","But she knew. Their current location was far from Shu State Prefecture City, right on the banks of the Chishui River. It would be difficult for the sound of their battle, no matter how loud, to reach the Prefecture City.","Besides, tonight was the Mid-Autumn Festival. Even if anyone was out and about, they wouldn’t be in this desolate stretch of wilderness.","As these thoughts raced through her mind, Pei Guanli couldn’t help but shout, \"Brother-in-law, you have to be careful!\"","Chen Yi was struggling just to stay alive; how could he possibly notice anything else?","In the short span of their fight, though he fought with all his might, there were still moments when he was overwhelmed.","His right arm, which had been corroded by the Noxious Miasma earlier, was once again tainted by it and had begun to swell painfully.","Yan Fusha’s claws had torn away a patch of skin and flesh from his chest, and the Noxious Miasma was seeping into that wound as well.","He had over a dozen other wounds, large and small. Dark red blood and pus seeped through his tattered robes, staining his body.","He was in a truly wretched state.","And yet, Yan Fusha was in an even worse state.","Although his aura hadn’t weakened—his True Essence, Fist Intent, and Noxious Miasma all still at their peak—his body had become even more savage and terrifying to behold.","Blood trickled from his eyes, nose, and mouth. Across his body, blackened veins bulged, faintly seeping blood.","His black Night Clothes had long since been dyed red with his own blood.","Yet Yan Fusha seemed to feel nothing, continuing his ferocious pursuit of Chen Yi without pause.","Every palm strike, every claw swipe, even attacks with his joints and limbs, were devastatingly powerful.","His Fist Intent channeled Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, unleashing waves of Noxious Miasma.","\"Die! Why aren’t you dead yet?\"","\"A peerless talent like you... I can’t let you mature. I absolutely cannot let you grow any stronger!\"","Chen Yi remained unmoved, his eyes never leaving Yan Fusha for an instant.","Even in his battered state, he had no intention of abandoning his goal of killing Yan Fusha.","He was just waiting for an opening.","Fortunately, with his knowledge of the Medical Dao, he could use the brief lulls between dodging and blocking to strike his own acupoints. This helped heal his injuries and slowed the rate at which the Noxious Miasma invaded his meridians and organs.","Otherwise, he wouldn’t have been able to last this long either.","Just then, a flash of golden light passed before Chen Yi’s eyes—","[In the seventh quarter of the Hai hour, you witnessed the Guiyun Academy’s Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala. You claimed the title of Poetry Champion with your ’Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn’. At Quchi, you used the Calligraphy Dao to manifest an immortal realm of jade palaces. Performance: Excellent.]","[Reward: ’Mid-Autumn River Map’, Opportunity +66.]","Chen Yi didn’t have time for a closer look; he hurriedly dodged another of Yan Fusha’s attacks.","The appearance of the large, golden words had almost gotten him struck in the face.","But it seemed that when it rained, it poured.","Just moments later, more golden light appeared—","[Daily Intelligence - Profound-rank Middle Grade: At the Zi hour, Yan Fusha and others from the Five Poison Sect kidnap Chen Yi, the live-in son-in-law of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, and Pei Guanli of the Mountain Race. A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","\"...\"","Chen Yi cursed inwardly, his temper flaring from the distractions of the golden text and the relentless attacks from Yan Fusha.","Seeing that Yan Fusha’s aura was finally beginning to wane, he whirled around and put all his strength into the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Body Technique, instantly putting three zhang of distance between them.","\"Where do you think you’re going?!\"","’Escape?’","Chen Yi let out a cold snort. He abruptly planted his feet, and in an instant, his True Essence surged through every fiber of his being."]},{"number":314,"title":"Chapter 314 - 221: Dragon-Falling Slays the Enemy, Spear Dao Perfection","paragraphs":["He didn’t even look at Yan Fusha’s position. He just spun around and executed a Retreating Lance.","It was the eighth form of the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique: Inverting Heaven and Earth!","The moment he thrust, the spear’s light split in two, like a pair of long golden dragons attacking Yan Fusha from above and below.","Meanwhile, Chen Yi himself was between the two golden dragons. His body and long spear became one, also transforming into a draconic form as he charged forward to kill.","Yan Fusha’s eyes widened, and a savage smile suddenly spread across his face.","\"A fine attack! Haha!\"","As he spoke, he never stopped moving. He met the three draconic spear gleams head-on, flipping his claws upward.","The five-colored Evil Poison coalesced into a ball.","He then pressed his claws downward, unleashing ten blades of Evil Poison.","An instant later, the three draconic spear gleams collided with the Evil Poison, erupting in a deafening roar.","BOOM, BOOM, BOOM...","The golden spear light scattered and the five-colored Evil Poison surged, shattering everything within a hundred-foot radius.","Boulders and trees alike were pulverized into fine debris that scattered in all directions.","Amidst the clash of deadly killing moves, time seemed to stand still.","Chen Yi clearly saw Yan Fusha’s savage face, as well as the several wounds left where the spear’s light had pierced his Protective True Gang.","He also saw the pustules forming on his own wounds where the Evil Poison had corroded his flesh.","In the next moment, inspiration struck.","Chen Yi gripped his long spear with both hands and twirled it twice, the golden spear light forming two Wind-Fire Wheels.","In an instant, he swept away all the surrounding Evil Poison.","Immediately after, without a moment’s thought, Chen Yi unleashed one of the four killing moves he had gained after his Dragon-Falling Spear Technique reached the Celestial Tier.","Dragon-Falling!","Chen Yi raised his long spear high without any flourish, then brought it down in a simple, unadorned chop.","But as he swung the long spear in a full circle, it traced a golden arc, like a crescent moon.","What followed was a disturbance in the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism that shook the area for a thousand feet around—","A dark cloud, only a thousand feet wide, instantly appeared in the night sky, and a bolt of golden lightning struck straight down.","It was like a mighty golden dragon, roaring as it rushed toward the defenseless Yan Fusha.","\"ROAR!!\"","As the dragon’s phantom struck Yan Fusha, a clear, drawn-out dragon’s cry echoed in all directions.","Faintly, a golden dragon phantom could be seen spiraling upward before vanishing into the dark cloud.","Chen Yi then appeared behind Yan Fusha, staggering as if from exhaustion.","Yan Fusha, in contrast, slowly turned his head. His surging True Essence Gang Qi was gone, the black, savage marks on his body had vanished, and all that remained was a shriveled husk.","He tremblingly raised a hand, pointed at Chen Yi with a stunned look in his eyes, and said, \"You... you’ve... Spear Dao Perfection...\"","The Martial Arts Realms, from entry-level, Minor Success, and Great Success to Perfection, are all about the application of the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","Different Realms allow one to borrow different amounts of power from heaven and earth.","At the entry-level, one forms the rudiments of a Martial Arts Mental Realm, gaining access to things like Sword Qi and Spear Qi to enhance the power of their Techniques.","The Minor Success Realm is when the Martial Arts Mental Realm is considered established.","One can receive a partial blessing from the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism and also gain unique ways to apply it.","For example, the Mountain and Gale aspects of the Fist Dao.","At the Great Success Realm, the power of one’s Techniques expands further. Fist Intent becomes heavier, Sword Intent becomes sharper, and their range grows wider.","These three Realms are the limit known to ordinary Jianghu People—the limit of human capability.","But it is a different matter entirely if one’s Martial Arts Cultivation reaches the Perfection Realm.","The most direct sign is a change in the world itself—lightning flashing and thunder rolling, rivers flowing backward, and so on.","As long as a person’s Cultivation and True Essence are sufficient to support it, even moving mountains and filling seas is not impossible.","Therefore, in Yan Fusha’s eyes, Chen Yi’s Dragon-Falling spear move, which had just triggered a change in the world, had already reached the realm of Perfect Spear Dao.","But what was the truth?","Chen Yi glanced at him and shook his head. \"Not yet.\"","A man’s words on his deathbed are said to be true; he had no reason to lie to Yan Fusha.","Who would have known that just as a faint, knowing smile appeared on Yan Fusha’s face and his body split in two, Chen Yi would see a brilliant Jin Guang before his eyes.","Rows of large golden characters appeared one after another—","[At the first quarter of the Zi hour, you witnessed Yan Fusha and others from the Five Poison Sect kidnap Chen Yi, son-in-law of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, and Pei Guanli of the Mountain Race. You personally slayed fourteen Evil Demons from the Five Poison Sect, including Yan Fusha. Performance: Excellent.]","[Reward: \"Thousand Poison Skill,\" Opportunity +45.]","[Spear Technique Advanced. Technique: Dragon-Falling, has broken through to Perfect Level. Gained a glimpse into the meaning of Spear Dao Perfection.]","[Spear Dao: Great Success. Progress +1000. Reached Perfection Realm.]","Chen Yi scanned the text, his face frozen in a daze. He then felt vast and profound mysteries of the Spear Dao flooding his mind.","’My Spear Dao... it really reached Perfection?’","Chen Yi read it over twice more to be sure, then couldn’t help but look at Yan Fusha’s corpse, a smile creeping onto his face.","\"My apologies, Elder Yan. I didn’t mean to hide it from you. The epiphany just came a little too suddenly.\"","’Heh, Spear Dao Perfection.’","’This really is a blessing in disguise.’","But before Chen Yi could celebrate for long, his vision went black and he collapsed backward.","He hit the ground with a THUD.","The areas on his body that had been corroded by the Evil Poison began to swell up, one after another.","Blood and pus oozed from the wounds.","Seeing this from the Chishui River, the joyous expression on Pei Guanli’s face turned to worry. She scrambled back to the Painted Boat to retrieve her various bottles and jars, then leaped directly off the boat and swam desperately toward Chen Yi.","A few moments later, Pei Guanli reached Chen Yi’s side.","Without even taking a moment to examine him closely, she took out some Antitoxic Powder and fed it to Chen Yi.","By now, her face was streaked with tears. \"Brother-in-law, don’t scare me.\"","\"You can’t let anything happen to you! Or else... or else...\"","Pei Guanli sobbed as she shook Chen Yi. \"Or else Sister Jinghong will never forgive me.\"","\"Brother-in-law, waahhh...\"","Just then, Chen Yi spoke weakly, \"Stop crying... and... and stop shaking me.\"","\"If you keep shaking me, I’m really going to die.\""]},{"number":315,"title":"Chapter 315 - 221: Dragon-Falling Slaying Enemies, Spear Dao Perfection","paragraphs":["Pei Guanli’s sobs ceased, and she broke into a tearful smile as she hugged him. \"Brother-in-law, you’re okay! You’re okay...\"","\"COUGH, COUGH...\"","Chen Yi tried feebly to push her away, but when he couldn’t break free, he simply let her hold him.","He gazed at the full moon peeking through the gaps in the dense canopy of leaves and thought to himself:","’That was genuinely dangerous.’","’The Five Poison Sect, Liu Zhaoxue of the Jing State Liu Family... This isn’t over!’","But what Chen Yi and Pei Guanli didn’t know was that, on a tree several hundred yards away...","Chen Yunfan was staring at them, dumbfounded.","To be precise, he was staring at Chen Yi lying on the ground, his face and eyes filled with utter disbelief.","’Brother Yi?’","’Is that Brother Yi?’","’Brother Yi has reached Spear Dao Perfection?!’","’Damn it, that’s impossible.’","’How is that even possible?’","’He, Chen Yunfan, had practiced Martial Arts since he was a child. After more than a decade of hard work, his Cultivation had only just broken through to the Lower Fourth Grade.’","’His Sword Dao had only just reached the Great Success Realm.’","’With this rate of progress, the family elders already called him a prodigy.’","’They said he had the greatest talent for Martial Arts the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family had seen in a century.’","’But if he was a once-in-a-century talent, then what did that make Chen Yi?’","’He was younger, his Cultivation was a bit lower, but his Spear Dao was immensely more powerful!’","’Father, Mother, Second Uncle, Great-Grandfather, Third Grandpa, Fifth Grandpa, you have to come and see this.’","’Brother Yi has made it big! He... damn it all... he’s reached Spear Dao Perfection!’","’Damn it all, how is that fair?’","’He had toiled and suffered since he was a child to cultivate his Martial Arts, and he couldn’t even show it, all so he could one day make a stunning debut.’","But before he could even make a name for himself among the scholars, before he could dominate the Jianghu, he discovered someone in his own family was already more incredible than him.","’Brother Yi, your Calligraphy Dao is at Perfection, and your Spear Dao is at Perfection too... Talent like yours puts your big brother in a really tight spot.’","A moment later, seeing that the corrosive effects of the Evil Poison in his body had subsided slightly, Chen Yi couldn’t help but speak again.","\"Stop crying.\"","\"Help me. Help me up.\"","Pei Guanli finally snapped out of it and hurriedly helped him sit up. \"Brother-in-law, are you feeling any better?\"","Of course, she could see for herself how he was doing.","The Evil Poison was still coursing through Chen Yi’s body. Apart from his face, which was relatively unharmed, the rest of his body was swollen and festering.","It was a truly gruesome sight.","But after checking himself with his Qi Observation Skill, Chen Yi sighed in relief.","\"It’s fine. They’re just superficial wounds. The Evil Poison didn’t reach my internal organs. I reckon I’ll be fully healed by tomorrow.\"","Her heart aching for him, Pei Guanli was about to touch his wounds when his words made her freeze. \"Tomorrow?\"","Chen Yi hummed in affirmation, took out an earring, and began to treat his wounds with it.","As he began Controlling Needle with Qi, he made sure to instruct her, \"When we get back, don’t mention anything that happened tonight.\"","\"Your Sister Wan’er is too pure-hearted. She can’t handle these sordid affairs. Plus, her health is poor. It’s better to save her the worry.\"","\"If she asks, we need to have our story straight. We’ll say you ran into some Jianghu People and almost got into a fight...\"","Pei Guanli nodded to show she had it memorized, all while watching his actions with curiosity.","\"Brother-in-law, is that ’Controlling Needle with Qi’? I remember Ah Ma saying that only the most incredible Medical Saint Hands can use it.\"","Chen Yi confirmed with a grunt and continued, \"Don’t worry about that for now. Just memorize what I told you. Don’t slip up like you did in front of your Sister Jinghong.\"","\"Don’t worry, brother-in-law. I—I promise I won’t give anything away.\"","\"Speaking of which, what happened with you? You were carrying so many vials and jars, and even Gu Insects. How did you get caught by the Five Poison Sect?\"","At the mention of this, Pei Guanli’s face flushed with indignation.","\"They—they’re horrible! They used a little kid to trick me!\"","\"I had just come out of the latrine when a child ran up to me, saying he couldn’t find his mother. I offered to help him look.\"","\"But as soon as we entered a small path, someone knocked me unconscious...\"","’Knocked unconscious, huh.’","’Being unconscious would be great right now.’","Chen Yunfan wished he were unconscious too.","That way, he could attribute everything before him to a dream, and not reality.","’Brother Yi is also a Medical Saint Hand...’","’Perfection in a Martial Dao, Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao, a Medical Saint Hand...’","Chen Yunfan rubbed his eyes. It wasn’t because his vision was blurry; he was genuinely about to cry.","He racked his brain but couldn’t figure out how Chen Yi had managed to cultivate.","The Calligraphy Dao was somewhat understandable.","Chen Yi had been a diligent student since childhood and had decent handwriting. Even when he was locked in the woodshed, he could still write and paint.","So, Chen Yunfan didn’t find his achievements in the Calligraphy Dao all that strange.","But what about the Martial Arts and the Medical Dao?","Chen Yi had never come into contact with any medical texts, at least not before he came to Shu State.","’In just a few short months, he cultivated the Medical Dao to Minor Success and learned Controlling Needle with Qi?’","What Chen Yunfan understood even less was when Chen Yi had started practicing Martial Arts.","After thinking it over, he could only come up with one possibility.","’All those years, Brother Yi wasn’t actually being punished by my mother. He was secretly practicing Martial Arts.’","’Five years to reach Great Success in the Spear Dao, and then breaking through to the Perfection Realm today when faced with a life-or-death crisis... it’s not impossible.’","’But was his practice of Martial Arts also arranged by my father?’","Chen Yunfan had no way of knowing, but he resolved to find a way to contact his father.","He was determined to ask him and get to the bottom of Brother Yi’s skills in the Martial Arts, the Calligraphy Dao, and the Medical Dao.","’He’s not human. He’s a monster!’","At this thought, Chen Yunfan took a deep breath, shot one last look in Chen Yi’s direction, and turned to head back toward the Prefecture City.","But after walking only a few hundred yards, he abruptly stopped and turned back to look toward Chen Yi, a look of dawning realization mixed with suspicion in his eyes.","’Spear Dao... Spear Technique...’","’The person who knocked me out that night... was it... was it Brother Yi?’","’And then he knocked me out, only to bring people to \"rescue\" me?’","Connecting the Spear Dao and Medical Dao that Chen Yi had just revealed, Chen Yunfan instantly put it all together, and an expression of profound grievance crept onto his face.","’The West Market Hundred Herbs Hall... Brother Yi goes there often.’","’And that night with Cui Qingwu’s incident, the Xiao Family was framed...’","’Damn it, damn it, damn it! Brother Yi, you’ve really put your big brother through the wringer!’","’You, you, you... You just wait!’","Any thought Chen Yunfan previously had of rescuing Chen Yi had long since vanished into thin air.","’Rescue him?’","’Rescue, my ass! This town ain’t big enough for the two of us!’"]},{"number":316,"title":"Chapter 316 - 222: Sharing the Moon, Even from a Li Away","paragraphs":["When Chen Yunfan returned to Guiyun Academy, the poetry gathering had already ended.","Liu Hong, Yang Ye, Liu Si, and other important officials from Shu State had already departed.","The remaining Academy Masters—Yue Ming, Zhuo Ying, and Lingchuan—were standing at the entrance, seeing off the guests from Yuelu Academy, Yingtian Academy, and others.","Their exchanges were filled with the usual pleasantries.","The other talented young men and women who had attended the poetry gathering were leaving the academy in twos and threes, their expressions showing they were still longing for more.","Their conversations were all about the events of the evening’s gathering.","Naturally, much of the talk was about *Song of the Water Melody* and their admiration for its author, Chen Yi, also known as Mr. Qingzhou.","Chen Yunfan paid them no mind. After scanning the crowd, he spotted Cui Qingwu, Xiao Wan’er, and the others, and walked over with a displeased look on his face.","Cui Qingwu noticed something was off about him. She thought for a moment before taking the initiative to approach him. \"What took you so long?\" she asked with a smile, before lowering her voice.","\"Chen... How is he? Why didn’t he come back with you?\"","Chen Yunfan stopped in his tracks and snorted. \"He’s dead.\"","\"Dead?\"","Cui Qingwu froze for a moment. She couldn’t help but glance back at the others, a silent warning for him to watch his words, before continuing,","\"What happened?\"","Chen Yunfan noticed her gesture. He glanced at Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wuge, and Shen Huatang before replying ambiguously,","\"I got there too late. Someone else had already intervened.\"","On the way back, Chen Yunfan had thought it all through.","Chen Yi had always kept a low profile, only revealing that his Calligraphy Dao had reached the Perfection Realm. He must have his reasons for doing so.","As Chen Yi’s older brother, it was only right for him to help conceal this.","As for the \"issues\" between him and Chen Yi, that was something for the two of them to resolve as brothers.","’Doesn’t that sound like a perfect example of brotherly love and respect?’","But what was the reality?","Chen Yunfan wished Chen Yi would stay hidden for the rest of his life.","Preferably until his own Martial Arts Cultivation had advanced and he too had broken through to the Perfection Realm.","That way, he would still be the Eldest Young Master of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, the Imperial Top Scholar of the Great Wei Dynasty, and a martial arts genius rarely seen in a century.","Otherwise, he feared that when he traveled the world in the future, people would see him and only say, \"That’s the older brother of the peerless genius, Chen Qingzhou.\"","And that would be... just fucking unbearable.","Cui Qingwu, of course, was unaware of Chen Yunfan’s \"dark\" thoughts. Hearing his explanation, she nodded and said, \"That’s for the best.\"","It was better for someone else to have performed the rescue, regardless of who it was, than for Chen Yunfan to have done it himself.","Earlier, after learning that Chen Yunfan had been hiding his Martial Arts Cultivation, Cui Qingwu had begun to regret letting him go to Chen Yi’s rescue alone.","The reason was simple.","The longer a trump card like this remained hidden, the more powerful its effect when finally revealed.","Her own position as a Silver Banner Officer in the White Tiger Guard, for example, was a hidden identity completely different from her public persona.","If anyone thought she was merely the young miss of the Qinghe Cui Family and tried to move against her, they would meet a much more miserable fate.","Xiao Wan’er held Xiao Wuge’s hand, her anxiety for Chen Yi deepening as she watched Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu whispering to each other off to the side.","She couldn’t help but glance at Shen Huatang, the question in her eyes unspoken but clear.","Shen Huatang understood perfectly and gave a slight shake of her head.","’All this talk about someone being dead or others intervening probably has nothing to do with the Young Master.’","’Otherwise, given the relationship between Chen Yunfan and the Young Master, his reaction would be completely different.’","Xiao Wan’er breathed a sigh of relief. She turned to look out at Kangning Street beyond the academy gates, searching for a familiar figure.","Xiao Wuge was also looking left and right. Seeing that most of the guests had departed, he couldn’t help but ask,","\"Big Sis, where did Brother-in-law go?\"","Xiao Wan’er shook her head gently. \"I... I don’t know either. He must have been delayed by something.\"","Just then, Chen Yunfan, who had overheard their conversation, exchanged a look with Cui Qingwu. They walked over together, and he said with a smile,","\"Brother Yi does have some business to attend to, but he should be back soon.\"","Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help asking, \"Young Master Chen, do you know what’s happened? Why isn’t he back yet, so late at night?\"","\"Didn’t he go with some people to the Quchi Painting Boat? Miss Xiao, you should know how those literary types are. Reciting poetry, composing couplets, a beauty in their arms... He...\"","Before Chen Yunfan could finish, Cui Qingwu discreetly gave his side a sharp pinch, cutting him off.","\"Sister Wan’er, don’t listen to Brother Yunfan.\"","Xiao Wan’er didn’t take him seriously, of course. She smiled. \"Young Master Chen is joking. I trust my husband is not a frivolous man.\"","Chen Yunfan privately scoffed. ’Him? Not frivolous?’","’He drugged his own brother unconscious and had the nerve to show up for a rescue mission. How could you call that merely ’frivolous’?’","’He’s an absolute animal.’","Just then, Liu Zhaoxue, who had yet to leave Guiyun Academy, walked over. She gave a slight curtsy and said,","\"Greetings, Sister Wan’er, Young Master Chen, Miss Cui.\"","Chen Yunfan shot her a sidelong glance and pretended not to hear.","Ever since the incident with the Three Towns’ summer grain being burned, his opinion of the Jing State Liu Family—and Liu Wen in particular—left a sour taste in his mouth.","Even if Liu Zhaoxue was the most beautiful woman in Jing State, he couldn’t be bothered to give her a second glance.","Xiao Wan’er felt the same. After a polite nod, she fell silent, simply holding Xiao Wuge’s hand and offering no reply.","Cui Qingwu glanced between them, a slight smile touching her lips. \"Why, Miss Liu, haven’t you left yet?\"","\"Your third uncle left before the poetry gathering was even over.\"","Liu Zhaoxue saw their expressions and understood what they were thinking. With an unruffled smile, she said,","\"My third uncle and I are not traveling the same path, so it would be an imposition for me to bother him.\"","As she spoke, she glanced around and asked, \"I wonder why Mr. Qingzhou isn’t here?\"","\"His *Song of the Water Melody* at the gathering tonight was truly astonishing. I was hoping I might have the chance to ask for his personal guidance on the art of poetry.\"","Cui Qingwu frowned to herself. ’This woman really knows how to touch a sore spot.’"]},{"number":317,"title":"Chapter 317 - 222: You Can Share the Moon from a Li Away, Too","paragraphs":["She and Chen Yunfan had just dispelled the suspicions of Xiao Wan’er’s group and were about to change the subject.","\"Miss Liu, you’re asking the wrong person. With Mr. Qingzhou’s current renown, his whereabouts are naturally not for people like us to know.\"","\"Isn’t that right, Sister Wan’er?\"","Xiao Wan’er went along with her, adding, \"As for my brother-in-law’s affairs, the Xiao Family will not pry too deeply either.\"","Liu Zhaoxue glanced at the two of them, then smiled and nodded. \"In that case, I will have to wait for another opportunity to ask.\"","Just as she was about to bow and take her leave, the TINKLE TINKLE of a Bell suddenly reached her ears, followed by a cheerful, teasing voice:","\"Sister Wan’er, Imperial Top Scholar Chen, and Xiao Wuge, you haven’t gone back to your estate yet?\"","It was none other than Pei Guanli, clad in a long red dress with a Bell on, her feet completely bare.","Xiao Wan’er breathed a sigh of relief upon seeing her. But when she glanced to Pei Guanli’s side and still saw no sign of Chen Yi, she asked:","\"Where’s your brother-in-law?\"","Pei Guanli stopped in her tracks and looked at her in confusion. \"My brother-in-law already went back to the estate.\"","\"He went back?\"","\"He went back?!\"","Many were surprised. The first exclamation came from Xiao Wan’er, Xiaodie, and the others, who hadn’t expected Chen Yi to leave the Poetry gathering so quietly.","The second one came from Chen Yunfan.","If he hadn’t already decided to cover for Chen Yi, he would have exposed the Mountain Race’s Tiger Girl right then and there.","’Brother Yi just had a brutal fight with a whole group from the Evil Demonic Dao. How the hell is he already back?’","Xiao Wan’er asked hesitantly, \"When did he leave? Why didn’t he wait for us? He didn’t even say anything beforehand.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli scratched her head. \"Well, my brother-in-law did ask me to come tell you. It’s just... it’s just that I forgot.\"","\"You forgot?\"","\"Kangning Street was just so, so lively, so I... I got distracted watching for a bit.\"","Xiao Wan’er chided her gently. \"You. Don’t let it happen again.\"","\"I won’t, I won’t.\"","Xiao Wuge looked up and asked, \"Sister Guanli, why did you and brother-in-law leave tonight? You missed all the fun.\"","’Why did we leave?’","Pei Guanli stuck out her tongue and explained just as Chen Yi had instructed. \"It’s, uh, all my fault.\"","\"Tonight, I heard some Jianghu People speaking disrespectfully to my brother-in-law, and then we...\"","\"In the end, my brother-in-law composed a poem that won them over, so I didn’t have to fight them.\"","\"But on the way back, I accidentally made him fall into the water. His clothes were soaked, so he had no choice but to head back to the estate first.\"","This half-true, half-false explanation made Xiao Wan’er unable to resist poking her on the forehead. \"You can’t be so reckless next time.\"","\"It’s a good thing your brother-in-law is okay. Otherwise, Second Sister would never let you hear the end of it.\"","Pei Guanli readily agreed, then stepped forward, took her hand, and giggled.","\"Sister Wan’er, it’s getting so late. We should hurry back too.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded slightly, then turned to Chen Yunfan and the others. She gave a slight bow. \"We’ve imposed on you all tonight. I hope we have the chance to meet again.\"","Cui Qingwu smiled and returned the bow. \"When I have a free moment in a few days, I will come to visit. I hope you won’t mind, Sister.\"","\"Of course not...\"","Chen Yunfan shot Pei Guanli a strange look.","’Now I get it.’","’This Tiger Girl ran back by herself just to create a cover story for Chen Yi.’","’It makes sense, now that I think about it.’","’Brother Yi’s fight with those people from the Five Poison Sect was brutal. His clothes were in tatters, so it’s true he couldn’t show his face at the academy.’","’It’s just...’","’Why do I still feel the urge to complain about it?’","A short while later, after exchanging a few more pleasantries and bidding farewell to Mr. Yue Ming and the others, they boarded their respective carriages and departed.","Only Liu Zhaoxue and the guards behind her remained, standing perfectly still as they watched the carriages disappear into the distance.","The moment Liu Zhaoxue saw Pei Guanli return unharmed, she knew something had happened to Yan Fusha and the others from the Five Poison Sect.","She didn’t know the exact circumstances, nor did she know how much Chen Yi and Pei Guanli knew about what had transpired.","But there was no way she was going to believe a word of Pei Guanli’s story.","’If those so-called \"Jianghu People\" were actually Yan Fusha and the Five Poison Sect, how could things have ended so peacefully?’","’Competing over Poetry and comparing Fist and Foot skills... it was all utter nonsense.’","「After a moment of thought.」","Liu Zhaoxue waved her hand, signaling her men to board the carriage. \"Let’s go take a look outside the city,\" she ordered.","’She wouldn’t be able to rest easy until she saw it for herself.’","Because it was the Mid-Autumn Festival, the Prefecture City’s gates remained open all night, allowing their carriage to leave without issue.","Liu Zhaoxue instructed the driver to head downstream along the Chishui River.","After stopping and starting for about an hour, they finally found some traces on a riverbank several dozen li away.","\"Miss, please look.\"","Liu Zhaoxue looked in the direction her subordinate was pointing, and a look of astonishment appeared on her beautiful face.","The area, which should have been a dense forest, now looked as if it had been plowed over by an ox.","Splintered wood and shattered rock were strewn everywhere.","Deep gouges were carved into the earth, along with traces of corrosion from some unknown substance.","Clearly, a vicious battle had just taken place here.","Liu Zhaoxue scanned the area, her brow furrowed slightly. \"Keep searching,\" she commanded. \"See if you can find any scraps of clothing or anything else left behind.\"","Her subordinates obeyed, fanning out from the epicenter to search the surroundings.","But even after turning the entire area upside down, they found nothing of use.","\"Miss, all that remains are faint fluctuations from the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism. It seems a Spearman, a Swordman, and an expert in poisons fought here.\"","Liu Zhaoxue grunted in acknowledgment, her expression growing even more severe.","’So...’","’Chen Yi and Pei Guanli left alive, Yan Fusha and the others from the Five Poison Sect are nowhere to be found, and this forest shows signs of a fierce battle...’","’All the signs confirmed her earlier suspicions—something had happened!’","’Something major!’","\"A master skilled with a Long Spear and an expert who uses a long Blade...\""]},{"number":318,"title":"Chapter 318 - 222: Even a *Li* Apart, We Can Share the Moon","paragraphs":["’Why does this feel so familiar? Was it those two masters who killed Liu Wen outside Iron Wall Town?’","’Did they kill Yan Fusha and his men to rescue Chen Yi and Pei Guanli?’","Liu Zhaoxue guessed, her expression flickering with uncertainty.","She didn’t much care if Yan Fusha and his people died. That had little to do with her.","What she worried about was whether Yan Fusha had exposed her before he died.","After all, Chen Yi’s status was no longer that of the obscure son-in-law of the Xiao Family. He was now a master of poetry, a master of the Calligraphy Dao, and an Instructor at Guiyun Academy.","If someone like that revealed her connection to the Five Poison Sect, she would face immediate and utter disaster.","And then there was Pei Guanli of the Mountain Race.","She was Granny Shan’s own granddaughter. If Pei Guanli found out Liu Zhaoxue was working with the Five Poison Sect, wouldn’t she send people to kill her on the spot?","At this thought, Liu Zhaoxue’s gaze fell on the furrows left in the ground by the long spears. She gritted her teeth and hissed,","\"We’re leaving. Back to Jing State tonight!\"","She had to go.","If she didn’t, she feared she would meet the same end as her second brother, Liu Wen.","’It just so happens that Third Uncle expressed his displeasure with me staying in Shu State tonight. When I return to Jing State, I’ll have an explanation for Father.’","With these thoughts, Liu Zhaoxue boarded her carriage and methodically arranged for people to stay behind in Shu State to continue preparations for Xinglin Hall.","Soon after, the carriage headed east.","As the carriage rumbled along, Liu Zhaoxue gazed at the bright moon outside her window and thought to herself:","’After some time, once I’m sure Chen Yi, Pei Guanli, and the others don’t know about my connection to the Five Poison Sect, I’ll have to find a way to storm back into Shu State.’","’But by then, returning will be incredibly difficult.’","...","「Outside Spring Lotus Garden, Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.」","A full moon hung in the sky, and a gentle breeze was blowing.","Wisps of floral fragrance drifted by, carrying the faint sounds of laughter.","\"...’May we all live long and share the moon’s beauty, though a thousand miles apart.’\"","\"Second Young Master-in-law is so amazing, to be able to write such beautiful, bittersweet lines.\"","\"I heard that when Third Master found out, he praised him nonstop, saying he must be the Wenqu Star reincarnated to have composed such a timeless masterpiece.\"","\"The Master praised him, too.\"","\"What did the Marquis say?\"","\"He said Second Young Master-in-law doesn’t know how to hide his talents, and that it was a waste to use such a poem to compete for some Poetry Champion title. He said it sullied such fine words.\"","\"Huh? Was the Marquis angry?\"","\"Of course not. The Master must have just thought it was a pity...\"","Listening to the discussions from the surrounding courtyards, Chen Yi thought to himself, ’News certainly travels fast.’","Fortunately, his fight with Yan Fusha tonight had taken place outside Shu State.","If they had come to blows on the Quchi river, he feared the talk in Shu State City wouldn’t just be about his \"Song of the Water Melody.\"","Instead, they’d be singing the praises of Chen Qingzhou’s Perfect Calligraphy Dao, Perfect Martial Arts, and Great Success in the Medical Dao.","What kind of uproar would that cause?","He reckoned that aside from a small number of people who would praise and admire him, the vast majority would just call him a scheming \"villain.\"","’If you aren’t a deeply scheming person, why hide who you are?’","After letting his thoughts wander for a bit, Chen Yi reviewed the night’s events in his mind. He relaxed slightly, certain that for the time being, no one had found out.","Before returning, he had cleared away the traces as much as possible.","Not only had he made Pei Guanli use Corpse-Dissolving Powder to get rid of the bodies of Yan Fusha and the others, but he had also deliberately used the Saber Dao to create confusion.","Even if someone investigated soon, it would be impossible for them to suspect him.","Unless someone had happened to see him fighting Yan Fusha.","And unless that person recognized him and also happened to be a gossip, he could keep his secret for now.","’I hope no one saw...’","Chen Yi sighed inwardly, but he also quietly prepared himself for the possibility of being discovered.","If the worst-case scenario really did occur, he wasn’t afraid.","Just as he had told Liu Lang, the worst that could happen was that he’d get a good scolding from Xiao Jinghong and the Old Master.","Just as he was thinking about this, he heard several sets of footsteps from a nearby corridor.","Among them were the laughing voices of Xiaodie, Cui’er, Juan’er, Pei Guanli, and others, mostly discussing the events of the poetry gathering.","Things like how the visiting scholar Pei Zhaoye and others outwardly conceded to \"Song of the Water Melody\" but were inwardly unconvinced.","How Li Huai’gu and Liu Zhaoxue had written short poems that received praise from several masters.","And how Chen Yunfan had been ridiculed, called the most ignorant Imperial Top Scholar in the history of the Great Wei Dynasty.","After listening for a moment, Chen Yi saw several figures approaching.","Leading them were, of course, Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge.","Chen Yi smiled and waved. \"Eldest Sister, my apologies. Something came up, so I was delayed and couldn’t attend the poetry gathering as planned.\"","Hearing his voice, Xiao Wan’er watched him from a distance with her beautiful eyes and nodded lightly.","\"I heard what happened from little sister Guanli.\"","\"As long as you’re alright, Brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi nodded and saw Pei Guanli behind her, her head held high in pride. He shot a discreet glare at her.","\"It’s getting late. Eldest Sister, you should get some rest.\"","\"Wuge, Xiaodie, Guanli, come back to Spring Lotus Garden with me.\"","\"Yes, Young Master.\"","\"Brother-in-law, you missed a lot of excitement tonight since you weren’t there.\"","\"Is that so? Why don’t you tell me about it later, Wuge?\"","\"Okay! I saw the whole thing...\"","Xiao Wan’er watched them enter Spring Lotus Garden, paused for a moment, and then quietly walked into Jiaxing Garden.","She was truly happy to see Chen Yi was safe and sound.","But... but the lines from tonight’s \"Song of the Water Melody\" weighed on her mind.","So much so that when she returned to Jiaxing Garden, changed her clothes, washed up, and lay down in bed, those words still echoed in her head.","\"...’People have sorrow and joy, they part and meet again; the moon dims and brightens, it waxes and wanes. Such is the way of things since time immemorial. May we all live long and share the moon’s beauty, though a thousand miles apart.’\"","\"’Share the moon’s beauty, though a thousand miles apart...’\"","Xiao Wan’er stared at the floral canopy above her bed with her beautiful eyes, murmuring,","\"Why must it be a thousand miles?\"","\"In truth, one can share the moon’s beauty from just a mile away.\"","As she thought this, Xiao Wan’er froze, then suddenly pulled the covers over her head and curled up into a ball.","’What... what am I thinking?’","’Second Sister and Brother-in-law are deeply in love. If they share the moon from a thousand miles apart, what does it matter?’","But despite her thoughts, her mind kept wanting to change that \"thousand miles\" to \"one mile.\"","She didn’t know how much time had passed.","Face flushed, Xiao Wan’er threw off the covers, quietly rose, and walked to her desk. She ground the ink, picked up her brush, and wrote on a sheet of Yunsong Paper:","\"Song of the Water Melody\"... ’Share the moon’s beauty from a mile away.’","Jiaxing Garden was exactly one mile from Spring Lotus Garden.","After writing, Xiao Wan’er looked at the signature—the two names, \"Chen Yi, Chen Qingzhou\"—and sighed softly.","\"You scoundrel...\"","「Meanwhile.」","Back in Spring Lotus Garden, Chen Yi was oblivious to all of this.","He was sitting cross-legged on his bed, not practicing the Four Symbols Skill, but using Silver Needles on his acupoints to treat his injuries.","Earlier, in his rush to clean up the scene and not worry Xiao Wan’er, he had only purged the Evil Poisonous energy from his body.","His external, superficial wounds had not yet healed.","While healing himself, Chen Yi also unfolded the chessboard in his mind, laying out a new game with his Great Success Chess Dao.","At this moment, he still didn’t know that Liu Zhaoxue had sensed something was wrong and had already fled Shu State overnight.","But even if he had known, he wouldn’t have cared.","Since they were already in a situation where one side had to be annihilated, the best outcome would be to turn them all into dead men.","That was better than having them constantly jumping around in his sight, being an eyesore.","’The Five Poison Sect, Liu Zhaoxue... They made me suffer such a great loss. I can’t just let this go!’","...","「At the same time.」","「Inside Tingyu Pavilion.」","Chen Yunfan had just returned to his residence when he ordered Ning Yu and Niu Shan to stand guard outside the central courtyard.","He didn’t go to rest, nor did he go to the study to read for leisure. Instead, to Chun Ying’s astonishment, he took out a Long Sword and began practicing his Swordsmanship.","\"Yo-Young Master, Miss Cui is still in the back courtyard. Y-You...\"","Chen Yunfan replied while brandishing his Long Sword, \"I can’t worry about that right now.\"","\"Besides, she already knows I practice Martial Arts. If she hears me, she hears me.\"","Chun Ying was stunned. \"Huh? H-How does she know?\"","\"I told her, of course.\"","Chen Yunfan stopped impatiently and looked at her. \"Do you people have a Cultivation Technique that can rapidly advance my Sword Dao?\"","\"We do, but...\"","\"Hurry up and write a letter to ask them for it. This young master needs to break through as soon as possible.\"","\"But you...\"","\"Don’t ask so many questions. Just do as I say.\"","\"Also, are you people in constant contact with my father? I want to write him a letter...\"","Chen Yunfan had no intention of telling her the real reason he was in such a hurry to improve his Sword Dao.","He was still planning to settle the score with Chen Yi after he cultivated his Sword Dao to the Perfection Realm.","’Hmph, with my Fourth Grade Realm Cultivation and a Perfect Sword Dao, I refuse to believe I won’t be able to beat that bastard, Brother Yi.’","’Just you wait!’"]},{"number":319,"title":"Chapter 319 - 223: The Dao of the Mortal Realm","paragraphs":["In the blink of an eye, ten days passed.","After the Mid-Autumn Festival, the weather was no longer as scorching as before, and could rightly be called crisp and refreshing.","With the exception of the southernmost areas of the Great Wei Dynasty, like Guangyue Prefecture and Jiao State, the rest of the land was cool and pleasant, with a gentle, warm breeze.","Yet the Wei People were busier than ever.","After the autumn harvest, farmers who grew crops began preparing for winter and the coming year, repairing dikes, reinforcing irrigation channels, and plowing the fields.","Merchants saw little change; they bustled about all year round, regardless of the weather or season.","Even the scholars were much busier than usual.","The busyness was because most students had to prepare for the upcoming County, Prefecture, and Academy Examinations, as well as the Annual Examination.","The dates for the County Examinations across the Nine State and Three Prefectures of the Wei Dynasty were not fixed, but were mostly concentrated between the ninth month and the first month of the following year.","Students who passed the County Examination could then participate in the Prefecture Examination in the second month, followed by the Academy Examination within a few months after passing that.","Passing the Academy Examination granted one the rank of a scholar, commonly known as a Scholar.","If one wanted to participate in the Provincial and Metropolitan Examinations, they first had to pass these preliminary exams to obtain the status of a scholar.","In short, once autumn arrived, students all across the Great Wei were preparing for the various upcoming examinations.","Even those who were already Scholars were the same; to maintain their status, they could not miss the Annual Examination.","However, after the Mid-Autumn Festival, while preparing for their exams, the students didn’t forget to enjoy some excitement.","For instance, they discussed which famous works had emerged from the poetry gatherings held in the various states and prefectures during the festival.","Even the famous courtesans of the Qin Buildings in different regions became topics of their discussions.","This was mostly for reasons of \"cultivating elegance\" or indulging in the \"romantic exploits of a talented scholar.\"","The students were long accustomed to this. Every year during the Mid-Autumn and Lantern Festivals, poetry gatherings were frequent, and famous works would appear one after another.","Thus, in previous years, students from all over would argue endlessly in the month following the Mid-Autumn Festival over which poem was the best.","These debates were even more heated than their discussions about which courtesan was the most beautiful or talented.","But this year, the situation was somewhat different.","Or rather, strange.","It wasn’t that the discussions had stopped, but that with the arrival of a poem titled \"Song of the Water Melody\" from Shu State, all other famous works lost any grounds for debate in its presence.","Even the staunchest supporters of poems written by other great masters had to admit it: \"Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn\" was the best work from all the Mid-Autumn poetry gatherings this year.","This wasn’t the conclusion in just one place, but a consensus shared by more than half the students across the Nine State and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei Dynasty.","Even several of the reclusive Great Masters from the academies, who hadn’t been seen in a long time, couldn’t help but offer their praise:","\"A Ci poem is superior when it transcends its original tune. Chen Qingzhou’s lines, ’I long to ride the wind and return there, yet I fear in those crystal towers and jade palaces, the heights would be too cold for me,’ are ethereal and profound.\"","\"The unrestrained and brisk nature of ’Song of the Water Melody’ is truly the work of a genius.\"","\"The first half of this poem is as if penned by a banished immortal who has taken human form, while the second half, mournfully beautiful, speaks of all there is to the mortal world.\"","The phrase \"speaks of all there is to the mortal world\" was enough to show the immense reverence that countless scholars held for \"Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn.\"","Though there were many opinions from various places, they could generally be summarized as: \"The greatest moon-praising Ci poem for the Mid-Autumn Festival of all time.\"","「Jiangnan Prefecture, Jinling.」","As the former capital of a previous dynasty, Jinling held the reputation of \"five hundred years of prosperity.\"","With Vermilion Bird Avenue as its central axis, the wards and markets on its east and west sides were the epitome of prosperity, stretching for nearly a hundred li.","The banks of the Qinhuai River, in particular, were lined with Qin Buildings, inns, and taverns, and the stream of travelers coming and going was endless.","From morning to night, there wasn’t a single moment that wasn’t bustling and noisy.","Fortunately, some of the residences on the riverbanks were relatively far from those clamorous areas; otherwise, it would have been difficult to live there.","Unfortunately for Sun Fu, who had just arrived in Jinling from Shu State, the small courtyard house he had purchased was near several Qin Buildings.","Every day before dawn, drunken patrons would stumble past his courtyard gate, muttering and groaning.","Some even went so far as to relieve themselves on the outer wall by his gate, making Sun Fu’s wife so angry she wanted to curse them out.","But that wasn’t even the worst of it.","The most outrageous part was the women from the Qin Buildings.","Perhaps because Sun Fu’s family were scholars, whenever they passed by, scantily clad women would cast flirtatious glances into their courtyard.","Sun Fu, of course, paid them no mind.","But his son, Sun Yunfeng—a handsome scholar—had a harder time with it.","Although Sun Yunfeng was over thirty and had a steady temperament, he had never been to a place like South City Yanhua Lane back in Shu State Prefecture City.","He’d had few opportunities to even see a woman from a Qin Building, let alone experience something like this.","As a result, this middle-aged man, full of Blood Qi, felt a little uncomfortable every time he met the gazes of those women.","His face would flush, and his heart would race, among other things.","Sun Fu didn’t have a good solution for this. He simply reminded his son of the adage that \"a wife who has shared the hard times must not be cast aside,\" and then let the matter drop after asking his wife and daughter-in-law to keep an eye on him.","\"Tomorrow morning, I will go teach at the Li Family Private School. Yunfeng, you should also go find a shop and get back to your old trade.\"","\"Yes, Father. I understand.\"","Sun Yunfeng didn’t dare to refute Sun Fu’s words, agreeing readily before continuing:","\"Over the past two days, I’ve tested the water from the Qinhuai River and the mountain springs of Zijin Mountain. Both can be used for brewing.\"","\"The flavor will be a bit inferior, though. After all, the water from the Chishui River is much sweeter.\"","\"A little inferior is fine. As long as it’s enough for our family to make a living, that’s all that matters.\"","After a bit more small talk, Sun Fu rose and went to his study. As was his custom, he took out the poetry collection gifted to him by Chen Yi to admire it.","The more he looked, the more delighted he became. He then took out his brush and ink to practice copying the Cursive Script.","He himself was not skilled in the Calligraphy Dao and his Realm was not high, but for a scholar, reading and writing were second nature, and his fondness for the calligraphy model went without saying.","He copied it twice.","He carefully put away the calligraphy model, preparing to study the brushstrokes of the Cursive Script."]},{"number":320,"title":"Chapter 320 - 223: The Dao of the Mortal World","paragraphs":["But before he could begin to sketch, Sun Yunfeng rushed over and said anxiously,","\"Father, Mr. Ju Yi of Jinling Academy is here to see you.\"","Sun Fu froze. \"Who did you say?\"","\"Mr. Ju Yi. He’s in the courtyard right now. You should...\"","Just then, a figure appeared outside the study and bowed slightly to Sun Fu.","\"Brother Changming, I hope you’ll forgive this presumptuous intrusion.\"","He showed no signs of age. He had distinguished, regular features, a mustache that drooped at the corners of his mouth, and a tall, slender frame. He wore a white long-robe beneath a blue scholar’s gown.","Merely standing in the room, he exuded an air of scholarly elegance.","Sun Fu hurried to his feet and returned the bow. \"It is I who should apologize for the poor reception. Please, forgive my lack of hospitality.\"","A great man’s reputation precedes him.","Mr. Ju Yi was not only the headmaster, Mr. Da, of Jinling Academy, but also a world-renowned master of philosophy.","He had numerous disciples, many of whom served as officials in the imperial court.","His standing in Jinling, and indeed throughout Jiangnan Prefecture, was comparable to that of Mr. Yue Ming from Guiyun Academy.","However, Mr. Ju Yi was clearly the more widely known of the two.","Sun Fu knew all this to be true, but he had no prior dealings with Mr. Ju Yi, nor any particular connection to him.","He truly hadn’t expected Mr. Ju Yi to seek him out.","\"You are too kind, Brother Changming.\"","The two men sat down, while Sun Yunfeng and his wife went to boil water for tea.","They exchanged a few pleasantries.","Mr. Ju Yi smiled. \"Brother Changming, you must be wondering why I’ve come today.\"","Sun Fu didn’t deny it, nodding. \"I have admired you by reputation for a long time, Mr. Ju Yi, but we’ve never had the good fortune to meet. So yes, I am indeed a bit puzzled.\"","\"Haha... That’s perfectly understandable, perfectly understandable.\"","\"My visit today is something of a fortunate coincidence.\"","After a pause, Mr. Ju Yi asked with a smile, \"Brother Changming, have you by chance heard about a certain Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala?\"","Sun Fu gave a wry smile. \"I’ve only just arrived in Jinling and have barely settled in. I haven’t yet had the chance to learn about the local poetry gatherings.\"","Mr. Ju Yi shook his head. \"Not one here in Jinling, but the Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala at Guiyun Academy in Shu State.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"The day before yesterday, a letter arrived from Shu State. It seems a masterpiece titled *Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn* emerged from Guiyun Academy’s poetry gala.\"","Sun Fu’s heart skipped a beat as he began to suspect the reason for Mr. Ju Yi’s visit.","He then heard Mr. Ju Yi continue, \"The author of this poem is none other than my former student, now the son-in-law who married into the Xiao Family, Chen Yi—Chen Qingzhou.\"","Sun Fu’s suspicions were confirmed. ’No wonder,’ he muttered to himself.","’No wonder Mr. Ju Yi sought me out at a time like this.’","\"Sir, you must have heard that I used to reside with the Xiao Family, and so you’ve come to ask about Chen Yi?\"","\"Qingzhou is indeed a great talent, especially gifted in poetry. He...\"","Mr. Ju Yi raised a hand slightly, a gesture of polite interruption. \"This student of mine has been brilliant since he was a child. I have no doubt about his literary talent.\"","\"I came today for one reason only: to ask you for confirmation, Brother Changming. Has Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao truly reached the Perfection Realm?\"","Sun Fu understood at once. He nodded and said, \"It is true.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Ju Yi’s smile broadened. \"Then the rumors are true. Qingzhou composed his poem at Quchi and used his Calligraphy Dao Realm to manifest an Immortal Realm.\"","\"It is a pity I am here in Jinling, so far from Shu State. Otherwise, I would have certainly gone to witness the splendor of Qingzhou’s Calligraphy Dao for myself.\"","An idea struck Sun Fu. He rose, walked over to his desk to retrieve a brocade box, and returned to his seat.","\"Had you asked for anything else, Mr. Ju Yi, I might not have been able to oblige.\"","\"However, just before I left for Jinling, I was fortunate enough to receive a gift from Qingzhou—a calligraphy scroll he wrote using his Perfect Calligraphy Dao.\"","Mr. Ju Yi’s smile froze. Murmuring an apology for his eagerness, he accepted the brocade box, took out the scroll, and gently unrolled it.","Instantly, a brilliant golden light flared, and a vision of a vast, sand-swept desert appeared.","\"...Fear no lack of friends on the road ahead; in all the world, who does not know you?\"","As Mr. Ju Yi read the lines aloud, his eyes fixed on the magnificent and soaring Mental Realm, he could not help but sigh in admiration.","\"This must be the ’Cursive Script’ mentioned in the letter from Shu State. Qingzhou... his Calligraphy Dao has truly reached a Realm that others can only dream of.\"","As the headmaster of Jinling Academy, he had of course seen countless treasured works.","He had seen scrolls left by Calligraphy Masters of previous dynasties, works by the Calligraphy Masters of today, and even numerous pieces written in the Perfection Realm of Calligraphy Dao.","But in his eyes, not a single one could compare to the scroll he now held.","It had nothing to do with the Realm itself, but because this \"Cursive Script\" was an entirely new style, distinct from the established Wei Qing’s Style.","Seeing his expression, Sun Fu said with a smile, \"You’re right, sir. At Qingzhou’s age, given time, he is certain to become a Calligraphy Master.\"","He considered himself part of Chen Yi’s family, in a way, so it was only natural for him to sing his praises.","Mr. Ju Yi nodded. \"It is a pity he has gone so far as Shu State. I fear he may never return in this lifetime.\"","Sun Fu’s heart stirred. He inquired, \"I heard that when Qingzhou was studying under you, his talents were already quite extraordinary.\"","\"Why did he fall into obscurity for so long afterward?\"","At this, Mr. Ju Yi paused, then suddenly let out a sigh. \"Mr. Yue Ming asked me that very same question in a letter just the other day.\"","\"If I were to say I don’t know the answer, perhaps neither you, Brother Changming, nor Mr. Yue Ming would believe me.\"","\"But that is the truth. And now, I find myself filled with regret and self-reproach.\"","At this, Mr. Ju Yi paused to think for a moment. With a resigned \"so be it,\" he continued his story.","\"Five years ago, during an academy recess, Chen Yi returned to the Chen Family in Jiangnan Prefecture.\"","\"He never returned to the academy after that. I sent letters to the Chen Family and even sent someone to pay them a visit, but the answer was always the same: Chen Yi had already become a disciple under another master.\"","\"I was displeased at first, but then I considered that the Chen Family has a heritage stretching back centuries. It wouldn’t be difficult for them to find a master more learned than I. So, I inquired no further.\"","\"But later, when Chen Yi failed to appear for two consecutive imperial examinations, I sensed that something was amiss.\"","\"But before I could send a letter of inquiry, news spread from the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family that they were having Chen Yi marry into the Xiao Family of Shu State. By then... it was already too late.\""]},{"number":321,"title":"Chapter 321 - 223: Speaking of All Earthly Matters","paragraphs":["Sun Fu frowned slightly and mused, \"Mr. Ju Yi, do you know why the Chen Family is acting this way?\"","\"Is it really as the rumors say, that Chen Yi was targeted by his stepmother, and that’s why he ended up in this situation?\"","Mr. Ju Yi sighed and shook his head. \"I do not know.\"","\"But from what I know of the Chen Family, I fear there are secrets behind this matter that outsiders aren’t meant to know.\"","\"Putting aside Madam Cui Yu of the Qinghe Cui Family, the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family alone—a prestigious clan with such a long-standing tradition and strict rules—would never stop a great talent like Chen Yi from seeking a government position through the examinations.\"","\"Even if Cui Yu disliked him, she would only have him leave the Chen Family to start his own branch. It wouldn’t have gone so far as to tarnish his reputation.\"","\"Besides, both Chen Xuanji and Chen Xuandu are anything but shortsighted or incompetent.\"","Sun Fu nodded slightly. \"This matter is indeed suspicious...\"","’The Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, the Qinghe Cui Family... for what purpose did they have Chen Yi marry into the Xiao Family?’","Suddenly, a possibility occurred to him—’The cuckoo occupying the magpie’s nest?’","’No, that can’t be it. How could Qingzhou do such a thing?’","After Mr. Ju Yi left, Sun Fu sat alone for a long time. In the end, he still didn’t believe Chen Yi was the type of person who would plot against the Xiao Family.","However, his belief was ultimately just his own opinion.","If Chen Yi cooperated with the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, or acted on their orders, the safety of the Xiao Family would certainly be at risk.","Sun Fu pondered for a long time before sighing. ’With a destiny as strong as a dragon-elephant and the luck of a leaping koi, he should be able to turn misfortune into good fortune.’","He decided to observe for a few more days. If he noticed anything amiss in Chen Yi’s actions, he would definitely write a letter to the Old Marquis.","’I hope Qingzhou doesn’t have any ill intentions...’","...","「Shu State, Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, Spring Lotus Garden.」","Just past three in the afternoon, the sky abruptly darkened.","Vast stretches of dark clouds gathered rapidly, and a torrential downpour began to fall with a great ROAR.","The rain hammered against the pond in the courtyard, creating a ceaseless PATTER.","Xiaodie yelped, covering her head with her hands as she ran toward the bamboo grove to gather the clothes that had been drying during the day.","Chen Yi, however, sat unperturbed in the pavilion sipping his tea, while beside him, Xiao Wuge scrunched up his face as he read and practiced his writing.","The past few days had been unexpectedly peaceful. No one had come to visit him about matters concerning the Guiyun Academy’s Calligraphy Studio, nor had anyone come asking about Quchi, the Painted Boat, or the Five Poison Sect. It was as if he had been forgotten.","Although Chen Yi was happy for the peace and quiet, he was still worried about his Martial Arts and Medical Dao being exposed, so he had been keeping an ear out for rumors.","After several days of paying attention, he came to a conclusion—the disappearance of Yan Fusha and the others had indeed not caused much of a stir.","There was only one rumor circulating in the city: \"Experts of the Upper Three Grades have been spotted outside Shu State City, suspected to be the other two culprits who burned the summer grain at Iron Wall Town.\"","It was also said that several Imprisonment Officers and Hundred Households from the Shu State Imprisonment Department had gone to take a look.","After that, there was no more news.","But Chen Yi knew Liu Zhaoxue of the Jing State Liu Family must have sensed something; otherwise, she wouldn’t have returned to Jing State so quickly.","’She probably doesn’t suspect me. I reckon she thinks, just like the rumors say, that it was the work of those two from Iron Wall Town.’","At the same time, Chen Yi knew Liu Zhaoxue would be back.","The reason was simple.","After the Mid-Autumn Festival, five Xinglin Halls had opened one after another in Shu State Prefecture City.","Although they weren’t located near the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, competitors are always enemies. The moment Xinglin Hall opened its doors, it began to squeeze out the business of all the other medicine halls in Shu State.","Even Hundred Herbs Hall was selling far fewer medicinal ingredients each day, to say nothing of the other medicine halls.","Fortunately, Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall’s main business was in tea beverages, so they had barely managed to earn fifty thousand taels of silver more than the previous month.","There was nothing more to be said about it.","Under these circumstances, he didn’t believe the Jing State Liu Family—or Liu Zhaoxue—would just let Xinglin Hall run rampant.","In addition, Chen Yi had also been following the aftermath of the summer grain incident in the Three Towns.","The news of Elder Master Xiao and Liu Hong being punished by the Holy Emperor had circulated for a few days, but by now, the talk had died down.","Few people inside or outside the Prefecture City mentioned it anymore, as if it had been forgotten.","However, many people were saying that Liu Hong had recently issued several public notices from the Governor’s Office.","There were notices about taxes, about corvée labor for canal repairs, and also about the arrangements for the Annual Examination for all Scholars.","Speaking of which, this last notice had something to do with Chen Yi as well.","He himself was a Scholar.","If he didn’t participate in the Annual Examination, or if he performed poorly, he could very well lose his title as a Scholar.","Chen Yi himself didn’t care about it, but Xiao Wan’er was quite concerned.","She had come by for two days in a row to ask his thoughts, and between the lines, she was clearly trying to persuade him to participate in this year’s Annual Examination.","She also said that even if he didn’t participate in the imperial examinations in the future, there were still many benefits to holding the title of a Scholar.","Things like exemption from labor services, not having to kneel before officials, and immunity from arbitrary punishment were all privileges enjoyed by those with a Scholar’s title.","But after careful consideration,","Chen Yi still decided not to participate.","’I’m part of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, Xiao Jinghong’s husband, and an Instructor at Guiyun Academy. So what if I don’t have a Scholar’s title?’","As for the Xiao Family,","the incident at Iron Wall Town had a much greater impact.","Not only did they have to spend money to buy grain and provisions for Iron Wall Town, but they also had to pay the grain tax for all Three Towns, resulting in a huge loss of silver.","It was said that Elder Master Xiao was in anguish day and night over the loss.","Besides that, there were a few other minor matters.","For instance, his own Martial Arts cultivation had reached Sixth Grade Perfection, and he would soon be able to break through to the Fifth Grade.","For instance, Yan Hai from Hundred Herbs Hall had already taken his men and left the Prefecture City to investigate the situation with the medicine halls in other counties and towns of Shu State.","For instance, Xiao Wan’er had prepared all the plans and regulations for the Medical Dao Academy and would soon be heading to the Xiao Family’s fief to survey a location for it.","For instance, Pei Guanli had written a letter to Granny Shan to complain about something, but there had been no reply yet.","For instance, Xiao Jinghong had sent a letter, saying that the construction of the Mutual Market was progressing well and that two market streets would be completed in another half a month.","The scale was comparable to the East Market in Shu State Prefecture City, with a full one hundred storefronts.","And...","As Chen Yi pondered these things while watching the rain fall on the pond, he heard footsteps behind him.","\"Second Young Master, Young Master Wuge, the Eldest Miss requests your presence for dinner.\"","Chen Yi was slightly taken aback and turned to look at the person who had arrived. \"Fairy Tingyun?\"","Xie Tingyun winked at him and chuckled softly. \"Young Master, Tingyun has not failed her mission.\"","’Not failed her mission?’","\"How many people from the Celestial Sect have come?\"","\"Not too many, not too few. Exactly one hundred and twenty-seven.\"","’How many? One hundred and twenty-seven?’","Chen Yi was secretly astounded. ’Did Xie Tingyun bring every disciple from the Celestial Sect with her?’"]},{"number":322,"title":"Chapter 322 - 224: Fifth Grade","paragraphs":["Chen Yi really hadn’t expected Xie Tingyun to bring so many disciples to Shu State. He didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.","Hundred Herbs Hall was indeed planning to expand, but Yan Sea and the others had only just left the Prefecture City.","No word had come back yet about the situation in the other counties and towns of Shu State.","Chen Yi hadn’t yet decided in which direction Hundred Herbs Hall should expand, or specifically, to which counties and towns in Shu State.","To say nothing of having any arrangements for the disciples of the Celestial Sect.","However, Chen Yi also knew it was useless to overthink it at this moment.","Xie Tingyun had already brought the Celestial Sect disciples here. In any case, he had to get them settled first.","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi said he would go to Hundred Herbs Hall tomorrow morning, first to put Xie Tingyun, this senior sister of the Celestial Sect, at ease.","\"Where are they now?\"","Xie Tingyun relaxed slightly and broke into a smile. \"A few too many people came, so I just told them to find their own places to stay for now.\"","\"Find their own places?\"","\"You may not know this, sir, but the Celestial Sect doesn’t have many silver coins.\"","\"When we came down from the mountain, we didn’t have much travel money on us, so...\"","\"...\"","An image immediately appeared in Chen Yi’s mind: a crowd of naive Celestial Sect disciples, performing in the East Market, begging in the West Market, and sleeping under a bridge in North City.","After a moment’s thought, he asked Xie Tingyun to wait, and told Pei Guanli and Xiaodie to hold an umbrella for Xiao Wuge and head to Jiaxing Garden first.","He returned to his study, took out two silver notes, and handed them to Xie Tingyun.","\"Two thousand taels of silver? Sir, you... you’re this wealthy?\"","Chen Yi smiled and said, \"I previously wrote a birthday verse for Duke Qian and received some silver from him.\"","\"Let me be clear, this two thousand taels of silver is a loan. Take it and get your junior sect brothers and sisters settled first.\"","\"After Shopkeeper Wang and I have discussed things, you can pay me back once you’ve earned some silver.\"","Xie Tingyun put away the silver notes and cupped her fist in thanks. \"Thank you, sir.\"","\"Don’t mention it...\"","As the big boss behind Hundred Herbs Hall, Chen Yi naturally didn’t want the Celestial Sect disciples to run into trouble in Shu State.","After all, he was relying on them to guard Hundred Herbs Hall.","It was only right to earn some goodwill in advance.","「A short while later.」","Chen Yi arrived at Jiaxing Garden, went straight to the wooden building where Xiao Wan’er was, and entered the living room.","When Xiao Wan’er saw him enter, she smiled, stood up, and invited him to sit.","Just as she was about to call for Xie Tingyun, she heard her say, \"Miss, I have to go settle one hun—a few of my junior brothers later. I’m afraid I won’t be able to join you for dinner.\"","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback for a moment. She glanced at the bewildered Shen Huatang and asked:","\"Weren’t your few junior brothers already settled in at Fengchun Building?\"","The smile on Xie Tingyun’s face froze. She didn’t dare look at Xiao Wan’er, and she especially didn’t dare look at Shen Huatang. She stammered:","\"A few other junior sisters have arrived as well. I can’t keep troubling you, Miss.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi was secretly amused. He knew at once that the senior sister of the Celestial Sect was playing the \"act first, report later\" game, deceiving everyone in the process.","Shen Huatang had figured it out as well.","Knowing her fellow senior sister as she did, she understood that Xie Tingyun was hiding quite a lot.","Only Xiao Wan’er suspected nothing, even telling Juan’er to go fetch some silver.","Xie Tingyun frantically waved her hands. \"No, no need for silver. The Second Son-in-law just gave me plenty.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused, her gaze falling on Chen Yi. \"Second Son-in-law?\"","’This Xie Tingyun is so unreliable,’ Chen Yi cursed inwardly, and had no choice but to repeat the explanation he’d given earlier.","After listening, Xiao Wan’er was still a bit doubtful, but with important matters to attend to, she only reminded Xie Tingyun to be careful and to speak up if she needed anything.","Xie Tingyun nodded, feeling slightly relieved.","Just as she was about to turn and leave, she saw Shen Huatang also excuse herself and exit the wooden building with her.","Xie Tingyun grimaced and said in a low voice, \"Junior Sister, it’s raining so hard. You don’t have to come with me, do you?\"","Shen Huatang ignored her, picked up two Oil Paper Umbrellas, and handed one to her, saying:","\"Senior Sister, it’s getting late. Let’s go and come back quickly.\"","Seeing this, Xie Tingyun pouted, took the umbrella, and began grumbling to herself.","’Now I can’t hide it anymore.’","’If Shen Huatang finds out so many junior brothers and sisters came, she... she’ll definitely give me an earful.’","Shen Huatang walked a good distance away and, seeing that she hadn’t followed, turned her head and called out, \"Senior Sister?\"","\"I’m coming, I’m coming! What’s the rush?\"","Hearing the two of them walk away, Chen Yi shook his head to himself, letting Xie Tingyun stew in her own troubles.","Xiao Wan’er watched Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang walk off into the distance through the window. Recalling her earlier doubt, she asked:","\"Brother-in-law, does the Celestial Sect disciples’ arrival in Shu State have something to do with you?\"","Chen Yi was startled for a moment but didn’t plan on hiding it. He nodded. \"It’s related, but not by much.\"","As he spoke, he recounted the time Xie Tingyun had come to him for help, and said with a smile:","\"It just so happened that Hundred Herbs Hall needed more people for its expansion, so I took the opportunity to put in a few good words for them.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded in understanding. \"As the senior sister of the Celestial Sect, it’s understandable that Tingyun would seek some opportunities for her sect mates.\"","After a pause, she asked, \"How are things going with Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","\"Counting the days, Shopkeeper Yan should have just arrived in Guangyuan. We should have news in a few days.\"","\"That’s fast progress. Just yesterday, Grandfather was asking about Hundred Herbs Hall. He said he wants to meet this Boss Chen.\"","Chen Yi picked at his food, calmly replying as he ate, \"I’ll ask Shopkeeper Wang when I go over tomorrow and see when Boss Chen will be back.\"","Xiao Wan’er sipped her hot soup and said with a smile, \"It would be best if Boss Chen could return in the next few days.\"","\"Because of the grain tax issue in the Three Towns, the estate has been spending a lot of silver these past two days. Grandfather is getting anxious.\"","Chen Yi was well aware of this. \"Wait for my news.\"","After a bit more small talk, Xiao Wan’er remembered the matter of the Annual Examination and couldn’t help but advise him:","\"Brother-in-law, the Annual Examination is crucial for your future prospects.\""]},{"number":323,"title":"Chapter 323 - 224: Fifth Grade","paragraphs":["\"If you have nothing more pressing, you should attend. As long as your scores aren’t too bad, you’ll just get a lecture at worst.\"","Before Chen Yi could speak, Xiao Wuge lifted his head and said, \"If you take the Annual Examination, Brother-in-law, you’re sure to take first place.\"","Pei Guanli, who was beside them, chimed in, \"Brother-in-law will have no problem, of course.\"","\"First place? He’s qualified enough to be the head examiner.\"","Chen Yi let out a helpless laugh. \"I haven’t touched those classics in a long time. I’m not confident I can pass the Annual Examination.\"","But when he saw the eager look in Xiao Wan’er’s eyes, he couldn’t bring himself to refuse outright. He just said,","\"There are still two months left, anyway. I’ll think about it.\"","A smile bloomed on Xiao Wan’er’s face, her bright eyes reflecting his image. \"That’s more like it,\" she said, her voice tinged with delight.","\"You aren’t just an Instructor at Guiyun Academy anymore. You’re also Mr. Qingzhou, whose fame has spread throughout the Great Wei Nine State and Three Prefectures. If you don’t have an official rank, you’re bound to become the subject of gossip among the world’s scholars.\"","’Let them talk.’","Chen Yi wanted to say as much.","But on second thought, he realized Xiao Wan’er had a point.","’It’s true that I don’t care for fame and fortune, but the world is full of mediocre, vulgar people.’","’If I don’t have an official rank, some people will undoubtedly show up just to cause me trouble.’","’Officials would demand I bow, scholars with ranks would look down on me, and members of Noble Families would mock me with scorn.’","The mere thought of such situations was a nuisance.","\"I’ll go to the academy in a few days and look over some of the classics.\"","\"Okay, good...\"","A short while later, they finished dinner.","Xiao Wan’er escorted him, Xiao Wuge, and Pei Guanli out of the wooden building. Gazing at the rain falling outside, she asked hesitantly,","\"I’m planning to visit my fief in a couple of days. I was wondering if you would have time, Brother-in-law?\"","She had spent the last while making all the necessary preparations for the Medical Dao Academy and now wanted to visit her fief to find a suitable location for its construction.","But since this was her first time undertaking such a project, she couldn’t help but feel a little unsure of herself.","Chen Yi guessed what she was thinking and nodded with a smile. \"If you’re not in a hurry, Sister-in-law, let’s plan for three days from now.\"","\"Tomorrow, I have to go to Hundred Herbs Hall to discuss the matter of those one hundred and twenty-seven Celestial Sect disciples with Wang Ji.\"","\"The day after tomorrow, I have two Calligraphy Dao classes at the academy.\"","Xiao Wan’er started to nod, then froze. Her beautiful eyes widened as she stared at him.","\"One hundred and twenty-seven?\"","\"That many disciples from the Celestial Sect came?\"","\"It was Fairy Tingyun’s decision. I have no idea how she managed to persuade the Celestial Sect elders.\"","\"Then Huatang... she doesn’t know about this yet, does she?\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"I’m guessing Fairy Tingyun is in for a rough night.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled. \"Huatang does have a rather cold personality.\"","\"But I’m sure it will be fine. Hundred Herbs Hall and Boss Chen can certainly find a place for the Celestial Sect disciples.\"","\"True...\"","As it turned out,","Xiao Wan’er had underestimated Shen Huatang.","No matter how cold and aloof she normally was, in the face of this situation, she was like a volcano on the verge of erupting.","After Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun left the Xiao Mansion in their carriage,","Shen Huatang had initially assumed Xie Tingyun was hiding a dozen or so fellow disciples at most.","But the carriage took a long, winding route, going from North City to West City, then from West City to South City, before finally stopping in the West Market.","It made frequent stops along the way, with Xie Tingyun keeping her head down as she notified their Celestial Sect junior brothers and sisters one by one.","By the end of it all, Shen Huatang’s expression was completely numb.","\"Just tell me. Exactly how many are there?\"","\"Fifty?\"","Xie Tingyun shook her head. \"Nope.\"","\"Eighty?\"","\"A little more.\"","\"A hundred?!\"","\"More... It’s one hundred and twenty-seven...\"","Shen Huatang asked through gritted teeth, \"Senior Sister, did you inform Master that you were bringing them down the mountain?\"","Xie Tingyun flinched. \"Master wouldn’t have agreed, so... I had them come down in batches.\"","CRUNCH.","Shen Huatang nearly ground her teeth to dust. \"You just wait! I’m writing a letter to tell Master everything right now!\"","\"Junior Sister, no, please...\"","...","Chen Yi had also underestimated Xie Tingyun.","But this situation only benefited him, so he decided to feign ignorance.","’I’ll just have Hundred Herbs Hall give them a bit more silver in the future.’","「After nightfall.」","The rain had lightened.","But on an autumn day, the rain carried a distinct chill.","Especially on a rainy night. The cool wind sent petals and leaves fluttering from the trees and flowers.","It lent an air of desolation even to the perpetually green Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi glanced at the sky, then instructed Xiaodie to give Xiao Wuge and Pei Guanli an extra quilt so they wouldn’t catch a chill.","Once Xiaodie had everything settled, he returned to his room and sat cross-legged on the bed.","After a brief rest, he began circulating his Four Symbols Skill.","Chen Yi had been cultivating diligently these past several days.","He had already reached Sixth Grade Perfection and was just one step away from breaking through to the Fifth Grade Realm.","He had originally planned to find another time to make his breakthrough at his residence on Chuansi Street.","But since Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang were both out of the mansion tonight, he decided not to wait any longer.","His True Essence surged through his limbs and bones like liquid mercury.","Wisps of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism condensed in his three great Seas of Qi: the Forehead Acupoint, the Chest Acupoint, and the Dantian.","This rapidly increased his Cultivation.","’Guide the Four Directions Spiritual Qi into the Sea of Qi, open the Four Divine Positions...’","As he recited the incantation for the Four Symbols Skill, the phantoms of the four Divine Beasts within his Forehead Acupoint—the Cyan Dragon, White Tiger, Vermilion Bird, and Black Tortoise—grew increasingly solid.","Four-colored streams of light flowed from their bodies, merging with his True Essence. This mixture circulated along the Twelve Main Meridians, drawing True Essence from his three great Seas of Qi and channeling it into the four phantom Divine Beasts.","An unknown amount of time passed.","\"ROAR!\"","\"SCREECH!\"","\"CRY!\"","\"HUMMM!\"","Chen Yi heard four deafening sounds ring out and echo ceaselessly in his mind.","The next moment, he felt a strange transformation in his True Essence. The mercury-like energy began to condense even further.","Amidst a flicker of four-colored light, his True Essence crystallized, becoming dazzlingly brilliant.","In a single circulatory cycle, the amount of his True Essence had more than doubled.","Its quality was also far beyond what it had been before.","Before he could investigate further, several lines of large, golden characters floated before his eyes:","[Cultivation successful. Cultivation: Lower Fifth Grade.]","[Four Symbols Skill (Earth Tier): Divine Position Spiritual Essence has advanced. The empowering effect of Wood, Water, Fire, and Gold Spiritual Qi has increased by fifty percent.]","Chen Yi glanced at the text with a small smile, then continued to guide his True Essence back into his three great Seas of Qi.","It was then that he discovered that within his Forehead Acupoint Sea of Qi, the Divine Beasts on the Four Divine Positions had become completely solid.","Where before there were only phantoms, they now had flesh and skin; even individual strands of fur were perfectly distinct.","After a moment of internal inspection,","Chen Yi understood what had happened. He slowly retracted his power, exhaling a faint, white Qi Sword.","His entire being felt reborn, much lighter than before.","He rose lightly to his feet. Looking down at himself, his smile grew wider.","’Martial Arts are truly miraculous,’ he thought. ’The Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism manifests internally as divine entities. They’re still tangible but without true substance for now. But as my Cultivation deepens, maybe I can make the Divine Beasts form real flesh, blood, and organs.’","That was the thought, anyway.","Chen Yi was already thrilled to have raised his Cultivation to the Fifth Grade.","In particular, the fifty percent increase to the empowerment from his Four Directions Divine Essence had led to significant improvements in all his Techniques.","Even the effects of his Four Symbols Skill, Big Spear Pile Skill, and Black Tortoise Concealment Technique—which he had thought were maxed out—had noticeably improved.","After another brief rest,","Chen Yi changed into a set of light clothes and slipped out to the Purple Bamboo Forest.","There, he began practicing all the techniques he had learned, one by one.","Mountain Shattering Fist, Hundred Flowers Palm, Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Body Technique, Meteor Butterfly Step, the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique, and the Brocade Spring Saber Technique.","Aside from the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique—which he had yet to fully integrate all the Profound Mysteries of, due to its Celestial Tier nature and his Spear Dao Perfection—he had already cultivated all his other Techniques to their absolute limit at his current stage.","The moment he began to execute them, Chen Yi noticed the difference.","The power of each Technique had increased dramatically, and the empowerment from his Divine Position Spiritual Essence felt like divine assistance.","Take the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique, for instance. Even without drawing upon the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism or unleashing his Spear Intent, its power was now comparable to what it had been with the full enhancement of his Great Success Spear Dao.","If he were to use his full power, he estimated a single spear strike would be enough to instantly kill Yan Fusha of the Five Poison Sect.","’If I’d had Fifth Grade Cultivation on the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival, how could a mere Yan Fusha have possibly injured me?’","Just then, the hour of Zi arrived. A dazzling golden light flared—","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Middle Grade: At the third quarter of the Hour of Hai, a Hidden Guard retrieves a secret letter at the wonton shop on Kangning Street. A minuscule Opportunity can be obtained.]","’The wonton shop...’","The smile on Chen Yi’s face grew wider. As he tidied up the Purple Bamboo Forest, he thought to himself,","’Ah, Lou Yuxue. She’s really something else now.’","Thanks to Ma Guan’s calligraphy, business at \"A Wonton Shop\" in Yunbian was booming.","Customers came and went in an endless stream.","When Chen Yi had gone to the academy to teach, he had glanced over once. The sight of Lou Yuxue, disguised as the busy proprietress, had almost made him laugh out loud.","’It really has been a while since I last went to say hello to an old friend.’","’And as it happens, I need the help of those White Tiger Guards for that other matter...’"]},{"number":324,"title":"Chapter 324 - 225: Cui’s Yunqing Building","paragraphs":["The Hidden Guard, or rather, the White Tiger Guard.","The more Chen Yi came into contact with them, the more he felt their purpose in Shu State was unclear.","Like the dark clouds obscuring the bright moon outside his window, the secrets behind them remained shrouded.","For example, he had already confirmed that Hawk, Ge the Third, and the others wanted him to become an official, gain prestige, or secure a position within the Xiao Family.","They essentially wanted him to possess \"prestige\" and \"power.\"","But what then?","Was he to be used as a puppet to control the Xiao Family, or something else?","If they wanted him to control the Xiao Family, the Old Master, Xiao Jinghong, and Xiao Wuge were three obstacles that could not be bypassed.","Unless the Hidden Guard made a move and killed those three, he would be unable to control the Xiao Family, no matter his official status or prestige.","Thus, after re-evaluating the Hidden Guard’s plans for him over the past few days, Chen Yi had a vague feeling that a crucial piece was still missing.","Then there were the Hidden Guard’s Lady Tiger and Simurgh Phoenix.","The former was hiding in the Bright Moon Building, her purpose unknown.","The latter hailed from the Qinghe Cui Family. Not only was her purpose for coming to Shu State a mystery, but her reasons for joining the White Tiger Guard were also strange.","Adding to that what Chen Yi already knew of the White Tiger Guard’s duties—specializing in infiltrating enemy nations and neighboring states, responsible for instigating defections and stirring up conflict.","Extrapolating from these duties, Chen Yi came to two possible conclusions.","First, the White Tiger Guard was treating Shu State like an enemy nation, intending to draw armies from other states to conquer it.","Second, they wanted to incite the Barbarian Race, Poshisu Country, and others to invade.","Regardless of their objective, it required Shu State to fall into chaos.","In other words, they needed to use the Xiao Family as a crowbar to stir up the entire state.","This was the most direct, effective, and fastest method.","’I’ll know their true purpose once I test it.’","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi cleaned up the mess in the Purple Bamboo Forest, returned to his room, changed into clean, comfortable clothes, and lay down on his bed.","He closed his eyes.","An immense, mountain-sized game board materialized in his mind.","On the board now were three more white stones than before.","One represented the Mountain Race, one the Celestial Sect, and the last represented Guiyun Academy.","Two Jianghu factions and a gathering place for scholars—all could be made to serve the Xiao Family through him.","There were also two new black stones.","The Five Poison Sect and the Bright Moon Building.","Because of Yan Fusha and her group, Chen Yi now directly associated the Five Poison Sect with the Jing State Liu Family.","As for the Bright Moon Building, there was little to say. They were classic pot-stirrers.","They would fight and kill for anyone who paid, simple as that.","As for the final black stone...","When placed, it would connect half the black stones on the board, forming a powerful position.","It represented none other than the financier who had previously paid Bright Moon Building’s Black Tooth to burn down the Three Towns.","In other words, the \"Anti-Xiao Alliance\" that Chen Yi had sensed.","However, he had only managed to uncover a few clues about them so far.","These included certain officials within the Inspectorate Office, the Governor’s Office, and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, as well as some merchants in the East and West Markets.","As for who else was behind it, he had only seen the tip of the iceberg.","Staring at the game board, Chen Yi pondered for a long time before his mind stirred.","He actually picked up the black stone representing the \"Hidden Guard,\" changed it into a white stone, and placed it on the \"eight-twelve\" position.","’The White Tiger Guard is one of the players.’","’They seem to have close ties and form alliances, but in reality, they exist outside the sphere of Shu State’s major family factions.’","’Therefore, just as they can become a pillar for those with malicious intent in Shu State, they can also be used by me.’","As Chen Yi calmly placed the stone, a smile touched his lips.","’My courage has grown quite a bit since my Martial Arts Cultivation improved.’","...","The night passed uneventfully.","Before dawn, the pitter-patter of rain echoed endlessly throughout Spring Lotus Garden.","It blended with the croaking of frogs.","As a cool breeze blew, Xiaodie changed into slightly thicker linen clothes. She tidied up the two wooden buildings efficiently before going to help Xiao Wuge get up and dressed.","For once, Pei Guanli was up early of her own accord, splashing barefoot in the puddles in front of the building.","Her cheerful laughter could be heard from time to time.","This caused Xiaodie, who was leading Xiao Wuge to the main hall and about to fetch breakfast from the kitchen, to glance over and say with a smile,","\"Be careful you don’t catch a cold.\"","\"I won’t, I won’t! A little rain and a few puddles won’t dare make me sick.\"","Pei Guanli waved a hand without looking back, continuing to hop and splash in the standing water. The bell on her chest jingled incessantly.","JINGLE JINGLE.","Hearing the sounds from outside, Chen Yi woke from his deep sleep.","He glanced at the sky outside the window. The clouds were still dark and the rain was steady, so he got up and stretched.","He had a lot to do today, so he couldn’t afford to sleep in.","After getting dressed, Chen Yi went downstairs, greeted Xiao Wuge, and pushed the door open to leave.","Xiao Wuge rubbed his eyes and followed him. \"Brother-in-law, are you going out today?\"","Chen Yi nodded casually. \"I promised Fairy Tingyun yesterday that I’d go to Hundred Herbs Hall to discuss arrangements for the Celestial Sect disciples.\"","\"Also, about your sister... the Old Master wants to see Boss Chen. I’ll go ask about it.\"","’Asking is pointless, though.’","’There’s no way my identity as Boss Chen Yu can be revealed anytime soon.’","’At least, not before Yan Sea and the others finish their tour of Shu State, and not before the plans to expand Hundred Herbs Hall are underway. I won’t appear as ’Chen Yu’ during this time.’","’During this period, it’s naturally impossible for me to meet with the Xiao family.’","’Not even the Old Master.’","Chen Yi knew the Old Master had already grown suspicious, suspecting that the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall was secretly helping the Xiao Family.","Under these circumstances, he didn’t need to be a genius to know that meeting the Old Master would inevitably lead to a round of questioning and probing.","So, for now, not showing his face was the best choice.","Xiao Wuge said \"Oh,\" then hesitated. \"Brother-in-law, can I go out with you?\""]},{"number":325,"title":"Chapter 325 - 225: Cui’s Yunqing Building","paragraphs":["Chen Yi watched Pei Guanli treading water and replied, \"I can’t.\"","After a pause, he looked down at Xiao Wuge and asked with a smile, \"Has your sister found you a new tutor?\"","\"It wasn’t my sister. It was... it was my second uncle.\"","\"Second Uncle?\"","’Xiao Xuanshuo?’","Chen Yi glanced toward the world outside Spring Lotus Garden and asked thoughtfully, \"What does he want you to learn?\"","\"The Martial Arts.\"","\"Hmm? I remember Xiaodie mentioning that you need to undergo Foundation Establishment at age six before you can practice the Martial Arts.\"","Xiao Wuge’s face soured. \"Second Uncle said I have to go to Jinling next March. I don’t have much time left in the mansion, so he wants to teach me some techniques before I leave.\"","\"That way, my Martial Arts progression might be a little faster once I’ve achieved Foundation Establishment.\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"Second Uncle is right. You really should learn a few flashy moves beforehand.\"","\"Huh? You think so too?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"As the legitimate heir of the Xiao Family, you’re destined to inherit the Marquis Position. How could you possibly neglect the Martial Arts?\"","\"Even after you leave Shu State for Jinling, you can’t let your Martial Arts training slide. Cultivate diligently and try to catch up to your second sister.\"","Xiao Wuge tilted his head up to look at him. \"My second sister is so incredible. There’s no way I could ever catch up to her.\"","Chen Yi casually patted his head and smiled. \"Plans are made in heaven, but success is achieved by man.\"","\"Who knows? Maybe your talent for the Martial Arts is even greater than your second sister’s.\"","\"Besides, your second uncle is doing this for your own good. Never mind me, even your sister wouldn’t stand in his way.\"","Xiao Wuge grunted in assent, a smile spreading across his face. \"I’ll do as you say.\"","’Plans are made in heaven, but success is achieved by man. I have to write that down, write that down.’","Not long after, Xiaodie returned with their meal. The group sat together, eating and chatting.","The conversation was mostly just Xiaodie and Pei Guanli chattering away.","Eight out of every ten sentences were about Chen Yi.","One moment, it was about how *Song of the Water Melody* had earned the praise of yet another great scholar or won the favor of some high official.","The next, it was about the exhibition hall at Guiyun Academy opening, and the endless stream of people flocking to see his *Post-rain Reflections*.","While praising his Perfect Realm Calligraphy Dao, people were even more eager to see the original calligraphy for *Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn*.","When the topic came to this, Xiaodie couldn’t help but ask, \"Young Master, what about that calligraphy piece you wrote?\"","Chen Yi took a bite of mooncake. \"It’s lost.\"","’That night’s battle with Yan Fusha had been brutal. The entire Painted Boat was torn to shreds. How could a piece of calligraphy possibly have survived?’","Xiaodie looked disappointed. \"I heard everyone by the banks of Quchi that night said they witnessed an Immortal Realm.\"","Pei Guanli said breezily, \"Brother-in-law can just write another one.\"","Chen Yi shot her a look and asked irritably, \"You want to see that again?\"","Pei Guanli immediately gave an awkward grin. \"Nope, nope.\"","’She had no desire to relive that night’s experience.’","’If Chen Yi hadn’t rescued her in time, she’d probably be six feet under by now.’","\"Speaking of which, I sent that letter home a long time ago. Why hasn’t Ah Ma written back yet?\"","\"Just be patient and wait.\"","Chen Yi replied. After finishing the porridge in his bowl, he added, \"Maybe she’s not in a hurry.\"","Pei Guanli crouched by the table, her mouth stuffed with mooncake, and mumbled:","\"Sh-she dotes on me the most. Sh-she has to be in a hurry.\"","After finally managing to swallow the mooncake, she continued, \"Don’t worry, Brother-in-law. If Ah Ma doesn’t make a move, I’ll find a way to help you get reve—\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yi flicked her on the head. \"Get what? You’re to stay put in the mansion for the time being. Don’t go anywhere.\"","Pei Guanli clutched her head and crouched back down properly, muttering, \"Fine, I won’t go out.\"","Seeing her get put in her place, Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge burst into carefree laughter.","But before their laughter could fade, a set of footsteps and the rumbling of wheels sounded from outside the garden.","A flicker of understanding passed through Chen Yi. He wiped the corners of his mouth.","Then he saw Wang Lixing wheeling Xiao Xuanshuo to the front of the wooden building.","Without so much as a glance at Chen Yi and the others, Xiao Xuanshuo addressed Xiao Wuge. \"Come out here.\"","Xiao Wuge glanced at Chen Yi. Seeing him smile and nod, he put down his bowl and chopsticks, rose, and stepped out of the wooden building to bow.","\"Second Uncle.\"","Apparently satisfied with his nephew’s respectful demeanor, Xiao Xuanshuo nodded. \"I have already spoken with Wan’er.\"","\"From today on, you are to be at the Martial Arts Arena at three in the morning and will return at noon.\"","\"Yes.\"","’Listening to them, Chen Yi knew that Xiao Xuanshuo’s words were meant for his ears as much as for Xiao Wuge’s.’","He rose and went outside, offering a deep bow with a smile. \"Qingzhou greets Second Uncle.\"","\"Now that Wuge is beginning his Martial Arts practice, are there any special preparations we should make here at Spring Lotus Garden? For his daily meals, for instance?\"","Xiao Xuanshuo glanced at him. His face remained impassive, but his tone was considerably milder than it had been initially.","\"I instructed Wan’er yesterday. You just need to follow the same preparations as Jiaxing Garden.\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"Qingzhou understands.\"","He then patted Xiao Wuge on the shoulder. \"Practice the Martial Arts well. If you achieve great things one day, your brother-in-law will give you a gift.\"","\"Really?\"","Chen Yi held out his palm and grinned. \"A gentleman’s promise?\"","Xiao Wuge slapped his hand against Chen Yi’s. \"I want *Song of the Water Melody*.\"","\"That doesn’t count as a gift.\"","\"Then what gift will you give me, Brother-in-law?\"","\"You’ll know when the time comes...\"","After a bit more idle chatter, Chen Yi watched Xiao Xuanshuo, Xiao Wuge, and Wang Lixing depart from Spring Lotus Garden.","’Time flies.’","’Before he knew it, half a year had passed since he’d arrived.’","’In another six months, Xiao Wuge would be setting off for Jinling.’","’Hopefully, the Xiao Family’s situation will have improved by then.’","Lost in these thoughts, Chen Yi lost his appetite for breakfast.","He instructed Xiaodie not to forget to ask Jiaxing Garden about Xiao Wuge’s dietary restrictions, then left Spring Lotus Garden by himself under an Oil Paper Umbrella.","A steady autumn rain was falling.","Beneath the overcast sky, the winding pavilions and halls of the Xiao Mansion were veiled in a layer of dim mist.","Though the flowers and plants remained lush and verdant, the scattered petals and fallen leaves created an unavoidable air of desolation.","Chen Yi seemed oblivious to it all, smiling and returning the greetings of the servants who bowed as he passed.","With the revelation of his Perfect Realm Calligraphy Dao, bolstered by *Post-rain Reflections* and *Song of the Water Melody*, his fame had recently skyrocketed.","This made his life within the Xiao Mansion considerably easier.","Besides Xiaodie’s daily reports on who was praising him now, the masters and mistresses of the mansion’s various residences had also begun to sing his praises.","Consequently, the attitude of the servants toward him had improved significantly.","It was a night-and-day difference from when he had first arrived at the Marquis’s Mansion.","Chen Yi paid it little mind, but upon reflection, he supposed it was a positive development.","At the very least, it meant he was now truly considered a member of the Xiao Family.","It was certainly better than constantly being called \"the Xiao Family’s runaway groom.\"","「An hour or so later.」","Chen Yi arrived outside the West Market Hundred Herbs Hall. Just as he was about to enter and find Wang Ji, he caught sight of the shop across the street out of the corner of his eye.","He stopped in his tracks, turning his head to look.","Outside what was supposed to be a restaurant, several young servants in green were hanging a sign.","What caught Chen Yi’s attention were the words on the sign: Cui’s Yunqing Building.","’Cui’s Records?’","’Yunqing Building?’","’Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu?’","Chen Yi’s mind raced. His gaze drifted to the restaurant’s second floor, where he could faintly make out a busy figure.","It was none other than the young mistress of the Qinghe Cui Family, the Hidden Guard \"Simurgh Phoenix\"—Cui Qingwu.","’The Lady Tiger opens a wonton shop, the Simurgh Phoenix opens a restaurant. Tsk, these Hidden Guards really are all cut from the same cloth.’","’But \"Cui’s Records\"...’","’Cui Qingwu is even using the Cui family name. Is she planning on settling down in Shu State for good?’","Chen Yi gave it another look before walking into Hundred Herbs Hall, lost in thought.","Wang Ji came forward to greet him, but before he could speak, Chen Yi cut him off with a raised hand. \"Shopkeeper Wang, the Eldest Miss requests your presence.\"","Naturally, it wasn’t really Xiao Wan’er who had invited him to the mansion.","It was just an excuse for Chen Yi to have Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao drive the carriage to his residence on Chuansi Street in North City.","With Cui Qingwu right across the street, he didn’t want to say anything that might arouse her suspicion.","A short while later, the carriage departed from the West Market.","Cui Qingwu, standing on the second floor, glanced down at the departing carriage. After a moment’s thought, she called for Huan’er.","\"Go and ask if Young Master Chen is free today. Invite him to Yunqing Building to sample our Lang Wine.\"","\"Yes.\"","’Cui Qingwu knew how much Chen Yunfan valued Chen Yi. Appealing to his interests was a sound strategy.’","’This was precisely why she had opened Yunqing Building across from Hundred Herbs Hall.’","’I originally wanted to open it near Guiyun Academy, but unfortunately, that woman is there.’","Cui Qingwu watched the carriage disappear into the distance, the corners of her lips curling slightly. \"I seem to have underestimated that woman’s tenacity.\"","\"To think she could make her wonton shop so successful.\"","\"In that case, I can’t afford to fall behind.\"","...","Chen Yi, of course, was oblivious to the schemes of the Cui family’s young miss. After having the carriage deliberately pass by the gates of the Xiao Mansion, he headed straight for his residence on Chuansi Street.","The moment he sat down.","Chen Yi gave an order. \"Wang Ji, go and bring Guard Liu here.\"","’He’d let the \"Sword Madman\" rest for long enough. It was time for him to get moving again.’"]},{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326 - 226: Merchants Pursue Profit, Parting Lightly","paragraphs":["「After Wang Ji left.」","Chen Yi sat still, letting Zhang Dabao apply his disguise as he asked a question.","\"When did the tavern across from Hundred Herbs Hall change hands?\"","Zhang Dabao, deftly combing Chen Yi’s long hair, replied, \"It’s been a while.\"","\"It must have been the day after the Mid-Autumn Festival. A very luxurious carriage pulled up outside, carrying a very beautiful young lady.\"","\"Ah, no, it was several very beautiful young ladies. They said they wanted to buy out the tavern.\"","\"At first, the tavern’s owner refused. But after the young lady had her people bring out several chests of silver, he agreed.\"","Chen Yi tilted his head and asked, \"Several chests of silver?\"","Zhang Dabao replied, \"You should have seen the spectacle.\"","\"There were quite a few customers in the tavern, and they all watched as the young lady had the chests opened, one after another, asking the owner if he would sell.\"","\"He wouldn’t sell for one chest, so she opened a second. It wasn’t until she opened the fifth chest—a full ten thousand taels of silver—that the owner finally gave in.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle. ’This is definitely something Cui Qingwu would do.’","To a certain extent, the Qinghe Cui Family was wealthier and more powerful than the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, and naturally, stronger than the Jing State Liu Family as well.","If even Liu Wen could mobilize three hundred thousand taels of silver, then Cui Qingwu, as the Cui Family’s direct daughter, would have far more silver coins at her disposal.","But what concerned him was that Cui Qingwu had opened her establishment directly across from Hundred Herbs Hall.","He didn’t know if she had done it intentionally or not.","’If it was intentional, what is her goal?’","’Surely she wouldn’t go to such lengths just for him, the owner \"Chen Yu\"?’","’But if it was unintentional, it was too much of a coincidence.’","After pondering for a moment, Chen Yi still couldn’t figure out Cui Qingwu’s intentions. He decided to put the matter aside for now and wait for an opportunity to ask Chen Yunfan later.","\"How has Hundred Herbs Hall been these past few days?\"","\"Same as always.\"","\"After Shopkeeper Yan left with his people, Shopkeeper Wang is the only one left in the hall. He’s so busy his feet don’t touch the ground. I get tired just watching him.\"","\"But Shopkeeper Wang said yesterday that business has been affected recently. A lot of customers who used to come to our hall for medicine have gone elsewhere.\"","\"It’s called... Xinglin something...\"","Chen Yi said, \"Xinglin Hall.\"","Zhang Dabao quickly agreed, saying, \"That’s the one,\" as he applied a light mask to Chen Yi’s face.","\"I don’t know what their background is, but they just opened and have already snatched a lot of business from the other medicine halls.\"","\"Shopkeeper Wang said that if it weren’t for the tea we serve at our hall, this month’s income in silver coins would probably be less than half of what it should be.\"","Chen Yi knew exactly what was going on.","Xinglin Hall had a renowned doctor in residence. Moreover, having just established themselves in Shu State, their medicine prices were even lower than Hundred Herbs Hall’s, so it was only natural they were squeezing out the competition.","However, that kind of three-trick pony approach would only work once.","If the Jing State Liu Family didn’t send more people, they would sooner or later find themselves in trouble, even with Liu Hong backing Xinglin Hall.","Shu State, after all, was not the Liu Family’s Shu State.","After a bit more small talk, seeing that his guest had not yet arrived, Chen Yi had Zhang Dabao bring him an Ancient Zither.","He took it, laid it across his lap, and casually plucked it a couple of times.","The notes from the Zither, some crisp, some dull, echoed through the main hall.","Zhang Dabao clapped his hands. \"I’ve long heard that you, boss, are a master of Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting. I imagine your Zither Dao must be just like your Calligraphy Dao.\"","He had been at Hundred Herbs Hall for so long, with people coming and going every day, that he had naturally heard about the Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala. He also knew that Chen Yi had won the title of Poetry Champion with \"Song of the Water Melody.\"","In his mind, since the boss’s literary talent and Calligraphy Dao were so outstanding, his Zither Dao couldn’t possibly be bad.","So, after speaking, he tilted his head, preparing to listen intently.","Chen Yi ignored him, merely looking at the five strings of the zither and placing his hands on either side.","He began to play.","TWANG—THUMP—CRACK!","The familiar trio of sounds from the Zither immediately rang throughout the courtyard.","The smile on Zhang Dabao’s face froze. He stared at him in astonishment.","Chen Yi seemed completely unaware, playing the score for \"Carefree Travel\" as if he were in his own world.","CRACKLE-CLACK, SNAP-CRACK, TWANG-THUMP-THUMP...","The series of sounds from the breaking zither strings was more piercing than the sound of the rain falling outside.","Zhang Dabao stared at him blankly. The string of noises echoing in his ears left him with only a single thought.","’The boss is quite good at fluffing cotton.’","’Sonorous and powerful, full of twangs.’","Soon, Chen Yi finished playing the piece.","Not only did he show no sign of embarrassment for his terrible playing, but he actually revealed a look of sudden understanding.","\"Finger Technique, Power Dao, and rhythm must be coordinated.\"","Then, before Zhang Dabao could ask, Chen Yi began plucking the strings again, playing \"Carefree Travel\" for a second time.","With the experience from his first attempt, he reined in most of his Power. Using the nimble fingers he had developed through Martial Arts, he played in a much more structured manner.","Although it still had nothing to do with being \"melodious and pleasant,\" it was enough to make Zhang Dabao abandon his plan to cover his ears.","’Perhaps the boss was just getting familiar with the Zither before.’","Before long, the second performance was over. Zhang Dabao clapped at the perfect moment and offered his praise:","\"Boss, your zither skill is... good.\"","He really couldn’t think of a more suitable adjective. Just managing to say the word \"good\" was his limit.","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"Good in what way?\"","\"It’s... well, it’s better than my playing, anyway.\"","Seeing Zhang Dabao’s sheepish grin, Chen Yi didn’t press him further. He summoned a light screen and glanced at it:","Cultivation: Lower Fifth Grade","[Opportunity: 525]","’Five hundred... I should be more frugal with these.’","With that thought, Chen Yi spent 11 Opportunity points to raise his Zither Dao to Minor Success.","Ever since gaining a huge amount of Opportunity from burning the summer grain of the Three Towns, he hadn’t spent any of it, aside from raising his Saber Dao to Great Success.","On one hand, it was because all the skills he had learned were already at the Great Success Realm, and raising them further required too much Opportunity.","On the other hand, he was also saving up with the intention of raising one of his Daos to Perfection.","After the Five Poison Sect’s attack, where he had an unexpected epiphany and achieved the Perfection Realm in Spear Dao, Chen Yi came to deeply understand the gap between the Great Success and Perfection Realms of Martial Arts.","If not the difference between heaven and earth, it was at least the difference between a sesame seed and a watermelon."]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327 - 226: Merchants Pursue Profit and Part Lightly (Part 2)","paragraphs":["To put it bluntly, when enhanced by the Perfection Realm of the Spear Dao, the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique was ten times more powerful than the Mountain Shattering Fist, the Hundred Flowers Palm, or the Brocade Spring Saber Technique.","Even when using just the Earth Tier version of the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique, it was still five times more powerful.","The difference was clear to see.","But before Chen Yi could play another song, Wang Ji arrived at the residence in a carriage, bringing Liu Lang with him.","The moment the carriage came to a steady halt, Liu Lang eagerly jumped down, his disguised, middle-aged face wreathed in smiles.","\"Boss, you finally remembered me.\"","Chen Yi set the Ancient Zither aside, calmly gestured for him to sit, and said, \"We’ll discuss your business later.\"","Liu Lang did as he was told and sat down, knowing it was inconvenient to talk with Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao present.","\"I’ve already waited this many days. I’m in no rush, no rush at all.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly and gestured for Wang Ji to also take a seat. \"How are the preparations for the Hundred Herbs Hall expansion coming along?\"","Wang Ji replied respectfully, \"I’ve already had my men find a secluded location to build a larger warehouse.\"","\"It will serve two purposes: one, to store various medicinal herbs, and two, to house the artisans who prepare the tea beverages.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then said, \"Prepare more medicinal herbs, and do the same for the artisans.\"","\"You’re right, Boss.\"","\"Lately, because of Xinglin Hall, the medicinal herb merchants in Shu State have started holding out for better prices. The cost of herbs for our tea beverages is already twenty percent higher than before.\"","\"No matter how high the price, acquire as much as you can. We don’t want to be caught short-handed after the Hundred Herbs Hall expands.\"","Wang Ji hesitated. \"But if we do that, I’m afraid the silver coins we have on hand won’t be enough.\"","Chen Yi had already anticipated this. \"Just tell me how much silver you’re short.\"","Seeing that Wang Ji’s worries were assuaged, he continued, \"Also, do you remember what I said before about recruiting guards?\"","Wang Ji nodded. \"You said that to guarantee the supply of our tea beverages, we needed to recruit some experts.\"","\"The people have arrived.\"","\"They’ve arrived?\"","\"A group of elite disciples from the Celestial Sect. There are quite a few of them, one hundred and twenty-seven in total. I’ll have them find you later.\"","Wang Ji’s mouth fell open. \"One hundred and twenty-seven?\"","Unexpectedly, Liu Lang, who was sitting beside him, was even more surprised. \"Boss, they’re all disciples of the Celestial Sect?\"","Chen Yi nodded and said with a smile, \"With Xie Tingyun, the Celestial Sect’s senior disciple, vouching for them, there shouldn’t be any mistake.\"","\"Is the Celestial Sect that desperate for money? I remember they don’t have many members—three hundred at the absolute most.\"","\"It’s a long story...\"","Chen Yi didn’t hide anything and briefly explained what had happened, adding a reminder:","\"Having the Celestial Sect disciples at Hundred Herbs Hall has its pros and cons. From now on, you all need to be more careful in what you say and do.\"","This was mainly directed at Wang Ji, who needed to watch his mouth to avoid exposing Chen Yi’s identity.","Liu Lang laughed. \"Good thing I didn’t kill Shen Huatang before, or I’d be in serious trouble this time.\"","Chen Yi shot him a glare, making him shut his mouth with an awkward laugh. Only then did Chen Yi wave his hand and say:","\"Wang Ji, take Dabao to the Xiao Family to find Fairy Tingyun first. You can decide how to arrange everyone.\"","Wang Ji acknowledged the order and headed straight for the Xiao Family with Zhang Dabao.","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi stood up, glanced at the sky outside, then closed the door and said with a smile:","\"Xiao Jinghong isn’t in Shu State lately, so we’re safe for the time being.\"","\"But there’s no guarantee when she’ll be back. From now on, you’d best maintain your disguise and act with more caution and discretion.\"","Liu Lang grimaced, asking with a hint of a headache, \"Boss, we helped the Xiao Family before, didn’t we? Why are we hiding like this?\"","\"For now, I don’t want her to know I exist. You’ll find out the specific reason later.\"","\"Fine, you’re the boss. I’ll do whatever you say.\"","\"But next time, I really can’t stay cooped up in one place for that long again. I nearly died of boredom...\"","Seeing Liu Lang rambling on, Chen Yi shot him a sidelong glance. \"If something like this happens again, should I find a couple of girls for you?\"","\"Yes, please! I mean... uh, no need.\"","Liu Lang caught his expression, and his heart skipped a beat.","’He knew all too well how good Chen Yi was at screwing people over. He didn’t want to be on the receiving end of one of those schemes.’","’After all, even someone as formidable as Black Tooth had been tricked to his death. What chance did he stand?’","\"Enough nonsense. I called you here for a serious matter.\"","After a pause, seeing that Liu Lang had quieted down, Chen Yi said, \"Next, I need you to keep a close watch on Liu Hong.\"","Liu Lang was taken aback. \"Who did you say?\"","\"The Shu State Governor’s Office. The Left Governor, Liu Hong.\"","\"Boss, you... you dare to scheme against even him? You... you... truly are a man destined for great things.\"","Chen Yi ignored him and continued:","\"You only need to watch him. Record what he does every day, who he meets, and what he says.\"","\"Other than that, do nothing extra. And most importantly, do not let him or anyone around him notice you.\"","Liu Lang wanted to ask why, but seeing that Chen Yi had no intention of explaining, he could only nod and accept the task.","Chen Yi saw through his thoughts but didn’t bother to explain. \"Knowing less isn’t a bad thing for you.\"","Liu Lang said nonchalantly, \"Don’t worry. What I’m meant to know, I’ll find out without asking.\"","He had been with Chen Yi for some time and was well aware of his methods.","It was just like the time he schemed against Xiao Dongchen.","If he hadn’t been there for the whole thing, seeing and hearing it all with his own eyes and ears, he would have never figured out Chen Yi’s plan.","It would be the same this time.","Even if Chen Yi told him everything, he reckoned he still wouldn’t be able to see the whole picture, so he decided not to ask any more questions.","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yi sent Liu Lang on his way.","Afterward, he removed his disguise and took a roundabout route before finally returning to the Xiao Family estate.","But as soon as he entered the front courtyard, Chen Yi sensed something was amiss within the residence.","The expressions of Liu Si’er and several other Armored Warriors were much graver than before.","After a moment’s thought, Chen Yi slowed his pace to eavesdrop on their conversation.","\"Those grain merchants are truly black-hearted. Taking advantage of the rain these past two days, they’ve gone and raised their prices without authorization.\""]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328 - 226: Merchants Pursue Profit, Parting Lightly (Part 3)","paragraphs":["\"And they have the nerve to say this year’s harvest was bad. Pah!\"","\"In the past, a *shi* of grain cost one tael of silver at most, but this time it shot straight up to one and a half.\"","\"It might not seem like a big jump, but the garrisons of the Three Towns are short four hundred thousand *shi*. All told, that’s an extra one hundred and sixty thousand taels of silver!\"","\"You’re telling me!\"","\"I heard the Third Master went in person and was completely rebuffed. I wonder if the Marquis will go himself.\"","\"He’ll go. Why wouldn’t he?\"","\"He should take us with him. I’d like to see how many heads they’ve got to dare and raise prices for no reason!\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi frowned to himself.","The day before yesterday, Xiao Wan’er had told him that the silver coins Elder Master Xiao spent buying grain had nearly emptied the family’s coffers.","It was just barely enough to cover the summer grain that had been burned in Iron Wall Town and to fill the shortfall in the grain tax.","Now, only a few days later, the price of grain had gone up.","Chen Yi didn’t have to think too deeply to know what was going on.","Someone had timed this perfectly, knowing the Xiao Family was short on silver, and was deliberately scheming against them.","’Thinking deeper... could this be the crime of deceiving the emperor?’","After all, the reason Elder Master Xiao had spent so much silver to buy grain was because of the Imperial Edict from the Capital Prefecture that arrived on the day of the Mid-Autumn Festival.","Unless the Elder Master was determined to deceive the emperor, he had no choice but to replenish the supply.","’The Jing State Liu Family?’","’Probably not.’","’Their schemes in Shu State are only just beginning. They shouldn’t have been able to coordinate with all the various parties to fix the grain price.’","’That only leaves one other possibility—those fat rats hiding in the shadows.’","Connecting this to the unusual fluctuations in the grain prices within Shu State Prefecture City right after news broke about the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain, Chen Yi already had his answer.","Aside from the Financier who hired Black Tooth of the Bright Moon Building, there was likely no one else who could have orchestrated this.","’This is an open conspiracy.’","’Elder Master Xiao... is probably in a difficult position now.’","Mulling this over, Chen Yi impassively held his umbrella as he crossed the central courtyard and arrived at the Spring Lotus Garden.","When Xiaodie saw him enter, she quickly put down what she was doing and came over to greet him.","She took the Oil Paper Umbrella from his hand while using a towel to wipe the light rain from his clothes.","Chen Yi let her attend to him, his gaze falling on Jiaxing Garden as he wondered if Xiao Wan’er had heard the news.","Xiaodie noticed his gaze and said with a smile, \"Young Master, I’ve already asked the Eldest Young Mistress, as you instructed.\"","\"From now on, I will instruct the kitchen staff to prepare Young Master Wuge’s meals separately to ensure his Martial Arts training is not hindered.\"","Chen Yi knew the news hadn’t reached the inner quarters yet, so he didn’t press the matter.","From the fact that the grain price had only risen to one and a half taels of silver, it was clear that those people were also worried that raising it too high would provoke the Elder Master to take drastic measures.","Therefore, the matter was both difficult and simple.","It was ultimately just a matter of spending more silver.","But why should they?","...","Chen Yi didn’t go anywhere that afternoon. He just holed up in the Spring Lotus Garden, practicing calligraphy and drinking tea.","He appeared carefree and at ease, but in his mind, he had already played out several games of chess.","He didn’t stop until after nightfall.","’They’re nothing more than a few fat rats... Hah!’","’If I can catch them all in one fell swoop, I’m sure the Xiao Family’s situation in Shu State will improve considerably.’","But after thinking for a long time, the one thing Chen Yi couldn’t figure out was why these people were targeting the Xiao Family.","The Jing State Liu Family had come to Shu State with the intention of seizing another’s territory, that much was clear.","But this \"Financier\" had made two moves, both related to the price of grain, which inevitably made him wonder.","Even if the Xiao Family got screwed over by them, they would only lose some silver.","They could always scrape it together if they had to.","As long as the Xiao family was still around, as long as Elder Master Xiao and Xiao Jinghong were still around, those people would be brought to account sooner or later.","’They can’t possibly just want to make a bit of silver, can they?’","Chen Yi stroked his chin and muttered, \"Then again, it’s not entirely out of the question.\"","Merchants chase profit.","The more chaos, the more they earn.","Especially when it comes to matters of war, any merchant with enough nerve can make a fortune.","There was no guarantee these people weren’t thinking the same way.","At this thought, Chen Yi couldn’t help but smile. \"If that’s really the case, then things are about to get interesting.\"","He just loved dealing with these kinds of fat cats."]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329 - 227: Hi, Miss Yuxue","paragraphs":["The third quarter past seven in the evening.","Night had fallen, but it was far from silent.","A torrential downpour filled Shu State Prefecture City with a cacophony of spattering and splashing.","This was especially true within Spring Lotus Garden, with its lush foliage.","The sound of rain hammering against the bluestone slabs and roof tiles was a clamor.","Although it didn’t affect Chen Yi, it made it difficult for Xiaodie, Xiao Wuge, and Pei Guanli to fall asleep.","This was particularly true for Xiao Wuge, who had just begun his journey in Martial Arts today at the Martial Arts Arena.","After dinner, he had scampered over, his face alight with excitement, to say he couldn’t sleep.","Chen Yi had no choice.","He could only listen to him talk about his Martial Arts Cultivation.","For example, his Second Uncle, Xiao Xuanshuo, had taught him the Stand Form. It wasn’t the Big Spear Pile Skill, but a Pile Skill set called [Little Yellow Court].","Although Xiao Wuge didn’t reveal the specific mnemonic verses for the technique, Chen Yi was able to deduce the general effects of the Little Yellow Court Skill from just a few snippets of conversation.","It seemed to be a Pile Skill designed to cultivate Innate Qi, which he would focus on before beginning Foundation Establishment to temper his physical body.","Realizing this, Chen Yi didn’t press for more details, only reminding Xiao Wuge to focus on his Cultivation.","They chatted and laughed, and the time slipped by until it was the Hour of Xu.","Chen Yi had just sent Xiaodie to take Xiao Wuge to rest.","After blowing out the oil lamp, he changed into a set of Night Clothes, found a Raincoat to throw over them, and quietly left Spring Lotus Garden.","He followed the muddy mountain path out of the Marquis’s Mansion, then changed course and headed first for his residence on Chuansi Street.","After having Zhang Dabao apply a disguise for him, he then set out for Kangning Street.","Fortunately, it was still raining. Kangning Street, which was usually filled with pedestrians even late at night, did not have many scholars and beauties meeting for private trysts.","The few passersby were mostly hurrying on their way.","There were also a few unrestrained scholars who, holding no umbrellas, were pouring wine from jars into their mouths and shouting incoherently:","\"The apes’ cries on both banks are endless, while my light boat has passed ten thousand mountains! Me, I’m going to pass those ten thousand mountains, hahaha...\"","\"Well recited, Brother Lin, magnificent! But I prefer the line written by Mr. Qingzhou—’May we all live long and share this moon, though a thousand miles may part us.’\"","\"Fine words, fine words...\"","Chen Yi pursed his lips and walked past the drunkards.","Before long, he arrived at There is a Wonton Shop by the Clouds, the one outside Guiyun Academy.","\"Oh?\"","Chen Yi was a bit stunned by what he saw inside the wonton shop.","He couldn’t help but look up at the night sky, then at the falling rain all around, confirming that it was indeed a late and rainy night.","’It’s so late, and there are still so many people in there eating wontons?’","But the facts spoke for themselves, and Chen Yi had no choice but to believe his eyes.","Even at this late hour, the wonton shop was still packed to the brim.","Of the thirteen tables in the main hall, more than half were full, and the rest were occupied by groups of two or three.","Furthermore, some men who had had too much to drink were still stumbling into the shop, hollering for the lady boss to bring them a two-liang serving of wontons.","This kept the several sturdy women in the shop busy without a moment’s rest.","One moment they were carrying bowls of wontons to the customers, the next they were clearing the leftovers from the tables.","Even Lou Yuxue wasn’t idle.","Standing behind the counter to collect silver and record accounts, her abacus rattled with a furious CLACK-CLACK-CLACK.","Every so often, she could be heard shouting at the top of her lungs, \"Two bowls of three-liang wontons, one liang of wine!\"","\"One bowl of two-liang wontons, with an extra liang of lamb!\"","\"Da Ya, come clear this table!\"","\"Bigfoot, get me...\"","Chen Yi studied Lou Yuxue carefully. After confirming that she wasn’t someone else in disguise, he almost burst out laughing.","’You’ve really made this business a roaring success, Lou Yuxue.’","Although he’d had mischievous intentions when he had Ma Guan leave that note, he truly hadn’t expected Lou Yuxue to be so earnest.","She was actually running this wonton shop at the academy’s entrance with all her heart and soul, and it was becoming more and more successful.","If Chen Yi hadn’t seen what Lou Yuxue was like back in South City’s Yanhua Lane, he would never have been able to connect the woman before him with that bewitching beauty.","Suppressing his laughter with great difficulty, he thought for a moment before striding openly into the wonton shop.","He scanned the room, found a seat in a corner, and sat down. Mimicking the other customers, he called out with a smile:","\"Lady Boss, a bowl of wontons, three liang of lamb, and a pot of wine!\"","Two diners next to him looked up in surprise, as if wondering who could possibly eat so much.","Over at the counter, Lou Yuxue, who was still working the abacus, was even more direct. She cursed in a gruff voice, \"Are you the reincarnation of a starving ghost? Who eats that much?\"","This caused the diners in the shop to erupt in laughter.","\"Lady Boss, it’s not like he isn’t paying. Why are you cursing him?\"","\"Just eat your food. Was I talking to you?\"","\"Lady Boss, if you act like this, who’s going to dare come back next time?\"","\"I’d be thrilled if none of you came! This life is just...\"","Lou Yuxue was about to continue her tirade when she suddenly saw the face of Chen Yi as he lifted his raincoat. She froze.","\"You...\"","Seeing that she recognized him, Chen Yi smiled and waved, silently mouthing the words, \"Hi, we meet again, Miss Yuxue.\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyes instantly became bloodshot, and she almost couldn’t stop herself from drawing a blade and charging over to hack that bastard to death.","Fortunately, she was still aware that many people around her were watching.","So she forced herself to suppress the rage in her heart and squeezed out a smile on her disguised, ordinary-looking face.","\"Esteemed customer, you’ve ordered quite a lot. You are truly an honored guest. Why don’t you... why don’t you dine upstairs?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle. He teased, \"Lady Boss, I can certainly go upstairs. It’s just...\"","\"It’s just that you should first make it clear: are you bringing me the wontons, or am *I* the wonton?\"","\"You’re not planning to eat me, are you?\"","The crowd was stunned for a moment at his words. When they understood, their laughter became even more unrestrained, with a few even slapping their tables.","\"Right, right, this brother is correct.\"","\"Lady Boss, you couldn’t have seen how handsome this brother is and decided to eat him up like a wonton, could you?\""]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330 - 227: Hi, Miss Yuxue","paragraphs":["\"Haha... If that’s the kind of business you’re talking about, I’d advise you to stay downstairs for your meal, friend. Give the rest of us a show.\"","Lou Yuxue ignored the teasing from the surrounding diners. She just glared at Chen Yi, gritting her teeth. \"Are you going or not?\"","Chen Yi immediately stood up. \"Alright, I’ll go. Satisfied?\"","\"The proprietress is so... beautiful as a flower. Even if she were to eat me alive, I’d secretly be overjoyed.\"","The crowd naturally burst into laughter again, catcalling that he should make a lot of noise while he was being \"eaten,\" just to liven things up for them.","Chen Yi smiled and cupped his fists, accepting their jests. He then gave Lou Yuxue a wink and headed up to the second floor.","Lou Yuxue glared resentfully at his back. She snapped, \"Bigfoot, watch the shop!\" before picking up the wontons, lamb, and beef Chen Yi had ordered and following him.","Naturally, this earned her a few more taunts from the diners.","It provoked Lou Yuxue so much she almost threw the wontons downstairs.","Fortunately, just then, she spotted where Chen Yi was. She held up the wontons and asked with a cold smile, \"Are you going to eat the wontons, or are you going to eat me?\"","Chen Yi pointed downstairs, then to a private room to the side. \"You choose,\" he said leisurely.","Lou Yuxue knew he meant she could either throw the food downstairs or go into the room with him. She instantly flushed red with anger, a blush so deep even her disguise-mask couldn’t hide it.","\"Follow me!\"","With that, she turned and walked towards a private room further in.","Watching her back, Chen Yi chuckled twice before following.","「The moment the door closed.」","Chen Yi sensed the rush of air behind his head. He dodged to the side, catching a glimpse of a small fist out of the corner of his eye. He smoothly reached out, grabbed it, and pulled.","SLAM.","He pinned Lou Yuxue’s entire body against the door.","\"Long time no see, Miss Yuxue. Still as fiery as ever.\"","Lou Yuxue struggled a couple of times, but finding she couldn’t break free, she turned her head to glare at him, spitting through gritted teeth, \"You bastard, you actually dare to show your face to me again? Aren’t you afraid I’ll kill you?\"","Chen Yi met her gaze and said with a smile, \"Not at all.\"","\"Miss Yuxue is such a gentle and generous person. After gifting me hundreds of thousands of silver, why would she kill me?\"","\"You scoundrel! Shameless!\"","\"It was you, you bastard, who broke your word! You despicably stole that silver! How dare you... How dare you...\"","Lou Yuxue thought of the silver Chen Yi had taken, thought of the demanding letters from Hawk, and her heart filled with rage and resentment.","\"Give me back my silver!\"","\"Give you back your silver?\"","Chen Yi pretended to think. \"It’s not impossible.\"","Lou Yuxue’s anger faltered. \"Really?\"","\"But I’m not giving it back. Instead, I want to partner with you on a very big deal.\"","\"Once it’s done, I guarantee you’ll earn a huge amount of silver.\"","\"You... Don’t even think about it!\"","Lou Yuxue started struggling again. \"You have no Jianghu ethics, and even less business integrity! I’ll die before I ever partner with you!\"","\"Don’t be so quick to refuse. Why not hear my plan first?\"","\"Fine. Let me go first.\"","Chen Yi took the opportunity to release her, taking a step back. \"Don’t try anything else,\" he warned. \"You know you’re no match for me.\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue gritted her teeth and lowered her hand. She huffed angrily, walking around him to sit at the table, her eyes filled with indignant fury.","Seeing her sit down, Chen Yi stopped teasing her. He sat down opposite her and started eating the wontons and lamb himself.","After swallowing a bite, he gave a thumbs-up. \"I have to say, this is actually really good. No wonder Miss Yuxue’s shop is doing so well.\"","Who knew that hearing his praise would only make Lou Yuxue angrier? She slammed her hand on the table.","\"If you’re going to eat, then eat! What’s with all the chatter?\"","\"And another thing, do you think I *want* to be running a shop here? Do you think I *want* this place to be successful?\"","\"If it weren’t for you, because you took that silver, would I... would I be reduced to this?\"","\"So after all that, you really are running this wonton shop with all your heart just to earn silver.\"","He paused, then asked curiously, \"So how much silver have you earned these past few days?\"","Lou Yuxue was about to answer, but then she remembered his usual roguish behavior and said warily:","\"However much I’ve earned is none of your business. Don’t even think about getting any ideas.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, shaking his head. \"A gentleman loves wealth, but he obtains it through the Dao. I only like to take what I deserve.\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyes widened. \"How do you have the face to say something like that?\"","\"Of the two hundred ninety thousand silver from before, one hundred forty thousand of it was mine.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi’s expression turned serious. \"No. It’s mine now.\"","\"If it weren’t for your one hundred forty thousand silver, why would I have thought of you first for this great deal?\"","In other words, how could they have met again if not for the debt between them?","Unfortunately, Lou Yuxue clearly didn’t understand such subtleties. She just held out a fair, delicate hand and huffed:","\"If you want me to partner with you, fine. Give me back my silver.\"","\"It’s gone. As I just said, that silver is the capital for this new deal.\"","\"You can’t start a joint venture without putting up capital, right?\"","\"You... that’s twisted logic! You... you bastard...\"","\"Get out! I... I don’t want to see you!\"","Chen Yi continued eating his wontons, unconcerned. \"Is Miss Yuxue sure she doesn’t want in on this?\" he asked with a smile.","\"If this deal goes well, the profits will be much, much greater than last time.\"","Lou Yuxue turned her face away, refusing to look at him. \"That’s only if you can actually get your hands on it,\" she huffed.","\"Partnering with you, not only would I get nothing, but I’d also attract a mountain of trouble. The loss would far outweigh the gain.\"","\"This time is different. I guarantee you’ll make a huge profit.\"","\"How much?\"","\"What?\"","\"How much silver can I earn?\"","Seeing him look over, Lou Yuxue explained, a little lacking in confidence:","\"I never said I’d partner with you. I’m just asking. It’s fine if you don’t want to tell me.\"","Chen Yi knew she was still on guard because of what happened last time. He smiled and held up five fingers.","\"Five hundred thousand silver.\""]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331 - 227: Hi, Miss Yuxue","paragraphs":["\"It’s all mine?\"","\"Of course.\"","Lou Yuxue was tempted, but she couldn’t bring herself to cooperate with Chen Yi.","\"You aren’t planning to earn five hundred thousand silver, then just fob me off with fifty thousand, are you?\"","’Heh, she’s getting smarter.’","Chen Yi was amused, but his words were utterly sincere. \"I guarantee you’ll get your five hundred thousand silver.\"","\"What about you? How much will you make?\"","\"Me? I should be able to make around eight hundred thousand to a million.\"","\"A mill—\"","Lou Yuxue tilted her head to look at him, astonished. \"What kind of big deal earns that much?\"","Chen Yi finished his wontons, wiped the corner of his mouth, and smiled. \"I’ll take that as you agreeing to team up with me.\"","Lou Yuxue froze, then suddenly gritted her teeth.","\"If you dare trick me again, I’ll have my superiors send an expert to kill you!\"","\"Miss Yuxue, now you’ve got the right idea.\"","\"As they say, even if we can’t be friends, we can still do business. Don’t turn your nose up at money.\"","\"Cut the crap. Tell me what this big deal is.\"","But Chen Yi just shook his head and said mysteriously, \"The time isn’t right. Let me plot it out first, and I’ll tell you when I’m ready.\"","Lou Yuxue glared at him and huffed, \"Who are you planning to scheme against this time?\"","\"It’s not the Jing State Liu Family again, is it? They brought a lot of silver with them to expand Xinglin Hall.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"No. As ruthless as I am, I wouldn’t target my own people.\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but curse him silently.","’That bastard. Everything he does is clearly for the Xiao Family’s benefit, yet he’s really acting like he’s one of the Liu family.’","With great effort, she suppressed her anger and said stiffly:","\"There aren’t many people in Shu State who can produce that much silver. You could count them on two hands, at most.\"","\"Even if you don’t tell me, I have my ways of finding out.\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"If you can find them, then more power to you.\"","He didn’t even know who was in the Anti-Xiao Alliance himself; he would be thrilled if Lou Yuxue helped him find them.","But he had already decided to make a move and deal with those people, so he would naturally investigate them thoroughly later.","As for whether he could actually earn that much money in the end...","He wasn’t too concerned.","The priority was to get the White Tiger Guard on his crooked ship first.","Just as Lou Yuxue was about to press him further, a flapping sound reached her ears. Outside the window, a goshawk was pecking at the paper pane.","Her expression changed. She stood up and hurried Chen Yi. \"Since you haven’t finished planning, we’ll talk after you have.\"","Chen Yi glanced over. He knew it was a secret letter from the Hidden Guard, and his eyes darted back and forth.","Then, before Lou Yuxue could react, he snatched the goshawk and deftly removed the secret letter from its leg.","\"Don’t you—\"","Before Lou Yuxue could stop him, Chen Yi had already opened the letter and was reading it quickly.","As he read, he muttered, \"B-23, A-16... Miss Yuxue, this must be your White Tiger Guard’s secret letter, right?\"","\"Why is it all just a bunch of gibberish?\"","Lou Yuxue strode forward, snatched the letter back, and glared at him with a cold expression.","\"Do you have any idea that spying on a White Tiger Guard secret letter is a capital offense?\"","Chen Yi silently memorized the contents of the letter. He didn’t try to snatch it back, just waved his hand with a smile.","\"You are the Court’s Hidden Guard. How could a little nobody like me dare to offend you?\"","\"But there’s no need to be so angry. I couldn’t make heads or tails of those scribbles anyway.\"","After all, he had already gotten what he wanted—","[Witnessed a Hidden Guard receiving a secret letter. Reward: Zither Score \"Spring Clear,\" Opportunity +34.]","[Evaluation: You arrived at the scene, heard the signal, and witnessed the event. You obtained the secret letter right under a Hidden Guard’s nose. Performance: Passable.]","Lou Yuxue stared at him for a long moment before huffing, \"Don’t do things that will get you killed. Otherwise, you will definitely regret it one day!\"","\"Yes, yes...\"","Before the words were even out of his mouth, Chen Yi’s gaze shot to the window. He instantly suppressed his presence and whispered in a low voice:","\"Someone’s coming!\""]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332 - 228: The Pavilion Master: What Kind of Personage?","paragraphs":["The visitor’s aura was unfamiliar.","Chen Yi offered a word of warning before silently slipping out of the room.","Lou Yuxue watched him leave with suspicion. She tilted her head and listened for a moment but heard nothing.","Just as she was about to speak, she suddenly heard a voice laced with amusement right by her ear:","\"Lady Tiger, this wonton shop of yours is doing pretty well.\"","Lou Yuxue froze and turned to look out the window.","She saw a plain-looking, middle-aged man in a raincoat ducking through the window.","\"Sir?\"","Lou Yuxue recognized the man and immediately dropped to one knee.","\"This is Lady Tiger. I was unaware of your arrival, Lord General. Please forgive me.\"","The middle-aged man known as \"General\" waved a dismissive hand. He took off his raincoat, revealing the roughspun clothes beneath, and spoke in a relaxed, deliberate tone:","\"There’s no blame for the unknowing. Rise.\"","\"Yes.\"","As Lou Yuxue got to her feet, she glanced toward the door, anxiously wondering if Chen Yi had actually left.","She knew just how formidable Lord General was.","If Chen Yi hadn’t left and was discovered eavesdropping nearby, she would be implicated as well.","As it turned out, Lou Yuxue knew Chen Yi all too well.","Chen Yi hadn’t left at all. He was hiding on the rafters in the adjacent private room, just one wall away.","’General? Lord?’","’So, this person is the superior to Lou Yuxue and the others.’","’A Golden Banner Officer?’","A smile touched Chen Yi’s lips. ’What a coincidence.’","Maybe he’d learn why these Hidden Guards were hiding in Shu State, stirring up trouble.","Before long, he heard their voices again.","General sat at the table and glanced at the leftovers before turning to Lou Yuxue to ask,","\"Has the secret letter from the Capital Prefecture arrived?\"","Lou Yuxue was visibly taken aback. \"Sir, a secret letter did just arrive, but I haven’t had a chance to look at it.\"","\"But... the Capital Prefecture? Forgive me, Sir, but I have never overstepped my authority to contact the Capital Prefecture privately.\"","\"Don’t be so tense. When I reported to the Pavilion Master, I asked them to send the letter here.\"","General finished speaking and held out his hand. \"Give it to me.\"","Lou Yuxue quickly placed the letter in his hand. \"Sir, should I withdraw for now?\"","’If she stayed, even if she didn’t learn the letter’s contents, she would still have to converse with General.’","’And if Chen Yi hadn’t left, the Hidden Guards’ affairs would be exposed.’","But General said casually, \"Stay. I have a few things to ask you.\"","Lou Yuxue didn’t dare hesitate, lowering her head and murmuring, \"Yes.\" A complicated look flickered in her eyes.","’That bastard... of all the times he could have shown up, it had to be just as Lord General arrived.’","’And what’s the deal with his cultivation?’","’How could he have sensed the General’s arrival before the General detected him?’","General, of course, was unaware of Lou Yuxue’s thoughts. He looked at the letter in his hand and asked,","\"The Pavilion Master is aware that Fledgling went to the Quchi Painting Boat that night, but he wants you to continue the investigation.\"","\"First, verify whether Fledgling actually met with the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall that night.\"","\"Second, he wants you to test Fledgling’s Martial Arts Cultivation.\"","Lou Yuxue was taken aback. \"The Pavilion Master still suspects Fledgling was involved in what happened that night?\"","General paused. Without looking up, he said, \"Perhaps.\"","\"Even I don’t believe Fledgling could have been involved, but since the Pavilion Master has given the order, you are to follow it.\"","\"Best not to have any slip-ups later and displease him.\"","Just as Lou Yuxue was about to assent, she suddenly remembered something. \"There is one small thing.\"","\"On the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival, Fledgling was seen on the Quchi. It’s suspected he was being held hostage as he left the Prefecture City on a painted boat.\"","\"What does that have to do with the burning of the summer grain in the Three Towns?\"","\"I learned afterward that there were signs of a battle outside Shu State City. It’s suspected that ’Liu Wu’ from Iron Wall Town and Liu Lang were involved.\"","\"Based on the timing, Fledgling couldn’t have been far from there.\"","General looked up slightly and mused, \"So you’re saying Fledgling is connected to Liu Lang and ’Liu Wu’?\"","\"Perhaps.\"","\"Investigate it thoroughly and report your findings to the Pavilion Master.\"","\"Yes...\"","Eavesdropping on their conversation, Chen Yi was also a bit stunned.","Chen Yi racked his brain.","’On the night the summer grain in the Three Towns was burned, the only slip-up I made was not being at the Spring Lotus Garden.’","’But it was a flaw that even Xiao Jinghong and Elder Master Xiao hadn’t noticed.’","’Yet the White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master, thousands of miles away, had caught on and intended to dig deeper...’","’Who in the world is this White Tiger Guard Pavilion Master?’","’How could he suspect me based on such a minor discrepancy?’","This was the second time Chen Yi had heard the title \"Pavilion Master.\"","The last time, that same \"Pavilion Master\" had accurately deduced that Xiao Dongchen, the \"Gray Wolf,\" was no longer useful and ordered Lady Tiger and Hawk to eliminate him after the incident with the Three Towns’ summer grain.","At the time, Chen Yi’s thoughts had been the same as they were now.","He had marveled at the Pavilion Master’s meticulous mind and been astonished by his acuity.","Truly an extraordinary individual.","’And then there was Lou Yuxue. Of all the damned luck, she had to go and connect the dots to what happened outside Shu State City.’","’Unbelievable...’","Just then, General asked, \"How is Simurgh Phoenix?\"","Lou Yuxue thought for a moment. \"She recently opened a tavern over in the West Market.\"","\"Aside from that, she spends nearly all her time with the Imperial Top Scholar. They even attended the Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala at Guiyun Academy together.\"","\"And the Liu Family?\"","\"On the day of the Mid-Autumn Festival, an imperial edict arrived from the Capital Prefecture reprimanding Old Marquis Xiao and Governor Liu Hong. Since then, the Liu Family has been much more subdued.\"","\"Liu Hong is occupied with transporting the grain tax to the Capital Prefecture and dealing with the Annual and Imperial Examinations. Liu Zhaoxue has returned to Jing State.\"","General nodded slightly, asking no more questions. He set down the secret letter, his gaze falling upon her as he said with a smile,"]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333 - 228: Pavilion Master, Who on Earth Is He?","paragraphs":["\"You’ve had a tough time lately.\"","\"Gray Wolf is dead, Hawk has fled to Guangyuan County, and Simurgh Phoenix defies orders. Three of Shu State’s four Silver Banner Officers are gone. I imagine it’s been hard on you.\"","Lou Yuxue lowered her head slightly. \"As a member of the White Tiger Guard, it is my duty to endure such hardships.\"","\"It’s not your place to say whether it’s your duty, nor is it mine. Only the Pavilion Master can make that decision.\"","\"The Pavilion Master has issued an order. Once you’ve thoroughly investigated the Bright Moon Building’s background, you will be promoted to Golden Banner Officer.\"","Lou Yuxue was stunned for a moment by the General’s words. When she recovered, she quickly bowed and said,","\"I thank you, Lord General, and I thank the Pavilion Master.\"","The General waved his hand, gesturing for her to sit while he continued,","\"But first, before you become a Golden Banner Officer, I need you to help me wrap things up in Shu State.\"","Lou Yuxue acknowledged and sat down beside him.","The General glanced at her, his expression turning serious. \"Enough pleasantries. Let’s get down to business.\"","His tone grew earnest as he asked, \"What’s the status of our contact with King Landu?\"","Lou Yuxue was reluctant to answer. ’But it’s too late now.’ She stopped worrying about whether Chen Yi had overheard them.","\"I followed your instructions and made contact with one of King Landu’s men the day before yesterday.\"","\"Given the time it takes, we should expect a reply in a few days.\"","The General thought for a moment before asking, \"Do you know where this contact of ours is hiding? Or what his identity is?\"","Lou Yuxue hesitated. \"I do not.\"","\"However, I do know that he’s from Poshisu Country.\"","\"He did his best to conceal it, but his accent is still subtly different from that of the Central Plains.\"","\"Someone from Poshisu Country...\"","\"Heh, that’s King Landu’s style, all right. Bold but meticulous, daring to do what others wouldn’t.\"","A smile touched the General’s face as he spoke. \"In that case, I’ll wait here for a few days.\"","\"There’s plenty to do in Shu State Prefecture City anyway. I can lend you a hand.\"","Lou Yuxue said quickly, \"I wouldn’t dare trouble you, My Lord.\"","\"It’s no trouble...\"","Meanwhile, Chen Yi listened in on their conversation, a few questions surfacing in his mind.","’Who is King Landu?’","’People from Poshisu Country?’","’Why are the White Tiger Guard contacting people from Poshisu Country?’","Before Chen Yi could ponder it further, he heard the Golden Banner Officer known as General speak.","\"I’ll be staying in the West Market for the time being. If you need me, you can find me there.\"","Lou Yuxue was taken aback. \"My Lord, you aren’t staying here?\"","The General pointed downward. \"Business is a little too good here. It’s never quiet, even at night. I’m afraid it’ll be too noisy for me.\"","\"My apologies, My Lord...\"","Before Lou Yuxue could finish, the General smiled and shook his head. He threw on his raincoat, said, \"I’m off,\" and leaped from the window, vanishing into the downpour.","Lou Yuxue bowed and simply watched him go in silence.","Meanwhile, Chen Yi quietly watched the General’s retreating figure, slowly deactivating the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique.","Only when he was certain the General was long gone did he let out a long breath. \"General...\"","Even though he’d only caught bits and pieces of their conversation, he was stunned by the sheer volume of information they contained.","The Fledgling—that was him.","The Pavilion Master, the Jing State Liu Family, Simurgh Phoenix, King Landu, Poshisu Country...","Some he knew of, some he didn’t.","But piecing it all together, he was still shaken by the sheer scale of an organization like the White Tiger Guard.","This was the Great Wei Dynasty’s White Tiger Guard, after all.","Just then, Lou Yuxue pushed open the door and scanned the room.","When she saw no one was there, her expression relaxed. ’He left early? That’s good...’","But the words had barely left her lips when Chen Yi, who had just processed what she said, poked his head out from the rafters. \"Looking for me?\"","Lou Yuxue started, looking up. Her eyes narrowed dangerously. \"You actually dared to eavesdrop on a secret meeting of the Hidden Guard?!\"","Chen Yi scoffed, leaping down from the rafters. \"You think I wanted to listen? It was just a coincidence.\"","\"Besides, you were being so cryptic. All that talk about ’Fledglings’ and ’Simurgh Phoenixes’—who knows what any of it meant?\"","Lou Yuxue was about to breathe a sigh of relief when Chen Yi continued,","\"But I am sure of one thing. You and that ’lord’ of yours were just speculating that I’m connected to this ’Fledgling’ person.\"","\"You...\"","\"Don’t deny it. I did kill some people with Liu Lang on the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival, but they weren’t your average Jianghu People. They were practitioners of the Evil Demonic Dao from the Five Poison Sect.\"","Lou Yuxue was taken aback. \"The Five Poison Sect?\"","Seeing that he had successfully diverted her attention, Chen Yi continued, \"The very same Five Poison Sect that has a blood feud with the Mountain Race, of course.\"","\"I don’t know where they’ve been hiding all these years to be able to make a comeback. And to think they’d even dare show their faces in Shu State.\"","\"But since I happened to run into them, I had no choice but to kill them.\"","Lou Yuxue eyed him suspiciously. After a moment of thought, she asked, \"So it was the Five Poison Sect who captured Granny Shan’s granddaughter and Chen Yi that night?\"","Chen Yi inwardly raised an eyebrow, but his voice was full of feigned confusion. \"Chen Yi, you mean Chen Qingzhou? And Granny Shan’s granddaughter?\"","\"You’re saying you didn’t kill those people to save them?\"","But before Lou Yuxue could respond, a smile spread across Chen Yi’s face.","\"Now that you mention it, I think I know who this ’Fledgling’ is.\"","Lou Yuxue’s expression faltered. \"You... You’re not the one who saved them?\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"If they had truly fallen into the hands of the Five Poison Sect, Miss Yuxue, who do you think could possibly have saved them?\"","\"The Five Poison Sect and the Mountain Race share a blood feud. If they had found Granny Shan’s granddaughter, they would have killed her on the spot. Why would they have spared her?\"","\"Besides, I heard about what happened that night.\"","\"That Mr. Qingzhou supposedly wrote a poem, ’Song of the Water Melody: Mid-Autumn,’ on the Quchi. Do you really think members of the Five Poison Sect have that kind of leisurely, refined taste?\"","Lou Yuxue mulled it over for a moment. In her heart, she was already starting to believe him.","’Based on my knowledge of those practitioners of the Evil Demonic Dao from the Five Poison Sect, if they’d really gotten their hands on Pei Guanli, they definitely would have killed her.’"]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334 - 228: Pavilion Master, Just Who Are You?","paragraphs":["’Then there’s Fledgling—Chen Yi. The Five Poison Sect has no grudge against Chen Yi, so it’s impossible that they’d go and capture him to make him write some poetry.","So I must have gotten it wrong...","But that bastard Liu Wu already knows Fledgling’s identity...","And given his relationship with the Xiao Family, he might even warn Fledgling later...’","At this thought, Lou Yuxue grew annoyed and asked, \"What exactly is your relationship with the Xiao Family?\"","Chen Yi knew she believed him and breathed a small sigh of relief. Instead of answering, he countered, \"Then why don’t you tell me who King Landu is?\"","Lou Yuxue became furious and couldn’t stop herself from slapping him. \"Speak, or else I... I’ll go find the Lord General right now.\"","Chen Yi took the slap, but a slight smile appeared on his face.","\"Miss Yuxue, this is my biggest secret. How could I possibly tell you so easily?\"","\"But I can guarantee one thing: my connection to the Xiao Family isn’t extensive. I’ve only had contact with a few of them.\"","’That’s right.’","’He was only on good terms with Xiao Jinghong, Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wuge, Elder Master Xiao, and Xiaodie.’","Lou Yuxue stared at him and snorted coldly. \"Why aren’t you saying you’re one of the Liu family now?\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"I did say that. You just didn’t believe me.\"","\"I don’t believe you now either. If you’re really one of the Xiao family, why do neither Elder Master Xiao nor Xiao Jinghong know you exist?\"","\"Oh? You even know that?\"","\"Hmph!\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi’s mind raced, and he spun a lie, \"The Xiao Family isn’t in a good situation right now. I didn’t originally want to intervene.\"","\"But my old master once received a favor from the Xiao Family, so I had no choice but to do a few things to help them out.\"","After listening, Lou Yuxue was somewhat convinced.","This explanation fit the situation in Shu State and would also explain why the Xiao Family didn’t know of \"Liu Wu’s\" existence.","After a moment of silence,","she continued, \"That big business deal you mentioned before, was that also to help the Xiao Family?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment and said, \"Yes and no.\"","The words had barely left his mouth when he saw that Lou Yuxue wanted to get to the bottom of it, so he decided to say a little more.","\"Since it has come to this, I won’t hide it from you anymore.\"","\"Do you know why the Five Poison Sect has appeared in Shu State?\"","\"Speak.\"","\"Because of the Liu Family. To be precise, because of Liu Zhaoxue.\"","Lou Yuxue had a sudden realization. \"You discovered the Five Poison Sect while undercover in the Liu Family?\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"The Jing State Liu Family has overreached. How many people in Shu State can stand the sight of them?\"","\"Plus, they’ve joined forces with an Evil Demonic Dao like the Five Poison Sect. Dealing with them can be considered ridding the people of a menace.\"","\"As for whether it helps the Xiao Family, I suppose it does. But this time, I won’t be stupid enough to just give the silver away.\"","He paused, a look of bitter resentment on his face. \"You have no idea what I was going through back then...\"","Lou Yuxue shot him a glance and snorted, \"Oh, I know.\"","\"It’s the same feeling you had when you stole the one hundred forty thousand silver that belonged to me!\"","\"...Don’t worry. I promise I’ll let you make a fortune this time.\"","\"You’d better!\"","\"So, can you tell me now? Why are you investigating Fledgling? And who is King Landu?\"","\"Stop prying!\"","\"For your own safety, I advise you not to meddle in the affairs of my White Tiger Guard!\"","\"If the Pavilion Master and the Lord General find out, you will surely die!\"","\"Er, can I take that to mean you’re worried about me?\"","\"Ah, you... Who—who’s worried about you, you bastard?!\"","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi bid farewell to Lou Yuxue and returned to the Xiao Family residence under the cover of night.","After much persuasion, he had finally managed to dispel Lou Yuxue’s suspicions.","But he knew that the key to clearing his name of being \"Fledgling\" and burning the Three Towns’ summer grain lay not with Lou Yuxue, but with that mysterious Pavilion Master.","Amidst the drizzling rain,","Chen Yi looked up at the cloud-covered night sky, a thoughtful expression on his face.","\"Looks like I’ll have to put on a big show...\""]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335 - 229: Brother-in-law, You’re Good at Painting, Right?","paragraphs":["Thoughts were just thoughts.","Chen Yi wasn’t too worried, though.","After all, he had overheard a great deal from the conversation between the General and Lou Yuxue that night.","All in all, he could deduce a few things and make preparations in advance.","It was just as he had always believed—known threats were not frightening. What was truly terrifying were the unknown troubles and schemes.","The unexpected attack by the Five Poison Sect, for instance, had left him in a rather difficult position.","But as he mulled things over on the way back to the Xiao Family residence, Chen Yi’s brow furrowed slightly.","’A Golden Banner Officer of the Hidden Guard has come to Shu State and is secretly in contact with someone who seems to be King Landu of Poshisu Country. They’re obviously plotting something big.’","’I’m afraid my plans will need some adjustments.’","’Fortunately, these three developments have surfaced relatively early...’","Three major shifts in one day. It made Chen Yi feel his luck was actually pretty good.","’The old master’s efforts to purchase grain for the Three Towns were obstructed. I can deduce this is the work of those \"Financiers\" hiding in the shadows.’","’The Hidden Guard wants to test me. I’ll have to find a way to completely dispel that Pavilion Master’s suspicions.’","’And finally, the General’s purpose for coming to Shu State...’","’Tsk. What a mess.’","Muttering to himself, Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden. He changed into a clean set of clothes, then went to his study and brewed a cup of hot tea to warm up.","He pondered for a long time.","Eventually, his expression eased considerably.","’Then there’s the Jing State Liu Family and the Five Poison Sect... It’s messy, to be sure, but it’s not an impossible situation to resolve.’","Chen Yi was well aware.","The more chaotic the situation, the more crucial it was to unravel it thread by thread. So long as he could sort out the key points, he would have a fighting chance.","Especially now, while he was operating alone, he absolutely could not afford to make a reckless move and tip off his enemies.","This was the only way he could resolve these problems quietly.","’When it comes down to it, I have to deal with the Jing State Liu Family first.’","The Liu Family was like a boulder blocking the Xiao Family’s path. Behind them hid countless people with ulterior motives, making it impossible to see the full picture, yet demanding constant vigilance.","Conversely, by dealing with the Liu Family, he could make an example of them to intimidate others, causing the so-called \"Financiers\" and anyone in Shu State with designs on the Xiao Family to have second thoughts.","Chen Yi watched the rain fall outside his window, a slight smile appearing on his face. ’You could say I’m trying to take the enemy general’s head from amidst a chaotic battlefield.’","’Xiao Jinghong, if you ever find out what your husband has done, please go easy on me.’","After watching for a moment longer, Chen Yi tidied up the study, then stood and returned to his room.","Just as he was about to sit cross-legged to begin his cultivation, a line of large, golden text floated before his eyes:","[Daily Intelligence · Yellow-level Top Grade: At the seventh mark of the Dog’s Hour, barbarian slaves will riot at the East Market Grain Store. A minuscule amount of Opportunity may be obtained.]","Chen Yi glanced at the text, taken aback.","’A barbarian slave riot?’","That was certainly a rare event.","He was, of course, familiar with the origins of the barbarian slaves—most were captured by horse bandits from Poshisu Country and sold in the Shu State region.","Their buyers were mostly Noble Families, who used them for plowing fields, farming, and other forms of hard labor.","Chen Yi recalled hearing about barbarian slave riots a few times before.","Apparently, every riot resulted in casualties.","But he had never seen one himself.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi closed his eyes and began his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","’Yellow Level is still a level, I suppose. I might as well go see what a barbarian slave riot looks like. It’ll be an eye-opener, at least.’","’And it’s at the East Market Grain Store, of all places...’","...","「The next morning.」","The overcast sky above Shu State had cleared considerably.","A gentle rain fell.","Xiao Wuge was up unusually early. He had already climbed out of bed before Xiaodie even came to knock.","He dressed and washed up.","When Xiaodie arrived with a basin of hot water, Xiao Wuge was already dressed, though his hair was still down and disheveled.","He ran a hand through his somewhat messy black hair and said sheepishly, \"Sister Xiaodie, I don’t know how to do my hair.\"","Xiaodie put down the basin, said, \"Pardon me, Young Master,\" and quickly went to have him sit down and comb his long hair for him.","In this era, men and women alike had long hair.","The only difference was the hairstyle.","A man’s hairstyle would differ based on his status and age.","For someone like Xiao Wuge, the Heir of the Marquis Mansion who had not yet come of age, his hair only needed to be neatly combed and tied with a Brocade Belt.","So Xiaodie quickly combed his hair neatly, helped him straighten his clothes, and said with a smile,","\"Are you up so early because you’re going to the Martial Arts Arena, Young Master?\"","Xiao Wuge chuckled. \"Nothing gets past you, Sister Xiaodie.\"","He had originally been somewhat resistant to Martial Arts practice, but after yesterday’s Cultivation and Chen Yi’s encouragement in the evening, his interest had grown significantly.","It was tiring, to be sure, but after thinking it over, he decided that practicing Martial Arts was better than studying in Jiaxing Garden.","It was only because the Martial Arts Arena was a bit more lively.","Besides his second uncle, Xiao Xuanshuo, and the others, there were also some children from the branch families. In his free time between Cultivation sessions, Xiao Wuge could even play around with them for a bit.","Xiaodie, of course, had no idea what Xiao Wuge was thinking. All she knew was that his willingness to practice Martial Arts was something to be happy about.","\"As long as you enjoy it, Young Master.\"","\"This way, the Marquis, the Eldest Miss, the Second Miss, and Master Chen will all be happy for you.\"","Xiao Wuge hummed in agreement and looked up at her. \"Can I eat a bit more this morning?\"","Xiaodie agreed wholeheartedly, but as she led him downstairs, she said with a laugh, \"I’m afraid I can’t make that promise, Young Master.\"","\"Huh? Why not?\"","\"Sister Huatang came over first thing this morning to say that the Eldest Miss has prepared breakfast and wants you and Master Chen to join her.\"","The smile remained on Xiao Wuge’s face. \"Oh, I see.\"","\"Then I’ll just go find my big sister and ask her to prepare some more for me.\"","\"Don’t you worry, Young Master. The Eldest Miss gave the kitchen their instructions early this morning. They’ve made your favorite fried pancakes...\"","Hearing the conversation from downstairs, Chen Yi also got up, washed his face, and got dressed.","He was going to the academy today, so he had put on a blue robe with deep cyan embroidery on the cuffs and hem.","He looked clean and sharp, projecting the refined and elegant air of a true scholar."]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336 - 229: Brother-in-law, You’re Good at Painting, Right?","paragraphs":["He went downstairs.","Seeing Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge chatting with Pei Guanli, he walked out of the wooden building with them and asked, feigning ignorance, \"What are you all talking about?\"","Xiao Wuge looked up at him and chuckled. \"Brother-in-law, Sister Guanli is teaching me how to cultivate in the Martial Arts.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Chen Yi glanced at the Tiger Girl, his stare causing her to lower the head she had just proudly lifted.","\"Brother-in-law, I’ve been practicing Martial Arts for years. I’m more than capable of teaching little Xiao Wuge.\"","\"Alright, alright. I know you’re skilled in the Martial Arts. From now on, when I’m not around, you can teach Wuge more often.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Of course not. At best, you can be a living training dummy for Wuge.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli pouted. \"Brother-in-law, you’re looking down on me...\"","Chen Yi didn’t bother explaining. He just smiled, tapped her on her smooth forehead, and started walking toward Jiaxing Garden, pulling Xiao Wuge along.","As he walked, he looked back and laughed. \"How could I dare look down on you? Granny Shan would skin me alive.\"","Pei Guanli rubbed her forehead, her pout turning into a grin. She trotted over happily and grabbed his other arm. \"Ah Ma would never do that.\"","\"You never know...\"","A short while later, the group arrived at Jiaxing Garden under a light drizzle.","Xiao Wan’er was already waiting outside the gate. When she saw them, her gaze fell involuntarily on the Tiger Girl’s hand.","She didn’t say anything about propriety, merely looking at Chen Yi with her gentle, tranquil eyes and beckoning to him.","\"Brother-in-law, come quickly. Before you leave for the academy, Tingyun and Huatang have something to discuss with you.\"","Chen Yi acknowledged her, then swatted Pei Guanli’s clinging hand away. He let go of Xiao Wuge and quickened his pace, asking with a smile,","\"Has Wang Ji already met with Fairy Tingyun and the others?\"","\"Yes, Wang Ji showed our family a great deal of respect. He had all the disciples from the Celestial Sect settled in within half a day yesterday.\"","\"It’s just that Hundred Herbs Hall hasn’t expanded yet, so for now they’ll have to make do with staying in the communal dormitories.\"","As they spoke, they entered the living room and began to eat and chat.","Aside from Xiao Wan’er, Xie Tingyun gave the most detailed account, thanking Chen Yi profusely.","\"It’s all thanks to you, Young Master. Shopkeeper Wang said that out of respect for you, he is giving my junior brothers and sisters a special salary of ten taels of silver per month.\"","\"Those with higher Cultivation, like my sixth junior brother and seventh junior sister, will receive fifty taels of silver per month. And I heard there will be bonuses during the holidays.\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"It has little to do with me.\"","\"Shopkeeper Wang already knew the Celestial Sect is a renowned and righteous sect in the Jianghu. Your fellow disciples are quite skilled, so it’s only right that he wouldn’t be stingy with the silver coins.\"","That’s what he said, but most of the one hundred and twenty-seven disciples from the Celestial Sect had Lower Three Grades Cultivation. Normally, even five taels of silver a month would be considered generous.","It was entirely because of Chen Yi’s influence that Wang Ji offered a monthly wage of ten taels.","The fifty taels of silver coins that the few high-level disciples with Middle Three Grades Cultivation would receive was also a high price.","It was a generous amount, at least when compared to an expert of the Middle Three Grades like Liu Lang.","At this moment, Shen Huatang also offered her thanks. \"Young Master, it’s all thanks to your help that Senior Sister will avoid being punished according to the sect’s rules this time.\"","Chen Yi was taken aback. \"Punishment?\"","Before Shen Huatang could continue, Xie Tingyun rushed forward and covered her mouth, saying with a strained laugh, \"No, no, Junior Sister Huatang misspoke. What punishment?\"","The Celestial Sect was, after all, a major and reputable sect. They rarely took on roles as guards for others, with the exception of Noble Families like the Xiao Family, which had ties to the Celestial Sect itself.","This time, Xie Tingyun had secretly brought so many disciples with her, so she did indeed deserve to be punished according to the sect’s regulations.","But because Hundred Herbs Hall was paying so well, she estimated that the elders of the Celestial Sect wouldn’t be too angry.","Besides the traditions passed down by the Sect, disciples who practiced Martial Arts still needed to eat, drink, and live. They had to buy medicinal herbs, pills, and other items, all of which naturally required silver.","After a bit more small talk, the matter of the Celestial Sect disciples was considered settled.","Chen Yi recalled the news he had heard yesterday and looked at Xiao Wan’er. \"I heard the price of grain has gone up?\"","The smile on Xiao Wan’er’s face faded slightly. She nodded gently. \"It has indeed risen a bit.\"","\"However, a message came from Qingjing Residence this morning, telling me not to get involved and not to use the funds from the treasury. Grandfather is handling it.\"","\"He also told me to continue with the preparations for the Medical Dao Academy as planned.\"","’The Old Master really understands Xiao Wan’er,’ Chen Yi thought to himself.","’Just like me, he was worried that Xiao Wan’er would pawn her jewelry or postpone the Medical Dao Academy to raise money.’","After some thought, Chen Yi said, \"In a few more days, the silver from Hundred Herbs Hall’s profit-sharing will arrive. We should be able to spare some of the surplus then.\"","\"Also, if the Old Master needs it, I have plenty of silver here that can be used for emergencies.\"","A smile returned to Xiao Wan’er’s face, but she feigned a reproachful tone.","\"I know you have silver, but the amount of silver coins needed to buy grain is immense. How could we use yours?\"","\"Even if I agreed, Grandfather would never allow it.\"","\"We’ll see how it goes.\"","Chen Yi replied, not pressing the offer of money any further, making it seem like a mere polite gesture.","But he knew in his heart that the rising grain prices were a plot against the Xiao Family by outsiders.","If they spent extra silver according to their enemy’s calculations, there was no guarantee the other party wouldn’t press their advantage and raise the price again.","It would be best to resolve this through other means.","Nevertheless, Xiao Wan’er was very happy to hear Chen Yi say this.","’Brother-in-law is willing to share in the Xiao Family’s hardships, willing to offer his own silver,’ she thought. ’This means he truly sees this place as his home.’","’At the very least, she would no longer have to worry about Chen Yi trying to run away from the Xiao Family again.’","’Of course, she had stopped worrying about that a long time ago.’","At this thought, Xiao Wan’er said with a radiant smile, \"While you go to the academy to teach the Calligraphy Dao today, Brother-in-law, I’ll prepare some things at home.\"","\"First thing tomorrow morning, we’ll set off for the fiefdom outside the city.\"","\"If all goes well, we can make it back before nightfall tomorrow.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but tease, \"And if it doesn’t go well?\"","Xiao Wan’er shot him a charming glare and chided, \"If it doesn’t go well, then we’ll just spend the night there.\"","\"There’s a residence on the fiefdom, built back when Father and Mother were still alive.\"","\"When I was little, Mother would take us there to stay for a while every summer.\"","\"And in that residence, there’s a painting hanging in the study... a village artist painted it for me, my second sister, and our father and mother...\"","Perhaps because Xiao Fengchun had been gone for several years, or perhaps because of Chen Yi, there was much less sorrow in Xiao Wan’er’s expression when she spoke of her parents.","She smiled and rambled on, telling many stories from her childhood, bringing smiles to the faces of everyone listening.","Only Xiao Wuge looked conflicted. \"Sister, Brother-in-law, I want to go outside the city with you too.\"","Xiao Wan’er laughed and patted him. \"You’re not allowed.\"","\"Weren’t you just clamoring about going to the Martial Arts Arena every day to practice your Martial Arts Cultivation? Have you forgotten so soon?\"","\"But I want to go see the portrait of Father and Mother you mentioned.\"","Hearing this, the smile on Xiao Wan’er’s face faded a little, and her expression grew complicated.","After a moment of silence, she shook her head and said, \"I’ll bring the portrait back with me when I return.\"","Although Xiao Wuge was disappointed, he didn’t press the issue. \"Sister, it’s a promise, okay? Don’t forget.\"","Before Xiao Wan’er could agree, Chen Yi said with a smile, \"She won’t forget. I’ll remind your big sister.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed softly in agreement. \"I won’t forget.\"","Just then, Pei Guanli, her mouth greasy from eating, rolled her eyes and said to Chen Yi with a mischievous grin,","\"Brother-in-law, aren’t you also skilled in calligraphy and painting? Why don’t you paint something for us when you have the time?\"","This time, it was Chen Yi’s smile that vanished. He said irritably, \"Don’t worry. I’d paint for anyone before I’d paint for you.\"","He still hadn’t practiced the Painting Dao. If he were to actually pick up a brush, he figured it would be just like his previous attempt at the Zither Dao.","—An absolute eyesore.","Fortunately, he had obtained a calligraphy and painting scroll titled *Mid-Autumn River Map* on the night of the Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala.","When he had time, he would have to work on his Painting Dao to avoid another encounter with an idle person like Pei Guanli, who loved to bring up sore subjects.","Xiao Wuge, naturally unaware of Chen Yi’s little secret, said with a hopeful expression, \"Brother-in-law, paint one for me! When I’ve achieved success in my Martial Arts training.\"","As he spoke, he even started to coax Xiao Wan’er.","\"Big Sister should get one too, right? Have Brother-in-law paint one for you. It’ll definitely be beautiful.\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced at Chen Yi and said with some hesitation, \"Wouldn’t it be too much trouble?\"","Seeing how things were going, Chen Yi said helplessly, \"It’s not that much trouble, it just takes some time...\"","’That settles it,’ he thought. ’As soon as I get back from the academy, I’m going to start practicing the Painting Dao.’","’If he didn’t master all four arts of Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting soon, he was bound to face many more embarrassing situations in the future.’"]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337 - 230: The One Who Tied the Bell Must Untie It","paragraphs":["After breakfast, everyone went about their business.","Xiao Wuge followed Xiao Xuanshuo to the Martial Arts Arena to practice Martial Arts.","Xiaodie and Pei Guanli returned to Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wan’er, along with Juan’er and Cui’er, packed their bags in preparation for tomorrow’s trip to the fief outside the city.","Chen Yi, meanwhile, opened his Oil Paper Umbrella and went to the front courtyard.","This time, he chose not to go to Guiyun Academy alone. After greeting a few of the Armored Guards, he instructed Liu Si’er to prepare a carriage.","Liu Si’er swiftly brought the carriage over. Once Chen Yi was settled inside, he drove it straight toward Guiyun Academy.","\"Young Master-in-law, you haven’t used the carriage in a long time. Do you have other plans today?\"","Since Ge the Third had left, he had been paying close attention to the Fledgling’s movements and had a decent understanding of him.","Unless absolutely necessary, this Young Master-in-law rarely left the Marquis’s Mansion.","Even when he did go out, it was only to two places: Hundred Herbs Hall or Guiyun Academy.","Most of the time, however, he would go alone, and he rarely ever took the carriage.","Chen Yi lifted a corner of the curtain. He glanced outside as he replied:","\"I haven’t been to Jishi Medicine Hall in a while. I thought I’d go take a look today.\"","Liu Si’er didn’t suspect anything and said with a smile, \"It’s true, you haven’t been to the East Market for some time.\"","\"A few days ago, accountant Liu was just talking to me about you. He said that if you were to write a calligraphy piece for Jishi Medicine Hall, business would surely be even better than it is now.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, unable to stifle his amusement. \"He certainly has a sharp mind.\"","’A piece of calligraphy from a Calligraphy Dao master in the Perfection Realm would, at a time like this, have an effect comparable to an Imperial Court gazette.’","’One only had to look at the wonton shop that had acquired a piece by Ma Guan to understand.’","If Chen Yi really were to write a piece for Jishi Medicine Hall and it was widely advertised, the scholars alone would swarm the place until it was packed to the rafters.","Not to mention the common folk who loved a good spectacle.","Even if only one percent of them actually needed to buy medicinal herbs or herbal teas, Jishi Medicine Hall would still make a fortune.","Liu Si’er said with a laugh, \"According to accountant Liu, a fierce tiger has recently entered the pharmaceutical trade in Shu State and has been stealing a lot of business from the other Medicine Halls.\"","\"Does the Young Master-in-law know which fierce tiger he was talking about?\"","Chen Yi was naturally aware of Xinglin Hall. He also knew it wasn’t just the Xiao Family Medicine Hall and Hundred Herbs Hall that were affected, but he pretended not to know.","\"Why don’t you tell me, Brother Si.\"","\"It’s Xinglin Hall from Jing State! They’re an old establishment with a history of several hundred years. I hear they have several Medical Saint Hands.\"","\"I’ve heard that name. They’ve come to Shu State?\"","Chen Yi replied casually, his gaze falling upon the pedestrians coming and going along the street.","The autumn rain carried a slight chill.","Most people out and about at this time had switched to thicker clothes. Even the scholars, who prided themselves on their dashing style, had added an inner lining beneath their robes.","Only the Wandering Martial Artists, who roamed the lands, were dressed casually, carrying weapons on their backs, unafraid of the changing weather.","Liu Si’er kept his eyes peeled, watching his surroundings as he drove the carriage. \"Sometime after the Mid-Autumn Festival, I think. Xinglin Hall opened a few shops here in our Shu State.\"","\"Their arrival has impacted the business of our mansion’s Medicine Hall. I just wonder if the mansion has enough silver coins.\"","\"Oh? Silver coins?\"","\"Young Master-in-law, you haven’t heard? On the day of the Mid-Autumn Festival, the Marquis was punished by the Holy Emperor. Not only does he have to make up for the grain shortfall in Iron Wall Town, but he also has to pay the grain tax.\"","\"Originally, the three hundred thousand taels of silver the Marquis confiscated from Master Dongchen would have been enough to handle it. But who would have thought that the grain merchants in Shu State have all gone mad recently, more than doubling the price of grain.\"","\"The Marquis is having a real headache over this. Yesterday, he even had the Third Master make a trip to the Governor’s Office, hoping the Government Office would intervene and regulate the prices.\"","Chen Yi’s heart stirred. \"What did the Government Office have to say?\"","Liu Si’er’s tone was slightly displeased as he said, \"They dodged the issue, claiming the grain merchants had legitimate reasons for the price hike.\"","\"They said the harvest in Shu State was poor this year, that even the grain tax collected was less than sixty percent of previous years. So what could they do about the grain merchants?\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"Do you know which areas had poor harvests?\"","\"I don’t know the specifics. I just heard it mentioned once in the mansion...\"","Doubt grew in Chen Yi’s mind. ’Those people are deliberately plotting against the Xiao Family. They wouldn’t leave such an obvious flaw in their plan.’","’There must be a place in Shu State with a poor harvest, and there must be a place that paid less in grain tax.’","’As I recall, the day after the summer grain in the Three Towns was burned, these same grain merchants raised their prices once before, but they quickly lowered them again.’","’But... what if there isn’t any place in Shu State with reduced grain production?’","’In that case, I would have to re-evaluate the power of the force behind these grain merchants.’","’Besides the Inspectorate Office in the Capital Prefecture, which was the first to report the matter after rumors began to spread slandering Xiao Jinghong for stealing what he was meant to guard, they must also have people cooperating with them in the Governor’s Office.’","’Collusion between officials and merchants.’","’In that case, for them to go to all this trouble... it can’t be as simple as just causing problems for the Xiao Family.’","As Chen Yi considered this, a helpless little smile appeared on his face.","’If the Xiao Family were just a little more ruthless, if they truly acted like the local tyrants of Shu State, my life would be so much easier.’","’But then again... the very reason I’m trying so hard to help the Xiao Family is precisely because of their loyalty, integrity, and kindness.’","Before long, the carriage stopped outside the gates of Guiyun Academy.","Chen Yi instructed Liu Si’er to find a place to rest for a while, then opened his umbrella and walked into the academy.","Liu Si’er looked left and right, then parked the carriage outside There is a Wonton Shop by the Clouds and went inside by himself.","\"Waiter, a bowl of wontons.\"","Lou Yuxue, who was behind the counter, glanced at him. Recognizing who he was, her eyes couldn’t help but drift toward Guiyun Academy.","She knew, of course, that Liu Si’er had temporarily taken over for Ge the Third in watching the Fledgling, so she guessed the Fledgling had come to the academy today.","After a moment’s thought, she went up to the second floor, wrote a secret letter, and summoned a waiter with an instruction:","\"Get a message to the Iron Banner Officer.\"","\"Yes, ma’am.\"","After the waiter had left, Lou Yuxue looked down at Liu Si’er from the window, her expression thoughtful.","’The Pavilion Master sent a letter ordering another investigation into the Fledgling. To test him, it would be best to have the Iron Banner Officer on the Xiao Family’s side make a move.’"]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338 - 230: Let He Who Tied the Bell Untie It","paragraphs":["Lou Yuxue was currently swamped with matters, making it inconvenient for her to act personally.","Besides, she had an important mission to attend to. She had to complete the task assigned by the Golden Banner Officer first.","’Liu Si’er, and that Iron Banner Officer called Uncle Gui... they should have a way.’","...","Since the exhibition hall opened, the number of people coming and going within Guiyun Academy had increased significantly.","Even now, before the Hour of the Rabbit, many visitors were still arriving.","Some were local to Shu State, while others came from beyond its borders.","As a result, Chen Yi spent a full quarter of an hour just returning greetings on his way.","Many who saw him for the first time pointed and gossiped, repeating rumors they had heard.","\"Is that Mr. Qingzhou?\"","\"He looks so young.\"","\"I hear he’s only twenty. He’s certainly an incredible person.\"","\"It’s a shame he married into the Xiao Family. His prospects for an official career are hopeless.\"","\"It’s better this way. Because he’s here teaching the Calligraphy Dao, people like us have a chance to receive his guidance.\"","\"True...\"","Chen Yi pretended not to hear. After meeting with Ma Guan, he headed straight for the study hall.","Two hours passed quickly.","Inside the study hall, the atmosphere among the one hundred students, plus Chen Yi and Ma Guan, was even more relaxed than before.","For one, Chen Yi’s understanding of the Profound Mysteries of the Calligraphy Dao grew deeper by the day, allowing him to teach with ease.","For another, unlike other teachers, Chen Yi didn’t just dryly read from a textbook. He explained the Profound Mysteries of the Calligraphy Dao in the simplest terms.","However, the students had been practicing Wei Qing’s Style since childhood, and it was difficult for them to suddenly write characters based on their own nature and suited to their own Dao.","That was why after so much time, no one else had achieved Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao like Ma Guan had.","Fortunately, a few students had reached the entry-level in the Calligraphy Dao, which was enough to dispel any doubts about Chen Yi’s ability to teach it.","Among them was Tang Ye of the Tang Family.","Before the class ended, Chen Yi gave his customary critiques, saying:","\"Tang Ye’s characters are beginning to show their own flair. If you practice six hundred characters a day, you should reach the entry-level in the Calligraphy Dao within a month.\"","Tang Ye was delighted to hear this. He rose and bowed. \"Thank you, Sir.\"","Chen Yi nodded, gestured for him to sit, and said with a smile:","\"The Great Dao is simple at its core. For any Dao Realm, if you find the right direction, understand your true self, and achieve unity of knowledge and action, you can walk the great path.\"","\"This is true for the Calligraphy Dao, as it is for Zither, Go, Painting, and even the Martial Arts.\"","This might be difficult for an ordinary person to articulate clearly.","But coming from Chen Yi, who had mastered the Zither, Go, Calligraphy, the Medical Dao, and the Martial Arts, his words carried a certain weight.","However, the scholars in the study hall were mostly skeptical of his words.","After all, achieving success in a single Dao was already difficult. To divide one’s attention between two or three Daos—even the most talented person would struggle to accomplish anything of note.","Chen Yi scanned the room, saw their doubts, and said with a small smile, \"Just remember this principle. You don’t need to overthink it for now.\"","With that, he instructed Ma Guan to stay behind and answer the students’ questions, then walked out of the study hall.","Just outside the door, Mr. Lingchuan, who had been waiting, bowed slightly. \"Listening to Mr. Qingzhou’s lesson has been incredibly enlightening.\"","\"I’ll have to try out a few things when I get back. Perhaps I can achieve Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao, just like the Headmaster and Zhuo Ying.\"","Chen Yi returned the bow and said, \"It’s just my personal take on it. Whether it’s useful or not depends on the individual.\"","He paused, then asked with a smile, \"Is Mr. Lingchuan collecting the calligraphy sheets today?\"","Mr. Lingchuan looked a bit sheepish. \"It’s a rule set by the Headmaster. I can’t refuse.\"","Chen Yi nodded, gestured for him to go into the study hall, and then took his leave to find Mr. Yue Ming.","Mr. Lingchuan watched him walk away, thought for a moment, then shook his head and entered the study hall to collect the calligraphy sheets Chen Yi had left from the lesson.","「Meanwhile.」","When Chen Yi arrived at Mr. Yue Ming’s residence, he was surprised to see Li Huai’gu there as well and couldn’t help but smile.","\"Brother Huai’gu, what brings you to the academy today?\"","Li Huai’gu gave a wry smile. \"To be honest, Brother Qingzhou, I am indeed here on important business.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, sat down beside him, and looked between him and Mr. Yue Ming. \"More trouble at the Government Office?\"","Mr. Yue Ming replied, his face showing his displeasure, \"That Liu Gongmo is truly absurd. He actually wants me to serve as the Vice Examiner for the upcoming Annual Examination.\"","\"Oh? Is that so?\"","Li Huai’gu nodded and said helplessly, \"If that weren’t the case, the Lord Governor wouldn’t have ordered me to come to the academy.\"","Chen Yi frowned to himself. Although the Annual Examination wasn’t tied to the imperial examinations like the provincial exams were, it was still a test of the scholars’ proficiency in a region.","In previous years, it had always been administered by an Academic Administrator appointed by the Capital Prefecture, who would tour the states and counties to prevent local cheating.","Furthermore, there was never a position for a Vice Examiner.","It was typically the Academic Administrator and his Staff Officers who handled the Annual Examination, with local authorities only playing a supporting role.","This included providing the examination venue—Guiyun Academy—as well as food, lodging, and maintaining order.","Under normal circumstances, the Prefect would be the one to coordinate these efforts.","\"Was this an order from the Lord Governor?\"","Mr. Yue Ming shook his head. \"Liu Gongmo wouldn’t dare. This must be the idea of Ma Shuhan, the Academic Administrator of Shu State.\"","\"Actually, Ma Shuhan and I have some history.\"","\"He previously sent someone to invite Zhuo Ying to serve as his scroll reader, but I sternly refused him.\"","\"This time, he wants me to wade into these muddy waters, likely with the intention of embarrassing me.\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"In that case, Headmaster, you can simply refuse.\"","\"But... Liu Gongmo wants me to ’vouch for’ the scholars of Shu State.\"","\"So he’s trying to put you in the hot seat?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment and instantly understood Liu Hong’s intention.","He wanted Mr. Yue Ming to act as a go-between to curry favor with the Academic Administrator of Shu State, in exchange for better results in the Annual Examination.","The method was simple and didn’t even involve actual cheating.","As long as Academic Administrator Ma slightly lowered the difficulty of the exam questions, the scores of the Shu State scholars would naturally see a significant boost."]},{"number":339,"title":"Chapter 339 - 230: The One Who Tied the Bell Must Untie It","paragraphs":["Conversely, if Academic Administrator Ma used his personal grudge against Mr. Yue Ming to create a difficult exam, the scores of the Shu State scholars would drop significantly.","Clearly, Liu Hong, the Governor, did not want to see such an outcome.","After all, he was in charge of the region; the people’s livelihood, academic administration, civil works, and so on were all part of his performance record.","It was common for him to use any means necessary to ensure Shu State thrived.","Li Huai’gu took a deep breath and said, \"Teacher, you need not worry about me. Although I have come on official orders, everything is for you to decide.\"","Mr. Yue Ming waved his hand. \"This has nothing to do with you.\"","After a pause, he looked at Chen Yi and asked, \"Qingzhou, what are your thoughts?\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"Something like this, being generous at others’ expense... if it were me, I’d spit in his face.\"","Mr. Yue Ming was so amused he couldn’t help but laugh. \"I admit, I’d also like to spit in Liu Gongmo’s face.\"","\"But if my personal grudge with Ma Shuhan really causes all the scholars of Shu State to fail the Annual Examination, I couldn’t bear it.\"","Chen Yi secretly shook his head. ’He’s so protective of his reputation. It fits Mr. Yue Ming perfectly.’","Even though Mr. Yue Ming didn’t serve as an official and was only dedicated to teaching numerous scholars at the academy, he was still burdened by his reputation.","Perhaps Liu Hong had seen this and that was why he’d sent Li Huai’gu to persuade him.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi said, \"The one who tied the bell must be the one to untie it.\"","Mr. Yue Ming was taken aback. \"Are you suggesting I reconcile with Ma Shuhan privately?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"No, you can’t.\"","\"With the Annual Examination so close, it’s inappropriate for anyone, including you, to meet privately with Academic Administrator Ma. It would give people reason to gossip.\"","\"The ’bell-tier’ I’m referring to is Governor Liu.\"","\"We just need to shatter his little scheme, and this matter will naturally have nothing to do with you, Headmaster.\"","Li Huai’gu’s spirits lifted, and he quickly asked, \"Brother Qingzhou, please speak your mind.\"","Meeting their gazes, Chen Yi lightly said two words: \"Yang Ye.\"","Li Huai’gu was stunned. \"The Right Governor?\"","Mr. Yue Ming understood and chuckled in amusement. \"You’re suggesting I show Liu Gongmo no courtesy at all.\"","Having Yang Ye handle this matter was indeed the most appropriate solution.","First, his official rank was the same as Liu Hong’s, so he had a say. Also, when the repercussions appeared later, the scholars wouldn’t blame Mr. Yue Ming.","Second, Yang Ye was advanced in age and preferred stability.","As long as it didn’t cross a line, he was easier to talk to than Liu Hong.","Plus, given Li Huai’gu’s relationship with Yang Ye, Mr. Yue Ming was confident he could ask Yang Ye for a small favor.","Chen Yi looked at him with a calm expression and said, \"Headmaster, what courtesy do you have to speak of with him?\"","\"Well... none, I suppose.\"","\"Exactly. It’s just the Annual Examination. It doesn’t affect their eligibility for the imperial examinations, so what if the scholars don’t do well?\"","Li Huai’gu looked between the two of them. Although he still had some doubts, he knew his teacher would probably not accept the position of Vice Examiner.","\"Teacher, do you need me to speak with Lord Yang?\"","Mr. Yue Ming glanced at him and sighed for some reason. \"Huai’gu, if you were as perceptive as Qingzhou, you might have a chance to fully display your talents in the official world someday.\"","\"...My apologies, Teacher. I have disappointed you.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi laughed. \"Brother Huai’gu has a pure and kind nature. As an official, he will surely bring blessings to his jurisdiction.\"","Mr. Yue Ming pointed at him and said with a scolding laugh, \"You’ve said all the good and the bad. What’s left for me, his teacher, to guide him with?\"","After a few jests, he looked at Li Huai’gu and said seriously, \"You don’t need to be involved in this matter. I will discuss it with Right Envoy Yang myself.\"","Li Huai’gu breathed a sigh of relief. \"In that case, I am relieved.\"","Seeing the matter settled, Chen Yi was about to get up and take his leave.","But Mr. Yue Ming stopped him and asked, \"You’ll be participating in this year’s Annual Examination as well, won’t you, Qingzhou?\"","Chen Yi paused, then pursed his lips. \"I’d rather not, but given the circumstances, it looks like I have no choice.\"","Liu Hong had issued several announcements emphasizing its importance, and who knew what he was planning.","If he didn’t participate, his Scholar title would surely be revoked.","Mr. Yue Ming nodded slightly and advised, \"The Annual Examination won’t be difficult for you, and it concerns the titles of the scholars. You mustn’t act willfully.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, then stood up to leave.","Seeing this, Li Huai’gu, who was beside him, also bowed to Mr. Yue Ming and followed him out of the courtyard.","\"Thank you for your guidance today, Brother Qingzhou. Otherwise, I truly wouldn’t have the face to see our teacher again.\"","Chen Yi smiled and said, \"The Headmaster was right about one thing.\"","\"Brother Huai’gu, you are too upright and kind. You’ll easily be taken advantage of while working in the Government Office.\"","Seeing Li Huai’gu’s ashamed expression, he continued, \"You and my elder brother, Chen Yunfan, are both in the Governor’s Office, so you should know what he’s like.\"","\"Don’t be fooled by his usual unreliable demeanor. He actually has a strong moral compass and knows what he can and cannot do.\"","\"Take the summer grain collection in the Three Towns, for example. My brother knew it was a hot potato and didn’t want to take it on.\"","Hearing this, Li Huai’gu recalled the previous incident and said with dawning realization, \"He was faking his illness?\"","Chen Yi said irritably, \"Sick or not, he wouldn’t have gone. He would have found a way to get out of it one way or another.\"","’However, the only reason Chen Yunfan managed to avoid it that time was because I unexpectedly intervened and poisoned the man unconscious.’","’In other words, I was indirectly responsible for Li Huai’gu having to make that trip to the Three Towns.’","As Chen Yi thought about this, he couldn’t help but add a few more words, \"In any case, be discreet and cautious at the Governor’s Office.\"","\"I will keep that in mind.\"","They walked for a while until they reached the academy gate.","Chen Yi remembered something and asked, \"I heard the summer grain harvest in Shu State was poor this year, and the grain tax couldn’t be fully collected?\"","Li Huai’gu nodded. \"That is indeed the case.\"","\"The recent heavy rains damaged more than fifty percent of the fertile land in several counties downstream of the Chishui River. The grain harvest was barely enough to get by.\"","\"Lord Liu couldn’t bear to see the common people starve, so he discussed it with Lord Yang, drafted a memorial, and after receiving the Holy Emperor’s approval, exempted some of the grain tax.\""]},{"number":340,"title":"Chapter 340 - 230: He Who Tied the Bell Must Untie It","paragraphs":["’Liu Hong...’","Chen Yi said thoughtfully, \"It seems grain prices in Shu State are about to rise.\"","\"It won’t have much of an impact,\" Li Huai’gu said with a smile. \"If prices rise too much, the two Governors will likely step in and regulate them.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him but didn’t say anything more.","’Given the current situation, even if the Governor’s Office does intervene, it’ll only be after the Xiao Family’s silver coins have been completely drained.’","After some more small talk, Chen Yi bid farewell to Li Huai’gu and found Liu Si’er outside the wonton shop.","It was nearly noon, and many students from the academy frequented the wonton shop. A long line had even formed at the entrance.","Many of the students who saw Chen Yi bowed. \"Sir, you’re eating here as well?\"","\"Why don’t you join us?\"","Chen Yi returned their greetings one by one, shaking his head with a smile. \"I have something to attend to, so I’ll be on my way.\"","With that, he boarded the carriage and told Liu Si’er to drive straight to Jishi Medicine Hall in the East Market.","The rain had stopped, and the sky was clearing up.","The sun shone from a vast, cloudless sky, its rays not as scorching as in summer.","A cool, pleasant breeze blew from time to time.","Chen Yi gazed out the window, making small talk with Liu Si’er. He didn’t dwell on the matter of Liu Hong and Mr. Yue Ming.","’What occupies my thoughts most is the identity of those manipulating the grain prices, and who is backing them.’","’From what I can tell so far, these people are quite powerful.’","’I need to find a way to identify them first. Acting rashly will only backfire.’","Before long, the carriage turned from Kangning Street onto South Street.","Chen Yi immediately spotted Xinglin Hall, situated not far from the Governor’s Office, and he raised an eyebrow.","’Great Success in Calligraphy Dao?’","He saw that the calligraphy for \"Xinglin Hall\" on the plaque outside the Medicine Hall was, astonishingly, written in Wei Qing’s Style at the Great Success Realm.","A brilliant, golden luminescence flowed from the characters, casting a dazzling radiance.","Even though it was noon, a steady stream of people went in and out of Xinglin Hall, many of them members of Noble Families dressed in fine silks.","Liu Si’er saw it too. \"You see that, Young Master?\" he said.","\"That Xinglin Hall has really established itself. They have a Medical Saint Hand in residence, which attracts a lot of wealthy merchants and gentry.\"","Chen Yi hummed in acknowledgment and said no more.","’The Medicine Hall business isn’t like others. Aside from the price of herbs, what truly matters are the Physicians and their formulas.’","’Ultimately, the hall that can actually heal the sick and save lives is the one that will have a constant stream of customers.’","’In contrast, a place like Hundred Herbs Hall, which started out by selling herbal teas, was considered no better than an Evil Cultivator by its peers.’","Soon, the carriage arrived at the East Market.","Chen Yi led Liu Si’er into Jishi Medicine Hall. To the surprise of Liu Quan, Ma Liangcai, and the others, he called for them to prepare lunch.","While telling the apprentices to prepare the meal, Liu Quan brought over the account books, his face all smiles.","\"Shopkeeper, please take a look.\"","Chen Yi took the books and glanced through them. He smiled. \"I heard business was slow, but from the looks of this, it’s not bad at all.\"","Liu Quan’s smile froze. He laughed dryly. \"It’s all thanks to your excellent management, Shopkeeper. Heh heh.\"","Chen Yi put the account books down, deciding not to make things more awkward for him. He announced,","\"You’ve all been working hard lately. Later, everyone can take two taels of silver. Consider it a bonus from me.\"","\"Thank you, Shopkeeper.\"","Chen Yi nodded. With some time to spare, he pulled Ma Liangcai into a back room.","\"Did you need something, Shopkeeper?\"","\"Shopkeeper Wang gave you some Medical Dao texts earlier. How are your studies progressing?\"","After Xiao Wan’er confirmed her plans for the Medical Dao Academy, Chen Yi had prepared some relevant medical texts and asked Wang Ji to give them to Ma Liangcai.","Part of the reason for his visit was to test Ma Liangcai’s progress.","Ma Liangcai looked troubled. \"I’m... I’m still studying them. Some parts are just really difficult to understand.\"","’Chen Yi was well aware of how difficult it was to study the Medical Dao. Many aspiring Physicians never got any hands-on experience, relying solely on rote memorization, which was never enough.’","He thought for a moment and said, \"Whatever you don’t understand, write it down.\"","Ma Liangcai was stunned for a moment, then overjoyed. He hurriedly took out a brush and paper and wrote down every single question that had been puzzling him lately.","Chen Yi read through the questions. ’Just as I thought,’ he mused, before writing out the answers one by one on the paper.","\"Yin Yang Five Elements, the organs and meridians, the Four Diagnostics, and the Eight Principles are the absolute fundamentals. Only when you truly grasp these can your study of the Medical Dao be considered entry-level.\"","\"You must first build a holistic framework in your mind before you can even think about diagnosis and prescribing treatments...\"","After more than an hour had passed, Chen Yi saw that Liu Quan and the others outside were growing anxious, so he finally said,","\"I’ll have Wang Ji send you more texts later. Improve your skills in the Medical Dao as quickly as you can.\"","Ma Liangcai looked down at the paper in his hands and bowed gratefully. \"Thank you for your guidance, Shopkeeper.\"","Chen Yi patted his shoulder. \"Let’s go. Time to eat.\"","’Ma Liangcai wasn’t exceptionally talented, but he was obedient and honest, and he had proven himself competent on several occasions.’","’It was no wonder I’m putting in the effort to teach him.’","’Of course, my true intention is to train a capable assistant so that matters concerning Hundred Herbs Hall and the Medical Dao Academy won’t all fall to me in the future.’","After lunch, Chen Yi wandered through the East Market alone, specifically looking for the grain merchants’ shops.","However, after making a few rounds, he couldn’t find any grain merchants who had purchased barbarian slaves.","He did, however, spot several caged barbarian slaves at a stall run by people from Poshisu Country, located deeper in the market.","\"This barbarian slave, young, strong. Fifty taels.\"","\"That one, thirty taels...\"","The man from Poshisu Country would occasionally crack his whip, striking the slaves and shouting curses to prove their docile nature.","\"Obedient, useful.\"","’Chen Yi couldn’t tell if the barbarian slaves were truly useful or not.’","’But he did notice that the scrawniest one among them seemed to be protected by the others.’","Whenever the man from Poshisu cracked his whip, the other barbarian slaves would subtly shield the young one.","’Are they just protecting the young?’","’Or did that young slave have a high status?’","Chen Yi couldn’t be sure. He silently committed their faces to memory before turning to continue his stroll through the market.","It wasn’t until late in the afternoon that he summoned Liu Si’er to return to the Xiao Family estate.","’A barbarian slave riot... I wonder if it was these slaves, or the other ones from the grain merchants.’","’Connecting the grain merchants with barbarian slaves just feels... odd. Something strange is going on...’"]},{"number":341,"title":"Chapter 341 - 231: Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting Finally Accomplished","paragraphs":["About an hour later, Chen Yi returned to the Xiao Family estate.","As he stepped out of the carriage, he noticed that the furrows on the brows of Wang Lixing and the others had smoothed out, unlike this morning and yesterday.","Chen Yi scanned the group, a guess forming in his mind. He simply smiled, offered a greeting, and headed straight for the Spring Lotus Garden.","Faintly, the conversation between Liu Si’er, Wang Lixing, and the others drifted to him from behind.","\"The price of grain went up again today. One stone of fine grain is one point eight taels of silver.\"","\"But the Marquis has decided not to buy grain. He’s going to borrow it.\"","\"Borrow? Who is he going to borrow from?\"","\"Guangyue Prefecture.\"","\"Duke Qian?\"","\"Who else could it be?\"","\"That’s actually a good method. Borrow grain to handle the emergency, and once the prices fall, we can just repay Duke Qian.\"","\"But this won’t be settled until the Marquis sends a letter to Duke Qian. It’ll probably take a few more days...\"","’Borrowing grain?’","Chen Yi chuckled inwardly. ’The Old Marquis is finally showing some cleverness.’","It was obvious someone in Shu State was digging a pit for the Xiao Family. No matter how the Marquis responded, there would be trouble.","He could either go head-to-head with the people behind the grain merchants or find a way to raise money.","But the Old Marquis’s roundabout approach of going to Duke Qian in Guangyue Prefecture was a different story.","The rise and fall of grain prices in Shu State would not affect the Xiao Family in the slightest, much less leave them vulnerable to being constrained and manipulated.","The most brilliant part was that the Old Marquis wasn’t buying, but borrowing.","He was still holding onto a large sum of silver.","This way, the Xiao Family could be on the offense or the defense, allowing them to hold out for much longer.","As for whether Duke Qian would lend them the grain...","Chen Yi pondered for a moment, a slight smile gracing his lips.","\"Whether he lends it or not, it won’t be the worst outcome.\"","It was a way to see who your true friends were in a time of hardship—far better than being stabbed in the back during a real disaster later on.","It was just that...","’This kind of news would be more effective if it were kept secret.’","Back inside the Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi looked left and right. Seeing no one around, he cocked his ear to listen.","From the Purple Bamboo Forest came the sound of Pei Guanli practicing her Martial Arts Techniques. \"I have to protect Brother-in-law! Next time, I definitely, definitely will...\"","Chen Yi was speechless. ’This girl has become obsessed.’","Ever since the incident on the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival, Pei Guanli had been practicing her Martial Arts more diligently than ever.","From time to time, Chen Yi would hear similar declarations and understood that the Tiger Girl was genuinely scared by what had happened.","His gaze then shifted toward Jiaxing Garden.","He could faintly hear Xiao Wan’er’s laughter drifting from that direction. \"...remember to bring rope for measuring.\"","\"As for paper, pens, and the like, bring a few extra sets.\"","\"Also, it might rain tomorrow, so bring a couple of extra sets of clothes... Hmm... Xiaodie, remember to prepare a set for the Second Young Master-in-law as well.\"","\"Additionally, Wuge won’t be going this time. We need someone to look after the estate. Xiaodie, Tingyun, I’ll have to trouble you two to stay behind.\"","\"Yes, Eldest Miss...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi hung the Oil Paper Umbrella in his hand under the eaves to dry, thinking:","’Xiao Wan’er is certainly dedicated to the Medical Dao Academy. She’s made so many preparations just for choosing a site.’","’Compared to her, I’m quite idle.’","Chen Yi looked at the fresh, natural beauty of the Spring Lotus Garden after the rain had passed, a smile forming on his face.","\"It’s not like I have nothing to do.\"","Of the four arts of Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, he was only missing one: the Painting Dao.","It was time to complete the set.","With that thought, Chen Yi went to his study, spread out a sheet of Yunsong Paper, mixed the ink evenly, and began to sketch and paint.","It had to be said, having his Calligraphy Dao at the Perfection Realm was also beneficial for learning the Painting Dao.","At the very least, his Pen Technique was already masterful. With just a few strokes and lines, the initial outline of a painting began to take shape.","But Pen Technique was only Pen Technique. The Painting Dao ultimately relied on Painting Skill, Painting Technique, the right pigments, and so on.","So, in the end, all he managed to paint was an outline.","Chen Yi grimaced, looking at the painting before him, which resembled the withered branches in front of a mass grave.","\"I was clearly trying to do a Pine and Cypress Painting.\"","Still, it could be considered a painting. So, after he wrote down the title and his signature, two lines of golden text floated before his eyes.","[Ink-Wash Painting study successful. Level: Initial Insight]","[Painting Dao: Uninitiated 0/1 (Upgradeable)]","Chen Yi glanced at it and immediately spent 11 Opportunity points to raise his Painting Dao to the Minor Success Realm.","The Profound Mysteries of the Painting Dao’s entry-level and Minor Success Realm instantly flooded his mind.","After a quick mental review, he spread out a new sheet of Yunsong Paper, simultaneously practicing the Pen Technique for Ink-Wash Painting while absorbing the Profound Mysteries of the Painting Dao.","The Painting Dao and the Calligraphy Dao indeed had much in common.","Besides the emphasis on negative space and the Mental Realm, the only differences lay in the form of expression and the Pen Technique.","It was like how Wei Qing’s Style emphasized straight, grand strokes, while Cursive Script focused on natural, free-flowing expression.","Ink-Wash Painting valued concept over likeness, but this expressive freedom made it difficult to render fine details.","Understanding this point, Chen Yi’s progress in his Ink-Wash Painting Technique was miraculously fast.","In just over two hours, his Ink-Wash Painting Technique went from Initial Insight to the Skilled Level.","While his skill wasn’t necessarily high, he had at least mastered the various painting methods for the blacks and grays of ink wash.","Chen Yi looked at the thirteen paintings on the Yunsong Paper before him, the corners of his mouth lifting into a smile.","’Now, my Calligraphy Dao is at Perfection, my Chess Dao at Great Success, and my Zither and Painting Daos are both at Minor Success.’","’Although the Realms are at different levels, I have indeed achieved something in all four arts of Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting.’","Just then, Xiaodie poked her head in. Her face lit up when she saw him. \"Young Master-in-law, when did you get back?\"","Chen Yi snapped back to reality and discreetly began to gather the sheets of Yunsong Paper from the table—especially the first few he had painted. \"A while ago,\" he replied.","After tucking the paintings into his sleeve, he beckoned to Xiaodie. \"Come and see how your Young Master-in-law’s painting is.\"","At his words, Xiaodie walked over. She glanced curiously at the table and said with a smile, \"Anything the Young Master-in-law paints is surely wonderful.\"","But when she saw the paintings, a puzzled look appeared on her face.","\"Young Master-in-law, are these all paintings of the same scene?\"","Much like a child who only likes bright colors, she couldn’t see any difference between the inky-black mountains and the gray-toned rivers."]},{"number":342,"title":"Chapter 342 - 231: Final Accomplishment in Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting (2)","paragraphs":["Chen Yi’s smile froze. He silently gathered up several paintings, leaving only the best one, and tossed the rest into the wastebasket.","\"You’re right, they are all the same scene... No need to keep so many of them then.\"","Xiaodie didn’t notice anything unusual about him. She just thought of something and asked,","\"Young Master, was it because Miss Guanli asked you to paint this morning that you started?\"","\"I suppose so.\"","Chen Yi gave a perfunctory reply and motioned for her to help him clean the desk. \"Is everything packed over at Jiaxing Garden?\"","\"Mhm, the Young Mistress brought a lot of things over this time. She also told me to pack a few more sets of clothes for you.\"","Xiaodie’s face fell with disappointment as she said, \"But I won’t be able to go with you this time.\"","\"The Young Mistress ordered me to stay behind and look after Young Master Wuge.\"","Chen Yi had heard about this already. After they finished tidying the desk, he said with a smile,","\"We’re not going there for fun. We have important business to attend to.\"","\"When I have some free time in a few days, I’ll take you on an autumn outing.\"","The autumn scenery might not be as vibrant as spring or summer, but the pleasant weather made up for it.","Walking around and seeing the sights would naturally reveal a different kind of charm.","Xiaodie lowered her head shyly. \"Young Master, as long as you take me with you, I’ll be happy to go anywhere.\"","\"Whether it’s for fun or for business, it’s all fine.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi pinched her cheek and pulled it a couple of times. \"I’m just worried you’ll get worn out.\"","\"Ah, Young Master, that hurts...\"","After they joked around for a bit, Xiao Wuge returned, and Chen Yi had Xiaodie prepare dinner.","During dinner, Xiao Wuge, as expected, talked about what he had seen at the Martial Arts Arena. His eyes lit up with excitement, showing his keen interest in Martial Arts.","Chen Yi just went along with it, not saying much.","’In his opinion, since Xiao Wuge would be going to Jinling in the future, having some Martial Arts skills would be very beneficial.’","’It was certainly better than him spending his ten years as a hostage cooped up like a noble lady, never setting foot outside.’","Pei Guanli, as usual, showed off her Martial Arts skills, patting her chest and saying, \"Tomorrow, I’ll teach you a powerful Palm Technique.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Of course, it’s true! Ask my brother-in-law if my Palm Technique is powerful or not.\"","Seeing Chen Yi nod, Xiao Wuge quickly exclaimed, \"Sister Guanli, I want to learn!\"","\"Don’t worry, leave it to me. It’s their fault Sister Wan’er and brother-in-law aren’t taking us out to have fun...\"","Chen Yi was speechless, then chuckled.","Pei Guanli had originally wanted to go with them to the Xiao Family’s fiefdom outside the city, but she had to stay at Spring Lotus Garden because she was worried about missing a message or a visitor from the Mountain Race.","Furthermore, Chen Yi was worried that people from the Five Poison Sect might come to Shu State again, so after much persuasion, he managed to talk the Tiger Girl out of it.","Fortunately, with Xiaodie and Xie Tingyun at the residence, there shouldn’t be any trouble with Pei Guanli teaching Xiao Wuge Martial Arts.","After dinner, the four of them went to rest.","As night fell, before Xiao Wuge, Xiaodie, and Pei Guanli were sound asleep, Chen Yi changed into a black long-robed gown and quietly left Spring Lotus Garden.","Weaving through the streets and alleys, he reached the outskirts of the East Market in just half an hour.","It was currently 8:30 PM. The rain had passed and the sky had cleared, revealing a bright moon and brilliant stars. There were quite a few people on the streets.","Most of them were common folk who had come to the East Market to see the spectacle.","They gathered in groups of three or five, crowding around street performers and shouting their approval from time to time.","Fortunately, there were many Jianghu People dressed in linen clothes, so Chen Yi’s black clothes and bamboo hat didn’t stand out too much.","He glanced at the crowded streets of the East Market, then at the few grain shops in the distance, his brow slightly furrowed.","’If the barbarian slaves riot here, it would probably cause an even greater commotion, wouldn’t it?’","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi decided to act according to the circumstances.","However, after waiting for nearly another half an hour, he still hadn’t seen any barbarian slaves appear, and he couldn’t help but feel puzzled.","Just then, a cry of alarm came from deep within the East Market: \"The barbarian slaves are killing people!\"","\"Someone, quick! The barbarian slaves are rioting!\"","\"Damn it, those barbarians dare to set fire to the grain shop’s warehouse!?\"","Faintly, Chen Yi could also hear some roars and the sounds of fighting.","His eyes narrowed. He scanned his surroundings, and seeing that no one nearby had noticed yet, he silently moved deeper into the market.","He was wrong.","He was completely wrong.","The barbarian slaves weren’t rioting at the grain shop’s storefront, but at the warehouse where the grain was stored!","Chen Yi passed through three alleys and saw flames soaring into the sky in the distance, with thick black smoke billowing everywhere.","In the dim light, he could make out several tall, sturdy figures fighting with more than ten guards in gray linen clothes.","He had to admit, the Barbarian Race was indeed uniquely gifted.","Although their Fist and Foot techniques had no structure, their powerful Physiques alone allowed them to match Martial Artists of the Lower Three Grades Realm.","Moreover, they seemed impervious to pain, letting themselves be hacked by blades and struck by clubs.","Not only did they not retreat a single step, but they charged and fought with fierce courage.","Chen Yi studied the barbarians and recognized them as the same barbarian slaves who had been locked in cages during the day.","One of them, a relatively thin barbarian slave, was easy to identify.","Even in the midst of such a fierce battle, several of the larger barbarian slaves were still protecting him.","In the lulls of the fight, the barbarian slaves would even turn back and shout something to the thin one.","Seeing this, Chen Yi frowned slightly, a trace of doubt rising in his mind.","’How did these barbarian slaves escape?’","’And after escaping, why didn’t they just leave quietly? Why cause such a huge disturbance instead?’","By this time, more and more people had noticed the commotion and were rushing over.","Among them were the government officials in charge of guarding the East Market, as well as many skilled Jianghu People.","Under these circumstances, the actions of these barbarian slaves seemed rather suspicious.","Just as Chen Yi was feeling puzzled, a flute suddenly began to play."]},{"number":343,"title":"Chapter 343 - 231: Accomplishment in Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting","paragraphs":["The flute’s melody was strange, shrill, and hurried, like a small boat bobbing up and down in a turbulent stream, in constant danger of capsizing.","The moment he heard the flute, Chen Yi’s True Essence instantly circulated throughout his body.","Inside his Forehead Acupoint Sea of Qi, Spiritual Essence flowed out from the Four Divine Positions, sealing his ears.","’This is... the Illusory Sound Sect’s Sound Killing Technique?’","Realization dawned on Chen Yi, and in a single step, he landed on a nearby roof, searching for the source of the music.","But before he could find the person striking from the shadows, he saw the granary guards in the distance standing completely still, allowing the barbarian slaves to kill them.","’Mind control?’","Seeing this, Chen Yi was now certain the attacker must be a deviant from the Illusory Sound Sect, a follower of the Evil Demonic Dao.","’No wonder these barbarian slaves managed to escape. Someone really is helping them.’","As he thought, he scanned his surroundings, his gaze mostly directed to the east of the East Market—toward the dark, sparsely populated shadows.","The now-unimpeded barbarian slaves were also fleeing in that direction.","However, as government officials were arriving, one of the barbarian slaves voluntarily stayed behind.","Facing the government officials, he shouted without looking back, \"Jiasule, go—\"","\"Fucking barbarian! You dare act so insolently within the borders of Great Wei?\"","\"Kill him!\"","\"Pursue!\"","Chen Yi ignored the chaos nearby and darted off in pursuit of the barbarian slaves.","As he leaped and bounded, he picked up a guard’s long blade, vanished into the shadows, and followed the barbarian slaves from a distance.","「Before long.」","Chen Yi saw a figure completely wrapped in black clothing appear diagonally ahead of him, staring at him with a sinister gaze.","\"Sir, stay out of this!\"","Chen Yi stopped, glanced at the distant barbarian slaves, pulled his bamboo hat down slightly, and asked:","\"From the Illusory Sound Sect?\"","As he spoke, he took another look with his Qi Observation Skill and frowned inwardly.","’Just a Seventh Grade Realm Martial Artist?’","\"Since you know the name of the Illusory Sound Sect, you should leave. Otherwise, don’t blame me for what happens next!\"","\"What happens next?\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head, walking toward him with the long blade in hand.","His steps seemed slow, but in reality, he had already used the Meteor Butterfly Step and appeared before the black-clothed man in the blink of an eye.","One strike—a flash of cold light.","A bolt of silken blade light slashed straight down—his Saber Intent as cold as frost.","Before the blade arrived, a chill had already enveloped a ten-zhang radius.","\"Great Success Saber Dao?!\"","The black-clothed man’s eyes widened, and he hastily raised the flute in his hand to block.","But it was too late.","As the light of the blade flashed past, the flute was split in two, and one of his arms was severed and sent flying along with it.","\"Ah—you!?\"","Before the black-clothed man could make another move, Chen Yi pressed the long blade to his throat, stopping the rest of his words.","The black-clothed man instantly broke out in a sweat, clutching his bleeding shoulder.","\"S-Sir... you... I...\"","\"I don’t know how I’ve offended you, but I beg you... I beg you to spare me...\"","Chen Yi’s eyes lifted slightly, revealing only the line of his jaw, and he asked coolly:","\"I’m curious, why are you helping those barbarian slaves?\"","The black-clothed man said frantically, \"I... it was for the reward from Bright Moon Building... P-please don’t blame me, I have no connection with the Barbarian Race.\"","He assumed Chen Yi was someone who hated the Barbarian Race, and so he begged repeatedly for his life.","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. ’Someone from Bright Moon Building?’","\"Isn’t Black Tooth dead?\"","\"I wouldn’t dare lie to you. I received the mission in the Western State... N-no, not Shu State.\"","\"Then do you know how those barbarian slaves escaped, and why they burned the grain?\"","\"They... someone knocked out those Poshisu Country horse bandits, allowing them to escape.\"","\"After that, after that they... Ah!\"","Before he could finish speaking, Chen Yi saw his eyes suddenly burst.","No, not just his eyes; blood gushed from his mouth, nose, and ears.","In just three breaths, the black-clothed man was dead.","Chen Yi frowned, glanced at the body, then scanned his surroundings.","After confirming there was no movement nearby, he used his Qi Observation Skill to examine the black-clothed man.","He saw strands of black qi spread throughout the man’s meridians.","Especially around the heart and head, the black qi was entwined, deep as ink, as if two large holes had been bored into those spots.","’It’s not poison or a Gu Insect, yet it can kill from a distance...’","’Poshisu Country’s Black Magic?’","’Did someone place a Black Magic curse on him beforehand?’","Chen Yi had long heard that the techniques cultivated by the Jianghu People of Poshisu Country were exceedingly bizarre, and he had also heard rumors of Black Magic.","’I never thought I’d encounter it here.’","This inevitably reminded him of the Poshisu native who had once controlled his body’s previous owner into fleeing a marriage.","At this thought, a chill entered Chen Yi’s eyes, and he immediately transformed into a black shadow, quickly chasing after the barbarian slaves.","But he followed the trail all the way to the East City Gate and saw no further sign of the barbarian slaves.","Even the footprints and bloodstains had vanished.","’It’s as if someone hid them in an incredibly short time.’","Unwilling to give up, Chen Yi slowly retraced his steps, searching.","’I’m certain of it. The one who took these members of the Barbarian Race hasn’t left the Prefecture City. Otherwise, I would have definitely seen something.’","’Strange,’ Chen Yi thought as he scanned his surroundings.","’Given that they’re barbarian slaves, they’d surely try to get back to the Barbarian Race after escaping.’","’This was the perfect chance, but they didn’t take it. Why?’","Chen Yi had no answer, so he stopped dwelling on it and focused on figuring out where the barbarian slaves might be hiding.","’North of here is the bank of the Quchi. Taking the waterway would be a good way to leave Shu State.’","’To the south... that would be east of Yanhua Lane.’","’It’s a place where the Mountain Race, people from Poshisu, and outsiders trying to make a living all reside. A real melting pot, which makes it a good place to hide.’","However, Chen Yi was more inclined to believe they’d gone toward Quchi in North City.","Just as he was about to head that way to investigate, he heard a light footstep behind him.","Following it came a lazy voice: \"You, I’m talking to you, the one with the blade.\"","\"Turn around slowly. Let your Uncle Liu see which master of the blade this is.\"","Chen Yi froze for a moment. ’Liu Lang?’","’What’s he doing here?’"]},{"number":344,"title":"Chapter 344 - 232: Some People Are Born Extraordinary","paragraphs":["’Isn’t Liu Lang supposed to be watching Liu Hong?’","’Why is he here?’","Before he could dwell on it, Chen Yi pulled a black mask from his robes, tied it securely around the lower half of his face, and turned to look.","\"Sword Madman?\"","Liu Lang was also dressed in night clothes and wearing a black mask. The Treasure Blade he’d gotten from Chen Yi was slung over his shoulder, and he was looking at him with his head slightly raised.","\"That would be me.\"","\"But you, hiding your face like this... that’s not how a Swordman should act.\"","Seeing that Liu Lang hadn’t recognized him, Chen Yi didn’t know whether to laugh or cry. \"Before you say that, you might want to take a look at yourself.\"","Liu Lang glanced down at himself, paused, then said, \"I am different from you.\"","\"Even in these night clothes, I am still open and honorable.\"","Chen Yi: \"...\"","’Damn it, how did I never realize he was so glib?’","Liu Lang paid no mind to his thoughts. He pointed his blade behind him and asked, \"Did you kill that Evil Demon from the Illusory Sound Sect over there?\"","Chen Yi nodded helplessly. \"Obviously.\"","Liu Lang’s eyes lit up at his words. He grinned. \"Your Saber Technique is not bad.\"","\"I heard a while back that the Mental Realm of Great Success Saber Dao appeared outside Shu State City. Some people even suspected it was me. Now it seems it must have been your doing.\"","Chen Yi shook his head without answering, asking instead, \"What if it was? And what if it wasn’t?\"","\"To test our blades.\"","Liu Lang watched him with great interest. \"It’s rare for a Great Success Swordman to appear in Shu State. How could I miss this opportunity?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t be bothered to beat around the bush with him any longer. He turned, lifted his bamboo hat with the tip of his blade, and stared straight at him, snapping:","\"I told you to keep watch, and you run off here to fight me?\"","Liu Lang froze. He looked him up and down, then asked hesitantly, \"Boss?\"","\"It’s you?\"","\"No, that’s not right! Not right at all!\"","It dawned on Liu Lang, and he stared at him in utter shock. \"You... how do you know Saber Technique?\"","\"And... and at the level of Great Success in Saber Dao!?\"","It was no wonder Liu Lang hadn’t recognized Chen Yi; it had never even crossed his mind that Chen Yi would use a blade.","After all, for someone who had already achieved Great Success in Spear Dao and Fist Dao, and was a Medical Saint Hand, no matter how supremely talented, it should be impossible to also succeed in the Saber Dao.","Biting off more than you can chew, right?","Chen Yi twirled his blade in a flourish. \"Is it that strange?\"","Liu Lang’s mouth fell open. \"Is... is it not strange?\"","Great Success in Spear Dao, Great Success in Fist Dao, and Great Success in Saber Dao too, on top of being a Medical Saint Hand...","A person like that... is not strange?!","Chen Yi chuckled, naturally understanding his shock, but he couldn’t explain. He simply said:","\"Some people are just born extraordinary. Like me.\"","He spouted nonsense with a straight face. \"The moment I was born, I had a Martial Arts Saint Body. Not only were All Meridians Connected, but I also possessed a Clear Mind Realm.\"","\"I can learn any Martial Art with a single glance, achieve Mastery after practicing it once, and break into the Dao Realm within a hundred days of training.\"","\"R-Really?\"","\"Of course it’s fake. A person like that doesn’t even exist in myths and legends.\"","Seeing Chen Yi’s expression, which seemed to say he was looking at an idiot, Liu Lang said with a face full of grief and indignation:","\"Whether you were telling the truth or not, I believed you.\"","\"Damn it all. I’ve lived for over twenty years, and only now do I know the meaning of ’there’s always someone better out there’.\"","\"I used to think General Jinghong reaching Sword Dao Perfection and Great Success Spear Dao at only twenty was the limit. I never thought you’d be even more outrageous.\"","He paused, leaned in closer, and stared at him for a long while.","\"Tell me the truth. Are you some hundred-year-old monster who’s disguised himself just to mess with me?\"","\"...Your grandpa’s the old monster.\"","Chen Yi cursed, and just as he was about to ask why Liu Lang was here, he suddenly heard voices in the distance.","\"Lord Hundred Households, there’s a body here!\"","\"Search the surroundings! Don’t miss a single clue!\"","’The Imprisonment Department’s Fang Hongxiu?’","’An acquaintance.’","An idea flashed through Chen Yi’s mind. He gestured for Liu Lang to wait, then darted towards Fang Hongxiu and her group.","Liu Lang had also heard the approaching people. Seeing Chen Yi head over, he could only follow resignedly.","But he was still muttering to himself, mostly along the lines of how such a person could possibly exist, calling him a monster and so on.","Chen Yi couldn’t care less what he was thinking.","After all, they had known each other for a long time and had worked together to trap and kill Black Tooth, Liu Wen, and Xiao Dongchen. It was no big deal if Liu Lang knew a few of his secrets.","He wasn’t too concerned about it.","「Soon.」","Chen Yi arrived where Fang Hongxiu and her people were.","He scanned the area. Seeing them searching outwards from the body of the Illusory Sound Sect’s Evil Demon, Chen Yi let out a cough to draw their attention.","\"Hundred Households Fang, searching like this won’t be very effective.\"","Fang Hongxiu gripped her blade, watching him warily. \"Who are you?\"","Chen Yi adjusted his bamboo hat and chuckled in response. \"Hundred Households Fang, you great personages are so forgetful. Have you forgotten me so quickly?\"","Before Fang Hongxiu could reply, a young Imprisonment Officer next to her reacted first:","\"You! You’re that bastard who’s shamed our Imprisonment Department time and time again!\"","Fang Hongxiu recognized Chen Yi as well and drew her blade immediately.","\"You still dare to show your face before my Imprisonment Department?\"","Chen Yi chuckled, replying nonchalantly, \"Hundred Households Fang, you must see things clearly. I have always treated the Imprisonment Department with the utmost respect.\"","\"Respect? How do you have the gall to say such a thing?\"","\"Have I not?\"","\"If that weren’t the case, how could you, Hundred Households Fang, and all your people still be alive?\"","\"If you count carefully, I’ve already spared your lives three times.\"","A flash of angry resentment crossed Fang Hongxiu’s eyes. \"You? It was clearly twice!\"","The moment the words left her mouth, she understood. \"You lecher, you... you...\"","Chen Yi said with a smile, \"This time counts as one, of course.\"","But seeing Fang Hongxiu’s expression darken, he changed the subject:","\"I was only speaking the truth. I hope Hundred Households Fang can forgive me.\"","\"Of course, don’t even think about making a move.\"","\"You know you’re no match for me... for us.\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang’s complicated feelings eased a bit. He grinned and said, \"You’d just be courting death.\""]},{"number":345,"title":"Chapter 345 - 232: Some People Are Born Extraordinary, Part 2","paragraphs":["\"...\"","Fang Hongxiu and the other Imprisonment Officers exchanged complicated glances.","Was Chen Yi a villain? Yes.","First, he had killed Liu Erhu right under their noses. Then, he rescued the black-robed man who had been fighting the Evil Demons from Bright Moon Building in the West Market.","According to the laws of the Great Wei, if the Imprisonment Department were to capture him, he would certainly be brought to justice.","But it was also true that they had twice escaped with their lives because of him...","After a moment of silence, Fang Hongxiu took a deep breath and asked, \"What exactly are you trying to do?\"","Chen Yi chuckled. \"Hundred Households Fang has finally asked the right question.\"","He pointed at the corpse on the ground. \"I killed him.\"","\"You... you...\"","An Imprisonment Officer was about to reprimand him, but Fang Hongxiu raised a hand to stop him, her cold gaze fixed on Chen Yi.","\"If you came here to provoke my Imprisonment Department, then I admit, you have certainly succeeded.\"","\"But mark my words, as long as I, Fang Hongxiu, remain with the Imprisonment Department, I will never let you get away with this!\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. \"Doesn’t Hundred Households Fang want to know why I killed him?\"","\"The laws of the Great Wei state that a murderer must pay with his life!\"","\"Am I supposed to pay with my life for killing a practitioner of the Evil Demonic Dao from the Illusory Sound Sect?\"","\"Illu...\"","Fang Hongxiu’s eyes widened in realization. She looked down at the body on the ground. \"He’s the one from the Illusory Sound Sect? The one who helped those barbarian slaves escape earlier?\"","Chen Yi spread his hands, a hint of a smile in his eyes. \"Of course.\"","\"So by killing him, I’ve done the public a service, wouldn’t you say?\"","\"...Hmph. We’ll see after I’ve confirmed his identity.\"","\"Suit yourself.\"","The atmosphere had grown strange. Fang Hongxiu turned her head and asked:","\"Earlier, you said our search here was a waste of effort. Do you know something else?\"","Chen Yi nodded, smiling. \"This man from the Illusory Sound Sect accepted a reward from Bright Moon Building in the Western State. His goal was to rescue those barbarian slaves.\"","\"And the one who instructed him, if I’m not mistaken, is a man from the Poshisu Country who practices Black Magic.\"","\"Poshisu Country? Black Magic? Are you sure?\"","\"Find an experienced forensic doctor to dissect this black-robed man, and Hundred Households Fang will naturally know if what I’ve said is true.\"","Fang Hongxiu thought for a moment, then nodded and asked, \"Anything else?\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"That’s it. That’s all I know.\"","\"Then why are you telling us this?\"","\"Do you even have to ask? Fine, I might as well tell you.\"","\"In my life, I’ve hated no one more than the people of Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race. I hope Hundred Households Fang can find them and bring them to justice.\"","Fang Hongxiu gave him a long, hard look. \"If you truly thought that way, you shouldn’t have stopped my Imprisonment Department from investigating earlier.\"","’Of course, she couldn’t just believe him after a few words.’","’However, being bested by him twice—and yet still being alive—inevitably complicated her perception of him.’","Chen Yi could somewhat guess what she was thinking. He just chuckled, said nothing more, and clasped his fist in a farewell salute.","Seeing him turn and leave, Liu Lang glanced at Fang Hongxiu and the others, then followed.","\"We’re... we’re just letting them go like that?\"","\"What else? You want to go arrest them?\"","\"We can’t beat them, we can’t beat them... I think when we get back, we should report this to Lord Thousand Households and have a public arrest warrant issued...\"","Listening to the officers’ chatter, Fang Hongxiu watched with a complicated expression as Chen Yi and Liu Lang disappeared into the distance. She then took a deep breath and said:","\"Enough idle talk.\"","\"Old Ma, you take this... Evil Demon from the Illusory Sound Sect back to the Government Office. Have Coroner Zhang take a close look.\"","\"Zhao Ming, you and San’er go to the grain store and ask about the situation.\"","\"The rest of you, with me. Let’s see if we can find any trace of those barbarian slaves or the Wandering Martial Artists from Poshisu Country.\"","’Her thoughts were a tangled mess, but the case still had to be investigated.’","’As for Chen Yi... Fang Hongxiu would never give up on capturing him!’","...","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yi led Liu Lang north in search of the barbarian slaves, a thoughtful expression on his face.","’The reason he’d told Fang Hongxiu the truth was, of course, not as simple as he’d let on.’","’It was simply because he was currently staying with the Xiao Family and had more pressing matters to attend to, making it inconvenient for him to continue the investigation himself.’","’The Imprisonment Department, on the other hand, had every reason to pursue the case, especially after the barbarian slaves’ escape tonight.’","’For all these reasons, Chen Yi had simply laid everything out, letting Fang Hongxiu and her people probe the enemy’s background for him.’","Just then, seeing that no one was around, Liu Lang couldn’t help but ask in a low voice, \"Boss, can you tell me, how did you become so accomplished in the Saber Dao?\"","’He couldn’t care less about the Illusory Sound Sect or the barbarian slaves; his mind was completely focused on Chen Yi’s Saber Dao.’","Chen Yi glanced sideways at him. \"Didn’t I already tell you? I’m exceptionally talented.\"","\"But, but...\"","\"No buts.\"","\"First, tell me why you came to the East Market. I clearly told you to tail that person.\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang stopped in his tracks and slapped his forehead. \"Damn it, I almost forgot.\"","Chen Yi stopped as well. \"What is it?\"","\"The person you had me follow has been running back and forth between the Government Office and his residence for the past two days. Nothing out of the ordinary.\"","’Is that so... I thought he might have come to the East Market tonight as well.’","Liu Lang shook his head. \"He didn’t, but his son did.\"","Chen Yi frowned slightly. He didn’t ask immediately, instead leading him to a more secluded spot before gesturing for him to continue. \"Tell me the details.\"","\"Tonight, I was keeping watch outside that person’s residence when I happened to see his son meeting with someone...\"","To be precise, it was Liu Hong’s second son, Liu Taofang, meeting with someone at night that had caught Liu Lang’s attention.","He was about to eavesdrop when he saw Liu Taofang mysteriously board a carriage and leave.","Curious, he decided to tail him, wanting to see where Liu Taofang was headed so late at night.","After a few twists and turns, Liu Lang arrived at the southwest of the East Market—in the alleys where wealthy merchants and gentry gathered.","But before he could sneak in, he was drawn by the commotion from the Saber Dao that Chen Yi was displaying.","\"...If the uproar from your Saber Dao hadn’t been so great, I’d probably still be there watching Liu Taofang.\""]},{"number":346,"title":"Chapter 346 - 232: Some People Are Born Extraordinary (3)","paragraphs":["Chen Yi grunted but didn’t blame him.","The whole night had been filled with oddities; Liu Lang’s mistake was just one more.","Still, Chen Yi had a nagging intuition that the night’s events were connected to those \"Financiers.\"","The reason was simple: the grain store and its granary.","That alone made him think of the recent spike in grain prices in Shu State.","’The granary was burned, the grain supply is down... so there’s even more reason for the price to rise.’","’But what about those barbarian slaves and the Black Magic Masters from Poshisu Country?’","Chen Yi couldn’t see the connection between the two events, nor could he be one hundred percent certain his guess was correct.","He could only put the thought aside for now and wait a day or two to see if things at the grain store would unfold as he suspected.","Fortunately, Elder Master Xiao had a way to handle it, so Chen Yi didn’t have to worry too much about the Dingyuan Army’s funds and supplies.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi gestured for Liu Lang to lead him to Liu Taofang’s location, instructing him as they went:","\"I’ll let it slide this time. From now on, I need you to keep a close eye on the members of the Liu Family—especially him, of course.\"","Walking ahead, Liu Lang chuckled sheepishly. \"Don’t you worry, sir. Next time, I wouldn’t be distracted even if the sky were falling.\"","\"You’d better...\"","A moment of silence passed.","Liu Lang couldn’t help but speak up again. \"Boss, uh... you remember what you promised me, right?\"","\"A sparring match?\"","\"Right, right...\"","\"Don’t worry, you’ll get your turn.\"","Chen Yi had no intention of letting someone as eager for a beating as Liu Lang get away.","After his life-or-death battle with Yan Fusha, he had gained a clear understanding of his own strength.","Even if his Saber Dao was on par with Liu Lang’s, he could still win easily by relying on his Spear Dao.","He’d have to teach Liu Lang a lesson he wouldn’t forget.","Just as he was thinking this, two lines of large, golden text appeared before his eyes:","[Witnessed the barbarian slave riot at the East Market Grain Store. Reward: Sound Killing Technique \"Fallen Soul Tune\" [Yellow Tier], Opportunity +16.]","[Evaluation: Arrived on scene, heard the commotion... performance was subpar.]","’A Sound Killing Technique? A Cultivation Technique from the Illusory Sound Sect?’","Chen Yi scoffed inwardly, mentally shelving this Evil Demonic Dao-style Cultivation Technique alongside the \"Thousand Poison Skill\" he had received earlier.","Practicing it was out of the question. At most, he might flip through it later to understand the Martial Arts routines of the Evil Demons from the Five Poison Sect and the Illusory Sound Sect, just to be prepared.","Not long after.","Chen Yi followed Liu Lang to the southwest of the East Market, stopping outside a three-courtyard mansion.","He was about to go in and investigate when he heard voices, and he quickly signaled for Liu Lang to conceal his presence and hide.","The next moment, he saw the mansion’s main gate open and several carriages drive out.","The coachmen drove the carriages out to wait, as more people were still walking out from inside.","He could faintly hear the soft sounds of talking and laughter.","\"Young Master Liu, I guarantee that aged corn of yours will fetch a good price.\"","\"With your assurance, sir, I can rest easy.\"","\"Just let me say this first: if you end up offending people, you’d better not involve me.\"","\"You should be well aware of my father’s temperament, sir.\"","\"Crystal clear, haha... Lord Liu is a man of integrity and justice. We all admire him.\"","As they spoke, a group of men emerged together.","Chen Yi sized them up. A young, gentlemanly-looking man led the way, followed by three older, middle-aged men. He thought to himself:","’Businessmen?’","Just then, his gaze froze as he looked at the last person to walk out from inside the gate.","—It was none other than Mr. Lingchuan from Guiyun Academy, Zhu Lingchuan!","’What’s he doing here?’","Before he had time to think, Chen Yi watched as Liu Taofang, Zhu Lingchuan, and the others said their goodbyes, boarded their carriages, and departed.","Seeing this, Liu Lang nudged him, silently asking what to do next.","Chen Yi’s mind raced. \"You keep tailing him.\"","\"And you?\"","\"I have something to do. Go, don’t mind me.\"","Liu Lang grunted his assent and stealthily tailed Liu Taofang’s carriage.","Chen Yi, however, remained where he was, his eyes fixed on the mansion before him, his mind racing.","’Liu Taofang, son of Liu Hong, the Governor of Shu State.’","’Zhu Lingchuan, of the Zhu Family, brother of the Deputy Commander of the Shu State Capital Commandery.’","’The owner of this mansion, the Lin Family... and the corn...’","’Could these people be the ones manipulating the grain prices?’","’The Financiers?’","A cold glint flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes as he immediately rose and slipped into the mansion.","The truth was only a few questions away."]},{"number":347,"title":"Chapter 347 - 233: What Nerve","paragraphs":["If it had only been Liu Taofang, or a gathering of young masters from Shu State’s other great Noble Families, Chen Yi might not have given it a second thought.","But the presence of both Liu Taofang and Mr. Lingchuan forced him to be cautious.","After all, the family backgrounds of these two were anything but simple.","Liu Taofang was the son of Liu Hong, the Left Governor of Shu State, and Zhu Lingchuan was the younger brother of Zhu Hao, the Deputy Commander of the Shu State Capital Commandery.","Furthermore, Liu Hong controlled Shu State’s finances and taxes, while Zhu Hao managed its salt and iron industries. It could be said they held immense power and wanted for nothing.","If one also included certain individuals from the Inspectorate Office, it meant that behind these men stood the three most powerful commissions in all of Shu State.","How could Chen Yi not grow suspicious when a group like that gathered to discuss matters related to \"corn\"?","As these thoughts raced through his mind, Chen Yi slipped silently into the Lin Mansion, following the sound of the middle-aged man’s footsteps.","The night was deep and still, yet this mansion was brightly lit.","From the front courtyard to the back, a guard was posted every ten steps.","The security around the back courtyard was especially tight.","Dozens of guards in short, cyan tunics with long blades at their waists had the back courtyard surrounded, sealing it off completely.","’Does a legitimate businessman need this many guards?’","’Even the Hundred Herbs Hall, which brings in tens of thousands of silver taels a month, only has a little over a hundred guards.’","’And that number is only after including the group of Celestial Sect disciples who were recently granted the status of guards.’","The more he saw, the more certain Chen Yi became that this place was anything but simple.","After scouting the area for a moment,","he used the cover of the shadows to slip past the guards one by one.","With his current Cultivation and Dao Realm, an average Middle Third-Grade Martial Artist would have a hard time detecting his presence.","Especially since he had his Great Success [Martial Arts·Step] to rely on.","Soon, Chen Yi reached the back courtyard and hid in a corner lush with flowers and trees.","He scanned his surroundings, and his eyes began to shimmer with a faint, fluorescent light.","He used his Qi Observation Skill to probe the auras of the people inside the back courtyard’s various rooms.","There were several dozen people in total.","Most were maids with no Martial Arts Cultivation, while a few were the masters of the mansion.","The middle-aged man hadn’t returned to his chambers to rest; instead, he was sitting alone in the study.","Through the window, Chen Yi could faintly make out his silhouette cast by the candlelight. He appeared to be hunched over his desk, writing something.","Just as he was about to move closer, he heard voices from inside the house.","\"Lv Liu, bring the ginseng soup. I’ll take it to the master to help him recuperate.\"","\"Yes.\"","Then, Chen Yi saw a woman of a certain age, still possessing a fading beauty, push open the study door. She wore a silk coat and carried a bowl.","\"Master, the night is late and cold. Drink this ginseng soup to regain your strength.\"","\"Just set it down.\"","\"Master, why did Lord Liu’s son, Mr. Lingchuan, and Lord Ye from the Inspectorate Office come here tonight? What has you so worried?\"","\"A business matter.\"","\"In that case, is there anything my younger brother could help with?\"","The middle-aged man stiffened at her words and replied, his tone displeased, \"I know you care for your side of the family, but your brother is a hopeless case.\"","\"Last time, I told him to find some trustworthy people to spread a rumor. And what did he do? He hired a bunch of local scoundrels and nearly ruined everything.\"","\"If anyone finds out that I was the one deliberately slandering General Jinghong, then my head, and the heads of everyone in your family, will roll.\"","\"Please forgive him, Master. My younger brother is uneducated and ignorant of the world. He still needs to be tempered.\"","\"Tempered? Haven’t I given him enough chances?\"","\"Let’s not speak of this anymore. Go and get some rest.\"","After a moment of silence,","the woman spoke again. \"Master, remember to drink the ginseng soup while it’s still hot.\"","\"I know...\"","Seeing the woman exit the study, Chen Yi waited for a moment before quietly sneaking over.","’So it’s confirmed. This man, Lin, is one of the \"financiers.\"’","’He was talking about the time they slandered Xiao Jinghong. That must have been the incident with the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain; it couldn’t be anything else.’","In the span of about three breaths, Chen Yi was outside the study door. He quietly pushed it open a crack and peered inside.","To his surprise, the middle-aged man was slumped motionlessly in his chair.","Chen Yi let out a soft sound of surprise and entered the study. After closing the door, he drew closer and used his Qi Observation Skill to examine the man’s condition.","He saw two streams of black qi coiling within the man’s body.","One stream snaked up from his five viscera to his Forehead Acupoint.","The other descended from above, riddling his internal organs with holes.","To put it bluntly—the man was all but dead.","Chen Yi’s gaze swept across the room and landed on the empty bowl on the desk. He instantly understood: the man had been poisoned.","’Of all the times to kill him, why now?’","Chen Yi frowned and immediately shattered several wolf-hair brushes.","From the shattered remains, he extracted several long, thin bamboo needles and quickly inserted them into major acupoints on the man’s torso.","Then, circulating his True Essence, he began Controlling the Needles with Qi, dispelling most of the potent poison in the man’s body and performing a simple repair of his heart meridian.","After about fifteen minutes of work, he finally managed to revive the man.","’I went through too much trouble to find someone who knows what’s going on. I can’t just let you die.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself, then raised a finger and tapped the man lightly between the eyebrows. \"Wake up.\"","As soon as the words left his lips, the middle-aged man slowly opened his eyes. His face was ashen as he stared at Chen Yi.","A moment later, a look of bitter resentment crossed his pale face. His lips trembled as he rasped, \"She... how could she...\"","But in his current, ravaged state, he was so weak that his voice was barely a whisper.","Chen Yi, of course, knew who he was talking about. He calmly pulled over a chair, sat down beside him, and said,","\"You don’t have much time. You’d better save your strength.\"","He had indeed brought the man back to life, but that didn’t mean he was healed.","If not for his Great Success Medical Dao, coupled with the fact that the man had only been poisoned for a short time, it would have been impossible to revive him at all."]},{"number":348,"title":"Chapter 348 - 233: How Dare You","paragraphs":["The poison was simply too terrifyingly potent; within a few breaths, it had corroded most of the victim’s internal organs.","The middle-aged man was also aware of his condition. He looked at him for a long moment before suddenly sighing, \"Thank you.\"","Chen Yi shook his head slightly. \"How about a more substantial show of gratitude?\"","\"Answer a few of my questions, and I’ll let you leave your last words.\"","After a pause, he stared at the middle-aged man and said, \"I’m sure you don’t want the family business you worked so hard to build to just disappear, do you?\"","Although Chen Yi wasn’t certain if the man’s wife was responsible for the poison, he knew that an audacious and reckless man like this one would never be content to die in such a manner.","After a moment of silence, the middle-aged man slowly nodded, his voice low as he said, \"Fine.\"","Chen Yi was not surprised by his choice and asked directly, \"Tell me about tonight.\"","\"What were you, Liu Hong’s son, and Mr. Lingchuan discussing?\"","The middle-aged man seemed surprised that he knew about this. He hesitated for a moment before answering, \"Business.\"","\"Young Master Liu’s family owns a great deal of fertile land and has hundreds of thousands of *shi* of grain in storage. He wanted me to help him sell it.\"","\"So that’s why you manipulated the grain prices?\"","The middle-aged man was stunned. \"You... How could you know?\"","’As I thought,’ Chen Yi said, \"I wouldn’t have come looking for you if I weren’t fully prepared.\"","The middle-aged man figured that made sense and continued, \"Young Master Liu needed too many silver coins. The usual grain prices wouldn’t be enough for him, so I came up with this Method.\"","\"What Method?\"","\"Burning the summer grain of the Three Towns to create a famine? Or using the Xiao Family’s large-scale grain purchase as an opportunity to drastically raise prices?\"","\"You... you...\"","Seeing the middle-aged man’s reaction, Chen Yi knew he had guessed correctly.","’These people really did it all for silver coins.’","Their plot was simple.","Once the summer grain in the Three Towns was burned, regardless of whether the Xiao Family had staged an inside job, the Dingyuan Army would need a large supply of grain.","This would inevitably cause grain prices in Shu State to soar.","Then, Liu Taofang could seize the opportunity to sell off his stored grain.","It was the same this time—Elder Master Xiao had been punished by the Holy Emperor and needed to replenish the grain for Iron Wall Town.","These people were seizing the chance to raise prices, most likely intending to force the Elder Master to buy grain at an exorbitant price.","Even more unscrupulously, once it drew the wrath of heaven and the resentment of the people, they could shift the blame onto the Xiao Family.","A scheme like this was nothing short of venomous.","Having figured it all out, Chen Yi asked in a cold tone, \"Did you also burn down the granary in the East Market yourselves?\"","The middle-aged man was even more astonished. \"The granary was burned down?\"","\"You didn’t do it?\"","\"No, it wasn’t! The East Market stored as much as a hundred thousand *shi* of grain. I... How could I possibly do something like that?\"","’It seems the incident at the East Market has a different cause.’","Chen Yi mentally noted this and continued his questioning, \"Did Mr. Lingchuan come here to sell grain as well?\"","The middle-aged man shook his head. \"No, he didn’t.\"","\"Mr. Lingchuan’s older brother, Lord Zhu Hao, has a shipment of ironware. He came here to entrust me with completing a transaction with King Landu, the Bandit King of Poshisu Country.\"","’Bandit King, King Landu... Horse bandits?’","Chen Yi’s brow furrowed slightly. This was the second time he had heard that name.","The first time, he had heard it from Lou Yuxue. Back then, the White Tiger Guard’s Golden Banner Officer, Jiang Xing, had mentioned contacting this person.","He just hadn’t expected that this King Landu wasn’t a Prince or Marquis from Poshisu Country, but the leader of a band of horse bandits.","’What would the White Tiger Guard want with him?’","However, now was not the time to investigate this matter, so Chen Yi simply said:","\"Privately selling ironware to another country is high treason.\"","The middle-aged man nodded with a bitter expression. \"I am just a merchant. If there is profit to be made, I don’t think about other things.\"","Chen Yi was well aware of that. He snorted. \"Last question. You’ve targeted the Xiao Family several times now. Is there any other reason for it?\"","\"N-no, there isn’t. We just found it opportune. Both times, our actions happened to make the grain prices rise faster.\"","\"Is that all?\"","The middle-aged man nodded repeatedly, coughing weakly. \"We... we only did it for silver coins. We never wanted to harm the Xiao Family...\"","’Harm them? How could Chen Yi not know the truth?’","The reason these people targeted the Xiao Family was simple—the Xiao Family’s power was declining, and they refused to associate with them.","Even if someone else had been in the Xiao Family’s position, they would have acted just as ruthlessly.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi gave him a deep look. \"You have half an hour to get your affairs in order.\"","With that, he rose and started to walk out.","However, when the corner of his eye caught a piece of paper spread out on the desk, he stopped and picked it up.","He saw that it was not written in the script of Great Wei, but in lines of strange, foreign-looking characters.","\"Is this the Poshisu script?\"","The middle-aged man opened his mouth, wanting to take it back, but seeing that Chen Yi was holding it firmly, he could only nod helplessly. \"Yes.\"","\"It’s for King Landu?\"","\"Yes...\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, put the paper away, and walked straight out of the study.","The middle-aged man watched him disappear, a desolate expression appearing on his face.","\"Don’t blame me, sigh...\"","\"I’m about to die. How can I care about so much?\"","Before he had even finished speaking, he used all his remaining strength to sweep everything off the desk, roaring desperately:","\"Guards!\"","\"Lin Huai, Lin Cheng, get in here, quickly!!\"","In an instant, several Guards arrived in the rear courtyard and rushed anxiously toward the study.","\"Master, what’s wrong?\"","\"The one... the one who harmed me was my wife! Get... get her, and her whole family!\"","\"I want them dead!\"","The people in the other rooms also came out to see what was happening when they heard the commotion.","Only the middle-aged mistress in the main hall was left slumped on the bed in disbelief, muttering endlessly.","\"No, Master, Master, it wasn’t me...\"","Before long, the middle-aged man’s voice came from the study again: \"Go... summon my son...\"","Chen Yi listened quietly for a moment, then slipped away.","The backlash from a dying man was bound to be bloody.","’But what did that have to do with him?’","’Still, he was lucky someone had made a move to poison the man; otherwise, he probably wouldn’t have been able to interrogate him and get anything tonight.’","「A short while later.」","Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden, changed out of his Night Clothes, and stood calmly by the window, gazing at the bright moon in the night sky.","Tonight’s events had truly exceeded his expectations.","He had thought it was just a minor commotion, never imagining it would lead to so many other matters.","He especially hadn’t expected that the so-called \"Financiers\" would be so audacious—burning the grain supplies of the Three Towns just for silver coins!","He knew that if such a thing were exposed, it would surely bring about a disaster that would cost them their lives.","Not only would the nine generations of the Lin Family have to die, but Liu Taofang, Zhu Lingchuan, and everyone in their families would have to die as well.","’Merchants chase profits. Sometimes their nerve is even greater than that of the Princes and Marquises who command armies.’","’What’s more, they have Liu Hong and Zhu Hao backing them?’","’But what role do those two play in all this?’","’Liu Hong’s part is hard to say for now, but Zhu Hao must be guilty of heinous crimes.’","For a man who dared to privately sell ironware to horse bandits from Poshisu Country, \"audacious and reckless\" was not a strong enough description.","After a moment of thought, a cold look appeared on Chen Yi’s face.","’The Governor’s Office, the Capital Commandery, the Inspectorate Office, and perhaps some of the Noble Families they’ve roped in... ’","’A behemoth like that... I’m afraid ordinary methods won’t be enough to deal with them.’","Killing them would certainly solve the problem once and for all.","But if he did that, Chen Yi couldn’t predict what would happen to Shu State afterward.","It might trigger upheaval in the Imperial Court or other State Capitals.","That would probably make the Xiao Family’s situation even worse.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi took a deep breath, his expression gradually calming.","’Demons and monsters, fiends and foul creatures... whatever they are, they’ve all shown their faces now.’","’As for the rest...’","...","「Meanwhile.」","In a residence about twenty *li* from the Xiao Family estate, Liu Lang was watching a nearby study with great interest.","His mind had been in turmoil, spurred by Chen Yi’s Great Success in Saber Dao.","Who would have known that after following Liu Taofang back to the Liu Family estate, he would see the esteemed Liu Hong waiting in the courtyard.","What surprised Liu Lang even more was that the moment Liu Hong saw Liu Taofang, he immediately slapped him twice across the face.","Now, nearly half an hour had passed.","Liu Hong was still in the study, whipping Liu Taofang and roaring curses as he did so.","\"You have some nerve!\"","\"Who told you to get involved with the Lin Clan Chamber of Commerce?\"","\"Do you have any idea what the Lin Clan Chamber of Commerce’s background is?\"","\"They’re people from the Ji State Trading Company! Are you trying to get me killed by associating with them?\"","Listening to Liu Hong’s furious curses and Liu Taofang’s begging cries, Liu Lang couldn’t help but smile.","All this talk of the Lin Clan Chamber of Commerce and the Ji State Trading Company was nothing compared to the touching scene of \"fatherly love and filial piety\" before him.","Liu Hong had no idea someone was watching from outside and continued to yell:","\"Speak! What have you been doing with that Lin Huai’an all this time?!\"","\"I... I didn’t...\"","CRACK!"]},{"number":349,"title":"Chapter 349 - 234: He Who Lacks Venom Is No Great Man","paragraphs":["\"Father, my alliance with Lin Huai’an wasn’t for my own selfish gain! It was to get a good price for the old grain in our Liu Family’s warehouses.\"","CRACK!","Seeing Liu Taofang was still trying to change the subject, Liu Hong struck him again with the whip.","\"I don’t want to hear your excuses!\"","\"Just tell me, what exactly did you and Lin Huai’an do for that silver!\"","At this moment, Liu Hong had lost all his usual calm and composure. He glared at Liu Taofang with a grim expression.","Even though he was only dressed in simple white robes, he still carried an air of authority.","Liu Taofang, on the other hand, was a mess. His brocade robes were in tatters, with thin lines of blood seeping through the tears.","Even so, he remained kneeling ramrod straight on the floor, not daring to move a muscle.","His rather fair-featured face was filled with terror and indignation.","\"I... I don’t know...\"","CRACK, CRACK, CRACK!","Liu Hong lashed him three times without mercy, leaving his flesh torn and bleeding.","\"You don’t know, or you don’t dare to say?\"","\"Do you think I won’t find out what you did just because you refuse to talk?\"","Liu Hong paused for a moment, glaring at him with ice-cold eyes. He asked in a low, heavy tone:","\"Setting fire to the summer grain in the Three Towns—was that your idea or Lin Huai’an’s?\"","Clutching his wounds, Liu Taofang looked up in astonishment and stammered, \"Father, you... how did you...\"","A flicker of rage flashed in Liu Hong’s eyes. Instead of reaching for the whip, he strode forward and kicked his son, sending him sprawling to the ground.","\"You wretched son! You wretched son!\"","\"How dare you! The absolute nerve of you!\"","\"Father, Father, I was wrong! I know I was wrong...\"","\"You know you were wrong?\"","\"No, you’re not sorry. You’re just hurting from the beating!\"","\"How could you commit such a treacherous act? You... are you trying to get your father killed?!\"","Listening to Liu Hong’s enraged shouts coming from the study, the smile on Liu Lang’s face receded slightly as understanding dawned on him.","’So they’ve found the person who burned the summer grain in the Three Towns. The one who gave thirty thousand gold to Black Tooth was actually Governor Liu Hong’s second son.’","’And who is this Lin Huai’an?’","After a moment’s thought, Liu Lang sneered to himself. ’It’s not important. As long as we have Liu Taofang, the boss can definitely dig up the others.’","’The boss even outmaneuvered and killed Liu Wen, the second son of the Jing State Liu Family. What’s one more second son from a lesser branch of the Liu Family to him?’","Liu Lang knew all too well how skilled Chen Yi was at scheming.","’Why rack my own brain when it’s so much easier to just pass this information on to Chen Yi?’","Besides, in his heart, Chen Yi, having achieved Great Success in the three Daos of Spear, Punch, and Blade, was already an existence comparable to an Immortal God.","He certainly wasn’t about to do anything unnecessary.","Just then, Liu Hong, who must have grown tired of the beating, threw the whip aside and said in a cold voice:","\"Aside from that incident, was the recent rise in grain prices in the Prefecture City also your idea?\"","Liu Taofang stiffened at the question. Clutching his wounds, he knelt up straight again and silently nodded.","Liu Hong stared at him for a long time, then suddenly sighed. \"Fang’er, before you did these two things, did you think through the consequences?\"","\"I... I did think about it... Once the summer grain in the Three Towns was burned, the Xiao Family would become... become the target of everyone’s anger.\"","\"And you weren’t afraid they would trace it back to you?\"","Liu Taofang said in a low voice, \"After discussing it with Lin Huai’an, I hired the Bright Moon Building to take action. They... they don’t know who we are.\"","Liu Hong gave him a noncommittal look. \"If you don’t want anyone to know, you shouldn’t have done it in the first place.\"","\"Luckily for you, the Xiao Family was prepared and killed all the attackers. Otherwise, with someone as capable as Xiao Yuan, how could he not have guessed who his adversary was?\"","\"Besides, your cousin Liu Wen also made a move, didn’t he?\"","He paused, then continued to ask, \"Before that, were you aware that Liu Wen was also participating?\"","Liu Taofang subconsciously shook his head. \"I didn’t know.\"","\"After Lin Huai’an and I decided on the plan, I... I didn’t ask about it again. It was all handled by Lin Huai’an; he was the one who found the people.\"","\"You didn’t hear a single word?\"","\"That’s right... But while I didn’t know my cousin Liu Wen was involved, I did know that someone else had approached the Bright Moon Building to do the same thing—burn the summer grain in the Three Towns.\"","\"Who?\"","\"A man from the Jianghu, called ’Sword Madman’ Liu Lang.\"","Liu Hong’s brow furrowed slightly. \"That name sounds familiar. I feel like I’ve heard it somewhere.\"","Liu Taofang quickly replied, \"Father, have you forgotten? When Liu Jing first came to Shu State, he hired this ’Sword Madman’ through the Bright Moon Building to rob the Xiao Family Medicine Hall of its medicinal supplies.\"","\"So it was him...\"","Outside the door, Liu Lang couldn’t help but grin upon hearing this.","’This Liu Taofang is a real fool.’","’Leaving such a huge matter entirely in Lin Huai’an’s hands and knowing nothing about it.’","’No, he’s not completely ignorant.’","’Liu Taofang must have asked about it once at the beginning.’","’But he stopped asking questions later when the boss started going in and out of the Bright Moon Building.’","With that thought, Liu Lang went back to listening to the father and son’s conversation.","\"Fang’er, you didn’t notice anything unusual after that?\"","\"Father, I... I don’t know what you’re referring to?\"","Liu Hong looked at him with an expression of utter disappointment, cursing:","\"Your cousin Liu Wen is dead, the Xiao Family’s Xiao Dongchen is dead, everyone from the Bright Moon Building and the military insiders in the Three Towns are dead—and you didn’t notice anything?\"","\"Stupid! Hopelessly stupid!\"","\"You, Liu Wen, and Xiao Dongchen were all played, and you didn’t realize a thing?\"","Liu Taofang opened his mouth, wanting to say something, but when he saw his father’s face, he couldn’t get a single word out.","\"Father, are... are you saying there was another group hiding in the shadows?\"","Liu Hong snorted. \"If I’m not mistaken, the person behind that Liu Lang put on the same show for all four of you: you, the Bright Moon Building, Liu Wen, and Xiao Dongchen.\"","Liu Taofang was stunned for a moment. \"A show? He... Why would he do that?\""]},{"number":350,"title":"Chapter 350 - 234: A Man Must Be Ruthless (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"The reason...\"","Liu Hong’s gaze shifted north, toward the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, as he spoke in a low voice,","\"If I’m not mistaken, that person must have done it to help the Xiao Family.\"","According to his deduction, Liu Wen and Xiao Dongchen must have been targeted by that person for some reason.","Then, that person took advantage of the Bright Moon Building’s trip to the Three Towns to eliminate all of them at once.","Realization dawned on Liu Taofang’s face. \"Dad, are you saying the three hundred thousand silver taels the Xiao Family got from Xiao Dongchen... belonged to my cousin, Liu Wen?\"","\"So you’re not completely hopeless.\"","\"I don’t know what method he used, but judging by the result, that person is no simple character.\"","At this, Liu Hong’s expression grew even colder.","\"Fortunately, you and Lin Huai’an were well hidden, so that person probably didn’t uncover your identity. Otherwise...\"","Otherwise, not only would Liu Taofang and Lin Huai’an have been targeted, but even he, the Governor, would likely have been implicated.","As the full picture became clear, Liu Taofang felt a wave of lingering fear.","Now he finally understood why Liu Hong was so furious.","\"Dad, then... then what should we do now?\"","Liu Hong shot him a look and snorted. \"Scared now, are you? Why didn’t you think more when you were blinded by greed?\"","\"I was wrong.\"","Seeing the remorse on Liu Taofang’s face, Liu Hong sighed internally.","This son of his couldn’t compare to his eldest; he was incompetent, shallow, and vainglorious. But he was still his son.","Blood is thicker than water, after all.","\"Fang’er, do you remember what I taught you and your brother when you were young?\"","\"To achieve great things, you must plan before you act.\"","\"Now, I will teach you a second lesson—to achieve great things, you must also be willing to use any means necessary.\"","Liu Taofang paused, a look of confusion on his face. \"Dad?\"","’The things I did with Lin Huai’an were all crimes punishable by beheading. Shouldn’t that count as using any means necessary?’","Liu Hong knew his son hadn’t understood. He lowered his voice slightly and said, \"Let’s put aside the matter of the summer rations for the Three Towns for now and just talk about the recent rise in grain prices.\"","\"When you and Lin Huai’an were plotting, were you planning to use Old Marquis Xiao’s punishment from the Holy Emperor as an opportunity to pin everything on the Xiao Family?\"","Liu Taofang nodded and admitted honestly, \"Yes, that was my intention.\"","\"The Xiao Family needs to prepare provisions for the Three Towns, so they’ll have to buy from the two markets. It’s only natural that would cause grain prices to rise.\"","\"Plus, the summer grain harvest in Shu State was poor this year, so a larger increase should be justifiable.\"","Liu Hong glared at him. \"And once the price is high enough, you sell off our family’s old grain reserves and make a huge profit, is that it?\"","\"I can’t hide anything from you...\"","\"But in doing so, did you ever consider how the Xiao Family would react?\"","\"They... they would probably approach Lin Huai’an to negotiate. I’ve thought about it. When the time comes, I’ll just have Lin Huai’an do Marquis Xiao a favor.\"","\"Do him a favor?\"","Liu Hong almost laughed in exasperation. \"What gives you the confidence to say something like that?\"","Liu Taofang looked at him, confused. \"Dad, does the Xiao Family really have any other options?\"","Hearing this, Liu Hong shook his head. \"You... you know too little about the Xiao Family, and even less about the Old Marquis.\"","\"The Xiao Family is indeed in a bind right now, but as long as the Old Marquis is alive, it’s difficult for anyone to use ordinary tricks against him... at least, not in Shu State.\"","\"Did you know that because of how recklessly you and Lin Huai’an have been raising prices, the Old Marquis is already planning to borrow grain from Guangyue Prefecture?\"","Liu Taofang was stunned. \"Borrow grain from Guangyue Prefecture?\" he asked in astonishment.","\"The Old Marquis... is he planning to borrow from Duke Qian of the Zhang Family?\"","Liu Hong snorted. \"Now do you see how foolish you’ve been?\"","\"It’s laughable that you decided to make a move without even a clear understanding of your opponent’s capabilities.\"","\"But Dad, Lin... Lin Huai’an said before that the Old Marquis is extremely proud and would never ask outsiders for help.\"","\"And you believe what he says?\"","\"Did you know that besides the old grain you control, Lin Huai’an has already prepared nearly a million shi of grain?\"","\"What?!\"","Liu Taofang stared at him blankly, his expression a mess of confusion.","He clearly hadn’t expected the Old Marquis to make such a choice, and he couldn’t fathom why Lin Huai’an hadn’t told him about this.","’Or... did Lin Huai’an know all along and was just playing me for a fool?’","Liu Hong glanced at him and waved a hand in annoyance. \"Get up and speak.\"","Liu Taofang pressed his lips together, kowtowed once while still kneeling, and only then carefully sat down on the edge of a chair.","After a moment of silence, Liu Hong tapped on the back of his chair and said, \"I know you were deceived by Lin Huai’an, so I can’t blame you for this matter. But from now on, you must not be so quick to trust others.\"","\"Yes, I understand.\"","\"No, you don’t!\"","\"Are you thinking of going to find Lin Huai’an after tonight?\"","Liu Taofang lowered his head without a word, his silence a clear admission.","Liu Hong, well aware of his son’s temperament, didn’t lose his temper again. He just said calmly,","\"Lin Huai’an may be a merchant, but for him to have gotten this far, he is obviously no pushover.\"","\"What’s more, he’s backed by that group from the Ji State Trading Company.\"","Liu Taofang nodded silently and asked in a low voice, \"Dad, you’ve been mentioning the Ji State Trading Company. What’s their background?\"","Seeing his son calm down so quickly, Liu Hong felt a flicker of relief.","\"The Ji State Chamber of Commerce? They’re a pack of jackals who are obsessed with money.\"","\"Although I don’t know much about them, I am aware of what they’ve been doing up north.\"","\"Up north?\"","\"Yes. They’ve made a lot of silver through the northern grasslands’ Mutual Market. Some of it is legitimate, and some of it isn’t.\"","Understanding dawned on Liu Taofang, and his eyes widened slightly. \"Dad, are you saying... they’re smuggling?\"","Liu Hong nodded slightly. \"Salt, iron, weapons, armor... as long as those nomadic races on the grasslands, who are little different from the Barbarian Race, can pay the price, there’s nothing the Ji State Trading Company won’t dare to sell.\"","\"Aren’t they afraid of being discovered?\"","\"Discovered by whom? And who would dare to discover them?\"","\"Everyone who knows has long been bought off, even some of the Nine Ministers in the Imperial Court...\"","Liu Hong stopped there and shook his head. \"You only need to understand one thing—Lin Huai’an is their man, the pawn they chose to replicate their northern operations here in Shu State.\"","Liu Taofang said nothing, simply staring at his father without blinking.","Of all that he had heard, this revelation hit him the hardest.","After a moment’s thought, he said in a bitter tone, \"Dad, then... does that mean I’ve been played by Lin Huai’an this whole time?\"","\"Why... why would he...\"","Liu Taofang suddenly realized something and looked at Liu Hong. \"Was he trying to drag you into it as well?\"","Liu Hong glanced at him, lifting his chin slightly. \"The fact that you figured that out means I didn’t waste my breath telling you all this.\"","\"That Lin Huai’an has been in Shu State for quite some time. How could he not have approached me?\"","\"Then... then you...\"","Before Liu Taofang could finish, Liu Hong waved his hand dismissively. \"He’s just a pawn. What right does he have to be on equal footing with me?\"","He paused, a cold sneer appearing on his face. \"Besides, he dared to plot against my son. How could I possibly let him get away with it?\"","Hearing this, a complex mix of gratitude and shame appeared on Liu Taofang’s face.","He had wanted to do something for the family, but it had backfired completely. In the end, his father still had to be the one to clean up his mess.","\"Dad, just tell me. What do you need me to do?\"","Liu Hong said flatly, \"Do nothing.\"","\"Starting today, you will stay in the mansion and go nowhere. No matter who comes looking for you, you stick to one story—you don’t know Lin Huai’an!\"","Liu Taofang didn’t understand why, but he nodded obediently and didn’t ask any more questions.","Seeing this, Liu Hong’s expression softened.","\"The Shu State of today is not the Shu State of five or ten years ago. The situation is so complex that an ordinary person could never make sense of it.\"","\"If I weren’t in the Governor’s Office and didn’t have a good understanding of certain noble families and individuals, I’m afraid I too would have been ensnared in someone’s plot.\"","He looked at Liu Taofang and continued, \"This disaster you’ve faced isn’t entirely a bad thing. From now on, learn more from your older brother and don’t make this kind of mistake again.\"","Liu Taofang first nodded, then, as if remembering something, asked, \"Dad, then... what about Lin Huai’an?\"","\"When I met with him tonight, we already decided on our next move. We were... we were going to keep raising the grain prices.\"","Hearing this, an inscrutable smile appeared on Liu Hong’s face. \"You don’t need to worry about that. Just stay put and rest easy.\"","\"But...\"","\"Why worry about a dead man?\"","’A... a dead man?’","’Who? Lin Huai’an?’","Liu Taofang felt a jolt of shock, and his gaze toward Liu Hong flickered with astonishment.","Liu Hong met his gaze and said calmly, \"Fang’er, remember what I told you today.\"","\"Those who wish to achieve great things must be willing to use any means necessary.\"","\"For anyone who stands in your way, there is only one outcome... death!\"","Outside the door, Liu Lang couldn’t help but shudder.","’He’d already guessed that the man named Lin Huai’an was likely one of the people he had seen outside that residence in the East Market.’","’He wondered if the man was now dead, just as Liu Hong had said.’","’No wonder.’","’No wonder the boss had sent him to watch Liu Hong—with this level of ruthlessness alone, Governor Liu Hong was someone who demanded serious attention!’"]},{"number":351,"title":"Chapter 351 - 235: Unexpected Visitor","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, within the Xiao Mansion.","In the main hall of the otherwise dim Qingjing Residence, an oil lamp quietly flickered to life.","The candlelight wavered.","Elder Master Xiao, draped in a thick, padded robe, leaned back in a Grandmaster’s Chair. He rubbed the bridge of his nose while listening to Xiao Jing’s report from the shadows.","\"...The barbarian slaves have not yet been found.\"","Seeing that the Elder Master remained silent, Xiao Jing continued, \"The major grain merchants in the East Market have suffered heavy losses. It’s said their warehouses contained a hundred thousand bushels of grain.\"","The Elder Master lowered his hand, his cloudy, bloodshot eyes turning to him. \"A hundred thousand bushels?\"","Xiao Jing nodded from the shadows. \"At least that much, if not more.\"","\"However, your subordinate has ascertained that those merchants have other storehouses, which should still contain a considerable amount of grain.\"","\"You suspect tonight’s events were just an act put on by those merchants?\"","\"To be honest, Marquis, that is precisely my suspicion.\"","The Elder Master frowned slightly, pondering for a moment before saying, \"That is indeed a possibility.\"","\"Willing to sacrifice a hundred thousand bushels so they can raise the price of grain again tomorrow... That is something those merchants are capable of doing.\"","But after saying that, he shook his head. \"However, the probability is low.\"","\"According to what you just said, those few barbarian slaves were rescued.\"","\"If the grain merchants were behind this, wouldn’t it have been better to just kill them and leave no witnesses?\"","Xiao Jing paused, then lowered his head. \"You are right, Marquis. I will investigate further.\"","The Elder Master said, \"Don’t make any moves for now.\"","\"A few merchants are irrelevant. What’s important is the person pulling the strings behind them.\"","\"In the territory of Shu State, if a few mere merchants dare to play such tricks against our Xiao Family,\"","As he spoke, a cold, self-deprecating look crossed his face. \"then it seems it’s time for this old, sick tiger to die.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jing stepped out of the shadows and knelt on one knee, his face full of shame. \"Forgive me, Marquis. It is my incompetence.\"","The Elder Master waved his hand. \"It has nothing to do with you.\"","\"In the end, it all goes back to that great battle. Fengchun and Wanqing died, and more than half of the Hidden Guard and the Punishment Hall were lost...\"","He recalled those past events, a desolate look appearing on his face as he sighed softly.","\"The Xiao Family suffered devastating losses, which has led to our current predicament.\"","Despite these words, Xiao Jing remained motionless on the ground, his heart still filled with self-blame.","The Elder Master glanced at him, saw through his thoughts, and a smile returned to his face.","\"Fortunately, I can still hold on for a while longer. A few old friends will still help me out for old times’ sake.\"","\"Let’s see... It’ll take that old codger Zhang Xuan two or three days to receive the letter, and another two or three days to reply. That gives me just enough time to see who is standing behind those grain merchants.\"","Xiao Jing understood his meaning and lowered his head. \"Rest assured, Marquis. I will do everything in my power to uncover them!\"","\"Just do your best.\"","The Elder Master added with a chuckle, \"I have been thinking a lot these past few days.\"","\"Sometimes, it is the will of heaven, which cannot be changed by human effort.\"","\"Just like when the summer grain from the Three Towns was burned. It was a perilous situation, but in the end, it was our Xiao Family that benefited.\"","The smile on his aged face widened. \"From this, you can see that Heaven has not abandoned the Xiao Family.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jing’s expression relaxed slightly. He replied, \"As long as you take care of your health, Marquis, the family will not fall.\"","\"You kid, you really know how to comfort an old man. I already have one foot in the grave, how am I supposed to ’take care’ of myself?\"","\"Forgive me, Marquis...\"","The Elder Master smiled, knowing he didn’t mean anything by it, and changed the subject. \"What about the other matter I had you look into?\"","\"Has that boss from Hundred Herbs Hall shown his face yet?\"","Xiao Jing replied with some exasperation, \"Ever since that night he spent with the Second Son-in-law on the Painted Boat, that Boss Chen Yu seems to have vanished into thin air. We still haven’t found any trace of his whereabouts.\"","\"I considered asking at Hundred Herbs Hall or questioning the Second Son-in-law, but I was worried it might be counterproductive.\"","The Elder Master grunted in acknowledgment and thought for a moment before waving his hand. \"Forget it, forget it.\"","\"The situation is complicated right now, and you don’t have many men to begin with. Focus on our primary targets for now.\"","After giving the order, he continued, \"After Hundred Herbs Hall expands, I’ll have Wan’er invite that Boss Chen.\"","Xiao Jing replied, \"Yes, sir,\" bowed, and stood to leave, but then he heard the Elder Master ask another question.","\"Has there been any word from Jinghong?\"","\"Reporting to the Marquis, all is normal on the General’s end. The Wu Mountain Mutual Market will be completed in a month at most.\"","The Elder Master smiled and nodded. \"Send a message for me. Tell her not to skimp on silver; she should spend what needs to be spent.\"","\"Since I’m already borrowing grain from Zhang Xuan, I might as well borrow some silver coins too. It will stop those blind fools from trying to make an issue of it.\"","Originally, he hadn’t planned on asking, but the current situation had forced him to take this undesirable course of action.","But once he had actually swallowed his pride, he realized: borrowing grain is still borrowing, and borrowing silver is also borrowing.","Why not solve some troubles once and for all?","Hearing this, however, left a bitter taste in Xiao Jing’s mouth.","He knew very well that the Elder Master had spent his life on horseback and was an immensely proud man.","Forget borrowing money or grain from others; even in the Xiao Family’s most difficult times, the Elder Master still provided for his old soldiers.","\"Take care, Marquis. I will write to the General at once.\"","\"Go on, go on.\"","After the man left, Elder Master Xiao sat alone for a moment before blowing out the oil lamp. His tall frame seemed to stoop a little as he walked slowly back to his chambers.","Only when he lay down on the bed did he let out a long breath, clutching his chest as he let out a few suppressed coughs.","’Oh, dear heavens, just let this old man hold on for a few more years.’","’Once I’ve crossed over to the other side, you can do with me what you will...’","...","Before dawn, the sky was dim and overcast. A cool autumn breeze blew, causing the lanterns hanging under the eaves of Spring Lotus Garden and Jiaxing Garden to spin gently, illuminating several busy figures.","Because Xiao Wan’er, Chen Yi, and the others were going out today, Xiaodie, Juan’er, and Cui’er had started their work early."]},{"number":352,"title":"Chapter 352 - 235: Unexpected Visitor (2)","paragraphs":["To avoid disturbing Chen Yi and the others, they moved as quietly as possible, placing the prepared luggage onto the carriage outside the garden.","Wang Lixing and Liu Si’er were waiting by the carriage, chatting idly from time to time.","\"I heard first thing this morning that a big fire broke out in the East Market last night. It was just put out.\"","\"Besides a few grain storehouses, several neighboring buildings were also hit, especially the cloth merchants.\"","\"I heard a warehouse storing medicinal herbs was also affected. Most of the herbs are gone.\"","Wang Lixing watched the entrances to Jiaxing Garden and Spring Lotus Garden as he asked in a low voice:","\"Has the price of grain gone up?\"","Liu Si’er grinned. \"Do you even have to ask? With those bastards’ personalities, after a loss this big, how could they not raise the prices?\"","\"That’s true...\"","As they chatted, Xiaodie, Juan’er, and Cui’er came over, each carrying a few small boxes.","Liu Si’er and Wang Lixing went forward to take them and placed them all in one of the carriages.","Xiaodie wiped the sweat from her forehead and said with a smile, \"The Young Master didn’t bring many things, this is all of it.\"","Beside her, Juan’er and Cui’er also said they were finished.","\"Thank you both for waiting. We’ll go back to attend to the Miss and Young Master now.\"","Wang Lixing nodded, gave the carriage a final check, and locked it.","\"Brother Si, the journey isn’t far, but it’s outside the city. Keep a careful watch.\"","Liu Si’er hopped onto the carriage and said, \"With Miss Xie and Miss Shen following, ordinary bandits won’t be able to get close.\"","\"I’m talking about the Second Young Master.\"","\"Don’t worry, I’ll keep a close eye on him.\"","Just then, Xiaodie, who had just gone back inside, emerged from Spring Lotus Garden with Xiao Wuge.","Wang Lixing said no more. He patted Liu Si’er on the shoulder and led Xiao Wuge toward the Martial Arts Arena.","Liu Si’er watched them walk away, then turned his head and asked with a smile, \"Miss Xiaodie, is the Second Young Master awake yet?\"","Xiaodie was on her way to the rear kitchen. Hearing his question, she replied, \"Not yet. Are you looking for the Young Master?\"","Liu Si’er thought of the secret letter he received yesterday and said with a nonchalant smile, \"Just asking.\"","Xiaodie, unsuspecting, hurried to the rear kitchen.","In fact, Chen Yi was already fully dressed and had calmly taken a seat in the living room.","He had naturally heard the voices outside, but his expression didn’t change at all. His eyes were fixed on the screen of light before him:","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Top Grade: In the third quarter of the Si Hour, Chen Yunfan will duel Cui Qingwu in swordsmanship inside Tingyu Pavilion. A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","Chen Yi read it twice and mused to himself.","’They’re dueling with swordsmanship... Tsk. I’m afraid Cui Qingwu has found out that my brother has been hiding his Martial Arts skills.’","’I just don’t know if he’s aware of Cui Qingwu’s identity. He probably is, right?’","In their previous few meetings, although Chen Yi didn’t have a good impression of Cui Qingwu, he could still tell how she felt about his brother, Chen Yunfan.","—In those eyes, there was room for no one but Chen Yunfan.","Under these circumstances, Chen Yi found it hard to believe that his brother truly disliked his fiancée, Cui Qingwu.","’Or maybe Chen Yunfan’s issue isn’t with Cui Qingwu, but with the Cui Family?’","That was also a possibility.","Chen Yi chuckled. \"It feels a bit like a case of bickering lovers. A pity I won’t get to see them duel.\"","He had to accompany Xiao Wan’er outside the city today to look at potential sites for the Medical Dao Academy. He might not even be back by the Xu hour, let alone the Wu hour.","With these thoughts, he closed the screen of light and his gaze shifted to the world outside his door.","The sky was just beginning to brighten as the stars and moon faded. Within Spring Lotus Garden, only the crisp chirping of insects could be heard.","The scenery was quite pleasant.","However, fallen petals and leaves were scattered across the garden.","Chen Yi watched for a moment, and his thoughts inevitably drifted to the events of last night.","A chessboard materialized in his mind, and one by one, Heizi fell onto the board.","They seemed as scattered as the fallen petals and leaves, but no matter where the Heizi were placed, they all surrounded a single, gleaming black piece in the center.","That piece represented none other than the Jing State Liu Family.","Or rather, Liu Hong.","Chen Yi casually picked up a white stone and moved it forward two spaces, placing it next to the white stone representing Elder Master Xiao.","’Yang Ye... If this Right Governor doesn’t act, it will be impossible to deal with Liu Hong.’","As he thought, he added another white stone. ’It just so happens that Li Huai’gu has been facing difficulties from Liu Hong recently, and Mr. Yue Ming is going to visit Right Envoy Yang.’","Chen Yi looked at the final board position forming in his mind, a slight smile gracing his lips:","’I’ve gone in circles, only to end up back where I started.’","He had originally planned to use Yang Ye to help the Xiao Family counterbalance Liu Hong, but Liu Hong’s repeated, proactive concessions had left him without an opening.","Now that he was certain Liu Taofang had made a move, he could no longer allow the Xiao Family to remain in such a passive position.","However, he also knew that Liu Hong would not be easy to deal with.","Liu Hong was the Governor of Shu State, and he had the Jing State Liu Family backing him. Trying to deal with him through ordinary means was clearly impossible.","At the very least, he couldn’t be as crude as he was when he eliminated Liu Wen and Xiao Dongchen.","With a plan solidifying in his mind, Chen Yi let out a long breath.","’Fortunately, Liu Hong isn’t invincible.’","’Liu Taofang is one of his weaknesses.’","’And so is the Jing State Liu Family.’","The faces of the Five Poison Sect, King Landu of Poshisu Country, and others appeared in Chen Yi’s mind, and the smile on his face widened.","’Even if I don’t manage to eliminate Liu Hong this time, I can use this opportunity to cut off a few of his claws.’","If the plan went smoothly, he might even reap greater rewards.","Just then, the JINGLE JINGLE of a bell could be heard.","Chen Yi snapped back to his senses and saw Pei Guanli peeking her head in from outside the door, a mischievous expression on her face.","But when she saw that Chen Yi’s expression remained unchanged, Pei Guanli stuck out her tongue and said, \"Aw, I didn’t even scare you, Brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. \"How old are you? Why are you still acting like a child?\"","Pei Guanli, displeased, walked over and tugged on his arm, insisting, \"I am not a child!\"","\"Yes, yes, you’re not...\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi reminded her to look after Xiao Wuge in the residence.","Pei Guanli readily agreed, chattering on about how her Martial Arts had improved a lot recently and that she would teach Xiao Wuge a Palm Technique tonight.","Chen Yi thought for a moment and said, \"That Hundred Flowers Palm of yours isn’t quite suitable. Why don’t you teach him some Step Technique first?\"","The Hundred Flowers Palm required too much flexibility, which was clearly something a boy like Xiao Wuge, who hadn’t even started Pile Skill Cultivation, couldn’t learn.","In comparison, the Meteor Butterfly Step was something Xiao Wuge could learn first.","Even if the effect wasn’t significant, it would still improve his Step Technique.","Pei Guanli heard this and nodded. \"Okay, I’ll listen to you, Brother-in-law.\"","「Not long after.」","Xiaodie returned with breakfast.","Chen Yi had a few quick bites, then took them to Jiaxing Garden to meet up with Xiao Wan’er.","Xiao Wan’er had already finished her meal by this time. Seeing him approach, she smiled and waved him over.","\"Brother-in-law, the things were prepared and loaded onto the carriage this morning. Let’s get going.\"","Chen Yi looked her over, then smiled, nodded, and said, \"Alright.\"","Perhaps it was his imagination, but although Xiao Wan’er was still wearing the same white cloak that covered her body, her figure seemed a bit more upright and proud today.","It even added a certain radiance to her stunningly beautiful face.","Xiao Wan’er, of course, was unaware of his thoughts as she walked out of Jiaxing Garden side-by-side with him.","As they walked, she said, \"I already had my people scout out a few locations in advance. We can go check them out directly.\"","\"If all goes well, we can finalize the location for the Medical Dao Academy today.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and was about to reply when he saw an Armored Warrior leading someone into the central courtyard.","The man was plain-looking, but tall and sturdy. He wore a black short-sleeved shirt and shorts, and was barefoot.","’A member of the Mountain Race?’","Before Chen Yi could ponder it further, he heard Pei Guanli exclaim in surprise from beside him, \"Brother, what are you doing here?\"","The newcomer paid her no mind, his eyes fixed forward. He walked over with stiff, formal steps and bowed to Xiao Wan’er.","\"Pei Qian of the Mountain Race greets the Eldest Miss.\"","However, his movements were very stiff, not at all as natural as those of the people from the Prefecture City.","Xiao Wan’er nodded lightly, gesturing that he didn’t need to be so formal, then turned to Pei Guanli and asked with a smile, \"This is your brother?\"","Pei Guanli nodded repeatedly. She walked over carefreely and slapped Pei Qian hard on the back.","SLAP.","Pei Qian staggered, grimacing at her. \"Little Sister, this isn’t the clan.\"","Pei Guanli paid that no mind, laughing as she said, \"Brother, so you get scared too.\"","\"Who’s scared?\"","Pei Qian muttered, then took a letter from his robes and presented it to Xiao Wan’er with both hands.","\"A letter from General Jinghong. Please accept it, Eldest Miss.\"","But as he said this, his eyes were fixed on Chen Yi, who was standing nearby, and his gaze held a hint of scrutiny.","Chen Yi saw his expression and secretly raised an eyebrow.","’If I recall correctly, Tiger Girl mentioned her brother was fond of Xiao Jinghong.’","’Sure enough, there’s no love or hate in this world without a reason.’"]},{"number":353,"title":"Chapter 353 - 236: The Son-in-law Has a Way with Words","paragraphs":["That was what he was thinking, but Chen Yi didn’t let it show. He simply stood calmly to one side.","He did a quick calculation. The Mid-Autumn Festival was just over ten days away.","If he subtracted the three to five days since Pei Guanli had sent her letter...","The Mountain Race must have sent Pei Qian to Shu State Prefecture City the moment they received it.","That wasn’t slow at all.","Besides, the fact that Pei Qian had produced a letter from Xiao Jinghong suggested he had also stopped at the Wu Mountain Mutual Market for some time.","However, Chen Yi was more concerned about the Mountain Race’s stance on the Five Poison Sect, and how many people Pei Qian had brought with him this time.","Just then, Pei Guanli voiced the question on his mind. \"Brother, did you come alone?\"","Pei Qian shook his head. \"No.\"","\"Third Grand-Uncle, Uncle Li, and Aunt Chu came with me. And Little Sister is here too...\"","He listed over a dozen names, bringing a look of delight to Pei Guanli’s round face.","\"Little Sister came too?\"","\"Where are they now? Take me to them. I haven’t seen them in so long.\"","Pei Qian hesitated slightly, then turned to Xiao Wan’er and cupped his fist. \"Thank you for taking care of my little sister these past days, Young Mistress.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled and nodded. \"It was no trouble at all.\"","After a few more pleasantries, she instructed Xie Tingyun to help arrange accommodations for Pei Qian.","Pei Qian thanked her again and accepted the offer.","He was about to offer a few more polite words when Pei Guanli grabbed his arm and started pulling him outside.","As she ran, she looked back at Chen Yi and called out, \"Brother-in-law, I’m going to hang out with my brother now! I’ll come find you after you get back to the mansion.\"","Then, as if remembering something, she stuck out her tongue and added, \"Oh, and teaching Xiao Wuge the Step Technique will have to be postponed for a day or two.\"","Chen Yi smiled and waved, calling after her, \"Be careful.\"","\"Don’t worry, don’t worry! My Third Grand-Uncle and Aunt Chu are very powerful people... um... and my brother is very powerful too.\"","Hearing this, Pei Qian seemed to stand a little straighter.","This couldn’t help but make Chen Yi chuckle a few times.","Seeing this, Xie Tingyun bowed to Xiao Wan’er before following the two Pei siblings out.","Xiao Wan’er watched them disappear into the distance, then smiled at Chen Yi. \"We should get going as well.\"","Chen Yi nodded. He called for Liu Si’er to go on ahead, then he and Xiao Wan’er boarded the second carriage.","Juan’er and Cui’er took their seats on the side.","Once Shen Huatang saw they were all settled, she drove the carriage out of the Marquis’s Mansion, following Liu Si’er’s carriage.","After they had traveled a few miles, Xiao Wan’er finally remembered the letter from Xiao Jinghong. She took it from her sleeve and began to read.","As she read, she told Chen Yi, \"Second Sister says she’s doing well.\"","Chen Yi glanced at her, his gaze falling on the letter in her hand, and nodded with a smile.","\"With the Madam personally overseeing the Wu Mountain Mutual Market, nothing untoward is likely to happen.\"","With Xiao Jinghong’s current Cultivation and Technique Realm, forget common bandits—even masters of the Upper Three Grades Realm probably couldn’t get close to her.","Besides, the presence of the Mountain Race members there was enough to intimidate most of the Jianghu in Shu State.","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement. She quickly finished the letter and handed it to him, saying with a smile,","\"Second Sister says that after the construction of the Mutual Market is complete, she still has to inspect the troops of the Three Towns. She wanted me to ask for your understanding.\"","Chen Yi took the letter. \"Of course, I understand,\" he said with a smile as he began to read.","The contents were largely as Xiao Wan’er had said; Xiao Jinghong’s letter mostly detailed her recent situation.","For instance, the first phase of the Wu Mountain Mutual Market’s construction was expected to be finished before the end of the tenth month.","It also mentioned her plans to inspect the Three Towns, when she might return home, and so on.","But when he reached the end, the smile on Chen Yi’s face froze. He turned to look at Xiao Wan’er, who had half-hidden her cheeks in the collar of her cloak, and raised an eyebrow.","\"The Madam wants me to inscribe a plaque for the Wu Mountain Mutual Market?\"","Seeing that he’d read that part of the letter, Xiao Wan’er blinked and said,","\"Second Sister wanted me to relay the message to you, but I thought it would be better if you saw it for yourself.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. \"It’s a simple matter. There was no need to be so formal about it.\"","Since he and Xiao Jinghong were married, he wouldn’t refuse something that was part of his duty.","Especially for a small thing like writing a few words, there was no need to be so roundabout.","But from this, he could easily tell that Xiao Jinghong must feel a little guilty—being away from home for so long right after their wedding, she felt she was in the wrong.","Xiao Wan’er covered her mouth and chuckled. \"Perhaps Second Sister was worried you might not agree.\"","\"After all, you’re now an Instructor at Guiyun Academy, as well as a master of Calligraphy and a great poet famous throughout all of Great Wei.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"That’s just empty fame.\"","He looked at Xiao Wan’er and said seriously, \"Big Sister, you mustn’t learn from the Madam. If you need anything in the future, you must tell me directly. There’s no need to be so polite.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er’s eyes flickered. \"I’ll remember that.\"","Perhaps feeling her words lacked conviction, she added,","\"Like with this trip to choose the fiefdom location, I... I wasn’t being formal with you.\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"That’s how it should be.\"","Meeting his gaze, Xiao Wan’er immediately shrank back into her collar, hiding the fair skin of her neck again as a faint blush colored her cheeks.","At this moment, silence spoke louder than words.","Inside, Xiao Wan’er was quite happy.","Although Chen Yi had only said a few perfectly ordinary words, to her ears, they were as sweet as morning dew.","She knew that Chen Yi already saw her as someone close to him.","Or even family.","A moment of silence passed.","Chen Yi folded the letter away. He lifted the curtain on one side to look outside. \"The weather is nice today,\" he remarked.","The autumn sky was high and clear, without a single cloud.","After several days of rain, the weather in Shu State had become much cooler and more comfortable.","Most people on the road had switched to thicker clothing; even the Wandering Martial Artists, who typically didn’t fear the cold, had done the same.","Xiao Wan’er poked her head out to glance outside the carriage. \"Yes, it’s already the end of the eighth month.\"","She paused, a thoughtful look on her face as she said, \"Next month... Around this time in previous years, I would have already been preparing to go to Wumeng Mountain.\""]},{"number":354,"title":"Chapter 354 - 236: The Young Master-in-law’s Formidable Mouth","paragraphs":["Before Chen Yi could reply, Juan’er and Cui’er, sitting up front, quickly turned around.","\"Miss, are you not planning to go this year?\"","\"Well... Miss, although your health is better than in previous years, it would be best to go and stay there for a while, just to be safe.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi lowered the curtain and turned to look at Xiao Wan’er. He saw her looking back at him and instantly guessed what she was thinking.","\"You want to ask Doctor Ma about it?\"","Xiao Wan’er said hesitantly, \"Once the location for the Medical Dao Academy is chosen, I want to hire the local laborers to begin construction.\"","\"In such a hurry?\"","\"Yes. While I’m feeling a bit better, I want to get the Medical Dao Academy built as soon as possible.\"","A slight smile appeared on Xiao Wan’er’s face as she looked at Chen Yi with gentle eyes.","\"When the time comes, you’ll have to help me with the calligraphy for it.\"","Chen Yi nodded in agreement. \"In that case, I’ll go get Ma Liangcai when we return.\"","As he spoke, a faint light shimmered in the depths of his eyes, and he gazed directly at Xiao Wan’er.","He could see strands of black energy still coiled around her body, most densely around her lower back.","After observing her for a moment, Chen Yi sighed to himself.","Although Xiao Wan’er was doing better than before, the medicine he’d prescribed only treated the symptoms, not the root cause. It could only slow the progression of her Extreme Cold Body’s affliction, not eradicate it completely.","However, because of his decoction, Xiao Wan’er no longer needed to make special trips to Wumeng Mountain and endure the ordeal of being scoured by its geothermal fire energy.","’Extreme Cold Body, Innate Life Gate Fire Decline... To replenish her Yang Fire Essence Qi would be as difficult as bringing the dead back to life.’","At his current Medical Dao Realm, Chen Yi estimated that even if he reached the Perfection Realm, he still might not be able to cure Xiao Wan’er completely.","’Fortunately, he still had time.’","Just then, Xiao Wan’er noticed his gaze. She instinctively glanced at Juan’er and Cui’er and, seeing they weren’t paying attention, let out a small sigh of relief.","She then glanced down at herself but found nothing out of the ordinary. She immediately shot Chen Yi a chiding look and asked,","\"Did you go to Jishi Medicine Hall yesterday?\"","Chen Yi saw the look in her eyes but didn’t look away. He simply smiled and nodded.","\"I went to take a look. It’s certainly quieter than before.\"","\"It’s because of the competition from Xinglin Hall, isn’t it? I already had someone inform the shopkeepers and told them not to worry.\"","\"We just have to do our best. Although the Medicine Hall’s business has been affected, the herbal teas from Hundred Herbs Hall are still earning a lot of silver.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement, composing herself. \"When I get back from the fief, I’ll have them send over the account books so I can go over them.\"","At the end of every month, she had to calculate the income and expenses for all their businesses. Only after the silver was deposited could she distribute the monthly allowances to the various households in the estate.","Chen Yi knew this as well. \"Right now, Hundred Herbs Hall is only in the Prefecture City. Once they expand, the family shouldn’t have to worry about silver anymore.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded lightly and said thoughtfully, \"It’s all thanks to that Boss Chen Yu.\"","\"Speaking of which, he hasn’t returned to the Prefecture City since he met with you the other day. I wonder when he plans to expand.\"","\"It should be soon.\"","\"Wang Ji has already recruited many people and is preparing to further increase the production of the herbal teas.\"","\"Oh? Then he must have quite a team now, right?\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but smile. \"Originally, the workshops combined had fewer than a hundred people.\"","\"But when you add in all the elite disciples from the Celestial Sect, the numbers become quite impressive.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er also covered her mouth and giggled. She looked toward the front curtain and said with a smile,","\"Huatang, remember to find some time to visit. See if your fellow sect members are facing any difficulties after arriving in Shu State. If there’s anything the family can do to help, feel free to make the arrangements.\"","\"On their behalf, thank you, Miss.\"","\"There’s no need for such formalities among family.\"","With that, Xiao Wan’er turned to Chen Yi and explained, \"Actually, my mother was a disciple of the Celestial Sect. The Sect Leader of the Celestial Sect, Elder Ni, was my mother’s master.\"","A look of realization dawned on Chen Yi’s face. \"No wonder Fairy Tingyun and Miss Shen came all the way to Shu State.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in affirmation. \"It’s all thanks to Elder Ni’s care.\"","Perhaps at the thought of her late mother, a shadow of sorrow passed over her features.","\"Back when my mother was still alive, she would go to Tian Mountain every year for a short stay. Each time she returned, she would bring me a few Snow Lotuses.\"","\"Unfortunately, my health was too poor back then to withstand the cold there, and later...\"","Listening to Xiao Wan’er recount these old memories, Chen Yi could tell her mood had soured, so he simply listened in silence.","In all the time he had been here, this was the first he’d heard Xiao Wan’er speak of her mother—his late mother-in-law.","Most of the time, she spoke of the late Duke Dingyuan, Xiao Fengchun.","It was only now that he learned that Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Jinghong’s mother, Fu Wanqing, had been an elite disciple of the Celestial Sect.","After an hour of idle chat, the carriage finally passed through the city gates and headed south along the main road.","Chen Yi had also learned much more about the father-in-law and mother-in-law he had never met.","For instance, how Xiao Fengchun was the Xiao Family’s most talented Martial Arts prodigy—though still a step below Xiao Jinghong, of course.","Or how Xiao Fengchun was diligent and magnanimous, earning him the deep respect and affection of everyone, from the Dingyuan Army to the other Noble Families of Shu State.","And how Fu Wanqing had once roamed the Jianghu, making a name for herself as \"Fairy Qing\" and becoming known as one of the four great fairies of the Jianghu.","Hearing this, Chen Yi saw Xiao Wan’er’s expression growing even more somber and couldn’t help but interrupt.","\"It’s a good thing you can’t practice Martial Arts.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze. \"It’s... good that I can’t?\"","\"Of course it is.\"","\"If you were like your mother, I’m afraid there wouldn’t be any ’Four Great Fairies’ in the Jianghu anymore.\"","\"Why not?\"","Seeing that he had successfully diverted her attention, Chen Yi breathed a sigh of relief and said with a teasing glint in his eye,","\"Because then, there would only be one fairy left in the entire Jianghu: Fairy Wan’er.\"","The words had barely left his mouth.","Juan’er and Cui’er both let out a laugh, and even Shen Huatang, who was driving the carriage up front, began to cough.","’This Second Young Master-in-law,’ she thought, ’his sweet-talking is really... on another level.’"]},{"number":355,"title":"Chapter 355 - 236: The Son-in-law’s Sharp Mouth","paragraphs":["Further ahead, Liu Si’er vaguely heard the sound of laughter and grumbled to himself.","’I wonder what those Fledglings are talking about.’","At that moment, Xiao Wan’er came to her senses, her face instantly flushing crimson.","\"That’s not what you said at all.\"","\"How could it not be?\"","\"W-Well, my second sister is more talented than I am.\"","\"That’s true. In that case, there are only the two celestial maidens of the Xiao Family.\"","\"And, and Little Sister Qingwu! Her talent for Martial Arts is quite good too.\"","\"Oh, her.\"","Chen Yi was tempted to say Cui Qingwu was ugly, but considering her relationship with Chen Yunfan—not to mention her own rather stunning looks—he just nodded.","\"That only makes three. We’re still one short of the Four Great Beauties...\"","With all the lighthearted banter, Xiao Wan’er was finally pulled from her reverie, proving Chen Yi’s shameless teasing hadn’t been for naught.","Seeing she couldn’t win the argument, Xiao Wan’er quickly changed the subject.","\"Some time ago, Little Sister Qingwu mentioned she wanted to come visit. I wonder when she’ll be here.\"","Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wan’er, who had once again burrowed her head down into her greatcloak, and asked with a smile,","\"When did you two get so close?\"","\"The Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala.\"","\"Actually, I can tell Little Sister Qingwu has very deep feelings for that brother of yours.\"","\"Oh? How can you tell?\"","\"You might not believe it, but...\"","Of course, Chen Yi believed it.","He could see it, too.","Perhaps his brother, Chen Yunfan, could as well.","It was just that he always felt Chen Yunfan was a bit of a flake—even more of one than he was.","As these thoughts crossed his mind, Chen Yi couldn’t help but recall the duel between Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu from earlier that day.","’Considering their respective levels in Martial Arts, Chen Yunfan should have the upper hand.’","...","The upper hand? It was far more than that.","Chen Yunfan didn’t know how to pull his punches.","If not for the fact that Cui Qingwu’s Cultivation was a full two Realms below his, he would have been itching to use his full strength.","Even so, just fifteen minutes into the duel, Cui Qingwu’s forehead was already beaded with sweat, and her arms and legs stung with a burning pain.","She furrowed her brow and glared at Chen Yunfan. \"You promised you would only use your Sword Dao at the Minor Success Realm!\"","Chen Yunfan, holding his sword in one hand, stood tall and straight. With a grim expression, he shook his head and said,","\"Using my full strength in our duel is the greatest respect I can show you, Qingwu.\"","Cui Qingwu opened her mouth to retort, but she knew he was just being difficult again.","\"Brother Yunfan, y-you’re cheating!\"","Chen Yunfan turned away from her, executing a flourish with his sword. \"Ah, Qingwu, you don’t know the pain in my heart.\"","\"Pain?\"","Cui Qingwu’s expression softened a little. \"Is Brother Yunfan’s heart aching because I’m hurt?\"","But to her surprise, Chen Yunfan shook his head again. \"Not at all.\"","\"My heart aches because your Sword Dao Realm is too low to help me improve my own Martial Arts.\"","He had been working tirelessly these past few days to raise his Sword Dao Realm as quickly as possible.","He practiced his Swordsmanship diligently, day in and day out.","But alas, the Martial Arts Realm prized intent and enlightenment, and his Sword Dao Realm seemed to have hit a bottleneck, refusing to advance in the slightest.","Chen Yunfan grew more and more anxious. ’At this rate, when will I ever be strong enough to go and beat up Brother Yi?’","That was why he had sought out Cui Qingwu for a duel—despite her being a notch below him in both Cultivation and Martial Arts—hoping the fight might spark a breakthrough.","Unaware of his true intentions, Cui Qingwu was instantly incensed by his words. Brandishing her Long Sword, she charged.","\"Take this!\"","\"A fine strike!\"","Chen Yunfan didn’t move an inch. He simply tapped his sword against her Long Sword, then with a flick of his wrist, slapped the flat of his blade against her waist.","\"Again!\"","\"Qingwu, we Sword Cultivators must be indomitable.\"","This time, his blade slapped against Cui Qingwu’s thigh.","\"Keep going!\"","\"Not bad...\"","After another fifteen minutes of this, Huan’er, who was watching from the side, could no longer bear to look. She couldn’t help but sidle up to Chun Ying, tug on her sleeve, and whisper,","\"Aren’t, aren’t you going to...\"","Before she could finish, Chun Ying, already knowing what she meant, raised a hand to cut her off. \"Soon.\"","\"What?\"","Just then, Ning Yu strode in from outside and handed a sheet of paper to Chun Ying.","\"...A reply.\"","Chun Ying thanked her, then took a few Steps away to avoid Huan’er’s gaze before unfolding the note and glancing at it.","[The Chen Family Patriarch’s return journey is unknown. Contacting him will be inconvenient.]","She understood. ’Inconvenient’ meant it was possible.","[White Robe Order: The ’Dragon’s Roar and Tiger’s Howl’ plan must be accelerated. Someone will contact you in the coming days.]","[Remember, do not let him notice!]","After reading the note, Chun Ying thoughtfully put it away, her gaze drifting toward Chen Yunfan in the center of the training yard.","’Someone else is coming to Shu State?’","After a moment of thought, Chun Ying rubbed her face, composed her expression, and called out to Chen Yunfan as if nothing were amiss.","\"Young Master, there’s good news.\"","Chen Yunfan paused, then retreated a few Steps and performed a swordsman’s salute. A smile broke across his stern face. \"I accept your concession.\"","When Cui Qingwu saw his smiling face, she nearly threw her Long Sword down in frustration.","\"Brother Yunfan, we’ll have a rematch another day.\"","\"Let’s not. Your Sword Dao Realm is too low. Why don’t you improve it a little first, then we can talk.\"","\"You...\"","’That clueless blockhead!’","Chen Yunfan, however, paid no mind to Cui Qingwu’s seething rage. He turned to Chun Ying’s side and asked,","\"You have news?\"","\"Yes. It seems the Patriarch can be contacted.\"","\"Well, don’t just stand there. I’ll go to the study and write a letter. You can send it for me afterward...\""]},{"number":356,"title":"Chapter 356 - 237: Brother-in-law, You’re Staying Tonight, Aren’t You?","paragraphs":["Just after nine in the morning, a flash of golden light appeared before Chen Yi’s eyes:","[Opportunity +6.]","[Assessment: Chen Yunfan defeated Cui Qingwu with overwhelming strength.]","[You were nearby, but heard nothing and saw nothing. An Opportunity descended from heaven, yet you did not claim it. Such is the way of the indolent.]","As expected, Chen Yunfan won easily.","Chen Yi learned the result and looked away. He continued to chat idly with Xiao Wan’er, lifting the carriage curtain to gaze outside.","The fief of Duke Dingyuan’s Xiao Family was located fifty li southeast of Shu State Prefecture City.","It was called Tonglin, a small town under the jurisdiction of the Prefecture City.","It was comprised of six villages and the town itself, which sat at the foot of the mountains near the Prefecture City.","It didn’t seem large, but in reality, these villages, the town, and several surrounding mountains were all part of the Xiao Family’s fiefdom.","Within an area of roughly two hundred square li lived more than two thousand households.","The original imperial edict from Emperor Wei at the founding of the Great Wei dynasty described it as a fief of three thousand households.","At that moment, the carriage had just turned off the main road and was now traveling along a path through the forest.","The crisp CLIP-CLOP of hooves on the road gave way to a duller THUMP-THUMP, and the carriage began to sway.","The dirt path beneath them was clearly uneven.","Without waiting for an order, the driver, Shen Huatang, pulled on the reins to slow their speed.","Fortunately, neither Chen Yi nor Xiao Wan’er was the delicate sort. They simply chatted and laughed occasionally as the carriage rocked along.","A faint smile touched Xiao Wan’er’s pale face as she looked out at the passing scenery.","\"This place has changed so much.\"","Lifting the curtain with one hand, she pointed with the other toward a few mountains in the distance and began to explain them to Chen Yi.","\"That’s Monkey Mountain. When I was little, Father used to take my second sister and me there to hunt. It’s full of small animals.\"","\"The one to the east is called Little Yun Mountain. I remember there’s a waterfall at the summit. My second sister even bathed there once.\"","\"The river channel between them was built when Father was still alive. He had it specially diverted as a tributary from the Chishui River.\"","\"From then on, the people of Tonglin were able to travel by boat to the Prefecture City for supplies, or to seek a living elsewhere...\"","Even though Xiao Wan’er hadn’t been here in a long time, her memory of the place was vivid. She had a story for every mountain and stream.","She could even name the families who lived in the mountain villages and along the riverbanks.","Chen Yi followed her pointing finger, taking it all in. \"I remember the Xiao Family doesn’t collect much in land rent from the fief each year, do they?\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement, her eyes still fixed on the roadside scenery as she smiled.","\"Originally, our ancestors waived the rent entirely. But after a few incidents, my great-grandfather’s generation established a new rule: a thirty percent land rent collected annually.\"","\"Thirty percent? That’s much less than the forty percent required by Great Wei law, to say nothing of the seventy percent some other Noble Families charge.\"","\"Yes. My great-grandfather said that by being only ten percent lower than the standard rate, it was still a blessing to the people, but also avoided condemnation from the other Noble Families.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly. ’The incidents on the fief that Xiao Wan’er mentioned must have truly disheartened her great-grandfather. Otherwise, the Xiao Family wouldn’t have gone from collecting nothing to taking a thirty percent rent for no reason.’","’It’s better this way, though.’","’As the old saying goes, a little help makes a friend, but too much makes an enemy. It’s always better to be moderately generous than to give everything you have.’","Soon, the carriage passed through a narrow mountain road and crossed a wooden bridge, arriving at Tonglin Town.","The stone-paved road that greeted them was much smoother.","Chen Yi glanced around, raising an eyebrow. \"This place... is quite nice.\"","The road was clean, flanked by dozens of wooden storefronts. Their uniform paint and design were quite aesthetically pleasing.","Other residences could be seen faintly in the distance.","Most were courtyard-style homes with gray walls and black-tiled roofs, not much different from what one might find in the Prefecture City.","Xiao Wan’er nodded and said with a smile, \"Father had these built to a uniform design as well.\"","\"When I was a child, he often said the Prefecture City wasn’t peaceful enough. He planned to live in Tonglin when he grew old.\"","It certainly seemed like a good place to retire.","Chen Yi was about to agree when he suddenly saw a dozen or so people jogging over to greet them.","Before he could ask, Xiao Wan’er instructed Shen Huatang to stop the carriage.","\"It’s Elder Ming and the others.\"","\"Elder Ming was originally my grandfather’s Personal Guard. After he was injured, my grandfather arranged for him to come here to manage the estate.\"","As she spoke, Xiao Wan’er was helped down from the carriage by Juan’er and Cui’er.","Chen Yi followed her out and saw the leader of the group, a stooped old man in simple linen, bow and say:","\"Kang Ming greets you, Eldest Miss.\"","The dozen or so people behind him bowed in unison.","Xiao Wan’er quickly told them to dispense with the formalities, then asked, \"Elder Ming, how did you know I was coming today?\"","Kang Ming straightened up, his expression tinged with excitement as he replied, \"The Third Steward sent word the day before yesterday.\"","\"Otherwise, I would not have known you were coming.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded in understanding, her expression softening. \"I only came to take a look around this time,\" she said gently. \"I didn’t mean to trouble you.\"","\"Nonsense, My Lady. If you returned to Tonglin with no one to look after you, the Marquis would surely have me flogged.\"","After a few more pleasantries, everyone was introduced.","The townsfolk were all quite friendly toward Chen Yi, saying that the name of Mr. Qingzhou had already spread throughout Tonglin.","A short while later, once Kang Ming understood the purpose of Xiao Wan’er’s visit, he dismissed the others and said with a smile,","\"My Lady, why don’t I first take you to the Xiao Mansion for lunch? Afterward, we can take a tour of the area.\"","Xiao Wan’er hesitated for a moment, then glanced at the sky and nodded. \"Then I’ll have to trouble you, Elder Ming.\"","\"It’s no trouble, no trouble at all...\"","The Xiao Family’s residence was located deep within the town, a sprawling complex with three successive courtyards, nestled between the mountain and a river.","In addition to Kang Ming and his family, three other elders were responsible for maintaining the residence.","Perhaps because it had been so long since they had seen anyone from the main branch of the Xiao Family, they were all quite emotional upon seeing Xiao Wan’er.","While they waited for lunch, a steady stream of fruits, melons, and pastries appeared on the table.","Xiao Wan’er couldn’t refuse their kindness, so she simply let them bustle about."]},{"number":357,"title":"Chapter 357 - 237: Brother-in-law, You’re Not Leaving Tonight, Are You?","paragraphs":["\"After Elder Ming arrived, his son retired from the Dingyuan Army to help manage the estate.\"","\"Previously, they were the ones who registered and collected the land rent, which the Third Steward and his men would then come to collect.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, asking, \"The other gentlemen must also be veterans of the Dingyuan Army, I presume?\"","\"Yes, Elder Fang and the others are too, but they were assigned here by my grandfather in recent years...\"","While they chatted and laughed, the group finished lunch. After a short rest, Kang Ming approached and asked,","\"Miss, which places would you like to see? I can lead the way.\"","Xiao Wan’er didn’t refuse. She had Shen Huatang bring a map and pointed to several circled locations on it.","\"We’ll go see all of these places.\"","After looking, Kang Ming hesitated. \"Miss, the roads outside of town are narrow. I’m afraid a carriage won’t be able to pass.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled. \"It’s no problem, we can walk.\"","\"Absolutely not! Someone of your stature...\"","After much persuasion, it was only when Shen Huatang spoke up that Xiao Wan’er finally agreed to go on horseback.","Chen Yi benefited as well, getting to ride there on horseback with Xiao Wan’er.","Before long, Liu Si’er came over leading two horses. He stopped a slightly shorter horse next to Xiao Wan’er and led the other one over to Chen Yi.","\"Sir, this one is spirited. You should be careful.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, took the reins, and vaulted onto the horse with a smile.","\"I’ve practiced riding before in Jiangnan Prefecture. No matter how spirited...\"","He hadn’t even finished speaking when the black steed beneath him suddenly reared, almost throwing him off.","\"Ngh—\"","The steed let out a long neigh.","Chen Yi instinctively moved to bring it under control, but a glimpse of Liu Si’er out of the corner of his eye gave him pause. Instead, he just yelled and gripped the reins tighter.","Xiao Wan’er saw this, her eyes widening in alarm as she cried out, \"Be careful!\"","At that moment, Shen Huatang leaped into action without hesitation, flying up and stomping on the horse’s head.","THUD!","Instantly, the black horse that was about to bolt dropped to its knees, its head pinned to the ground by Shen Huatang’s foot.","As the horse went down, Chen Yi tumbled to the side, ending up in an undignified heap on the ground.","Xiao Wan’er didn’t think twice, rushing over to check on him, her expression anxious as she asked,","\"Are, are you okay?\"","Chen Yi clambered to his feet, covered in dust. He rubbed the side of his face, grimacing in pain. \"I’m, I’m fine.\"","To make the act more convincing, he discreetly gave himself a couple of bruises, and half of his face swelled up before their very eyes.","Upon seeing this, Xiao Wan’er’s delicate brows knitted together for the first time. She whirled around to face Liu Si’er.","\"What is the meaning of this?\"","Liu Si’er immediately dropped to his knees. \"Please forgive me, Miss. I was careless and caused Sir to be injured. I await your punishment.\"","\"You...\"","Before Xiao Wan’er could finish, Chen Yi waved his hand with a smile. \"It’s just a scratch. Nothing serious.\"","Seeing that Xiao Wan’er was still glaring at Liu Si’er, Chen Yi gently tugged her sleeve and continued, \"Wan’er, there’s no need to punish Liu Si’er. It was my own fault for being careless.\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced back at him, her beautiful eyes reflecting his swollen face. She hesitated, then nodded.","\"Elder Ming, do you have any liniment? Please bring some over.\"","\"Yes, I’ll go get it right away.\"","Chen Yi naturally didn’t refuse. His gaze fell upon the black horse, a faint glint flashing in his eyes.","He then discovered what was wrong with the horse—a Silver Needle was embedded deep in its rump, reaching the bone.","Upon seeing this,","Chen Yi glanced at the sweating Liu Si’er out of the corner of his eye and inwardly scoffed.","’What a... clumsy test.’","He had already learned from Lou Yuxue that the Hidden Guard planned to test him to see if he possessed any skill in Martial Arts.","He’d thought Lou Yuxue would handle it personally, but who would have thought that woman would delegate the task to Liu Si’er.","If Chen Yi hadn’t been on his guard just now, he might have exposed his body’s abnormal strength.","After all, he had tempered his body to a solid foundation back when he was at the Ninth Grade, possessing the Power of Three Symbols.","By now, his physical strength had progressed even further, reaching the Power of Four Symbols.","He could have easily subdued that black horse with his physical power alone.","As these thoughts passed through his mind, Chen Yi offered a few more words of comfort to Liu Si’er, while mentally adding another strike against his name.","’I only broke one of his limbs last time. It seems I went too easy on him.’","「A short while later.」","After applying the liniment for Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er looked at the shorter horse beside her and said hesitantly,","\"To avoid any more accidents, Brother-in-law, why don’t you... sh-share a horse with me.\"","A blush spread across her face before she could even finish speaking.","Chen Yi was stunned for a moment. He glanced at the expressions of Shen Huatang and the others, then magnanimously accepted.","\"In that case, thank you, Wan’er.\"","Shen Huatang, of course, saw their expressions and simply sighed to herself without saying anything.","Juan’er and Cui’er, on the other hand, gave them much stranger looks.","They both knew what Chen Yi had done before—he had lifted their miss’s blanket.","However, it was clear that neither of them dared to say a word.","「A moment later.」","And so, as Xiao Wan’er’s face burned red, Chen Yi sat behind her, holding the reins together with her.","\"Wan’er, it’s getting late. We should get going.\"","Xiao Wan’er suddenly felt a warm breath tickle her ear. She immediately shrank her neck into her cloak and stammered, \"Let’s, let’s go.\"","Kang Ming glanced at them. Although his expression was a little odd, he decided he was just overthinking things.","This second son-in-law was famous throughout Shu State and was also General Jinghong’s husband; he didn’t seem like a libertine at all.","To avoid making a big fuss, Xiao Wan’er had Liu Si’er, Cui’er, and Juan’er wait at the residence for the time being.","She then had Kang Ming lead the way, and left the residence with Chen Yi and Shen Huatang.","However, Xiao Wan’er soon began to have some regrets.","It had been fine back in town, where the roads were smooth, and she could maintain her posture to avoid contact with Chen Yi.","But once they left town, the roads were mostly dirt paths riddled with potholes, causing the small horse to bob up and down unsteadily.","It was inevitable that the two of them would brush up against each other.","It got to the point where Xiao Wan’er didn’t know where to look. She hid half her face in her cloak, wrapping herself up tightly.","Chen Yi, in contrast, looked perfectly calm.","In his heart, however, he felt a certain sense of relief.","’A cloak really is a wonderful thing. So thick, so warm... it really puts my mind at ease.’","Fortunately, after about half an hour, they arrived at the first location.","Xiao Wan’er finally remembered their business. Calming herself, she said,","\"Brother-in-law, this place is the closest to town, and it’s a spacious area at the foot of Monkey Mountain. What do you think?\"","Chen Yi surveyed the area and nodded. \"With its green mountains and clear waters, it’s quite nice.\"","After a pause, he looked toward Monkey Mountain and asked, \"Elder Kang, there must be quite a few medicinal herbs on this mountain, right?\"","Kang Ming shaded his eyes with his hand and looked at Monkey Mountain. \"You’re not wrong, Sir. There are indeed some medicinal herbs on the mountain.\"","\"It’s mainly because Monkey Mountain is so overgrown that wild beasts often prowl here. Ordinary folk don’t dare to come.\"","Chen Yi nodded. Looking at Xiao Wan’er, who was right beside him, he explained with a light chuckle,","\"Wan’er, this place is quite good.\"","\"The main purpose of the Medical Dao Academy is to train Physicians, and identifying medicinal ingredients is something they must master.\"","\"With the convenience of Monkey Mountain, they can follow their Instructors up the mountain to gather herbs and apply their knowledge in the future.\"","Xiao Wan’er endured the tingling sensation in her ear and looked at Monkey Mountain. \"So we’ll decide on this place?\"","Seeing the blush behind her ears, Chen Yi’s eyes darted about mischievously. \"No rush. Let’s check out the other spots.\"","\"Alright...\"","Upon hearing this, Kang Ming continued to lead the way.","Only Shen Huatang, who had been keeping a close eye on Xiao Wan’er and Chen Yi, subconsciously tightened her grip on her Long Sword.","’This second son-in-law... Just how long does he plan on sharing a horse with the miss?’","But when she saw Xiao Wan’er’s expression, she couldn’t help but sigh. Forcing herself to turn away and survey the surroundings, she made a silent vow:","’You scoundrel, if you make one more indecent move, I will definitely... report you to General Jinghong!’","Of course, Chen Yi had no idea what Shen Huatang was thinking.","And naturally, he had no intention of taking advantage of Xiao Wan’er, either.","At most, he was using the opportunity to tease her a little and enjoy her rare, bashful expression.","Xiao Wan’er vaguely understood. Amidst her shyness, she couldn’t help feeling both amused and annoyed.","If Shen Huatang and Kang Ming weren’t there, she would have certainly given Chen Yi a piece of her mind.","Unfortunately, even after they had seen the last location, she never found the chance.","\"What do you think, Brother-in-law?\"","Seeing that their business was concluded, Chen Yi put aside his playful thoughts and considered the matter seriously.","\"Let’s go with the place at the foot of Monkey Mountain.\"","\"The other locations are either too far from town, making travel inconvenient, or too close to the villages, which would inevitably cause disturbances.\"","A smile appeared on Xiao Wan’er’s face upon hearing his reasoning. \"Then it’s decided.\"","With this matter settled, she was naturally in a good mood.","\"After we return to the manor tonight, I’ll have someone come here first thing tomorrow morning for a detailed survey.\"","\"Alright...\"","Kang Ming, who had been listening to their conversation, asked, \"Miss, Sir, are you still planning to rush back to the Prefecture City tonight?\"","\"It’s nearly dusk. By the time you get back, I’m afraid the city gates will already be closed.\"","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback. Just as she was about to insist, she suddenly felt a few drops of water on her face.","She looked up to see that the sky had, at some point, become overcast with dark clouds.","Seeing this, Xiao Wan’er said hesitantly,","\"Brother-in-law, perhaps we shouldn’t go back tonight...\""]},{"number":358,"title":"Chapter 358 - 238: If the Second Son-in-law Were the Eldest, Then...","paragraphs":["Chen Yi and the others had originally hoped to return to Shu State Prefecture City.","But as the torrential rain began to fall, even returning to their residence in town became a challenge.","Fortunately, Shen Huatang had brought an umbrella, allowing Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er to take shelter beneath it.","As a result, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but lean into Chen Yi’s embrace.","The downpour had turned the road to mud, and the pony’s steps were unsteady, causing the two of them to sway atop its back.","At first, Xiao Wan’er was still reserved, deliberately trying to keep some distance from Chen Yi.","But as the wind and rain grew fiercer, her already frail body began to show signs of discomfort.","Even though she wore a thick cloak over a sable vest, her entire body felt like a block of ice, radiating a bone-deep chill.","Chen Yi naturally felt it, and after a moment’s thought, he understood.","’An Extreme Cold Body can’t tolerate the wind and chill, let alone being battered by a storm like this.’","He hesitated for a moment.","Glancing at Shen Huatang leading the pony ahead, Chen Yi wrapped one arm around Xiao Wan’er’s waist and secretly pressed a finger against her Mingmen acupoint—on the center of her lower back, level with her navel.","Feeling his arm tighten around her waist, Xiao Wan’er weakly turned her head, her pale lips parting slightly.","\"You...\"","Wary of Shen Huatang and Kang Ming ahead of them, she swallowed the word \"don’t\" and simply gazed at him with her bright eyes.","Chen Yi knew what she meant. \"Your cloak is so thick,\" he said with a smile. \"Let me warm up a bit, too.\"","As he spoke, he channeled his power through his fingertip.","Faint wisps of True Essence flowed from him into her, slowly warming her body.","The weakness and chill in Xiao Wan’er’s body instantly began to subside. A warm current seemed to wash over her, dispelling the cold from within.","She didn’t know the reason, but she didn’t overthink it, simply attributing it to the effects of the medicine she had been taking recently.","\"I...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yi tightened his arm around her waist and asked with a grin, \"You’re not going to be that stingy, are you?\"","Flustered, but unable to protest outright, Xiao Wan’er subtly used her arm to pull her cloak over Chen Yi’s audacious hand, hiding it from the view of Shen Huatang and Kang Ming.","After doing this, Xiao Wan’er breathed a small sigh of relief.","But at the thought of the rogue behind her, a faint blush colored her cheeks and she said reproachfully:","\"You... you should practice your Martial Arts more.\"","\"Look at Huatang and Tingyun. They’re not affected by wind or rain, or by scorching heat or bitter cold.\"","\"And Wuge, he’s been going to the Martial Arts Arena every day recently. I heard Second Uncle has praised him a few times.\"","After hearing this, Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle, thinking to himself:","’She’s forgotten the pain as soon as the wound’s healed. The moment her body warms up a little, she starts lecturing me.’","However, he knew Xiao Wan’er was sensitive, so he didn’t argue and just readily agreed.","\"Desperate times call for desperate measures. Who would have thought it would rain on a clear day?\"","\"That’s just how autumn is in Shu State...\"","Up ahead, Shen Huatang heard their conversation and glanced back. When she saw their posture, her brow furrowed slightly.","After a moment’s thought, she turned her head straight back and couldn’t help but quicken her pace.","’That Second Young Master is really too much. What’s he doing, pressing so close to her?’","’Hmph. I’d better hurry back to the residence to keep him from pulling any more stunts.’","Apparently, Shen Huatang had only noticed that Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er were too close and hadn’t detected the faint wisp of True Essence from Chen Yi.","They walked on, stopping and starting, as the rain grew heavier and heavier.","But the two on the pony seemed completely oblivious, talking and laughing the whole way.","It was mostly Xiao Wan’er talking about the Medical Dao Academy—things like her plans for it, building several study halls, dormitories, storehouses, and so on.","\"I hope I can find a suitable dean and Instructors before the academy is completed.\"","Chen Yi considered this. \"Medical Saint Hands won’t come for just any reason, but it’s not out of the question.\"","Xiao Wan’er tilted her head and asked, \"You have a way?\"","\"It’s just a matter of spending more silver. Of course, you also have to make a compelling case, appealing to both reason and emotion, about the benefits of the Medical Dao Academy.\"","\"That may be so, but I hope the first dean is not only an expert in the Medical Dao, but also has medical ethics and the ability to teach.\"","Seeing Xiao Wan’er’s hesitation, Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"It’s not that difficult.\"","\"After we get back, just have someone identify all the Medical Saint Hands within the Great Wei territory, and then send letters to each and every one of them.\"","\"Invite all of them?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"Wan’er, the Medical Dao Academy you’re building is the first of its kind in the Great Wei Dynasty. An achievement that will go down in history—how could it not have high standards?\"","Although Chen Yi didn’t know which Medical Saint Hands existed in the Great Wei Dynasty, he understood human nature.","Medical Saint Hands are human, too. And humans have passions and desires; they’re driven by fame and fortune.","The higher you raise the bar for the Medical Dao Academy, the more you’ll attract truly capable people.","Xiao Wan’er still didn’t quite grasp the key point. \"Will that really work?\"","In her view, Medical Saint Hands were reclusive. A mere invitation by letter might seem disrespectful.","Chen Yi knew she was thinking of something like Uncle Liu Huang’s three visits to the thatched cottage and immediately said:","\"If you’re concerned, why not invite them here on the pretext of treating someone, without mentioning that the academy will be evaluating them?\"","Hearing this, a smile appeared on Xiao Wan’er’s face. \"That could work.\"","After a pause, she asked again, \"Then who would be a suitable patient?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow, gave her waist two light squeezes, and said with a smile, \"You.\"","\"Me?\"","\"No, no, that won’t work. When I was a child, my father took me to see every renowned doctor. News of my condition has already spread throughout the Great Wei.\"","\"If they find out it’s me, I’m afraid none of them will come.\"","Chen Yi realized that was true. Even Medical Saint Hands were only at the Minor Success Realm; it was fundamentally impossible for them to cure Xiao Wan’er.","He thought for a moment.","He said gravely, \"Then it can only be the Old Master.\"","Xiao Wan’er was slightly taken aback. \"Grandfather?\""]},{"number":359,"title":"Chapter 359 - 238: If the Second Brother-in-law Were the Eldest, Then...","paragraphs":["Then she realized, and her smile grew even wider as she said:","\"Once I’m back at the mansion, I’ll go discuss this with Grandfather. I hope he won’t refuse.\"","\"Unlike my own condition, Grandfather’s poor health is due to injuries accumulated from his years on the battlefield. Perhaps someone out there can truly heal him.\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"The world is a vast place, full of talented and extraordinary people. I’m sure a Divine Doctor exists somewhere.\"","He had mentioned the Elder Master for this very reason.","In fact, he had once used his Qi Observation Skill to examine Elder Master Xiao’s physical condition—and the outlook was not optimistic.","Beyond his old wounds and ailments, the most critical factor was the Elder Master’s advanced age; he didn’t have much time left.","An ordinary Medical Saint Hand would likely be helpless in this situation.","Unless, of course, he took action himself.","Even if he couldn’t completely cure the Elder Master either, he could still extend his life, ease his suffering, and make it easy for him to live another ten or twenty years.","Two hours later, the sky had long since grown dark. Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, and the others finally returned to their residence in town.","They washed up, changed their clothes, and had dinner.","The group settled in for the night.","However, since this residence was much smaller than the Marquis’s Mansion, Chen Yi’s room was directly across from Xiao Wan’er’s.","Shen Huatang, along with Juan’er and Cui’er, kept watch from the antechamber inside Xiao Wan’er’s room.","Liu Si’er was simply assigned a servant’s room next to the stables.","With nothing else to do, Chen Yi lay down on his bed early.","Worried that Shen Huatang might notice any disturbance, he didn’t even practice his Four Symbols Skill.","But before he could drift off to sleep, a knock sounded at his door.","\"Brother-in-law, are you asleep?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. ’Xiao Wan’er?’","He sat up, called out in response, and went to open the door. Standing there were Xiao Wan’er and Shen Huatang.","They were both fully and neatly dressed, unlike Chen Yi, who was only in a light, comfortable robe.","Xiao Wan’er glanced at him, then lowered her head slightly. \"I... My apologies for disturbing your rest.\"","Seeing the paper and brush in her hands, Chen Yi guessed it had to do with the Medical Dao Academy. He stepped aside and invited them in.","\"Still awake so late? Eldest Sister, you’re truly losing sleep over the Medical Dao Academy.\"","Xiao Wan’er was a bit embarrassed that he had seen right through her, but with her straightforward nature, she didn’t just turn and leave.","Instead, she placed the paper she was holding on the table and spread it out. \"I sketched a rough draft. Please, take a look.\"","\"This quickly?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow and took the paper for a look.","Xiao Wan’er was a skilled painter.","With just a few strokes, she had outlined the general layout of the Medical Dao Academy.","The layout of the mountains and streams, the courtyards, and the residences she drew were identical to the scenery they had seen outside Monkey Mountain that day.","After looking it over, Chen Yi thought for a moment before picking up a brush and beginning to make his own modifications to the drawing.","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback. She moved to stand beside him, her bright eyes fixed on the paper without blinking.","Shen Huatang, standing nearby, paid no mind to the Medical Dao Academy. Her gaze was fixed solely on Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er.","As she watched them, she couldn’t help but sigh to herself.","She found herself recalling the conversation she had overheard between Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er earlier that day.","Their talk of an \"incurable disease\" made it impossible for her not to feel a sense of sympathy for Xiao Wan’er.","’If he were the Eldest Miss’s husband instead of the Second Miss’s, he and the Eldest Miss would be quite a good match.’","’What a pity...’","But whether it was a pity or not, neither Chen Yi nor Xiao Wan’er was concerned. At that moment, their minds were focused solely on the Medical Dao Academy.","Before long,","After a few strokes from Chen Yi’s brush, the simple sketch on the paper was completely transformed.","The academy was still built against the mountain, but compared to Xiao Wan’er’s drawing, his version was a clear step up in both layout and configuration.","He had, in particular, connected the study halls for the Medical Research Institute to the nearby waterway, making the academy’s layout far more practical.","Furthermore, Chen Yi had added several pavilions and terraces, as well as plans for the academy’s future expansion.","He looked at the sketch on the paper and explained to Xiao Wan’er:","\"You won’t need too many people at the start. About a hundred students should be enough to get the academy up and running.\"","\"Four study halls, twenty dormitories, and a small courtyard for the instructors will be more than enough.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded instinctively. She looked from the layout on the paper to Chen Yi, then suddenly asked:","\"Brother-in-law, are you an expert painter as well?\"","Chen Yi blinked. \"Eldest Sister, shouldn’t you be focusing on the academy?\"","He didn’t deny it, though. With a smile, he continued, \"My Painting Dao is merely at the entry-level. I still have a long way to go.\"","This wasn’t false modesty.","His Painting Dao had indeed reached the Minor Success Realm, but since he had only been studying it for a short time, his proficiency with techniques like ink wash painting wasn’t high. It was only a small step above the Initial Insight level.","But that wasn’t how it sounded to Xiao Wan’er.","She said with a look of admiration, \"Brother-in-law, you’re truly incredible.\"","Although she had long known Chen Yi was a master of Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, she had only witnessed his skills in Calligraphy and Chess—and his atrociously bad Zither Dao.","Now that she saw him demonstrate his skill in the Painting Dao, she felt an inexplicable sense of joy.","Chen Yi chuckled, at a loss for words. \"Let’s just focus on the blueprint and see if anything else needs to be added.\"","\"No, I think it’s perfect. You’ve been much more thorough than I was.\"","\"How about this—once the Medical Dao Academy is built, I’ll invite you to be an instructor.\"","\"Me? I don’t know the first thing about the Medical Dao. What would I teach? Surely you don’t expect me to teach them Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting.\"","\"Why not...\"","’That’s not a good idea at all.’","If Chen Yi had any intention of getting deeply involved with the Medical Dao Academy, he wouldn’t have gone to the trouble of cultivating Ma Liangcai; he would have recommended himself long ago under the guise of \"Chen Yu.\"","Besides, he had other matters to attend to.","Matters like Guiyun Academy, Jishi Medicine Hall, Hundred Herbs Hall, and other, even more important affairs.","After a few more moments of small talk, Xiao Wan’er remembered the painting she had mentioned earlier and led Chen Yi to the chambers where her parents once lived.","With a CREAK, the door opened.","Shen Huatang lit the oil lamp inside.","As the flame illuminated the room, Chen Yi’s gaze immediately fell upon the painting hanging in the center.","It depicted Xiao Fengchun in a fine brocade robe, Fu Wanqing in a long pink gown, and two children with brilliant smiles.","Chen Yi studied it for a moment and thought with a sigh, ’No wonder Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Jinghong, and Xiao Wuge are all so strikingly beautiful.’","Even though it was only an ink-and-wash painting with less-than-refined brushwork, he could still tell that Xiao Fengchun had been a handsome man, and Fu Wanqing was a peerless beauty, truly worthy of her title as one of the Four Celestials of the Jianghu.","Xiao Wan’er’s gaze also fell upon the painting, and the faint smile on her face slowly faded, replaced by a touch of sorrow in her eyes.","\"So many years have passed, and I’ve still never been able to forget...\"","She trailed off, not finishing her thought.","But Chen Yi knew she was speaking of Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing. After a moment’s thought, he bowed deeply toward the painting.","\"Father-in-law, Mother-in-law, your son-in-law, Chen Yi, courtesy name Qingzhou, pays his respects.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze, tilting her head to watch him. The sadness on her face instantly dissipated, and she covered her mouth to hide a smile.","\"You really should be bowing.\"","\"When you fled your wedding to Second Sister, you missed the ceremony with her.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"I seem to recall us redoing it later in the Punishment Hall, no?\"","Xiao Wan’er shot him a look. \"How could that possibly count?\"","After a pause, she looked back at the painting, her voice softening slightly.","\"If Father and Mother were still alive, they certainly wouldn’t have let you off so easily.\"","\"If they were, perhaps I never would have been able to join the Xiao Family.\"","Chen Yi was well aware that the only reason he had been able to marry into the Xiao Family was due to their decline and their lack of a new generation of talent.","If Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing were still alive, neither Xiao Wan’er nor Xiao Jinghong would have ever needed to recruit a man to marry into the family.","Given the Xiao Family’s legacy, the sisters would have likely been able to choose ideal husbands for themselves.","At the very least, they would have found someone of Chen Yunfan’s caliber.","It certainly wouldn’t have been his turn, a mere concubine’s son from the Jiangnan Prefecture’s Chen Family.","After a few moments, Xiao Wan’er took the painting down from the wall. She began rolling it up carefully as she said with a smile:","\"Brother-in-law, when you have a free day, would you be able to help me create a copy of this painting?\"","\"I’d like to have one for Second Sister and another for Wuge.\"","Watching her, Chen Yi nodded. \"Let me practice my Painting Dao a little more first.\"","He knew Xiao Wan’er couldn’t move on from the memory of her late parents, so he had no intention of refusing.","It was just that his skill in the Painting Dao was genuinely unrefined at the moment; any copy he produced would lack the proper spirit.","If he waited a few more days, he was confident he could achieve a much better result.","After a few more words, the three of them returned to their respective rooms.","Chen Yi glanced at the room across from his, a faint smile gracing his otherwise calm expression.","’Good night, Xiao Wan’er.’","Just then, midnight arrived, and a flash of golden light appeared—","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Top Grade: At the sixth quarter of the Hai hour, the Hidden Guard, Lady Tiger, will meet with a person from Poshisu Country at the Spring Rain Building in Yanhua Lane. A small Opportunity can be obtained.]","’Lady Tiger... Lou Yuxue?’","’Someone from Poshisu Country... one of King Landu’s people?’"]},{"number":360,"title":"Chapter 360 - 239: No Business at the Government Office, to the Brothel...","paragraphs":["Chen Yi knew that Lou Yuxue, under orders from the General, had recently been in secret contact with King Landu’s people from Poshisu Country.","However, he didn’t know the Hidden Guard’s purpose for contacting King Landu.","Furthermore, according to that merchant surnamed Lin, King Landu was the Bandit King of Poshisu Country.","’King Landu...’","Chen Yi lay on the bed, murmuring the name to himself.","Although he didn’t know much about King Landu, he could easily gauge the man’s capabilities. He was important enough to warrant the attention of a Golden Banner Officer of the Hidden Guard, and he was able to purchase ironware from Mr. Lingchuan through the merchant Lin.","’Horse bandits?’","’It’s rare to see horse bandits operating at this level.’","But Chen Yi had heard a few things about Poshisu Country before.","Many of the horse bandits there were former soldiers who specialized in robbing merchants from the Wei Dynasty and the Buddha Country along the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","The more capable ones even dared to raid the Barbarian Race and capture Barbarians—that was how the barbarian slaves in Shu State came to be.","Under such circumstances, it would be more accurate to call them Poshisu soldiers in bandits’ robes rather than actual horse bandits.","As Chen Yi thought this, he pulled a piece of paper from underneath the Five-section Spear strapped to his arm. He used the faint light from outside the room to read its contents.","’A horizontal stroke, a hook, another hook, a left-falling stroke...’","’The script of Poshisu Country really is hard to decipher.’","What Chen Yi held was none other than the letter for King Landu that he had gotten from the man surnamed Lin.","’It’s probably about negotiating a trade with King Landu.’","’Tomorrow, I’ll have Wang Ji find someone who can read the Poshisu script.’","After mulling it over, Chen Yi put the paper away again, closed his eyes, and fell into a deep sleep.","He slept soundly, but in the room across the way, Xiao Wan’er tossed and turned, unable to sleep.","Her eyes would flutter open from time to time.","Shen Huatang, who was sitting and leaning against the door with her sword, noticed the movement. After a glance at the soundly sleeping Cui’er and Juan’er, she rose lightly and came to the bedside.","\"Miss, can’t you sleep?\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed softly in reply. She pulled the covers around herself and sat up, leaning against the pillows. In a low voice, she said:","\"I haven’t been back here in so long. My mind feels unsettled.\"","All things considered, five years had passed since the deaths of Xiao Fengchun and Fu Wanqing.","She should have been used to it by now, but being here, she couldn’t help but remember her childhood.","And after seeing that painting tonight, she felt a pang of sadness.","Shen Huatang had an inkling of what she was feeling but didn’t know how to comfort her, so she simply sat by the bed and kept her company.","Outside the window, the rain pattered noisily.","Inside the dim room, it was silent and still.","After sitting in a daze for a moment, Xiao Wan’er took a deep breath to dispel the stifling feeling in her chest. She offered a gentle smile and said:","\"Are your fellow sect members all settled in? Are they getting used to it?\"","Shen Huatang hummed in affirmation. \"The conditions are better than on the mountain.\"","\"Shopkeeper Wang found them a place to live—two large, three-courtyard mansions—and even assigned a few servants to attend to them.\"","\"Besides their monthly allowance, they don’t have to worry about food, clothing, or daily expenses. Hundred Herbs Hall is covering everything.\"","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback. \"That sounds quite generous, doesn’t it?\" she asked, surprised.","If nothing else, she was well aware of the state of her own family’s medicine halls.","Even though the terms offered to the shopkeepers, physicians, and apprentices in their own medicine halls were good, there was still a gap compared to what Hundred Herbs Hall provided.","Shen Huatang nodded and said thoughtfully, \"I asked my senior sister, but she doesn’t know why either.\"","\"Perhaps it’s as Wang Ji said—the Second Master negotiated these terms with him.\"","\"My brother-in-law?\"","\"Yes. Or perhaps it has to do with us being from the Celestial Sect.\"","Shen Huatang clearly leaned toward the latter explanation.","Although the Celestial Sect rarely ventured into the Jianghu, it still had some renown.","This was especially true of her master Ni Hai Mountain’s generation, who had roamed the Jianghu for several years and accomplished a few major, attention-grabbing feats.","Her own generation, in contrast, was not as famous.","Only her eldest senior sister, Xie Tingyun, had represented the Celestial Sect in the Jianghu, killing some regional menaces who were causing harm.","Furthermore, the Celestial Sect was located in the remote Western State, a vast and sparsely populated land with few resources, so its name didn’t spread far in the Jianghu.","This was also why she hadn’t insisted on her junior martial brothers and sisters coming down the mountain to join Hundred Herbs Hall.","At the very least, it could earn some prestige for the Sect.","And of course, resources.","Xiao Wan’er glanced toward the door and windows and said thoughtfully, \"Perhaps.\"","She, however, was more inclined to believe that Chen Yi had mediated on their behalf, prompting Wang Ji to give the Celestial Sect disciples better treatment.","Of course, that was just her feeling on the matter.","Shen Huatang turned her head to look at Xiao Wan’er. Even in the dimness, she could still make out her expression.","After a moment’s thought, she hesitated—a rare thing for her—and asked, \"Miss, you seem to hold the Second Master in very high... regard?\"","She had wanted to say \"care for,\" but in the end, she couldn’t bring herself to be so blunt.","Xiao Wan’er tensed. She snuck a sideways glance at her, her voice lacking confidence as she replied, \"I... I suppose so.\"","\"My brother-in-law is deeply learned and exceptionally capable... I... I just hope he can teach Wuge more.\"","’After all, this was the most suitable reason.’","’That had been her original intention, and for now, Xiao Wuge’s progress was living up to her hopes.’","’But at some point, his shadow had taken root in her heart.’","’Yes... it probably started with that poem...’","Shen Huatang, still not quite convinced, pressed on, \"Miss, the Second Master is indeed outstanding, just like the Second Miss.\"","She deliberately stressed the word \"second.\"","Xiao Wan’er of course caught the emphasis. After a brief silence, she said faintly, \"Yes, they are both wonderful.\"","\"I wonder if their future children will inherit their qualities.\"","She paused, her voice dropping until it was nearly inaudible.","\"I hope I’ll be around to see that day...\"","Hearing this, a complex look crossed Shen Huatang’s face. She sighed inwardly, finally understanding what was in her miss’s heart.","\"Don’t worry, Miss. You will definitely get better.\""]},{"number":361,"title":"Chapter 361 - 239: No Business at the Government Office, to the Pleasure Quarters...","paragraphs":["Xiao Wan’er chuckled but said no more, simply arranging her pillow and lying down.","\"Go to sleep.\"","\"Alright...\"","...","An unknown amount of time passed.","He drifted in a daze.","Chen Yi found himself in a courtyard, laughing and talking with others.","Xiao Wan’er was there, as was Xiao Jinghong.","The strange thing was, they both addressed him in the same way.","Xiao Wan’er: \"Husband, Wuge will be back from Jinling soon. Shall we go and greet him?\"","Chen Yi: \"Alright, alright...\"","Xiao Jinghong: \"Husband, if you grant my sister one request, you have to grant me one as well.\"","Chen Yi: \"Alright, what is it?\"","\"Come spar with me.\"","\"A spar? No, no, absolutely not.\"","\"Husband, it’s not good to favor the new and forget the old.\"","As she spoke, Xiao Jinghong drew the long sword from her waist, a gentle smile on her face.","\"Husband, watch the blade.\"","In the next instant, a dazzling flash of sword light streaked across the sky, heading straight for Chen Yi’s head.","GASP—","Chen Yi gasped and shot up in bed.","A sliver of light shone into the room through the window.","It was accompanied by the sound of rain lashing down.","Chen Yi let out a long sigh of relief, wiping the cold sweat from his brow. ’Thank goodness it was just a dream,’ he muttered.","’There was no way Xiao Wan’er would ever call me husband.’","After collecting himself, Chen Yi got up and dressed. He looked at his reflection in the copper mirror, forcing a smile onto his face.","’My lady, you certainly gave me a hard time in that dream. From now on, you can’t be pointing blades and swords at your husband anymore.’","’It’s far too dangerous.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself, then pushed the images from his dream to the back of his mind and walked straight out of his room.","It was just past five in the morning.","Xiao Wan’er, Shen Huatang, and the others were already ready to go. Liu Si’er had even fed the horses their fodder at the crack of dawn.","Soon, they had finished their breakfast.","Without lingering, they all boarded the carriage.","Kang Ming and the others had wanted to see them off, but on Xiao Wan’er’s orders, they simply stood outside the residence and watched them depart.","They waited until the carriage vanished into the veil of rain.","Only then did the elderly servants and Kang Ming’s family return to the residence, their expressions not overly sentimental.","\"It’s a good thing that the Young Miss is building a Medical Dao Academy here. She’ll probably come stay here often in the future.\"","\"Perhaps the Marquis will come with her.\"","\"The Marquis?\"","Kang Ming froze at the words. A nervous look crossed his weathered face, and he quickly began waving his hands and giving orders.","\"Then what are you all standing around for?\"","\"While we still have some time, repair the entire residence, inside and out! Clean everything!\"","\"We can’t have the Marquis arrive and see that we’ve let the place fall into disarray.\"","\"Yes, yes...\"","Of course, Chen Yi, already far away, was unaware of all this.","On the way back, however, he sensed something unusual about Xiao Wan’er, who was sitting beside him.","Not much, just a hint of it.","Ever since they had boarded the carriage, Xiao Wan’er kept glancing at him and smiling, which nearly made him think he’d buttoned his clothes crookedly.","\"You seem to be in a good mood today.\"","\"I’ve settled a matter that was weighing on my mind, so of course I’m in a good mood.\"","\"The Medical Dao Academy? This is just the first step of a long journey. We’ve barely even started.\"","\"You’re right. Perhaps I’m celebrating too soon.\"","Xiao Wan’er said with a smile, \"What’s the story behind this ’long journey’ of yours?\"","Chen Yi smiled and lifted a corner of the curtain to look out at the pouring rain. He changed the subject, \"This rain today... it’s really coming down.\"","Her beautiful eyes reflected his silhouette. She didn’t press the matter, only silently pulling her cloak tighter around herself.","’It’s impossible anyway, why trouble myself over it?’","’Besides, my body... I don’t have much time left.’","With this in mind, Xiao Wan’er nudged Chen Yi with her elbow. When he turned to look at her, she said with a smile:","\"Last night, you promised you would copy those two paintings for me.\"","Chen Yi paused. \"What about it?\"","\"Oh, nothing. I was just thinking... I’d like you to paint a few more. Not copies, but portraits. One of me, one of my sister, one of Wuge, one of Grandfather... and one of you.\"","\"Separate portraits, or all together?\"","Seeing that he didn’t refuse, a hint of joy touched Xiao Wan’er’s lovely face.","\"Whatever you prefer. But it would be lovely to have one of all of us sitting together, like the one of Father and Mother with my sister and me.\"","Chen Yi nodded in agreement.","’I don’t know what’s on her mind, but it’s a small favor. I can just treat it as practice for my Painting Dao.’","Before long, the carriage passed through the south gate of Shu State Prefecture City and onto South Street.","Chen Yi glanced at the sky and said, \"I have to make a stop at Hundred Herbs Hall. You all can go on ahead.\"","Xiao Wan’er didn’t ask any questions, simply telling Shen Huatang to stop the carriage.","As Chen Yi stepped down from the carriage, she asked, \"Will you be back for lunch?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"No, I’ll be mooching a meal off the folks at Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","He had a lot to do today and estimated he wouldn’t be done within a couple of hours.","Xiao Wan’er smiled. \"Have Wang Ji take you to a restaurant. If you’re short on silver, I have some here.\"","\"There’s no need...\"","Chen Yi looked at her stunning face, beautiful whether she was smiling or pouting, and the strange feeling in his heart intensified.","’Did something happen last night?’","’How is it that overnight, Xiao Wan’er seems so much more cheerful?’","Just as they were about to part ways, a voice called out from a short distance away, \"Brother Yi?\"","Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er looked toward the sound and saw Chen Yunfan, Cui Qingwu, and their companions waving at them.","Following behind them were Chun Ying and Cui Qingwu’s maid, Huan’er.","’What a coincidence,’ Chen Yi muttered to himself, but kept a neutral expression as he waved back a greeting.","Xiao Wan’er, for her part, did not leave, instead stepping down from the carriage.","When Cui Qingwu saw her, she quickened her pace and held the oil-paper umbrella she was carrying over Xiao Wan’er’s head. \"Sister Wan’er, it’s been too long.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled and nodded. \"Yes, it’s been a while since the Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","\"I was just saying I should come find you, but who knew the new restaurant would open and things would suddenly get so busy.\""]},{"number":362,"title":"Chapter 362 - 239: No Business at the Government Office, Off to the Pleasure House...","paragraphs":["\"A restaurant?\"","\"Yes, I just opened it. It’s called Yunqing Building, right by the West Market.\"","\"Oh, that’s wonderful...\"","As the two beauties chatted and laughed, the atmosphere between Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan grew a little strange.","He wasn’t sure if it was his imagination, but Chen Yi noticed a peculiar look in Chen Yunfan’s eyes as he looked at him.","It was a mix of wistfulness, indignation, and a hint of smugness.","He, of course, had no idea that Chen Yunfan had found out about him killing Yan Fusha of the Five Poison Sect that day.","After a moment’s observation, he decided he must have been mistaken.","After all, who could possibly look both indignant and smug at the same time?","\"Brother, you’re not on duty today?\"","Seeing how calm he was, Chen Yunfan suppressed the urge to run him through with a sword, as well as the smug satisfaction of knowing his secret. He lifted his chin and said:","\"Nothing much happening at the Government Office today. I was going to the brothels—ahem... to Qingwu’s new restaurant to listen to some music.\"","He had been cooped up for days and was going stir-crazy.","Seeing his slow progress in the Sword Dao, he decided to stop forcing it and relax for a bit before resuming his cultivation.","Chen Yi nodded in understanding. He had seen Yunqing Building earlier when he went to Hundred Herbs Hall.","\"Perfect. I was just about to head to Hundred Herbs Hall myself. Let’s go together.\"","Before Chen Yunfan could reply, Cui Qingwu’s eyes lit up. She tugged on Xiao Wan’er’s arm and said:","\"Sister Wan’er, see? Even Mr. Qingzhou says so. You should come with us too, right?\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced at Chen Yi.","Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wan’er, then at the eager Cui Qingwu and the equally eager Chen Yunfan, and said with a smile:","\"Why don’t you go try it out as well, dear?\"","\"It’s quite a coincidence. You were just saying you wanted Shopkeeper Wang to treat you to a meal at a restaurant.\"","A smile blossomed on Xiao Wan’er’s face. She turned and instructed Liu Si’er to take Cui’er and Juan’er back to the manor first.","Shen Huatang, naturally, remained by her side, not leaving her for a moment.","Before long, the two groups set off together for the West Market.","However, that woman Cui Qingwu was rather domineering, immediately linking arms with Xiao Wan’er and sharing an umbrella as they walked ahead.","There was nothing to be done.","So, the two brothers, Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan, could only fall into step behind them.","Worse still, Chen Yi had to hold his own umbrella, while Chen Yunfan had Chun Ying holding one for him.","Seeing this, Chen Yunfan shot him a smug look, waggling his eyebrows and tilting his head up slightly.","\"Just got back from outside, Brother Yi?\"","Chen Yi paid no mind to his petty one-upmanship and grunted in acknowledgment. \"I went to the farming estate outside the city.\"","\"The Xiao Family’s?\"","\"Mine.\"","Chen Yunfan froze, then stared at him in astonishment. After looking him up and down, he clucked his tongue.","\"Impressive, truly impressive. Mr. Qingzhou is worthy of being General Jinghong’s husband, after all.\"","That being said, his feelings were somewhat complicated.","’Yes, Brother Yi married into the Xiao Family. It’s only natural for him to be completely devoted to their interests.’","’Besides, the Chen Family... Mother...’","Thinking of this, Chen Yunfan suddenly understood why Chen Yi had hidden his Martial Arts Cultivation and his knowledge of the Medical Dao.","If he were in Chen Yi’s position, he might have made the same choice.","Unconsciously, Chen Yunfan fell silent.","Even the displeasure he’d felt over Chen Yi’s secrecy had mostly dissipated.","Of course, only *mostly*.","Chen Yi just smiled, unconcerned. \"They say, ’Marry a chicken, follow the chicken; marry a dog, follow the dog.’ Why can’t I?\"","He showed not the slightest awareness that, as a husband who had married into his wife’s family, he was considered a second-class citizen.","Chen Yunfan broke into a laugh, grumbling, \"Even so, you’d better remember that your name is still in the Chen Clan Genealogy. And as your older brother, I share your blood.\"","\"Huh? They didn’t remove my name from the genealogy?\"","\"I’d like to see them try! Even if Father and Second Uncle gave the order, I’d write it right back in for you.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, taking it as a joke.","He was far away in Shu State now, and had married into the Xiao Family. It was highly unlikely he would ever return to Jiangnan Prefecture in this lifetime.","Under these circumstances, what difference did it make whether his name was in the Chen Clan Genealogy or not?","Beside them, Chun Ying listened silently to their conversation, her gaze occasionally drifting to Chen Yi’s figure. She couldn’t help but feel a little emotional.","’The Young Master was in a bad mood originally. He even lost his temper with me this morning.’","’Who would have thought that just by seeing Chen Yi, he’d become a completely different person, all smiles and laughter?’","Thinking of this, Chun Ying pouted slightly.","Just as she was lost in thought, she suddenly heard Chen Yunfan ask, \"Brother Yi, do you want to write a letter to Father?\"","Chun Ying’s mouth fell open, and her heart tightened. ’Young Master, oh, Young Master, why do you say everything that comes to your mind?’","Chen Yi was obviously unaware of this. He shook his head without a second thought. \"What for? I don’t want to.\"","Chen Yunfan looked at him and raised an eyebrow. \"You don’t want to tell the old man anything?\"","\"I know you feel wronged that Mother arranged for you to come to Shu State...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi held up a hand to cut him off. \"Stop. I don’t feel wronged at all.\"","He didn’t want Xiao Wan’er or Shen Huatang to get the wrong idea.","Especially not about feeling wronged.","He was living a leisurely life every day; he couldn’t be happier. ’Wronged, my ass.’","Chen Yunfan paused, then said thoughtfully, \"I remember, when Father left for the Western Continent, you wrote a poem for him...\"","\"You really don’t want to send the old man your regards?\"","Chen Yi paused, then shook his head again. \"Forget it. I’m doing just fine in Shu State. I have nothing to say to him.\"","Besides, he wasn’t the one who wrote \"Farewell to Chen Xuanji in Jinling.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yunfan didn’t press the matter further. He simply made a mental note of it, planning to write a supplementary letter to their father when he got back.","He had to find out, one way or another, if their father knew that Chen Yi had married into another family.","Before long, the group arrived at Yunqing Building.","Just as Chen Yi was about to find an excuse to slip away for a moment, he heard a commotion coming from the direction of Hundred Herbs Hall.","\"Shopkeeper Wang, you can’t blame us for this...\""]},{"number":363,"title":"Chapter 363 - 240: King Landu, Domineering","paragraphs":["Amid the clamor, a portly, middle-aged man in dark blue brocade robes backed out of the Hundred Herbs Hall.","He was flanked by two young servants; one held an umbrella for him, while the other supported him to keep him from falling.","In contrast, Wang Ji had shed his usual welcoming smile, now waving his hand with a displeased expression, as if shooing him out the door.","\"Boss Jia, the contract was signed, and I’ve already sent the silver coins to your estate. Now you’re telling me the goods are gone, breaking the contract without any intention of compensating for the loss. Are you trying to bully Hundred Herbs Hall because we’re a small establishment?\"","\"Shopkeeper Wang, you can’t put it like that. I... I also didn’t expect the medicinal herbs to be burned up by a fire as soon as they arrived at the East Market Warehouse.\"","\"Whoever burned your herbs is who you should go after. All Hundred Herbs Hall wants is for the transaction to be completed!\"","\"Shopkeeper Wang, you... you’re asking for the impossible.\"","\"It was a group of barbarian slaves who burned down that grain store two nights ago. Even if the Government Office captures them, they won’t be able to compensate for my losses.\"","\"If you don’t agree, you’ll... you’ll be driving my Jia’s Medicine Shop into the ground.\"","\"Then do you have any idea how important that batch of herbs was to my Hundred Herbs Hall? Your loss is a loss, but ours isn’t?\"","After speaking in a cold voice, Wang Ji caught sight of Chen Yi and the others across the street, and his expression immediately turned a little unnatural.","Just as he was about to greet them, he saw Chen Yi shake his head slightly. He then saw Chen Yi give him a meaningful look—invite Boss Jia back inside to continue the discussion.","’Invite him?’","Wang Ji understood the gesture and gave a wry smile to himself.","’I’ve already thrown all civility out the window and said things that can’t be taken back. How am I supposed to invite him back in now?’","But he had no choice. The boss had spoken, and he had to obey.","Then, the still-scowling Wang Ji instantly put on a smiling face.","\"However, business is business, and being accommodating to others is being accommodating to oneself. I’ve just thought it over, and I agree that I shouldn’t have pushed you so hard.\"","The middle-aged man froze, staring at him blankly. The conciliatory words he had just prepared got stuck in his throat. \"You... you’re...\"","Before he could finish, Wang Ji strode forward, grabbed him by the arm, and started pulling him back into Hundred Herbs Hall.","As they walked, he said with a smile, \"I was angry just now and said some harsh things. I hope you can forgive me, Boss Jia.\"","\"Shopkeeper Wang, you... you’re truly... Ah, it was I, Old Jia, who wronged you this time.\"","\"It was an accident. Neither of us wanted this to happen, right?\"","\"Come, let’s go back inside and continue our discussion. We’ll see if we can minimize the losses for both our businesses...\"","The sudden reversal not only stunned the onlookers who had stopped to watch, but also left the guards of Hundred Herbs Hall completely baffled.","\"What’s wrong with the Shopkeeper? Just a moment ago, he was telling us to act according to the situation.\"","\"I don’t get it.\"","\"Maybe he just had a change of heart?\"","Clearly, none of the people around could understand the reason for Wang Ji’s sudden change.","But they mostly understood that Hundred Herbs Hall’s business was about to be affected—with the ordered herbs unexpectedly burned, everyone from patients getting prescriptions filled to customers coming for the tea drinks would feel the impact.","\"Let’s go, let’s go! Everything else can wait, but we can’t run out of the tea drinks.\"","\"I’ve got four wives at home! Without that Divine Bull Tea to restore my vigor, how am I supposed to handle it?\"","\"My wives need a bottle of Beauty Tea every few days, and I have to keep some Old Platinum Tea in stock for the elders in the family...\"","For a moment, business at Hundred Herbs Hall actually became even more brisk.","Even more people were now flocking to the shop.","Seeing this, Chen Yunfan glanced at Chen Yi and asked thoughtfully:","\"Are the effects of Hundred Herbs Hall’s tea drinks really that good?\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"They are indeed quite good. I had the chance to drink some before, through my cooperation with Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","As the one who had developed the recipes himself, he was naturally well aware of their effects.","While they couldn’t cure all illnesses, they certainly had the effect of strengthening the body and prolonging life.","This was because he added a special medicinal catalyst to every serving of tea—one that could draw Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi into the body to harmonize yin and yang.","For this reason, Chen Yi had specifically instructed Wang Ji to personally add that ingredient just before the tea was served.","As long as Wang Ji kept his mouth shut, it wouldn’t matter if the recipe was lost; no one could replicate the effects of the Hundred Herbs Hall’s teas.","Cui Qingwu overheard their conversation and asked, \"I heard that the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall created all those tea drinks?\"","Xiao Wan’er replied hesitantly, \"I suppose so. I’ve never asked Boss Chen Yu about it specifically.\"","Cui Qingwu hummed in acknowledgment and asked no more questions, pulling her into the restaurant.","At this, Chen Yi looked at Chen Yunfan and said with a smile, \"Brother, I’m going to make a trip to Hundred Herbs Hall. I’ll be back in a bit.\"","Chen Yunfan had long suspected that he was the so-called Boss Chen Yu.","So when he heard Chen Yi say this, he secretly rolled his eyes, turned without a word, and led Chun Ying into the Yunqing Building.","’The bond between us really has faded. This guy... he’s still hiding things so deep.’","’And to think I wasted all that sadness on him for marrying into the Xiao Family.’","So he decided that while he could let everything else go, his determination to give Chen Yi a good beating would not change.","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea what Chen Yunfan was thinking. After they were a good distance away, he calmly headed for Hundred Herbs Hall.","He bypassed the slightly crowded main hall and, cupping his hands in a fist, smiled at Zhang Dabao, who was standing guard outside the inner hall.","\"Excuse me, please announce that Chen Yi of the Xiao Family Medicine Hall has come to visit Shopkeeper Wang.\"","Zhang Dabao bowed impassively and said, \"Please wait a moment, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","After speaking, he scrambled upstairs and then quickly came clattering back down.","\"Mr. Qingzhou, this way, please. The Shopkeeper is waiting for you upstairs.\"","Chen Yi gestured for him to continue standing guard, then calmly walked up to the second floor.","At that moment, Wang Ji was already waiting at the top of the stairs with the boss surnamed Jia. When they saw him coming up, both men bowed slightly and greeted him with a smile:","\"Mr. Qingzhou.\"","\"Jia Yuzhi of Jia’s Medicine Shop, an honor to meet you, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded in acknowledgment, then said, \"It would be more familiar if you both called me Shopkeeper Chen.\""]},{"number":364,"title":"Chapter 364 - 240: The Domineering King Landu","paragraphs":["Of course, he knew that was unlikely.","He had already gained some renown in Shu State for his Calligraphy Dao and Poetry, but it was mostly scholars who paid him any mind.","However, ever since his \"Song of the Water Melody\" from the Mid-Autumn Poetry Gala spread, there were likely few people in all of Shu State who didn’t know his name.","This was especially true for those who had witnessed the \"Human World Immortal Realm\" at Quchi. Through word of mouth, they had come to see him as something of an Immortal.","Jia Yuzhi was no exception. His expression gave no hint that just moments ago, he had been agonizing over his own losses.","After a few pleasantries, the three of them entered a private room inside.","Chen Yi glanced around and raised an eyebrow. \"Shopkeeper Wang, you’ve really spared no expense.\"","He hadn’t noticed it the last time he was here, but looking again, he saw the private room had been completely transformed.","It wasn’t that the furnishings had changed, but that the wood, bricks, and tiles had all been replaced with materials that offered better soundproofing.","To say nothing of the rest, the Fragrant Willow Wood used for the single window set into the wall was worth a thousand taels of Gold alone.","It was even more valuable than the wood chosen for the Old Master’s Qingjing Residence.","A smile appeared on Wang Ji’s face, and a hint of delight flashed in his eyes as he said:","\"You flatter me, Mr. Qingzhou. My boss was the one who instructed me to do all this.\"","’This man knows what he’s doing.’","Chen Yi nodded to himself, took a seat first, and said, \"I hope my sudden visit hasn’t disturbed you two.\"","Wang Ji smiled and replied that it was no disturbance at all, then proceeded to introduce Jia Yuzhi.","\"This is Boss Jia, the owner of Jia’s Medicine Shop, which has been supplying the Hundred Herbs Hall with medicinal ingredients.\"","\"Just now, the two of us were discussing the arrival date for the next shipment of ingredients.\"","Chen Yi said, \"Oh?\" and looked at Jia Yuzhi, asking bluntly, \"I heard just now that Boss Jia’s medicinal ingredients met with some disaster?\"","Hearing this, a bitter expression crossed Jia Yuzhi’s face.","\"I won’t hide it from you, Mr. Qingzhou. I don’t know which deity I’ve offended this time, but I’ve been struck by a terrible string of bad luck.\"","\"The day before yesterday, a fire broke out in the East Market Grain Store’s warehouse, and it burned down most of the storeroom where I kept my ingredients.\"","\"Thankfully, Shopkeeper Wang has been understanding and hasn’t blamed me. Otherwise, I’d be too ashamed to show my face at the Hundred Herbs Hall again.\"","Wang Ji privately pursed his lips. ’If the Master hadn’t given the order, I’d have made this Old Jia compensate us with half his fortune.’","For the Hundred Herbs Hall’s upcoming expansion, he had expanded the workshop and recruited more staff, investing tens of thousands of silver coins in total.","Who could have known that after all his preparations were complete, the most crucial ingredient supply would be gone? How could he not be furious?","Chen Yi was, of course, aware of all this.","But in his view, silver coins could be earned again, and if the medicinal ingredients were gone, they could find other merchants to buy from. A few days’ delay wouldn’t have a major impact.","He was more concerned about the situation at the East Market Grain Store.","\"I hear that several grain stores in the East Market lost a lot of grain in the fire?\"","Jia Yuzhi nodded, clearly annoyed. \"An estimated loss of over a hundred thousand shi of grain.\"","\"And the price of grain has risen again?\"","\"You’ve heard? That’s right, it’s gone up quite a bit. Right now, the price of grain in the East and West Markets has soared to two and a half taels of silver per shi.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding.","If he remembered correctly, the price before he went to Tonglin Town was one and a half taels.","For the price to jump another whole tael of silver in just two or three days was somewhat surprising even to him.","’That merchant surnamed Lin is already dead, and several grain store warehouses have been burned. What’s the point of the price rising so high?’","’Do they even have any grain to sell?’","Chen Yi suddenly thought of Liu Taofang, the second son of the Liu Family. He guessed it must be his old-stock corn.","As he was thinking, he heard Jia Yuzhi continue, \"Speaking of tragedies, I, Old Jia, am not the most tragic case.\"","\"The most tragic one is Lin Huai’an, the owner of the Lin Family Grain Store.\"","Chen Yi looked at him and asked, \"How so? Did the Lin Family Grain Store suffer the greatest losses?\"","\"It was more than just that.\"","Jia Yuzhi leaned in with a secretive air. \"On the very night the East Market Grain Storehouse was burned, Lin Huai’an of the Lin Family Grain Store was murdered.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"I heard he was poisoned by his own wife.\"","\"If it weren’t for a final burst of clarity before he died, during which he arranged his affairs, the Lin Family would probably be in complete chaos right now.\"","Jia Yuzhi sighed as he spoke. \"He was a pitiful man, too.\"","\"To think he came to Shu State from Ji State all by himself, spent five years building such a massive enterprise, only to end up like this.\"","Beside them, Wang Ji couldn’t help but chime in, \"My Hundred Herbs Hall is pitiful, too.\"","Jia Yuzhi gave an embarrassed laugh and repeatedly cupped his hands. \"My apologies. Rest assured, I will do everything in my power to replenish your stock.\"","\"Let’s hope so...\"","「After a few more moments of conversation.」","Aside from the matters of the East Market Grain Store and the Lin Family, Chen Yi also learned that the few barbarian slaves were still missing.","The Imprisonment Department and the government officials had searched fruitlessly for clues and were now reportedly conducting a house-to-house search.","\"Didn’t those people from Poshisu Country go cause a scene at the Government Office?\"","\"They went, of course they went.\"","Jia Yuzhi said with a gloating expression, \"But it was no use.\"","\"Our Great Wei Dynasty has never been on good terms with Poshisu Country. A few years ago, when the Barbarian Left King attacked Mengshui Pass, Poshisu Country’s troops even took the opportunity to raid our borders.\"","\"Under these circumstances, why would the Lord Prefect pay any mind to those human traffickers from Poshisu Country?\"","\"Not only that, but the Young Master of the Lin Family Grain Store, Lin Zhenghong, didn’t even have time to arrange the funeral before he took his men to find those human traffickers, demanding they compensate the grain store for its losses.\"","Wang Ji couldn’t help but ask, \"Did those people from Poshisu Country agree?\"","A look of regret appeared on Jia Yuzhi’s round face. \"If they had, I wouldn’t have had to come to you for help today.\"","\"Don’t be fooled by their ability to traffic barbarian slaves; they’re just underlings following orders.\"","\"The real decision-makers aren’t in Shu State at all.\"","Chen Yi took the opportunity to ask, \"I’ve heard there’s a powerful group of horse bandits over in Poshisu Country, led by someone called King Landu?\"","Jia Yuzhi froze for a moment upon hearing the name. A hint of fear appeared on his face as he said, \"Mr. Qingzhou, you know of King Landu as well?\""]},{"number":365,"title":"Chapter 365 - 240: King Landu, Overbearing","paragraphs":["\"What? Is he not well known?\"","\"Not at all. It’s just that we merchants who travel frequently never dare to call him by his ’bandit title’ directly. We mostly just call him the ’Bandit King’.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"And why is that?\"","\"That King Landu is a ruthless character. Not only is he greedy and domineering, but his methods are vicious.\"","\"Merchants who travel the Ancient Tea-Horse Road year-round, whether they’re from our Great Wei Dynasty, the Western Buddha Country, or even Poshisu Country, all have to give him a pound of flesh.\"","\"Even I...\"","Jia Yuzhi paused, a fearful look on his face. \"Most of the shopkeepers I sent to Poshisu Country to procure herbs were either killed or wounded.\"","\"King Landu has his rules. All passing merchants must hand over half their goods. If you dare to run, he’ll kill everyone. If you dare to hide anything, he’ll kill half of you. If the count is wrong, he’ll kill one person, just depending on his mood.\"","Wang Ji clearly didn’t know the details about King Landu and asked, \"How can our Great Wei Dynasty tolerate someone like that?\"","Jia Yuzhi gave a bitter smile. \"Shopkeeper Wang, there’s something you don’t know.\"","\"That King Landu isn’t just a simple horse bandit. He’s also the blood brother of the king of Poshisu Country, and he has nearly twenty thousand men under his command.\"","\"Unless the Marquis personally leads the Dingyuan Army back to Poshisu Country, it would be impossible to annihilate them.\"","\"What’s more, that King Landu was taught by the Jade Dragon National Preceptor of Poshisu Country. His Martial Arts cultivation reached the Grandmaster realm long ago. Ordinary Martial Artists would just be throwing their lives away if they went after him.\"","Grandmaster...","Martial Arts was divided into nine realms: the lower, middle, and upper, each with three stages.","And Grandmaster was a realm above those nine.","A Martial Artist who reached this realm possessed strength beyond human limits.","Chen Yi frowned to himself. ’No wonder the Hidden Guard takes King Landu so seriously.’","Having learned most of what he wanted to know, he signaled for Wang Ji to send Jia Yuzhi away first.","After he left,","Chen Yi then took out the letter Lin Huai’an had written to King Landu. While making small talk with Wang Ji, he began writing on the table.","[This afternoon, find someone who can read the Poshisu script. They must be trustworthy. Have them translate the contents of this letter for me.]","[Wait for me tonight at the residence on Chuansi Street.]","Wang Ji nodded after reading, carefully took the letter, and wrote back: [Sir, the medicinal herbs haven’t arrived yet. The Hundred Herbs Hall workshop has been somewhat affected. I’m afraid things will be delayed for a few days.]","Chen Yi waved his hand, signaling that it was no matter, and said with a smile, \"I only came here to ask when Boss Chen Yu will be returning to Shu State.\"","He held up three fingers.","Wang Ji understood immediately and said, \"I’m afraid Mr. Qingzhou will be disappointed. My boss should be back in three months, around New Year’s Day.\"","Chen Yi smiled and exchanged a few more words before getting up to leave, his mind a whirlwind of thoughts.","After learning about King Landu’s situation, he grew even more curious about the Hidden Guard General’s intentions for contacting him.","’Surely this bunch of White Tiger Guards, who see it as their duty to destabilize neighboring countries, haven’t also turned traitor, have they?’","After a moment of thought,","Chen Yi shook his head to himself. ’Probably not.’","’If even the White Tiger Guard were siding with the enemy and funding them, then the Great Wei Dynasty might as well just be overthrown. There’d be no point in trying to maintain it.’","\"I need to see what these Hidden Guards are really up to.\"","Without lingering, Chen Yi went straight to the Yunqing Building and immediately spotted a lovely figure waiting by a second-floor window—Xiao Wan’er.","The two of them looked at each other and smiled.","Xiao Wan’er waved to him, her face blooming into a smile that brightened the gloomy, rainy day.","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, then walked up the stairs to the second floor and entered a spacious and magnificent private room.","Glancing around, he clasped his fist in a salute and said with a smile, \"My apologies for keeping you all waiting.\"","Cui Qingwu didn’t respond.","Chen Yunfan, leaning back in his chair, waved a hand for him to sit. \"Since when did you become so polite, Brother Yi?\"","As Chen Yi sat down with Xiao Wan’er, he retorted just as impolitely:","\"What can I do? My dear brother is now the Assistant Governor of the Shu State Governor’s Office. I wouldn’t dare overstep my bounds.\"","\"...You actually care that I’m an Assistant Governor?\"","Seeing the two start to bicker, Cui Qingwu tugged on Chen Yunfan’s sleeve and gestured for Huan’er to serve the food.","\"Why are you two still like a couple of kids?\"","Chen Yunfan tilted his head up and said, \"I’m not. Can’t say the same for Brother Yi, though.\"","Chen Yi was about to fire back when Xiao Wan’er, beside him, also gave him a little tug and asked in a curious tone:","\"Little Sister Qingwu, were they like this when they were little, too?\"","Seeing her expression, Cui Qingwu’s interest was piqued. She smilingly began to recount the \"history\" between the two brothers, Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan.","Even though Chen Yunfan shot her a look to stop, she kept on talking without a pause.","Chen Yi, on the other hand, didn’t mind. Hearing \"his own\" stories from someone else’s mouth was a novel experience.","\"...In short, Qingzhou was highly regarded back then, while Brother Yunfan, on the other hand, was punished many times.\"","After listening, Xiao Wan’er covered her mouth and giggled. \"So the rumors from Jiangnan Prefecture were all true. My husband really has been clever since he was a child.\"","Chen Yunfan pouted. ’Brother Yi is still plenty clever now.’","’In fact, he’s incredible.’","’Not only has he reached Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao and the Martial Arts Dao, he’s even accomplished in the Medical Dao.’","’In comparison, he, the older brother, had nothing on Chen Yi except for a disposable title as Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office.’","’It’s just pathetic.’","Once the dishes were all served, Cui Qingwu brought over a jar of wine, filled the cups for Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan, and said with a smile, \"Have a taste.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, clinked cups with Chen Yunfan, and then drained his in one go.","He wasn’t a man who enjoyed wine—not in this life, and not in his last one either.","So, as the wine went down, he only tasted a hint of sweetness and smoothness, and not much else.","Chen Yunfan, however, was more of a connoisseur. After drinking, he smacked his lips. \"Not bad. It’s got a sweet flavor.\"","Cui Qingwu said with a smile, \"This is my Yunqing Building’s Lang Wine, brewed with spring water from Wumeng Mountain and the upper reaches of the Chishui River. It has a natural sweetness, so even the new vintage tastes good.\"","Watching the three of them laugh and joke, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but feel a little envious.","She wanted to have a taste too, but alas, her body wouldn’t allow it.","Chen Yi glanced at her, noticed her mood, and placed a pastry on her plate. \"The food should be pretty good, too,\" he said with a smile.","Xiao Wan’er’s envy instantly vanished. She gave a gentle nod and began to eat in small, delicate bites.","After three rounds of drinks, Chen Yunfan remembered something and asked, \"Brother Yi, you’ll be participating in the Annual Examination this time, right?\"","Chen Yi heard this and asked in surprise, \"You want to persuade me too, Brother?\"","\"Persuade?\"","\"I don’t want to participate, but alas...\"","Chen Yi glanced at Xiao Wan’er, earning a reproachful look from her, and then continued:","\"Alas, I have no choice but to participate.\"","Chen Yunfan paused, put down his chopsticks, and said with a serious expression, \"You have to participate.\"","Chen Yi’s heart skipped a beat. \"Oh? And why is that?\"","\"Because that Academic Administrator...\""]},{"number":366,"title":"Chapter 366 - 241: Autumn Letter to My Wife","paragraphs":["\"Academic Administrator Ma Shuhan has sent word that all men in Shu State who hold scholarly honors must attend. Those who do not will be stripped of their honors and forever barred from the imperial examinations.\"","Chen Yunfan looked at Chen Yi and said gravely,","\"You’ve missed the Annual Examination twice before. Even with Jinling Academy vouching for you, you were still demoted from a scholar to an apprentice student.\"","\"If you miss it this time, you can imagine the consequences.\"","Seeing Chen Yi remain silent, he continued, \"Furthermore, Ma Shuhan has also submitted a memorial to the Imperial Court, petitioning the Holy Emperor to change parts of the Sixth Rank Demotion Step.\"","\"Oh? What did he change?\"","Chen Yi knew of the Sixth Rank Demotion Step. It was essentially an evaluation system with grades, similar to \"Excellent, Good, Fair, Poor,\" or \"A, B, C, D.\"","Ranks ranged from \"First\" to \"Sixth,\" with First being the highest and Sixth being the worst.","First and Second Rank scholars received rewards, while Third Rank was considered a pass, with neither reward nor punishment.","But for the Fourth Rank, punishment was administered—usually a rap on the knuckles from an Academy Master.","Fifth and Sixth Ranks were even more severe. In lesser cases, the student was expelled from the academy. In more serious cases, they were stripped of their scholarly honors, demoted to a basic student, and forced to start over.","Chen Yunfan’s expression was unusually serious as he said, \"For anyone below Third Rank, their scholarly honors may be revoked, subject to review.\"","\"Subject to review?\"","\"Yes. Besides the Academic Administrator’s evaluation, they will also consult the Shu State Governor’s Office, the Academy Masters, and respected elders for their recommendations. That’s what ’subject to review’ means.\"","’So there’s some room to maneuver,’ Chen Yi realized.","’The evaluations from the Government Office, the masters, and so on... it all came down to the people involved.’","’If the right people are chosen, the Shu State scholars can expect results similar to previous years.’","’But if the wrong people are chosen... who knows what will happen.’","Suddenly, Chen Yi thought of the conversation he had overheard between Li Huai’gu and Mr. Yue Ming at Guiyun Academy.","He recalled how Ma Shuhan, the Academic Administrator of Shu State, had invited Mr. Yue Ming to be the Vice Examiner for the upcoming Annual Examination.","He remembered Mr. Yue Ming saying that he and Ma Shuhan didn’t get along, and that the invitation was likely a deliberate attempt to cause trouble for him.","As these thoughts passed through his mind, Chen Yi asked nonchalantly, \"When did Academic Administrator Ma make this decision?\"","\"He came to the Governor’s Office yesterday to announce it.\"","\"From his tone, it’s clear he wants to teach the Shu State scholars a good lesson.\"","\"I have no idea what he gets out of this. It’s ridiculous.\"","Seeing Chen Yunfan grumbling, Chen Yi inwardly understood and asked with a smile, \"Did the two Governors not object?\"","He knew that in the Great Wei Dynasty, the post of a state’s Academic Administrator was not a high one—Junior Fourth Grade at most.","It was a far cry from Liu Hong and Yang Ye’s ranks.","However, an Academic Administrator wasn’t a local official. The position was more like that of an imperial envoy, typically appointed directly by the Holy Emperor to assess the performance of a state’s scholars.","This gave the position its unique nature—they could report directly to the emperor.","’So even if Liu Hong and Yang Ye were unhappy with Ma Shuhan’s methods, they probably wouldn’t show it too openly,’ Chen Yi thought.","Chen Yunfan took a drink of wine and said disdainfully, \"Of course Lord Yang is dissatisfied. He’s in charge of Shu State’s academic affairs, so how could he let that fellow Ma run amok?\"","\"But what could he do? Liu Hong agreed to it.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Lord Liu supported it?\"","He pieced it together in his mind.","’By now, Mr. Yue Ming should have already met with Yang Ye and politely declined the Vice Examiner position.’","’Did Ma Shuhan tell Liu Hong about his plan to petition for changes to the Sixth Rank Demotion Step ahead of time?’","’But why would he agree?’","’After all, if the scholars of Shu State failed the Annual Examination en masse, it would only reflect poorly on a high official like Liu Hong, who was in charge of the region. There was no benefit for him.’","’Unless... the two of them planned it together.’","Chen Yunfan grunted in agreement, put down his wine cup, and continued his persuasion. \"I’m guessing that Ma fellow is up to no good.\"","\"You should just go ahead and take it this time. With your talent, passing the Annual Examination will be a piece of cake.\"","A smile touched Chen Yi’s lips as he nodded. \"You have a point, Brother.\"","’I had already decided to take the exam, especially now, given these bizarre circumstances.’","’I’m curious to see what Ma Shuhan... or rather, Governor Liu Hong, is planning.’","Chen Yunfan glanced at him and snorted, \"You’ve been as stubborn as a mule since you were a kid. It’s rare to see you so agreeable.\"","’But,’ he also thought, ’if it hadn’t been for the ’accident’ five years ago, Chen Yi would have likely already passed the higher examinations and become an official. He never would have ended up in this situation.’","’Ultimately, I’ll have to ask Mother, Cui Yu, to find out the real story.’","They continued to eat, drink, and chat.","Chen Yunfan did most of the talking, complaining about how busy the Governor’s Office was and how he, an Assistant Governor, had really drawn the short straw.","\"With Xiao Dongchen’s death, I’m the only Assistant Governor left in the Government Office. Not only do I have to handle my own duties, I have to take over his as well.\"","\"If Li Huai’gu didn’t help out, I’d never have a moment to spare.\"","When Chen Yunfan mentioned Xiao Dongchen, Chen Yi, who knew the full story, understood that the man’s death was no great loss. Nevertheless, Xiao Wan’er’s expression grew a little unnatural.","Seeing this, Cui Qingwu, who was sitting nearby, changed the subject. She smiled and said, \"All this hard work must come with great rewards, Brother Yunfan.\"","Chen Yunfan raised his eyebrows at her words, then turned to Chen Yi with a smug look.","\"Qingwu is right. After all the work I’ve done, I should at least get a First Class rating on my year-end performance review.\"","’He’s showing off again,’ Chen Yi thought with a private smile, but he still offered a few words of praise.","\"Right after you passed the highest examinations, Brother, you were held in high regard by the Holy Emperor and appointed Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office for Shu State. Your official career should be smooth sailing from here on out.\"","But the smile on Chen Yunfan’s face faded. He pursed his lips and said, \"That man is not so benevolent.\"","\"Oh? There’s more to it?\"","\"It’s not apparent yet, but based on what I saw and heard in the Capital Prefecture, that man is a brilliant and ambitious strategist. He never does anything without a reason.\"","\"His posting me and Li Huai’gu to Shu State... I reckon he has other plans down the line.\"","Chen Yi had suspected as much himself. At first, he’d guessed that Chen Yunfan was sent to Shu State to succeed Yang Ye as the Right Governor."]},{"number":367,"title":"Chapter 367 - 241: Autumn Letter to My Wife","paragraphs":["But now that Chen Yunfan was being so forthright, he actually felt a little more suspicious.","Perhaps the Emperor on the Dragon Throne was playing an even bigger game on the chessboard that was Shu State.","Just then, Cui Qingwu stood up again to refill their cups, smiling as she spoke.","\"This is supposed to be a private dinner, so let’s not talk about official business, shall we? What do you say, Sister Wan’er?\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced at Chen Yi. Seeing the smile on his face, she nodded as well.","Cui Qingwu took in their interaction, and her smile brightened.","’There’s something going on with these two...’","By mid-afternoon, they had eaten and drunk their fill.","Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, and the others then rose to leave.","Cui Qingwu and Chen Yunfan followed them outside the restaurant to see them off.","Cui Qingwu took the umbrella from Chun Ying to hold it for Chen Yunfan and said, \"Sister Wan’er, once business at the restaurant stabilizes in a couple of days, I’ll come visit you at the Xiao Mansion.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded lightly and replied with a smile that she would be welcome anytime.","In contrast, the brothers Chen Yunfan and Chen Yi were not so formal, simply exchanging a few casual jokes.","But when Chen Yunfan saw Chen Yi acting so carefree, he couldn’t resist adding a few words of advice.","\"Brother Yi, you’re famous now. Your Calligraphy Dao has reached Perfection, and you’re an Instructor at Guiyun Academy. It’s inevitable that you’ll attract the envy of others in the future.\"","\"You should spend more time on your Martial Arts Cultivation, so you’re prepared if some reckless fool comes looking for trouble.\"","\"You’re the one who needs to be careful, Brother. Your fame as the Imperial Top Scholar is unmatched, and you’re not even married yet. You might get kidnapped and forced into marriage one of these days.\"","Before Chen Yunfan could even speak, Cui Qingwu, who had overheard their conversation, immediately exclaimed, \"Who would dare?!\"","Chen Yunfan shot Chen Yi a glare, as if to say, ’Way to touch a sore subject.’ He then waved his hand dismissively. \"Brother Yi is just joking. Don’t take him seriously.\"","He then turned to Xiao Wan’er. \"Miss Wan’er, you’ll have to make sure my brother here spends more time on his Martial Arts Cultivation.\"","However, it was obvious his words had little to no effect.","Xiao Wan’er just smiled gently, her beautiful eyes resting on Chen Yi, and offered no response.","At this, Chen Yunfan sullenly shut his mouth. He muttered a few words under his breath and waved for Chen Yi to leave.","’Just you wait. Sooner or later, I’ll beat you into submission and make you admit how amazing your big brother is.’","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea what was on Chen Yunfan’s mind. They said their goodbyes, and he escorted Xiao Wan’er back to the Xiao Family.","Faintly, he could still hear Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu’s conversation.","Things like, \"Don’t worry, Brother Yi was just joking,\" and \"You know my skills better than anyone.\"","It seemed Chen Yi’s earlier teasing had worked, leaving Cui Qingwu a little worried.","Chatting and laughing, the members of the group went their separate ways, their figures vanishing into the curtain of rain.","But in a tailor’s shop not far away, a middle-aged man dressed in the linen clothes of a servant was watching them.","He watched for a moment, a faint smile appearing on his face.","’Simurgh Phoenix, Fledgling, the eldest young master of the Chen family...’","’They’ve all changed quite a bit since arriving in Shu State.’","After a moment of thought, he beckoned to the shopkeeper behind him. \"Contact Simurgh Phoenix. Have her meet me here at midnight.\"","\"Yes...\"","...","The rare day out had greatly improved Xiao Wan’er’s mood.","Aside from settling on the site for the Medical Dao Academy in Tonglin Town, this was the first time she had enjoyed such a relaxed meal out with friends.","Unlike her previous appointment with Liu Zhaoxue at Yingchun Building, which she attended with Chen Yi, this time she felt completely at ease in the company of Cui Qingwu and Chen Yunfan.","Of course, Chen Yi’s presence had something to do with it as well.","All in all, Xiao Wan’er was in high spirits.","Even in the afternoon, as she bustled about Jiaxing Garden, a smile remained on her face.","\"Juan’er, take this rough sketch to Master Lai. Ask him to take his people to Tonglin Town to have a look, and to provide detailed blueprints as soon as possible.\"","\"Yes, Miss.\"","\"Cui’er, go ask Wuge when he’ll be back. He’ll be dining in the garden tonight.\"","\"And Huatang... hmm... I’ll have to trouble you to go to Spring Lotus Garden. Please let my brother-in-law know. Also, tell him to write a letter back to my second sister.\"","After everyone had dispersed, Xiao Wan’er went to the study, took out a brush and paper, and began to write her own reply to Xiao Jinghong.","[My Dearest Second Sister, all is well at home.","Grandfather is in good health, though his appetite and sleep have been affected recently by his worries over provisions for the Three Towns.","Fortunately, Grandfather has already thought of a solution...]","Xiao Wan’er’s brush paused. Images of Chen Yi’s recent situation and that poem of his surfaced in her mind, and she hesitated before continuing to write:","[You must have heard about the poem Qingzhou wrote on Mid-Autumn Night.","In my opinion, he was using the poem to express his feelings. He must have been thinking of you... ’May we live long and share the moon’s beauty, a thousand miles apart.’ See how beautiful those words are?]","Having written this, Xiao Wan’er let out a long sigh, but a look of relief appeared on her face.","\"Second Sister, just this once, I’ll allow myself to be selfish...\"","After putting the letter away, Xiao Wan’er got up and took Cui’er with her to Qingjing Residence.","She had to ask the Old Marquis for his opinion on the matter she and Chen Yi had discussed the previous night.","It wasn’t just about choosing a suitable dean for the Medical Dao Academy. She also truly hoped that a Divine Doctor from the Great Wei Dynasty would come to Shu State.","If so, perhaps the Old Marquis’s grave illness could truly be cured.","「Spring Lotus Garden.」","When Shen Huatang arrived, she found Chen Yi in his study, painting.","She glanced at his work only for a moment before relaying Xiao Wan’er’s instructions.","After listening, Chen Yi nodded. \"I’ll write it and send it over later.\"","Shen Huatang hesitated slightly, swallowing the words that had risen to her lips. She bowed and turned to leave.","Things were different now.","Back then, Chen Yi had just married into the Xiao Family, and on top of that, he had fled on their wedding day. Her impression of him had been terrible.","Now, with Chen Yi’s fame soaring, the attitude of everyone in the Xiao Family, from top to bottom, had changed.","It wasn’t just Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Jinghong; even the Old Marquis showed him special favor.","To say nothing of Xiao Wuge, who was always by Chen Yi’s side."]},{"number":368,"title":"Chapter 368 - 241: Autumn Letter to My Wife","paragraphs":["Shen Huatang was aware of this, so she could no longer be as outspoken as she had been before.","At this thought, she sighed. \"In that case, I can only let General Jinghong down.\"","There was nothing she could do. She could only pretend that nothing had happened.","Of course, Chen Yi was unaware of what others were thinking. After finishing a landscape painting with a few deft strokes, he began to write a letter to Xiao Jinghong.","This time, he didn’t write a poem as he usually did. Instead, he wrote a letter home in his capacity as her husband.","It was filled with warm inquiries and cheerful updates on his current situation.","At the end, however, Chen Yi thought for a moment and added a poem. He even made a point of writing it in his Perfection Realm Cursive Script:","\"Threads of rain and needles of wind weave the late autumn air,","I laugh at my restless heart, which loves to climb the stair.\"","\"The letter is written, like wild geese as clouds begin to part,","With the Jianghu’s waves now still, so too is my heart.\"","\"I only urge you to eat well, pity the mums so thin,","And don’t resent the slow boat for the distance we are in.\"","\"In this world, we are partners of mist and rosy haze,","Not envying the bonded ducks, but the free gull’s wandering ways.\"","A Mental Realm materialized, enveloping the study, though it didn’t spread to cover all of Quchi like his *Song of the Water Melody* had.","Yet, in the breaking dawn of the rainy autumn day, the figures of Chen Yi and Xiao Jinghong could be seen sitting side by side within it.","Chen Yi looked up with a slight smile. \"My dear, seeing how much effort I’m putting in, I hope you’ll go easy on me in the future.\"","He wasn’t asking for much—only that when Xiao Jinghong eventually found out about all the things he had done, she might hit him a little less hard.","With that in mind, he added a few more lines.","[*Autumn Letter to My Wife*. A poem for our mutual encouragement.","Finally, I’ve decided to participate in this year’s Annual Examination. It’s just a formality, so don’t read too much into it.","I still remember the promise we made. I hope you do, too.]","’What promise?’","’The promise, of course, was that he would spend his life as an idle, live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family.’","’Although the Xiao Family’s circumstances had forced him to offer help from the shadows, he had no intention of toiling away forever.’","’Once he was certain that all the malicious forces in Shu State had been dealt with, he still yearned for that good life of \"picking chrysanthemums ’neath the eastern fence, and gazing leisurely upon the southern peak.\"’","Chen Yi blew the ink dry, sealed the letter in an envelope, and his gaze drifted to the window.","The rain was falling harder now.","Amid the RUMBLE of thunder, a cold wind whipped through the flowers and trees. Drifting leaves and petals were slapped against the stone slabs by the downpour.","Layer upon layer.","It was chaotic, yet possessed a rare tranquility.","Chen Yi loved nature and quiet. He loved sunny days and rainy days alike.","The one thing he didn’t like was trouble.","He especially disliked people disturbing his tranquil and carefree life.","People like Liu Hong and Ma Shuhan. People like the Hidden Guard and their Financiers. People like King Landu and Lin Huai’an.","’Your schemes in Shu State originally had nothing to do with me,’ he thought, ’but you never, ever should have dragged the Xiao Family into this.’","Even though Chen Yi knew the Xiao Family was an unavoidable piece of the puzzle in Shu State, he still wished those people had actively avoided them.","Whether or not they could have was no longer his concern.","Afterward, Chen Yi resumed painting to hone his Painting Skill and integrate the Profound Mysteries of the Painting Dao.","His progress was surprisingly good.","Including the past two days, he had painted around a hundred pieces in total and had completely absorbed the Minor Achievement Painting Dao, elevating his Ink-Wash Painting to the peak of proficiency.","The only drawback was that Ink-Wash Painting emphasized spirit over form. It was full of charm for landscapes, but wasn’t quite adequate for painting portraits.","Thus, before dinner, Chen Yi began to study other Painting Techniques.","Techniques like fine-line ink drawing and meticulous, heavy-color painting.","Eventually, he came up with a solution.","’I just need to prioritize intent and fuse ink-wash, line drawing, and meticulous colored painting into a single style.’","’Chen Yi’s thinking was simple.’","’He had the Painting Dao on his side, which already gave him profound guidance on all sorts of Painting Techniques. As long as he could achieve his desired effect, what did the specific technique matter?’","’It would just mean spending a little more time practicing the Painting Dao.’","Having made his decision, Chen Yi was no longer in a rush.","Seeing that it was getting late, he called for Xiaodie to tidy up the study.","After Xiao Wuge returned, they had dinner, and then everyone retired to their respective rooms to rest.","With each autumn rain, the weather turns colder.","Autumn was a season for sleeping early and rising early.","Unfortunately, after returning to his room, Chen Yi only cultivated his Four Symbols Skill for about two hours before getting up and changing into a set of Night Clothes.","Under the cover of the deserted, rainy night, he slipped out of the Xiao Family residence and headed straight for the house on Chuansi Street.","Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao were already waiting for him there.","While Zhang Dabao began applying his disguise, Chen Yi asked Wang Ji, \"Is the letter translated?\"","Wang Ji hastily produced a stack of papers and handed the top two sheets to him. His expression was grave as he said:","\"My lord, the contents of this letter are... you had better see for yourself. This humble one dares not say more.\"","He had taken precautions that afternoon.","When he’d found someone to translate the letter, he had deliberately copied its contents onto dozens of separate scraps of paper. Only after they were all translated did he piece the message back together.","Although some sentences were disjointed and fragmented, it didn’t prevent him from discerning the letter’s true contents.","He hadn’t realized the gravity of it until he looked. The revelation had chilled him to the bone.","Chen Yi glanced at him, having already guessed some of the letter’s contents, and began to read it calmly.","[For the personal attention of King Landu. I, Lin Huai’an of the Ji State Trading Company, extend greetings on behalf of my master.","The two previous transactions between you and our Ji State Trading Company were concluded to the great satisfaction of all. This time, I wish to propose another trade with you.","Ten thousand *shi* of Refined Iron, two thousand sets of Heavy Armor and horse barding, two thousand Refined Iron Hundred-Refined Blades...]","Chen Yi frowned slightly as he finished reading.","’Ji State Trading Company?’","’It seems that Jia Yuzhi mentioned that name this afternoon...’"]},{"number":369,"title":"Chapter 369 - 242: A Most Vicious Scheme","paragraphs":["Besides the Ji State Trading Company, the items Lin Huai’an was trading with King Landu also left Chen Yi stunned.","Ten thousand shi of Refined Iron—over seven hundred tons.","It might not seem like much, estimated to be only a tenth of the Great Wei Dynasty’s annual output of Refined Iron.","But a single blade or sword only weighed three to five pounds.","Over seven hundred tons of Refined Iron was enough to forge two hundred thousand swords and blades.","Although from what Chen Yi knew of the Poshisu Country, their forging techniques were far inferior to those of the Great Wei Dynasty.","But if this iron was used for other purposes, such as Armor or daily necessities, it could still significantly increase the Poshisu Country’s strength.","And what’s more, there were also two thousand sets of Heavy Armor and horse barding, plus two thousand Refined Iron Hundred-Refined Blades?","One could just imagine: once these items were in King Landu’s hands, he could instantly equip a force of two thousand heavy cavalrymen.","And that wasn’t even counting the two previous transactions for unknown items...","As Chen Yi considered this, he turned to Wang Ji and asked, \"How much do you know about the Ji State Trading Company?\"","He only knew that Ji State was to the northeast of Shu State, separated by You State and Jing State, but this was the first time he had ever heard of the Ji State Trading Company.","Wang Ji hesitated. \"Forgive me, Sir. I have only heard of them in passing and don’t know the specifics of the Ji State Trading Company.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, not blaming him.","After a moment of thought, he instructed, \"Find a way to make some inquiries. See if that Boss Jia knows anything.\"","He paused, then added a reminder, \"If anyone asks, just say the Hundred Herbs Hall is looking to expand its partnerships beyond Shu State.\"","Wang Ji quickly nodded in agreement.","He didn’t know what his master planned to do, but the contents of that letter made his blood run cold.","After a moment’s hesitation,","Wang Ji said, \"Sir, there is something I must say, though I don’t know if it’s my place.\"","Chen Yi, his eyes still on the letter in his hand, replied without looking up, \"Speak.\"","\"Sir, for the Ji State Trading Company to dare trade with the Poshisu Country—and in contraband like Refined Iron and weaponry, which are strictly controlled by the Imperial Court—one can only imagine how powerful their connections and backing must be.\"","\"If they find out that we know about this, won’t we... won’t we...\"","Wang Ji gritted his teeth. \"Won’t we bring disaster upon ourselves?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"Scared?\"","\"No, it’s not that...\"","\"It’s fine if you are. It’s only natural.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi put the two letters away and brought his hand down on the thick stack of paper on the adjacent table.","The paper instantly disintegrated into fluttering scraps.","\"But often, the very thing you fear most is what comes to pass.\"","\"In a situation like this, what do you think we should do?\"","Wang Ji, who had been bowing, froze. He raised his head slightly to look at Chen Yi, his expression conflicted.","The next moment, he gritted his teeth fiercely. \"Then it doesn’t matter who they are—they have to die!\"","Just as Chen Yi had said, fear was a natural instinct.","Especially now that the Hundred Herbs Hall’s business was thriving and he had established a livelihood for himself, he was terrified of losing everything he had worked so hard to gain.","But he also knew that everything he had now was thanks to Chen Yi.","They would prosper together, and they would fall together.","Therefore, whatever Chen Yi decided to do, whatever he ordered, Wang Ji just needed to obey and carry it out to the best of his ability.","\"Rest assured, Sir. I will get to the bottom of this Ji State Trading Company.\"","Chen Yi chuckled at his words and shook his head. \"For traitors of this magnitude, the most you’ll be able to find is superficial information.\"","\"If we want to uncover their true background, our only lead is likely Lin’s Grain Store.\"","\"Lin’s Grain Store... Lin Huai’an?\"","\"The very same.\"","\"But you don’t need to worry about that. For now, just focus on expanding the Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"Once word comes back from Yan Sea, you can begin.\"","Wang Ji felt a sense of relief and bowed. \"I will remember your instructions, Sir.\"","「A moment later.」","Chen Yi finished applying his disguise, then put on a Raincoat and a bamboo hat.","He glanced at the sky outside the window, then turned to Zhang Dabao with a thoughtful expression and asked:","\"Back when you were apprenticed to ’One Finger,’ you must have gotten to know some of the Jianghu People in Shu State, right?\"","Zhang Dabao nodded, his eyes burning with intensity. \"What are your orders, Sir?\"","Chen Yi smiled and gave his instructions. \"I also need you to keep an eye on people from the Poshisu Country within Shu State.\"","\"Find out where they’re living and what they’re doing here in Shu State.\"","He was very pleased with Zhang Dabao’s fearless, youthful energy.","He had far more drive than Wang Ji, the Medicine Hall Master.","After Zhang Dabao accepted the task, Chen Yi added a word of caution, \"There are experts among those from the Poshisu Country. Be extremely careful.\"","\"Don’t worry, Sir. I may not have many other skills, but a small task like this won’t be a problem.\"","Chen Yi patted his shoulder, gave a few more instructions to Wang Ji, and then left the residence.","Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao respectfully saw him off.","\"Dabao, from now on, you must serve the Sir with all your heart.\"","\"Yes, Shopkeeper.\"","\"Don’t call me Shopkeeper. We can just call each other brother.\"","\"Shopk—...Brother Wang.\"","Wang Ji smiled, chatted with him for a bit, and then left as well.","After this, he finally understood his place at Chen Yi’s side.","As Chen Yi’s plans grew more ambitious, the situations they faced would only become more severe and dangerous.","Many of them would be beyond his ability to handle as the Shopkeeper of the Hundred Herbs Hall.","So, he just needed to focus on the task at hand, expand the Hundred Herbs Hall throughout Shu State, and perhaps even across the Nine State and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei. Then he could retire with his work accomplished.","Chen Yi, of course, paid no mind to the thoughts of Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao.","To him, the Hundred Herbs Hall was still just a minor piece in his grand design, one he could afford to lose.","It would only become truly useful to him if it managed to expand across the Nine State and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei.","For now, at best, the Hundred Herbs Hall could provide him with some funds to alleviate the Xiao Family’s difficulties.","After leaving Chuansi Street, Chen Yi used the cover of night to bypass the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion and make his way to South Street."]},{"number":370,"title":"Chapter 370 - 242: A Most Vicious Plan","paragraphs":["By now, it was late in the evening.","Amid the thunderstorm, the number of pedestrians had dwindled significantly.","Even the patrolling government officials and Imprisonment Officers were nowhere to be seen.","Only a few shops and government offices along South Street still had people on guard.","Dull yellow lanterns swayed, illuminating the surroundings and faintly revealing the sheets of falling rain.","Taking advantage of the deserted streets, Chen Yi slipped over to the Liu Family residence, not far from the Governor’s Office.","He scanned the area.","Seeing no sign of Liu Lang, he deactivated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, and his True Essence began to circulate freely within him once more.","Then, he shattered a piece of rubble with a palm strike before his figure vanished into a corner.","Before long, Chen Yi saw a sneaky figure approaching.","When the man arrived, he surveyed his surroundings. Seeing no one, he let out a soft sound of confusion.","\"No one’s here?\"","Chen Yi recognized the voice. Confirming it was Liu Lang, he gave a soft cough and stepped out from the shadows.","\"Over here.\"","Liu Lang started. \"Boss?\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly and gestured for him to move away. \"This isn’t the place to talk.\"","The two then left the Liu Family residence one after another, hurrying toward South City’s Yanhua Lane.","Only after they had gone a good distance and found a secluded corner did Chen Yi finally stop.","Following behind him, Liu Lang asked with a smile, \"Boss, what brings you out tonight?\"","\"If you hadn’t come, I was planning to look for you tomorrow.\"","Chen Yi asked calmly, \"What have you found?\"","At his question, a slight smile appeared on Liu Lang’s face. \"I have indeed found something.\"","\"Do you remember the granary fire over in the East Market?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow, a few suspicions immediately forming in his mind. \"What did you overhear at his place?\"","\"If I’m not mistaken, he was the one who killed that merchant collaborating with his second son, the one called Lin Huai’an.\"","Hearing Liu Lang’s words, Chen Yi’s expression shifted slightly. \"You’re saying he sent someone to kill Lin Huai’an? You heard this with your own ears?\"","Liu Lang nodded repeatedly, pointing to his ear. \"That night, after I followed Liu the Second home, that old fox was waiting for him at the door.\"","\"The moment they met, he didn’t say a word. He just grabbed a whip and gave Liu the Second a vicious lashing.\"","\"Only after that did they start talking about it. Tsk, tsk. It took me a while to understand what was going on.\"","Chen Yi frowned subconsciously, his mind racing.","He had witnessed Lin Huai’an’s death firsthand—it had been by poisoning.","He had originally thought it was the work of that insatiably greedy wife, but now it seemed there was a hidden secret he hadn’t known.","’So it was Liu Hong?’","As he thought, Chen Yi spoke. \"Tell me everything you heard, word for word.\"","Without a second thought, Liu Lang recounted everything he had overheard that day.","Things like how Liu Taofang and Lin Huai’an had conspired to burn the summer grain supply of the Three Towns, then drive up grain prices in Shu State, intending to sell off their family’s old stock.","Furthermore, after doing all this, they planned to blame it on the Xiao Family, claiming that Elder Master Xiao’s grain purchases were what caused the price hike.","He also mentioned that Lin Huai’an was from the Ji State Trading Company, among other things.","\"...In the end, that old fox ordered his second son not to leave the house anytime soon, and told him to deny everything if anyone asked about Lin Huai’an.\"","After hearing the full story, Chen Yi’s brow furrowed even deeper.","Not only did Liu Hong know that Lin Huai’an was from the Ji State Trading Company, but he also knew what the company was doing up north—smuggling salt, iron, and weapons.","’Since Liu Hong knew all this, why would he kill Lin Huai’an?’","’Was it just because Liu Taofang was involved?’","Chen Yi thought it over and over, feeling that a man like Liu Hong wouldn’t have killed Lin Huai’an for such a simple reason.","This was especially true after learning from Liu Lang that Liu Hong suspected there were other reasons behind the deaths of Liu Wen and Xiao Dongchen.","He now knew that Liu Hong was an extremely cunning and meticulous man.","’A man like that must have a deeper motive for his actions.’","Immediately after, another question surfaced in Chen Yi’s mind:","’How did Liu Hong find out about Liu Taofang and Lin Huai’an’s conspiracy ahead of time?’","’Thinking it over, there’s only one possibility: someone must have tipped him off!’","’And only two parties could have done that—someone close to Liu Taofang, or someone close to Lin Huai’an.’","’Furthermore, given that Liu Hong was able to order Lin Huai’an’s death, the latter is more likely than the former.’","As Chen Yi considered this, a cold, harsh look appeared on his face.","’It seems I’ve underestimated this Governor.’","Liu Lang, oblivious to these thoughts, saw him remain silent for a long moment and couldn’t help but ask:","\"Boss, what do you want me to do next? Should I keep an eye on that old fox?\"","Chen Yi snapped back to reality at the question and took a deep breath. \"Keep watching him for a few more days.\"","\"I need to clarify a few things before I decide on the next step.\"","What he had learned from Liu Lang tonight forced him to re-evaluate Liu Hong.","He also had to rethink his subsequent plans and make some adjustments.","He had to avoid trying to steal a chicken only to lose the rice used to lure it.","Fortunately, after devising his plan to deal with the Liu Family and Liu Hong, he hadn’t acted rashly, instead sending Liu Lang to watch them.","There was still plenty of time to scheme and lay his groundwork.","If not for this, he likely would have underestimated Liu Hong’s capabilities and made a critical misjudgment.","Hearing this, Liu Lang said with great interest, \"That old fox is hiding his hand so well. I’m curious to see what he’s planning, too.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, then thought for a moment before asking, \"Who has he met with recently, and what has he been doing?\"","\"Most of the time, he’s at the government office handling official business.\"","\"He leaves his residence before dawn every day and only returns from the Governor’s Office in the evening. He rarely has visitors.\"","At this point, Liu Lang paused. \"Although, a man with the surname Ma has visited twice.\"","\"He comes alone each time and huddles with Liu Hong in the study, talking about mysterious things.\"","Chen Yi’s heart skipped a beat. He looked at him and asked, \"Ma Shuhan?\"","\"Yes, that’s the name.\"","\"But I saw they were just talking about things like scholars, the Annual Examination, and the imperial exams, so I didn’t pay much attention.\"","\"During their conversations, did they mention Mr. Yue Ming, or the names of anyone else in Shu State?\"","Seeing how concerned he was, Liu Lang began to think back carefully.","\"Mr. Yue Ming... I think so. There were quite a few other names too, like Mr. Zhuo Ying and Mr. Lingchuan.\"","\"Oh, right, and also Right Governor Yang Ye, as well as names from the Tang Family and the Wan Family.\"","\"Tang Zixing?\"","\"No, it was someone named Tang Yeren.\"","\"That Ma fellow said he also holds the rank of a Scholar, and if he doesn’t pass the Annual Examination, it would definitely infuriate his old man.\"","\"Then Liu Hong said something like—’If that weren’t the case, why would I go to all this trouble?’ and then the two of them started laughing.\"","Liu Lang grinned. \"Looks like they’re scheming against someone. But don’t the Annual Examinations happen regularly anyway?\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi raised a hand to quiet him as a flash of insight struck him.","He thought he understood Liu Hong and Ma Shuhan’s plan—to use the Annual Examination to eliminate their rivals.","Simply put, they would win over those who could be won over, and get rid of those who needed to be gotten rid of.","\"I see.\"","’No wonder Ma Shuhan wanted to submit a memorial to change the penalties of the Sixth Rank Technique.’","’Only by doing so could he cooperate with Liu Hong to blackmail the other scholars from the Noble Families.’","’Tang Ye, for example.’","’His father is the Inspector General of the Inspectorate Office.’","’If, after this Annual Examination, Tang Ye only achieves the third rank—or is stripped of his title for placing below the third rank—it would certainly damage the Tang Family’s reputation.’","’Not only would it waste several years of Tang Ye’s life, but it would also implicate Tang Zixing, the Inspector General.’","’Conversely, if Tang Zixing were to align himself with Liu Hong, then Tang Ye’s results in the Annual Examination would surely be outstanding.’","’He might even take the top spot in the subsequent imperial exams.’","’As for someone like him, the son-in-law of the Xiao Family, giving him a fourth-rank result would be enough to send the reputation he had built up from his poetry and calligraphy plummeting.’","’Most importantly, Ma Shuhan would be the public face of it all, making it difficult for anyone to suspect Liu Hong was the one pulling the strings.’","’I’m afraid Ma Shuhan’s purpose in inviting Mr. Yue Ming to be the Vice Examiner is to frame him for the poor performance of Shu State’s scholars in the Annual Examination, isn’t it?’","’I have to say, this is a truly venomous scheme!’","’It’s a plan to kill three birds with one stone!’","Chen Yi watched the rain fall around him, thinking silently, ’It seems this Liu Hong’s ambition is no small thing.’","’No wonder he was able to establish a firm foothold in Shu State on his own, despite only being from the third branch of the Jing State Liu Family.’","’This ability to leverage power for his own gain is beyond that of an ordinary person.’","Seeing his expression, Liu Lang raised an eyebrow. \"Boss, is something wrong?\"","\"No. Go back and keep a close watch on him, especially when that Ma Shuhan comes to visit...\""]},{"number":371,"title":"Chapter 371 - 243: To Control and Not Be Controlled","paragraphs":["Liu Lang was about to leave, but when he saw Chen Yi standing there with an aloof expression, he found he couldn’t quite bring himself to go.","\"Boss, you promised to cross blades with me. When might that be?\"","Chen Yi paused, tilting his bamboo hat up slightly. He smiled and asked, \"Are you that impatient?\"","Liu Lang chuckled. \"I only have two pleasures in life. The first is a brothel, and the second is crossing blades, so...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi waved a hand. \"I understand.\"","\"The eighth day of the ninth month, at the first quarter of the Zi hour. I will wait for you on the Chishui Riverbank.\"","Liu Lang froze for a second, then his face lit up with joy. \"Ten days from now?\"","\"Boss, you’re the one who set the date. You can’t back out of it.\"","Chen Yi gave him a sidelong glance. \"I hope you’ll still be smiling so happily then.\"","He had to fight Liu Lang eventually. It didn’t matter if it was sooner or later.","Besides, with his current Martial Arts Cultivation and Technique Realm, while he couldn’t guarantee victory over Liu Lang, he had a good chance of winning within ten moves.","Of course, that was assuming he used the Spear Dao.","If he were to use a blade, he figured he would need a few more days of practice.","Liu Lang was completely unaffected by the comment. His hand went to the hilt of his blade as he said fervently:","\"The victor lives, the vanquished dies. What greater joy is there than to prove one’s Dao in such a way?\"","Chen Yi shot him an annoyed glare. \"Get lost.\"","’It’s just a sparring match. How did it turn into a fight to the death in his mouth?’","\"You got it.\"","Liu Lang just smiled, unbothered, and darted off in the direction of the Liu Family estate.","Chen Yi watched him disappear into the curtain of rain and shook his head to himself.","’No wonder Liu Lang managed to earn the moniker \"Sword Madman\" in the Northern Desert. The man has more than a few screws loose.’","’But on the bright side, people like him are refreshingly straightforward.’","’At least he’s easier to deal with than Liu Hong, the Ji State Trading Company, or the White Tiger Guard.’","The thought of Liu Hong and the Ji State Trading Company sent Chen Yi’s mind reeling.","Liu Hong, Ma Shuhan, the Annual Examination...","Liu Taofang, the Ji State Trading Company, the rising price of grain...","Lin Huai’an, King Landu, ironware, Heavy Armor, Refined Iron...","And the connection between the White Tiger Guard’s General and King Landu...","All the recent events flashed through Chen Yi’s mind like images in a zoetrope, quickly forming a vast web.","They were like scattered pieces on a chessboard, intricate and complex.","He could faintly see some of the connections, as if a single thread ran through them all.","But the image was hazy, and he couldn’t see how it all connected.","Chen Yi tilted his head back to look at the dim, lightless night sky, letting the rain patter against his face.","’I’m still missing some clues. Just a few more.’","’Looks like I’ll have to muddy the waters a bit.’","As the classics on Military Strategy say: Compel the enemy, but do not be compelled by them.","In other words, you must maneuver your enemies, not be maneuvered by them.","Only by seizing the initiative can you turn their order into chaos, their courage into cowardice, and their strength into weakness.","This is the essence of fishing in troubled waters.","Chen Yi lowered his gaze, pulled his bamboo hat down slightly, and turned toward the Spring Rain Building in Yanhua Lane.","’When it comes to muddying the waters, there’s no one better for the job than a Hidden Guard.’","「A moment later.」","Chen Yi arrived quietly outside the Spring Rain Building, surveying the brightly lit and decorated brothel.","After the Three Towns’ summer grain was burned, Xiao Jinghong had led a raid on this place because Black Tooth and others from the Bright Moon Building had been hiding here.","The ones who needed to be captured were captured, and the ones who needed to be killed were killed.","The Spring Rain Building had now reopened. While the name was the same, its owner had changed.","Chen Yi had no idea who it was.","But based on tonight’s intelligence, the fact that Lou Yuxue could arrange a meeting with the man from Poshisu Country here made it easy to deduce that the Spring Rain Building was still under her control.","Chen Yi glanced around before walking into the Spring Rain Building as if he owned the place.","He paid no mind to how his attire set him apart from the self-proclaimed scholars and refined gentlemen who frequented such establishments.","The madam and pimp just inside the door, however, had no choice but to take notice.","The madam stared at Chen Yi, sizing him up, then shot a look at a nearby pimp.","The pimp hurried over, bowing and smiling. \"Sir, are you here for pleasure or to find someone?\"","Without breaking his stride, Chen Yi took off his bamboo hat and tossed it to the man. \"Both.\"","Perhaps it was because his disguised face was so ridiculously handsome, but both the madam and the pimp seemed to relax.","\"Who are you looking for, sir? I can ask around for you.\"","Chen Yi ignored him and looked up toward the second floor—where the private rooms were.","From behind one of the walls, he could hear the voice of Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue, apparently giving someone orders.","\"...bring them up. Avoid the guests downstairs.\"","After listening for a moment, Chen Yi turned to the fawning pimp and said, \"Black Tooth.\"","The smile on the pimp’s face froze. He subconsciously glanced back at the madam, who was watching them.","The madam quickly recovered, gliding over with a charming smile and subtly nudging the pimp out of the way.","\"So, you’re looking for our Black Girl? What a coincidence. The lass just learned to play the zither. I’ll have her attend to you tonight.\"","She said this loudly enough for others to hear, so as not to disturb the nearby guests.","But then, she lowered her voice. \"Sir, Black Tooth is dead. You’ve come to the wrong place.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"In that case, Miss Lou Yuxue is here, isn’t she?\"","The madam’s expression changed. She stared at him in astonishment. \"You... you...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yi pointed upstairs. \"She’s coming now. So it seems she is in.\"","The next moment, Lou Yuxue, dressed in a stunning red gown, appeared behind the third-floor railing.","However, Lou Yuxue was clearly displeased. Her downward gaze seemed to ask, \"What the hell are you doing here, you bastard?\"","Chen Yi waved a casual greeting, completely unbothered. \"Am I coming up, or are you coming down?\"","\"Get your ass up here.\"","’Such coarse, unpleasant words.’","Fortunately, Chen Yi wasn’t bothered. He gave the madam a smiling wave and headed straight for the third floor.","He could faintly hear people in the main hall below asking who Lou Yuxue was."]},{"number":372,"title":"Chapter 372 - 243: To Subdue, Not to Be Subdued","paragraphs":["Some of the more impatient and wealthy men had already started shouting bids at Madam Bao.","\"Will that lady perform a dance for us tonight? I’ll offer fifty taels of gold.\"","\"I’ll offer a hundred taels!\"","\"My apologies, esteemed guests. That lady is a master who teaches the girls here at the Spring Rain Building to play the zither and sing. She does not entertain patrons...\"","A wave of disappointed sighs followed.","Chen Yi found this amusing. Watching Lou Yuxue from a distance, he teased, \"As expected of Miss Yuxue. A single performance for a hundred taels of gold.\"","Lou Yuxue shot him a fierce glare. \"Follow me inside!\"","Chen Yi smiled and followed her into a quiet room in the back.","Glancing around, he said, \"This place has changed a bit. Heavy Willow Wood, Iron Sinking Wood... you must have spent a lot of silver.\"","Lou Yuxue ignored him.","Chen Yi didn’t seem to mind, continuing to ramble on.","From the room’s decor to the servants wearing black iron masks, he critiqued everything one by one.","\"So the Bright Moon Building is back in Shu State? But why don’t I see any of those Evil Demonic Dao types?\"","Lou Yuxue stopped, unable to take it anymore. She spun around and yanked him into the nearest quiet room.","The moment the door closed, she stared at Chen Yi, her teeth clenched. \"How in the world did you find me?\"","\"Tonight is the very first day this place has reopened as a Bright Moon Building stronghold!\"","A look of realization dawned on Chen Yi’s face. He muttered, ’No wonder no Evil Demons have shown up,’ then said with a smile:","\"What’s so hard about finding you here in Shu State? Have you forgotten about the wonton shop incident?\"","Of course, Lou Yuxue hadn’t forgotten.","But for a member of the White Tiger Guard who prided herself on being an expert in stealth and concealment, being found so easily time and time again was simply unacceptable.","\"Are you... are you going to tell me or not?\"","\"You want to know?\"","Chen Yi walked around her and sat down, looking at her with a leisurely air. \"I’m not telling you.\"","’Without that intelligence tip, there’s no way I would’ve known where Lou Yuxue was.’","’But even if I told her, she probably wouldn’t believe me.’","’So I might as well not say anything.’","\"You!?\"","Lou Yuxue glared at him in frustration, but there was nothing she could do.","She was supposed to be the one holding all the cards, yet in front of Chen Yi, she was always the one who ended up on the losing end.","A moment later, Lou Yuxue took a deep breath. The dim candlelight cast her shapely shadow on the wall, its full, rounded silhouette striking.","She then sat down opposite Chen Yi, her heavily made-up face regaining its composure as she asked calmly:","\"Out with it. Why did you come looking for me this time?\"","\"Is it time to start that thing we agreed on before?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow, surprised she had regained her composure so quickly. After a moment of thought, he said:","\"Yes and no.\"","Before Lou Yuxue could ask, Chen Yi continued to explain, \"I’ve made some headway on that matter, but a few conditions are still not in place.\"","\"I came to find you this time to ask for a favor.\"","\"Speak.\"","\"Can you find a way to get me some grain?\"","\"How much?\"","\"At least one hundred thousand shi. The more, the better.\"","Lou Yuxue’s eyes widened instantly. \"One hundred thousand shi? And you say ’the more, the better’? Do you think I’m the Lord Pavilion Master?\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"You have to spend money to make money.\"","\"If we want to earn some silver coins, we need some bait to lure those people onto the hook.\"","\"Those people? Who exactly are you trying to deal with?\"","The words had barely left her mouth when a flash of insight struck Lou Yuxue. \"Grain? Are you going after the grain stores?\"","\"Don’t tell me it’s those few in the East Market.\"","Chen Yi smiled and retorted, \"And why can’t it be them?\"","\"I’m sure you’ve heard about the East Market Grain Store’s warehouse being burned down a couple of days ago. If even a few barbarian slaves dare to make a move against them, why can’t we?\"","Lou Yuxue’s brow furrowed instantly. \"Do you have any idea who those people are?\"","\"The Ji State Trading Company.\"","\"You... If you already know, then why...\"","Chen Yi spread his hands, a half-smile on his face. \"Because they’re rich, of course.\"","’Judging by Lou Yuxue’s reaction, she must know the inside story on the Ji State Trading Company.’","’Even if not everything, she knows at least a little.’","’Good.’","’Saves me the trouble of explaining.’","With that thought, Chen Yi continued, \"I’ve received word that besides what was burned, they still have no less than a million shi of grain on hand.\"","\"At current market prices, that’s nearly three million in silver coins. Aren’t you tempted?\"","Hearing this number, Lou Yuxue remained unmoved. Instead, she stared at him and said, enunciating each word:","\"I advise you to give up this idea. It’s very dangerous!\"","\"What, is even a White Tiger Guard Silver Banner Officer like you afraid of the Ji State Trading Company?\"","\"Afraid? Of course I’m afraid!\"","\"Do you know what kind of people make up the Ji State Trading Company? Are you aware of who’s standing behind them?\"","Chen Yi shook his head honestly. \"I don’t know, and I don’t care.\"","\"I only know that they have piles and piles of silver, and that none of them are good people.\"","\"Instead of letting that silver sit in their hands, I’d rather take it and do something more meaningful with it.\"","’Those words sounded reasonable, but they were actually full of holes.’","’He was just trying to needle Lou Yuxue, hoping to fish for some information about the Ji State Trading Company.’","Lou Yuxue was about to retort instinctively, but she caught herself when she saw the smile on his face.","\"Are you trying to trick me into talking?\"","\"Ah, you found me out.\"","\"You...\"","Chen Yi waved his hand. \"It’s not entirely a trick. I really do plan to make a move on them.\"","\"Don’t tell me you didn’t know they were the Financiers behind the plot to burn the summer grain from the Three Towns.\"","The look of frustrated anger on Lou Yuxue’s face froze. \"Them?\"","’I really didn’t know about that.’","’Black Tooth had always been the one contacting the Financiers, which made me think it was some Noble Family in Shu State with a grudge against the Xiao Family.’","Now that she knew the Financiers were the Ji State Trading Company, a lot of things instantly clicked into place.","Especially the recent rise in grain prices in Shu State, and the appearance of barbarian slaves and people from Poshisu Country in the East Market.","’Could King Landu already be cooperating with the people from the Ji State Trading Company?’","’If so, this is bad!’","Of course, Chen Yi had no idea what Lou Yuxue was speculating. He just nodded and said, \"The very same.\"","Then, a mischievous look appeared on his face. \"Miss Yuxue, in exchange for this piece of information, aren’t you going to offer some kind of reward?\"","Lou Yuxue snapped out of her thoughts. She studied him pensively for a long moment before finally speaking.","\"It’s not that I can’t tell you about the Ji State Trading Company.\"","\"Although they operate secretly and keep a low profile, quite a few people within the Great Wei Dynasty have heard their name.\"","\"But since there are no leads to investigate, even those who’ve heard things don’t dare to speak of them easily.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi placed his hands on the table and leaned in a little closer. \"Sounds like they have a very deep background.\"","’Obviously, that was a stupid question.’","’A group of people capable of illegally selling the Great Wei Dynasty’s ironware and Refined Iron wouldn’t dare to do so, not even if they had ten times the courage, unless someone powerful was backing them.’","Lou Yuxue grunted in acknowledgment. \"Let me be clear up front: just because I’m telling you this doesn’t mean I agree to deal with them alongside you.\"","Chen Yi nodded and said with a smile, \"I don’t believe you can just stand by and watch all that silver slip away.\"","Lou Yuxue ignored his teasing. After some thought, she said gravely, \"The Ji State Trading Company is indeed based in Ji State, but its internal network isn’t limited to Ji State.\"","\"They can’t possibly be spread across all Nine State and Three Prefectures, can they?\"","\"Not far off.\"","\"With the exception of the Jiangnan, Guangyue, and Capital Prefectures, they have people all across the lands of the Nine State.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi said, \"Really?\"","Lou Yuxue glanced at him. \"Scared now? It’s not too late for you to back out.\"","Chen Yi didn’t answer, the smile fading from his face. \"Continue.\"","Seeing that he wouldn’t give up, Lou Yuxue snorted. \"Do you know why I’m here in the Bright Moon Building?\"","\"In fact, the backer behind the Bright Moon Building is the Ji State Trading Company!\"","This time, Chen Yi was genuinely surprised.","He never would have imagined that the Bright Moon Building, so famous in the Jianghu, was actually propped up by the Ji State Trading Company.","’No wonder.’","’No wonder Black Tooth is so obsessed with money. His attitude of valuing wealth over life is nothing like that of Jianghu People.’","’Turns out his style was never that of a Jianghu person, but that of a merchant.’","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi suddenly started laughing. \"Interesting. I really underestimated them.\"","He had only considered that the Ji State Trading Company was backed by the Imperial Court and Noble Families; he’d completely forgotten about the \"Jianghu\" angle.","With that, he looked directly at Lou Yuxue and asked, \"So, is your mission to investigate the Bright Moon Building or the Ji State Trading Company?\"","Lou Yuxue glared at him. \"Telling you this much is already against the White Tiger Guard’s rules, and now you want to ask about my mission?\"","\"Fine, fine. If you won’t say, you won’t say. Let’s get back to the Ji State Trading Company.\"","\"There’s no more.\"","Chen Yi froze. \"That’s it? What about who their people are, their layout and schemes in Shu State, or who their backers are?\"","Lou Yuxue said in exasperation, \"If I knew all that, why would I need to hide in the Bright Moon Building...\"","She didn’t finish her sentence, suddenly realizing her slip.","But Chen Yi had already caught on, and he said with a smile, \"Oh, so *that’s* your mission.\"","\"You bastard!\""]},{"number":373,"title":"Chapter 373 - 244: Peacock, White Elephant, Golden Lion","paragraphs":["Lou Yuxue knew she couldn’t do anything about \"Liu Wu.\"","Not unless she could uncover his true identity.","In fact, it wasn’t for lack of trying.","Over the past few days, she had exhausted nearly every resource to investigate all the Noble Families in Shu State, big and small.","Some were close to the Xiao Family, while others were on bad terms with them.","But no matter how she probed, she couldn’t find the slightest trace of \"Liu Wu.\"","It was as if the man had appeared in Shu State out of thin air, coming and going without a trace.","That would have been one thing.","After all, Lou Yuxue could use her own methods to play the long game with \"Liu Wu.\" Sooner or later, she would uncover his background.","But what she couldn’t wrap her head around was why \"Liu Wu\" knew so much about the White Tiger Guard’s secrets.","He not only knew the identities of several members—Gray Wolf, Hawk, and others—but he even knew their individual missions.","For her, a Silver Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard, this was nothing short of a profound humiliation.","Fortunately, Chen Yi didn’t know what Lou Yuxue was thinking. Otherwise, he would have roared with laughter and said, \"But you’re the one who told me.\"","Her expression at that moment would surely have been a sight to behold.","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi looked at Lou Yuxue, who was still glaring at him, and said with a smile, \"Relax, relax. I’m not an enemy of the White Tiger Guard, and I have no intention of obstructing or sabotaging your mission.\"","\"On the contrary, I can even help you.\"","Lou Yuxue snorted. \"On the condition that I help you first, is that it?\"","Chen Yi nodded, saying without the slightest hint of a blush, \"A fair trade. You help me, I’ll help you. Neither of us will owe the other a thing.\"","\"But you owe me one hundred fifty thousand taels of silver.\"","Lou Yuxue clearly wasn’t going to fall for the bastard’s words again.","She had been too careless before, and that was how she’d fallen into his trap.","As a result, of the two hundred thousand taels of silver the White Tiger Guard had acquired, only fifty thousand remained.","To this day, she still didn’t know how she would face Hawk. Her only option was to earn as much silver as possible to make up for it.","Fortunately, with Bright Moon Building back in business, she no longer had to rely on A Wonton Shop to earn that pittance.","Chen Yi inwardly pursed his lips, knowing that if he didn’t show some genuine sincerity, it would be difficult to get Lou Yuxue to act.","Especially when the opponent was a behemoth of unknown strength like the Ji State Trading Company.","After a moment’s thought, he proposed, \"What if I pay for your help? Surely that’s acceptable?\"","Lou Yuxue stared at him, slightly stunned, and frowned. \"You’re still not going to give up on this?\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"The arrow is already nocked. I have to let it fly.\"","After weighing his options, he had decided to target the Ji State Trading Company first.","More precisely, he would target the grain stores in the East Market, especially Lin’s Trading Company, where Lin Huai’an was based.","For one, the people running the grain stores had already started jacking up prices, affecting hundreds of thousands of citizens in Shu State.","He just needed to add a little fuel to make the flames burn hotter and higher.","For another, Lin’s Grain Store was backed by the Ji State Trading Company, giving it plenty of power.","Once turmoil struck the grain stores and drew the attention of the Ji State Trading Company, then both Liu Hong and King Landu of Poshisu Country might reveal their hands.","Only then could Chen Yi fish in troubled waters.","Lou Yuxue, of course, was unaware of his grand scheme. But even just considering the plot against the grain stores, she remained hesitant.","It wasn’t that she didn’t dare.","Rather, she feared that if she acted in her capacity as the proprietor of Bright Moon Building, it might interfere with her next mission.","After a moment’s thought, she made an exorbitant demand. \"One hundred thousand shi of grain for three hundred thousand taels of silver.\"","Chen Yi’s smile faded. In a displeased tone, he said, \"Miss Yuxue, are you taking me for a fool?\"","\"If I were going to pay three taels of silver per shi of grain, why would I even need to work with you?\"","Lou Yuxue hadn’t expected him to agree. It was time to show her hand.","\"Two hundred thousand taels.\"","\"No deal. The most I’ll pay is one tael of silver per shi, and I need three hundred thousand shi.\"","\"Three hundred thousand shi? What do you take the White Tiger Guard for? The Great Wei Grain Store?\"","Chen Yi feigned surprise. \"Aren’t you?\"","He refused to believe that a group as secretive and deeply embedded as the White Tiger Guard didn’t have control over some businesses.","Never mind anyone else; just the Spring Rain Building under Lady Tiger’s control had to be generating a handsome monthly income.","And that wasn’t even mentioning Simurgh Phoenix.","After all, Cui Qingwu hailed from the Qinghe Cui Family—one of the most prominent clans in the Great Wei Dynasty. Their family fortune was undoubtedly immense.","Lou Yuxue stared at him for a long moment before suddenly asking, \"Tell me the truth. What are you really trying to do?\"","\"Is this really just about getting silver from those grain stores in the East Market?\"","\"What else would it be?\"","\"Hmph. I suspect you’re using this as an opportunity to procure grain for the Xiao Family.\"","Chen Yi was struck speechless for a moment, then chuckled. He’d almost forgotten about that.","The Xiao Family was also in desperate need of grain right now, so it was only natural for Lou Yuxue to think that.","\"You don’t need to worry about my specific intentions for the grain. You just need to decide whether or not you’ll agree to this deal.\"","Chen Yi then took ten crisp, new gold notes from his robes, slapped them on the table, and looked at Lou Yuxue with a smile.","\"If you agree, I can give you these right now—ten thousand taels in gold—as a deposit.\"","Lou Yuxue’s gaze dropped, sweeping over the stack of gold notes. She was a little surprised.","She hadn’t expected \"Liu Wu\" to be so forthcoming this time, and a sliver of doubt crept into her mind.","’I clearly told him about the Ji State Trading Company’s situation, and that they’re the ones backing Bright Moon Building. Why isn’t he afraid?’","’Wealth has always tempted men, it’s true, but you rarely see someone as reckless as ’Liu Wu’—all for money, with no regard for his life. Isn’t he afraid of the Ji State Trading Company finding out and bringing their thunderous wrath down on him?’","After a moment of contemplation, Lou Yuxue came to a decision. ’This is too big. I need to pull someone else into this mess with me.’","\"I can’t give you an answer right now. Meet me here again tomorrow night, at this same time.\"","\"You should have just said so.\"","Chen Yi smoothly swept the gold notes back up, muttering something about the White Tiger Guard’s Silver Banner Officer being so indecisive.","Lou Yuxue heard him perfectly clearly, and her eyelid twitched in irritation.","Just as she was about to curse him out, two knocks sounded at the door."]},{"number":374,"title":"Chapter 374 - 244: Peacock, White Elephant, Golden Lion","paragraphs":["Her expression immediately turned serious. She stood up and said, \"I have something to attend to. I’ll be leaving now.\"","Chen Yi took note of the time. He knew she was going to meet the visitor from Poshisu Country, so he asked with a smile,","\"What’s the rush?\"","\"If it’s convenient, perhaps you’ll let me tag along and have a look?\"","\"Get lost!\"","Seeing Lou Yuxue hurry out of the private room, Chen Yi let out a soft chuckle, put on his bamboo hat, and followed.","As he walked, he took out a black cloth and masked his face with it.","Lou Yuxue noticed his movements and stopped to look back at him, her expression now one of clear annoyance.","\"This is business for the Bright Moon Building. What are you doing following me?\"","Chen Yi’s eyes held a hint of a smile as he said, \"I am Liu Lang of the Bright Moon Building. Have you forgotten, Miss Yuxue?\"","Lou Yuxue froze for a second, then her brows shot up. \"If you dare follow me one more step, our deal is canceled!\"","Chen Yi, unafraid of her threat, simply pointed to the end of the dim corridor. \"They’re here.\"","\"Hm?\"","She turned to look but saw no one. Just as she was about to reprimand him again, she heard his voice in her ear.","\"Three.\"","\"Two.\"","\"One.\"","Before the word had left his lips, two tall figures completely shrouded in black robes appeared at the end of the corridor.","Lou Yuxue froze upon seeing them. She shot him a vicious glare out of the corner of her eye, well aware that now was not the time to drive this bastard away.","She then hissed through her teeth, \"Not a word!\"","If she weren’t keenly aware that she and everyone else in the Spring Rain Building were no match for \"Liu Wu,\" she would have made this bastard suffer the full force of the White Tiger Guard’s signature skills.","As these thoughts crossed Lou Yuxue’s mind, a bewitching and alluring smile had already surfaced on her face.","\"Welcome, honored guests. Forgive me for not greeting you sooner.\"","As she spoke, she took the opportunity to size up the two robed figures.","Thanks to \"Liu Wu’s\" earlier warning, she already knew the two visitors from Poshisu Country possessed extraordinary strength.","They were stronger than her, at the very least.","Yet, the last time she had contacted them, the liaison provided by the General was only in the Lower Three Grades Realm.","It was easy to deduce, then, that these two robed men were far more formidable than her previous contact from Poshisu Country.","Chen Yi, standing beside her, wasn’t thinking so deeply. He gave the two a curious glance before falling silent behind Lou Yuxue.","Using his Qi Observation Skill, he had already gauged their Martial Arts Cultivation.","Fifth Grade, Fourth Grade.","Both were in the Middle Three Grades.","Just then, the two robed men arrived before them. The leader’s emerald-green eyes reflected the figures of Lou Yuxue and Chen Yi as he spoke in a stiff, halting voice,","\"Miss Yuxue, please find a quiet... place... for a detailed discussion.\"","The black-robed man at his side kept his head lowered and said nothing.","Lou Yuxue laughed charmingly, turning to the side with an inviting gesture and leading them into a private room.","Chen Yi followed close behind, but he was the first to take a seat, leaning back in his chair with the relaxed air of someone just there to observe.","’These two are interesting.’","’The one who spoke has slightly lower Cultivation, while the silent one’s is actually higher.’","’Are they trying to hide their true strength?’","Lou Yuxue had no time to reprimand Chen Yi for his lack of decorum. She simply gestured for the two robed men to be seated.","But just as she was about to exchange a few pleasantries, she saw the robed man who had spoken earlier look at Chen Yi and ask,","\"Miss Yuxue, could this be... Elder Black Tooth?\"","Lou Yuxue’s smile never wavered as she shook her head. \"He is an Earth-level Assassin from my Bright Moon Building, Liu... Liu Lang.\"","Playing his part, Chen Yi lifted his bamboo hat slightly. \"I am Liu Lang,\" he said with a smile. \"I greet our two honored guests.\"","The robed man’s eyes flickered slightly. \"’Sword Madman’?\" he asked.","Chen Yi glanced at him, slightly surprised. \"The very same.\"","He clearly hadn’t expected the \"Sword Madman’s\" fame to have reached Poshisu Country.","’This man must have spent some time in Shu State to have heard the name Liu Lang.’","The robed man gave a slight nod and pointed to himself. \"Ge Muxiao.\"","Then he pointed to the man beside him. \"Lv Jiunan.\"","Lou Yuxue smiled and nodded, then discreetly stepped on Chen Yi’s foot, signaling him to keep quiet.","\"May I ask, Ge Muxiao, which General you are under the Peacock Banner?\"","’Peacock Banner?’","’He must be referring to King Landu’s band of horse bandits.’","As Chen Yi thought this, he lowered his head, becoming as still as a wooden statue.","Then he heard the robed man, Ge Muxiao, speak in halting official Wei Dynasty dialect,","\"I am merely a Golden Lion Warrior under His Majesty, not a General.\"","Lou Yuxue’s gaze shifted to Lv Jiunan. \"And you?\"","Ge Muxiao was about to answer when the previously silent man, Lv Jiunan, spoke in a deep, hoarse voice, \"Peacock Warrior.\"","Chen Yi’s eyes narrowed, his mind stirring.","’It’s him—the Black Magic Master from Poshisu Country who made my predecessor flee his own wedding!’","’Lv Jiunan...’","’I can’t believe he’s one of King Landu’s men.’","What Chen Yi didn’t understand was why one of King Landu’s men would make a move against him.","’Was it because of the Xiao Family?’","’But that doesn’t add up.’","’The horse bandits of Poshisu Country aren’t like the Noble Families of Shu State. There’s no reason they should fear Xiao Jinghong remaining with the Xiao Family.’","’Unless... he was acting on someone else’s orders...’","Lou Yuxue, not noticing anything was amiss with him, showed a flicker of surprise as she said,","\"I’ve heard that under King Landu’s Peacock Banner, there are three orders of great warriors: the Peacock, the Golden Lion, and the White Elephant.\"","\"Among them, the Peacock Warriors, being the rarest, are the most revered. I never expected you to be one of them.\"","Ge Muxiao looked at Lv Jiunan, seemingly surprised that he had spoken.","After a moment’s hesitation, he nodded slightly. \"After you contacted our man last time, Miss Yuxue, Brother Jiunan took great interest. He has come today specifically to meet with you.\"","\"I am grateful.\"","\"So, can you be frank with us, Miss Yuxue? What exactly is this business you wish to discuss?\"","Just as Lou Yuxue was about to answer, her eyes swept over to Chen Yi at the side. She secretly gritted her teeth, then said with a smile,","\"A certain honored client has commissioned the Bright Moon Building to arrange a meeting with your King Landu.\""]},{"number":375,"title":"Chapter 375 - 244: Peacock, White Elephant, Golden Lion","paragraphs":["Hearing this, Chen Yi kept his head lowered, his expression unchanged as if he hadn’t heard a thing. Inside, however, a strange feeling began to stir.","’Isn’t that honored guest the White Tiger Guard’s Golden Banner Officer, General?’","’Strange.’","’Why does he want to meet King Landu?’","\"You wish to see His Majesty?\"","Ge Muxiao subconsciously glanced at Lv Jiunan beside him. Seeing that Lv Jiunan merely stared sharply at Lou Yuxue with no intention of speaking, Ge Muxiao shook his head and said,","\"Miss Yuxue, you should be well aware that His Majesty remains exclusively in the Poshisu Country. It is impossible for him to set foot within the borders of the Great Wei Dynasty.\"","Lou Yuxue was prepared for this. She smiled and replied, \"The honored guest has already made himself clear on that point.\"","\"If King Landu is agreeable, our guest is willing to personally travel to the Ancient Tea-Horse Road to meet him.\"","Hearing this, and before Ge Muxiao could speak, Lv Jiunan asked in his unchanging, flat tone,","\"Miss Yuxue, what is this person’s identity?\"","\"Forgive me, sir. I can only reveal his identity if His Majesty agrees to the meeting.\"","Lv Jiunan’s gaze darkened as he stared at her. \"If you won’t tell us, there will be no meeting.\"","Lou Yuxue’s smile froze. She clearly hadn’t expected him to be so aggressive, and the pressure mounted.","\"You...\"","At that moment, Chen Yi lifted his head slightly.","That single motion was enough to draw the gazes of both Ge Muxiao and Lv Jiunan. Even Lou Yuxue paused to look at him.","Chen Yi took in each of their expressions before his gaze settled on Lv Jiunan, a hint of amusement in his eyes.","\"Even back in the Northern Desert, I had heard of King Landu’s fame.\"","\"I’ve heard he’s a personal disciple of the Poshisu Country’s National Preceptor, and a Grandmaster Realm expert to boot.\"","He paused. Seeing Ge Muxiao and Lv Jiunan show a hint of pride, his tone shifted.","\"But from what I’m hearing today, it seems King Landu’s courage doesn’t quite live up to his reputation.\"","Lou Yuxue was instantly furious. She knew this man was incapable of saying anything decent, but she never thought he’d be this venomous.","’Especially at a time like this! Those two...’","Sure enough, before Lou Yuxue could think of a way to salvage the situation, two powerful auras instantly enveloped the private room.","A chilling presence, like a phantom’s shriek, coiled around her, pressing down with immense weight.","But only for an instant.","An equally sharp and domineering aura erupted from Chen Yi, as violent as a striking blade, and instantly shredded the chilling presence around them.","He faced them two-on-one, not only refusing to shy away from their combined might but meeting it with the force of a dragon.","Ge Muxiao flew into a rage. \"You dare?!\"","With that, he slammed his hand on the table and shot to his feet, thrusting out a palm.","But before his arm could fully extend, Lv Jiunan at his side raised a hand to stop him.","Ge Muxiao faltered. \"Brother?\"","Lv Jiunan patted his hand, signaling for him to sit down, his gaze never leaving Chen Yi.","\"Worthy of the name ’Sword Madman.’ Judging by the power of this Sword Intent alone, you have already grasped thirty percent of the true essence of your master, Senior Sword Ghost.\"","Chen Yi remained seated, unmoving, simply watching him with a faint, unreadable smile.","\"Brother Lü... you’re a Black Magic Master?\"","Lv Jiunan didn’t answer. After scrutinizing Chen Yi for a moment, he turned to Lou Yuxue and asked,","\"Does what the ’Sword Madman’ said also represent the position of the Bright Moon Building?\"","Lou Yuxue gave a bitter, internal smile. She was in an impossible position.","But since things had already come to this, she could only nod and say, \"My apologies. He’s from the Northern Desert and has a bit of a temper.\"","Before anyone else could speak, she continued, \"However, those are the rules of the Bright Moon Building. Until we receive a reply from King Landu, I’m afraid I cannot reveal the identity of our honored guest.\"","Lv Jiunan gave a slight nod and rose to his feet. \"We will consult with His Majesty and give you our reply.\"","With that, he turned to Chen Yi and bowed slightly. \"Your Excellency, ’Sword Madman,’ your skill is impressive. I look forward to our next meeting.\"","Ge Muxiao, who was standing nearby, snorted at the sight and stalked out of the private room first.","Lv Jiunan followed right behind him.","Once the two had left and their footsteps faded, Lou Yuxue finally took a deep breath and said through clenched teeth,","\"Why did you do that? Are you trying to ruin this for me on purpose?\"","\"You knew they were King Landu’s men! This was a task from the Lord General!\"","Chen Yi glanced at her and said calmly, \"They were never going to relay your request to King Landu right now anyway.\"","\"You... How can you say that?! Why not?!\"","\"If I’m not mistaken, Lv Jiunan is the Black Magic Master who rescued those barbarian slaves from the East Market.\"","Lou Yuxue froze, the anger on her face stiffening. \"He’s the one who rescued them?\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"Since they’re still in Shu State, those barbarian slaves must be here too.\"","\"Under these circumstances, do you really think they care about your request?\"","\"But... but then why did they even come to see me? Wouldn’t it have been simpler to just refuse from the start?\"","\"I’m not sure. Perhaps... perhaps these Poshisu horse bandits need something from the Bright Moon Building...\"","At this, Chen Yi stood up and started to walk out.","Lou Yuxue, after a moment’s shock, snapped back to reality and blocked his path. Staring at him, she demanded, \"Be clear. What could they possibly want from us?\"","\"You... you know something else, don’t you?\"","Chen Yi turned his head and met her gaze directly, not shying away in the slightest.","Seeing her determined expression, the kind that wouldn’t let go until she had an answer, he thought for a moment before pulling a piece of paper from his sleeve and handing it to her.","\"Read this. You’ll understand.\"","With that, Chen Yi didn’t hesitate further. He walked around Lou Yuxue and left.","As he walked, he listened intently, heading in the direction Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao had taken, in pursuit.","...","「Meanwhile.」","After leaving the Spring Rain Building, Lv Jiunan headed south, his expression dark.","Ge Muxiao followed behind him, his own expression wavering between anger and uncertainty.","After they had walked for some distance, he could no longer hold back. \"Brother, why didn’t you let me kill him?\"","Lv Jiunan glanced at him, his tone grim. \"We couldn’t have killed him back there.\"","\"You... you mean his blade?\"","\"Yes. Your Martial Arts Cultivation and Technique are far inferior to his, and I am not skilled in close-quarters combat.\"","\"If we had fought there and alerted the others within Shu State City, neither of us would have escaped.\"","A flicker of resentment crossed Ge Muxiao’s eyes. \"So we just let him insult His Majesty?\"","Lv Jiunan stopped in his tracks. \"The Wei Dynasty has a saying: ’As long as the green mountains remain, there will be no shortage of firewood.’ It won’t be too late to strike after we’ve escorted the Left King’s son out of Shu State.\"","Ge Muxiao could only nod. \"What do we do now, then?\"","\"Are you still planning to use the Bright Moon Building’s power to draw away those barbarians?\"","\"There’s no rush.\"","\"Since Lou Yuxue is so eager for a meeting with His Majesty, she’ll naturally come looking for us again...\""]},{"number":376,"title":"Chapter 376 - 245: Everything Becomes Clear","paragraphs":["The night rain drifted down.","The roads were nearly empty.","Chen Yi silently trailed five li behind Ge Muxiao and Lv Jiunan. He infused his ears with True Essence, listening to their conversation from afar.","The Left King’s son?","The Left King...","Chen Yi knew of only one person who held the title of \"Left King\"—Left King Mu Hage of the Barbarian Race.","He was the one who had led the Barbarian army north to attack Mengshui Pass five years ago, causing the deaths of Xiao Fengchun, Fu Wanqing, and many others from the Xiao family.","’The Left King’s son is in Shu State?’","An image of the young barbarian he had seen on his last trip to the East Market immediately surfaced in Chen Yi’s mind.","He recalled that the young barbarian had been subtly protected by the other barbarian slaves, which did suggest he was a barbarian of noble status.","’But how could the son of Left King Mu Hage be abducted by people from Poshisu Country, brought to Shu State, and sold as a barbarian slave?’","’How strange.’","What Chen Yi found even stranger was—","Lv Jiunan and his companion were also horse bandits from Poshisu Country. If they wanted to rescue the Left King’s son, why not directly approach the people from Poshisu Country who were selling the barbarian slaves in the East Market?","Why would they instead choose to hire an Evil Demon from the Illusory Sound Sect in the Western State to rescue the barbarian slaves?","Unless... the Poshisu Country horse bandits who had abducted the Left King’s son were not part of the same group as Lv Jiunan.","As he thought, Chen Yi muttered to himself, ’Going through all this trouble seems unnecessarily complicated.’","After a moment of thought, he still had no leads, so he decided to stop overthinking it.","As long as he kept a close watch on Lv Jiunan and the others, he would eventually uncover the truth.","Just then, a golden light flashed before his eyes—","[Witnessed Hidden Guard Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue discussing important matters with horse bandits from Poshisu Country. Reward: Zither Score \"Autumn Rain,\" Opportunity +63.]","[Evaluation: You arrived, you heard, you saw. You acted to intimidate Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao of Poshisu Country without arousing the Lady Tiger’s suspicion. Your performance was adequate.]","Chen Yi glanced at the notification and pursed his lips. He then used the cover of night to continue tailing Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao from a distance.","This Opportunity certainly made tonight’s risk worthwhile.","The surroundings were silent save for the clamor of the falling rain.","The bamboo hat on Chen Yi’s head was particularly noisy, the PATTER PATTER of the rain endless.","But with his full concentration, the sounds around him flowed into his ears, even clearer than the raindrops.","This was especially true for Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao’s conversation and footsteps.","\"Tomorrow night, go to the Lin Family and investigate Bright Moon Building. See if you can find out who wants to see the king.\"","\"Yes, General.\"","\"Hmm?\"","\"Gen... Brother, I forgot...\"","\"We’re in Shu State now. You need to be careful with every word and action.\"","’General?’","Chen Yi frowned. ’It seems there’s more to this Lv Jiunan than meets the eye.’","He just didn’t know if this \"General\" was an official rank from Poshisu Country, or a self-appointed title among King Landu’s horse bandits.","About an hour passed.","Chen Yi followed Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao as they circled from South City to the West Market, and then from the West Market to North City.","At one point, they even scaled the city wall to venture outside.","After much weaving and winding, Chen Yi finally noticed that Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao had stopped.","Chen Yi zipped to the top of a nearby courtyard wall and looked out from a distance.","He saw Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao land on a Painted Boat on Quchi.","It was brightly lit.","Two other young men dressed in brocade came out and bowed. \"Brother Lü, Brother Ge Mu.\"","Lv Jiunan nodded slightly. \"Let’s talk inside.\"","\"Please...\"","Seeing them enter the Painted Boat, Chen Yi executed the Meteor Butterfly Step, silently closing the distance by two li and landing atop a three-story wooden building not far from Quchi.","He focused his gaze.","A flag hung from the Painted Boat—it was emblazoned with the character \"Liu.\"","’Liu? As in Liu Hong?’","’Or Liu Si? Or maybe one of the other Liu Families in Shu State?’","’And those two young men...’","Chen Yi thought for a moment, but they didn’t seem familiar, so he put it out of his mind.","But at that moment, no sound came from the Painted Boat, which told him it must have a soundproofed room.","His brow furrowed, and he risked moving another two li closer.","It wasn’t until he reached the edge of Quchi that he could faintly hear some sounds coming from inside the Painted Boat.","The sounds weren’t clear, but they were enough for him to make out the gist of the conversation.","A strange voice said, \"...after burning the Ji State Trading Company’s grain storehouse, did those barbarian slaves notice anything?\"","Lv Jiunan replied in a low voice, \"I don’t think so.\"","\"This time, we came to rescue them at Lord Liu’s request, which already broke the rules of the Pirate Alliance. It’s impossible to send them back to barbarian territory via the detour on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"This matter requires you to step in...\"","The young voice chuckled. \"Brother Lü, there’s an old saying in the Wei Dynasty: ’one task, one master.’ Since you’ve started the job, why not see it all the way through?\"","Lv Jiunan didn’t reply.","But Ge Muxiao spoke up coldly. \"My king has already made it clear: the Pirate Alliance must not be broken.\"","\"If those human traffickers find out we were behind this, the newly stabilized Pirate Alliance will surely fall apart.\"","\"With what could your father, Liu Hong, compensate the king for such a loss?\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. ’Liu Hong’s son?’","As he recalled, Liu Hong had only two sons.","The elder was Liu Taoyao, and the younger was Liu Taofang.","The former was a scholar who, though he passed the provincial exam, did not place in the top three of the final imperial examination. He had since become a government official.","He was a minor official, a Senior Seventh Grade tax collector at the Shu State Governor’s Office.","The latter was a good-for-nothing, idle scholar who was currently still studying at Guiyun Academy.","Given the situation, the man on the Painted Boat was likely Liu Taoyao.","’So, Lv Jiunan rescuing those barbarian slaves was at Liu Hong’s request?’","Chen Yi frowned slightly, replaying the events of that night in his mind.","First, after the barbarian slaves set fire to the East Market Grain Storehouse, they were rescued by Lv Jiunan."]},{"number":377,"title":"Chapter 377 - 245: Everything Becomes Clear","paragraphs":["’But because of the so-called Pirate Alliance in Poshisu Country, Lv Jiunan hadn’t taken them out of Shu State, which was why he planned to ask the Bright Moon Building for help.’","’Of course, Liu Hong and his people might have been the ones who requested this.’","’Second, Lin Huai’an and Liu Taofang had teamed up to manipulate grain prices in Shu State. When Liu Hong found out, he then conspired against Lin Huai’an.’","’That’s not right.’","’The sequence of events is wrong.’","Chen Yi shook his head to himself. ’The timing is wrong.’","’Liu Hong must have found out what Liu Taofang was doing ahead of time, which is why he had those barbarian slaves burn the granary before they escaped.’","’That would make sense.’","At this thought, a cold, sharp glint flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes as he looked at the Painted Boat.","’He hadn’t expected Liu Hong to be audacious enough to collude with the Barbarian Race.’","’He had originally thought that someone as calculating and deeply scheming as Liu Hong would be a \"Powerful Minister\" solely focused on the pursuit of power.’","’But now it seemed he was also a treacherous official who betrayed his own country and would stop at nothing to achieve his goals.’","Just then, Liu Taoyao’s smiling voice came from within the Painted Boat. \"...In any case, this affair is beneficial to you, Brother Lü.\"","\"My father promised your King that once this is accomplished, he will gift you and your people the horses and carriages of several trading companies that often travel the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.\"","\"This business alone will be enough for you to make a fortune.\"","Lv Jiunan’s tone was as cold as ever. \"My Peacock Banner is fond of wealth, it’s true, but we don’t take just any money.\"","\"If your father hadn’t written to the King, and if this matter didn’t involve the Barbarian Left King Mu Hage, you couldn’t have offered enough silver to make our leader break the rules of the Pirate Alliance.\"","\"Of course.\"","\"That is why my father ordered me to cooperate fully with you and Brother Ge Mu, and to let you take the lead in all things.\"","Liu Taoyao then asked, \"I wonder, is the Spring Rain Building willing to take this job?\"","Before Lv Jiunan could speak, Ge Muxiao snorted, \"Someone’s interfering.\"","\"Oh? Who would be so bold as to ruin things for you two?\"","\"’Sword Madman’ Liu Lang. Some worthless punk from the Jianghu!\"","\"Him?\"","Liu Taoyao sounded slightly puzzled. \"If I recall correctly, isn’t the ’Sword Madman’ about as powerful as you two?\"","\"His skill with the blade has reached Great Success. My big brother and I can’t take him down quickly.\"","\"Hmph. If that weren’t the case, he’d already be a dead man!\"","\"I have no doubt about your strength, of course, but the top priority right now is to get Asutai and his men back to barbarian territory.\"","\"You two must not act rashly.\"","\"As for Liu Lang...\"","Liu Taoyao paused for a moment before continuing with a smile, \"With your strength, Brother Lü, you were able to control that runaway groom right under the Xiao Family’s noses. How could a worthless Jianghu Swordman be any different?\"","Lv Jiunan remained silent.","But a deeper chill had already settled in Chen Yi’s heart.","’So it was the Liu Family!’","’A moment ago, he wasn’t certain if the Liu Family was involved when Lv Jiunan used Black Magic to make his predecessor flee the wedding.’","’Now, he was certain—the Liu Family was behind it!’","’No wonder.’","’With Liu Hong’s ambition, he must not want to see Xiao Jinghong remain secure within the Xiao Family.’","’If he could get rid of her live-in husband, Liu Hong could then find other ways to make the Xiao Family cast Xiao Jinghong out, further weakening their power.’","Seeing that Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao had no intention of speaking, Liu Taoyao continued with a laugh:","\"It’s a pity that the Xiao Family’s son-in-law was lucky enough to escape with his life. Otherwise, my father would have sent a generous gift.\"","\"Speaking of which, I have a few questions. I wonder if you could enlighten me, Brother Lü?\"","\"Speak.\"","\"That day, you told me you had succeeded. Why didn’t the Xiao Family’s son-in-law die? Is there someone in the Xiao Family who can bring the dead back to life?\"","There was a moment of silence.","Lv Jiunan finally replied coolly, \"It must have been Xiao Jinghong.\"","\"Oh? Don’t tell me she’s skilled in the Medical Dao in addition to Martial Arts?\"","\"Xiao Jinghong arrived too quickly that day. I hadn’t yet made that piece of trash kill himself before I had to sever the connection. She must have used some Secret Technique to revive him afterward.\"","\"Or perhaps...\"","\"Agrippa!\"","Chen Yi was about to listen further when he heard Lv Jiunan utter something in the Poshisu language.","It was brief and its meaning was unclear.","Immediately after, the sound of their conversation vanished.","Faintly, he heard two muffled whooshes.","Chen Yi frowned slightly. Keeping himself hidden, he looked over from a distance.","He saw that Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao had left the Painted Boat and were hovering in mid-air, scanning their surroundings as if searching for something.","’Hm? Did they discover me?’","Before he could ponder it further, Chen Yi heard a laugh ring out by his ear.","The laugh was as high-pitched and innocent as a child’s.","’Huh?’","Chen Yi turned his head and saw a foot-tall Wooden Man rushing toward him from the grass not far behind.","Finger-thick bronze chains hung from the Wooden Man’s body, making a rattling sound as it ran. RATTLE, RATTLE.","Even more unnerving, its eyes were blood-red. Paired with that shrill, childish laughter, it was a bizarre and horrifying sight on this dim, rainy night.","Just then, Lv Jiunan’s voice came from the distance: \"Die!\"","Chen Yi’s eyes narrowed, his entire aura changing in an instant.","Sharp Metal Qi surged toward the heavens, erupting in a dazzlingly brilliant golden light.","In the blink of an eye, a flash of spear light shot through the Wooden Man, splitting it in two.","With a HISS, the shrill, ear-piercing laughter and the rattling of chains vanished.","All that remained was the din of the rain and the slowly fading glow of Spear Intent.","This time, Chen Yi did not use his Saber Dao. Instead, he directly used the Spear Intent of the Perfection Realm to break Lv Jiunan’s Black Magic.","At the same time, he removed the black cloth from his face and used his Pile Skill to bulk up his frame, making himself look two sizes larger to prevent Lv Jiunan and the others from realizing he was \"Liu Lang.\"","\"Perfect Spear Dao?!\"","\"Who are you?!\"","When Lv Jiunan saw the brilliant light pierce the dark clouds and rain in the night sky, his expression changed dramatically.","Beside him, Ge Muxiao looked as if he were facing a powerful foe, and had already drawn the long blade from his waist.","Hearing this, Chen Yi raised a hand to pull his bamboo hat back, letting it hang behind him. He stepped slowly to the edge of Quchi and looked toward the Painted Boat, asking impatiently:","\"I’m the one who should be asking who the hell you are.\"","\"I was just stopping here to rest. Why’d you attack me for no reason?\"","A fierce light flashed in Lv Jiunan’s narrow eyes. \"Resting?\"","\"Then why were you just standing there, not moving?\"","\"Damn it! It’s the middle of the night. Was I bothering you by trying to get some sleep here?\"","Chen Yi made no mention of having heard the conversation inside the Painted Boat, continuing to curse angrily:","\"What? You Black Magic Masters from Poshisu Country really think Shu State is your personal desert? You think you own the place?\"","\"Instead of keeping your tails between your legs like the dogs you are, you turn around and try to bully me?\"","\"You!?\"","Just then, Liu Taoyao’s voice came from inside the Painted Boat: \"Brother Lü, please stay your hand.\"","\"In my opinion, this gentleman is no villain.\"","After a pause, he continued, \"Besides, this is Shu State territory. If you two make a scene here, you will inevitably attract the attention of others.\"","He didn’t need to say it.","Lv Jiunan had already decided to stand down after seeing Chen Yi’s Perfect Spear Dao.","The reason was just as Liu Taoyao had said—making a move here would only draw unwanted attention.","In fact, if it weren’t so late at night, with the sounds of revelry from the other Painted Boats on Quchi masking the noise, their earlier commotion would have already alerted many people.","Even so, Lv Jiunan could already hear footsteps approaching in the distance, likely belonging to the Imprisonment Officer and other government officials on night patrol.","At this thought, Lv Jiunan signaled for Ge Muxiao to return to the Painted Boat while saying coldly to Chen Yi:","\"My apologies. I misunderstood the situation.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. His gaze swept over the Painted Boat, and seeing that Liu Taoyao had not shown himself, he continued to curse, refusing to let the matter go.","\"A simple ’misunderstanding’ and that’s it?\"","\"If I hadn’t been strong enough just now, I would’ve fallen victim to your Black Magic!\"","\"You...\"","Before Lv Jiunan or Ge Muxiao could speak, Liu Taoyao interrupted, \"What would it take for you, good sir, to forgive these two brothers of mine?\"","\"Brothers? You’re from Poshisu Country too?\"","\"No...\"","\"You’re not from Poshisu Country, yet you call them your brothers? Have you no shame?\"","Chen Yi berated him, and seeing the looks on Lv Jiunan’s and Ge Muxiao’s faces grow even more furious and embarrassed, he abruptly changed the subject.","\"Pay up with silver.\"","Perhaps because his change in topic was so abrupt, no one on or off the Painted Boat responded.","After a few moments, Liu Taoyao finally said with a laugh, \"Of course.\"","\"How about one thousand taels?\"","\"Are you trying to wave off a beggar?\"","\"Three thousand.\"","\"Heh, I am a famous and powerful master of the Jianghu. Do you think a mere three thousand taels is enough to dismiss me?\"","Hearing this, Liu Taoyao seemed to get angry as well. His voice deepened as he asked, \"Then name your price, sir.\"","\"Not much. Five thousand taels of silver will suffice.\"","\"Fine.\"","\"You may come aboard the Painted Boat to retrieve it yourself.\"","Chen Yi paused for a second, glancing at Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao, who were glaring at him like tigers from the Painted Boat. Then, he broke into a wide grin.","\"I doubt you’d dare try any tricks. I’ll come aboard!\""]},{"number":378,"title":"Chapter 378 - 246: Leaving Him Powerless to Turn the Tide","paragraphs":["That being said,","Chen Yi would never gamble with his own life. He was already gripping a bottle of Immortal Drunk in his hand.","With a single step, he was aboard the Painted Boat.","He tilted his head up slightly, his disdainful gaze sweeping over Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao until their eyes twitched. Only then did he turn and enter the Painted Boat.","As he walked, he muttered to himself, \"The Black Magic of Poshisu Country has some substance.\"","\"A pity it’s all for show.\"","Back in the East Market, Chen Yi had already discerned some of the secrets of Black Magic from that Evil Demon of the Illusory Sound Sect.","It seemed strange, but in reality, it was just a Cultivation Technique from the Evil Demonic Dao—unfit for the grand stage.","It likely involved using some sort of Secret Technique to plant an \"Artifact\" inside another’s body, then using True Essence to create vibrations for the purpose of long-distance control and assassination.","When cultivated to a profound Realm, its power would be further enhanced by tapping into the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","To put it bluntly,","Black Magic was similar to Witchcraft and the Poison Dao, but it lacked their variety and practicality.","This was especially true for a Martial Artist like Chen Yi, whose Cultivation and Techniques had both reached a certain Realm.","Once he was on guard, trying to kill him with Black Magic would be next to impossible.","Seeing his brazen, disdainful attitude, Ge Muxiao clenched his fists, his eyes wide and practically spitting fire.","The explosive True Essence within him stirred, ready to erupt.","Beside him, Lv Jiunan appeared much calmer. He revealed none of his aura and showed no intention of making a move.","Only his gray eyes were grim and cold, a flicker of contemplation occasionally surfacing within them.","’The clothes on this man... they seem identical to the ones I just saw on the ’Sword Madman,’ Liu Lang?’","’Is he Liu Lang?’","’Or is he a Wandering Martial Artist who has achieved Spear Dao Perfection and Great Success Saber Dao, merely impersonating Liu Lang?’","Lv Jiunan couldn’t be sure.","Even though he was from Poshisu Country and knew little about the Jianghu of the Wei Dynasty, he had still heard of certain supremely talented experts.","For example, there was Xiao Jinghong, who had already reached Upper Three Grades Cultivation and Sword Dao Perfection at the tender age of twenty.","There was also Shui Hetong of Fengyue Building—a closed-door disciple of Immortal Bai, whose Fist Dao was said to possess the power to ’topple a thousand miles of mountains and rivers’.","And Hua Huixiang of Martial Arts Mountain, who had reached the Second Grade Realm at a young age.","But a Martial Artist like the one before him, who had achieved Spear Dao Perfection at such a young age, was a rare sight in any era.","If, on top of that, he also possessed Saber Dao at the Great Success Realm, then he would be rarer still.","He would be nearly on par with Xiao Jinghong, renowned for his Spear and Sword Dual Mastery.","Therefore, after careful consideration, Lv Jiunan concluded that this young Wandering Martial Artist was probably just wearing the same clothes as Liu Lang.","Thinking of this, he suddenly called out, \"Liu Lang.\"","Chen Yi stopped in his tracks. He turned, raising an eyebrow. \"Oh? You’ve met my brother Liu Lang?\"","He was, of course, aware of Lv Jiunan’s suspicion.","But when he saw that they didn’t attack, he knew the two of them must be unsure of his identity—they were merely suspicious.","Fortunately, his reactions had been swift, and he had altered both his movements and his Techniques.","Otherwise, he wouldn’t even have had a chance to negotiate tonight; his only options would have been to fight or flee.","Lv Jiunan forced a smile onto his grim face. \"I just had a very pleasant conversation with the ’Sword Madman’.\"","Hearing this, Ge Muxiao’s furious expression froze. He turned his head to look at him. \"Big Brother, you... He...\"","Lv Jiunan raised a hand to cut him off. \"I am Lv Jiunan of Poshisu Country. May I ask for your esteemed name, brother?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, tilted his head up slightly, and said contemptuously, \"Liu Wu.\"","With that, he walked deeper into the Painted Boat.","Lv Jiunan watched him go, his brow furrowed as he silently repeated the name Liu Wu.","’That’s obviously a fake name.’","’But that won’t stop me from having someone look into it.’","After all, a Wandering Martial Artist who had reached Spear Dao Perfection couldn’t possibly be a nobody.","Chen Yi, naturally, was unaware of Lv Jiunan’s thoughts. After entering the Painted Boat, he scanned his surroundings, his gaze landing on the two young men.","One of them was handsome, dressed in black brocade with silver thread embroidering his cuffs and sash. He carried himself with an air of nobility.","The second was dressed as a scholar in a long, grayish-white robe and a square cap. His features were plain, but his eyes were calm and steady.","After sizing them up, Chen Yi held out his hand. \"Hand over the silver.\"","The black-robed Liu Taoyao was also studying him. Seeing how direct he was, he gestured to the young man by his side. \"Shichang.\"","The young man took out several silver notes from his sleeve and silently placed them in Liu Taoyao’s hand.","Liu Taoyao took them and placed them directly into Chen Yi’s hand, saying with a smile, \"I am Liu Taoyao.\"","\"Brother Liu Wu, there have been many misunderstandings tonight. I hope you can forgive us.\"","Chen Yi took the silver notes and counted them. \"It’s a good thing I have some skill. Anyone else would have already been killed by those Poshisu Country scoundrels just now.\"","Sensing that Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao had entered behind him, he rested his palm on the Five-section Spear on his forearm and continued,","\"Liu Taoyao, is it? Take a piece of advice from me: people from foreign lands don’t understand benevolence, righteousness, propriety, wisdom, or integrity. It’s best to have little to do with them.\"","\"You—!\"","Before Ge Muxiao and Lv Jiunan could speak, Liu Taoyao stopped them with a look and smiled at Chen Yi.","\"I will take Brother Liu’s lesson to heart.\"","After a pause, he added with a smile, \"Since fate has brought us together, why don’t you sit and have a drink with us, Brother Liu?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, then jutted his chin toward Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao.","\"I don’t care for people from Poshisu Country. You’ll have to excuse me.\"","Ge Muxiao, naturally, glared at him furiously.","Lv Jiunan, however, simply stared at him in silence.","Liu Taoyao exchanged a look with the young man beside him, their expressions complex and difficult to read.","But just as Chen Yi was about to leave, a clear voice rang out from the edge of the Quchi.","\"Who was fighting here earlier?\""]},{"number":379,"title":"Chapter 379 - 246: Render Him Powerless","paragraphs":["Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. ’Fang Hongxiu?’","Liu Taoyao was the first to react. He instructed the young man by his side, \"They must be from the Imprisonment Department. Go turn them away.\"","The young man accepted his orders and walked out of the Painted Boat.","Liu Taoyao then clasped his hands toward Chen Yi and smiled. \"As the old saying goes, ’no fight, no friendship.’ Why must you keep us at such a distance, Brother Liu?\"","\"Besides, some rather inconvenient people have arrived outside. It’s better for you to take refuge here, Brother Liu, than to be disturbed by them.\"","Perhaps worried that Chen Yi would refuse again, he pointed outside the Painted Boat.","\"And with this storm raging tonight, staying inside the boat is much better than sleeping in the mud outside, wouldn’t you agree?\"","Chen Yi said, unmoved, \"It was your people who disturbed me first.\"","Liu Taoyao’s smile never wavered. He offered a quick apology, then shot Lv Jiunan a look.","Lv Jiunan nodded in understanding, forcing a smile onto his face.","\"My little ghost sensed something strange just now and disturbed you, young brother. I hope you’ll forgive us.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. While keeping his attention focused outside the Painted Boat, he still shook his head.","\"We walk different paths and cannot make plans together. I have silver now; I can buy my own alcohol.\"","Before anyone else could speak, Chen Yi walked out of the Painted Boat. In a flash, he drifted back to the shore.","Seeing this, Liu Taoyao frowned. He had no choice but to signal Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao to stay out of sight before following Chen Yi out of the Painted Boat.","At that moment, Fang Hongxiu was questioning the young man named Zhao Shichang. Seeing Chen Yi emerge, she quickly moved to intercept him.","\"Wait.\"","Chen Yi pulled the bamboo hat from his back onto his head and glanced sideways at her. \"What is it?\"","He had already overheard Fang Hongxiu asking Zhao Shichang for details. The gist was that he had revealed a bit of his skill while drinking.","Fang Hongxiu sized him up, a flicker of recognition in her eyes. Her tone grew suspicious.","\"Who are you? Were you the one who just made a move over Quchi Lake?\"","Chen Yi tugged his bamboo hat down slightly, revealing a sharply defined jawline. He lowered his voice and chuckled, \"The name’s Liu Wu.\"","\"If Hundred Households Fang is referring to that burst of Spear Intent, then yes, that was me.\"","Fang Hongxiu’s eyes widened. \"You...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yi leaned in closer, raised a finger to his lips in a \"shush\" gesture, and said with his back to the Painted Boat:","\"If there’s nothing else, I’ll be taking my leave.\"","As he spoke, however, he made two quick hand signals to Fang Hongxiu, telling her to stay calm.","Fang Hongxiu, having recognized him, shot him a glare. She then turned toward the Painted Boat on the lake, clasped her fist, and said:","\"Since it was a misunderstanding, we won’t disturb Lord Liu’s pleasant evening.\"","After exchanging a glance with Zhao Shichang, Liu Taoyao replied, \"Thank you for your trouble.\"","He didn’t forget to clasp his hands toward Chen Yi with a smile. \"My apologies, Brother Liu. Tonight was rather inconvenient. We’ll have to share a drink on the boat another time.\"","Chen Yi just smiled and shook his head. He gave Fang Hongxiu another hand signal, then leaped away into the distance.","Fang Hongxiu understood his signal. After a moment’s hesitation, she waved her hand and led her people away.","A few of the Imprisonment Officers muttered as they walked, \"That guy looks kind of familiar.\"","\"I thought so too. He looks like that guy from...\"","Before he could finish, Fang Hongxiu slapped him on the back. \"Less chatter,\" she chided. \"Hurry up and scout the area for any other disturbances.\"","\"Yes, Lord Hundred Households...\"","「Once everyone was gone.」","Liu Taoyao stared into the dim, rainy curtain, the smile on his face slowly fading until his expression was completely sullen.","The young man called Shichang, however, was much calmer. After scanning their surroundings, he bowed respectfully and said:","\"Young Master, let’s talk inside.\"","Liu Taoyao grunted in acknowledgment and turned back into the Painted Boat.","Inside, he found Lv Jiunan sitting cross-legged at the table, wisps of an icy, sinister aura radiating from his body.","Ge Muxiao stood guard beside him, his expression vigilant.","Liu Taoyao’s expression flickered. After a moment’s thought, he decided not to disturb Lv Jiunan and instead turned to Ge Muxiao.","\"Is Brother Lü using a Secret Skill to track that Liu Wu?\"","Ge Muxiao merely nodded, not daring to speak for fear of disturbing Lv Jiunan.","Seeing this, Liu Taoyao’s expression eased slightly. He turned his head and asked, \"What is your assessment of this Liu Wu?\"","Zhao Shichang pondered for a moment. \"He’s rather odd.\"","\"For one, his previous location was too close to the Painted Boat.\"","\"With his level of Martial Arts Cultivation and Technique Realm, if he had intended to eavesdrop, he should have been able to hear our conversation.\"","\"Secondly, judging by his attitude toward Brother Lü and Brother Ge Mu, it’s easy to conclude that he is not one of us.\"","Liu Taoyao nodded slightly. \"My thoughts exactly.\"","He paused, his brow furrowing. \"If he did hear our conversation, I’m afraid...\"","Zhao Shichang naturally understood what he meant. His gaze fell upon Lv Jiunan as he said:","\"Young Master, the crucial thing now is to confirm his identity.\"","\"If he’s just some ordinary Jianghu wanderer, that’s one thing. The real danger is if he has connections to certain people in Shu State.\"","Liu Taoyao followed his gaze. \"For now, we can only rely on Brother Lü.\"","But no sooner had the words left his mouth than Lv Jiunan’s eyes snapped open. His face was a mask of fury as he growled, \"Liu Wu!\"","Liu Taoyao was taken aback. \"Brother Lü, what is it...?\"","Lv Jiunan snorted, his tone icy. \"He discovered the Secret Skill I was using.\"","\"I don’t know what Method he used, but he was able to detect the Black Magic I placed on him. And not only that...\"","He paused, looking out from the Painted Boat with a wary expression. \"He was even able to destroy it in one strike.\"","Liu Taoyao and Zhao Shichang exchanged a look, frowning. \"Brother Lü, are you saying he’s coming back for us?\"","Lv Jiunan shook his head. \"I don’t know.\"","\"But to avoid implicating you both, I must take my leave first.\"","Earlier, besides being wary of Chen Yi’s strength, he had also been concerned about Liu Taoyao and the others being present.","If a fight were to break out here, never mind the outcome, his connection to Liu Taoyao would surely be exposed."]},{"number":380,"title":"Chapter 380 - 246: Leaving Him Powerless to Recover","paragraphs":["A deeper worry was that the contact between Liu Hong and King Landu had been discovered.","Seeing this, Liu Taoyao spoke a little faster. \"Brother Lü, I have a presumptuous request.\"","\"I hope you can investigate his identity for me.\"","\"Just now, when you spoke with him, didn’t you mention the ’Sword Madman’ Liu Lang? Why not start with Liu Lang?\"","As he and Ge Muxiao changed into black clothes, Lv Jiunan said,","\"That matter must be handled sooner rather than later. If Bright Moon Building is unusable, I hope Young Master Liu has another method.\"","Liu Taoyao’s expression hardened. He said in a low voice, \"Rest assured, Brother Lü. I will discuss it with my father shortly.\"","Lv Jiunan nodded, said no more, and left the Painted Boat with Ge Muxiao.","「After they left.」","Liu Taoyao waited another moment. When Chen Yi didn’t return, he breathed a small sigh of relief.","\"Shichang, do you think it was a coincidence that he came here tonight?\"","Zhao Shichang pondered for a moment before replying calmly, \"It should be a coincidence.\"","\"After all, before tonight, Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao had only appeared in public once.\"","\"The time at the East Market? Yes, Lv Jiunan is careful enough. If he had been followed when he rescued Asutai, he would have noticed long ago.\"","Liu Taoyao paused, then raised a hand. \"Shichang, let’s go. Back to the residence.\"","\"We need to let Father know about this as soon as possible.\"","...","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yi stood five li from Quchi, True Essence swirling in his hand to envelop a bug the size of a pinprick.","’Black Magic really is cut from the same cloth as the Poison Dao and the Witchcraft and Gu Dao.’","If not for his Qi Observation Skill, he never would have discovered the Black Magic Lv Jiunan had placed on him.","Chen Yi looked at the bug in his hand, his thoughts racing.","’Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao came to Shu State at Liu Hong’s request to rescue those barbarian slaves.’","’Especially the son of the Barbarian Left King, who seems to be called Asutai.’","’As long as I follow this thread, I’ll definitely find evidence of Liu Hong’s collusion with the Barbarian Race.’","For him, killing Liu Hong or Liu Taoyao would be simple, but it wouldn’t resolve the Xiao Family’s predicament.","The best result would be to have the Xiao Family eliminate Liu Hong themselves.","Only then would it serve to make an example of him, and only then could the Xiao Family regain their power in Shu State.","As for Lv Jiunan...","A horse bandit from Poshisu Country, and a General under King Landu at that—what difference did it make if he was killed sooner or later?","He would let him live for now. Perhaps he could still get evidence from him to take down Liu Hong.","’But I still need to find where they and those barbarian slaves are hiding.’","At this thought, a smile appeared on Chen Yi’s face.","All in all, it was good news.","Just then, the sound of light footsteps came from a distance.","Chen Yi looked toward the sound and saw Fang Hongxiu approaching alone.","He lifted his bamboo hat, greeting her with a smile. \"Hundred Households Fang, you got here fast.\"","Fang Hongxiu, dressed in a raincoat and bamboo hat, gripped the long blade at her waist and snorted, \"What the hell are you up to?\"","\"How did you get mixed up with Liu Taoyao?\"","She knew that Chen Yi had acted to help the Xiao Family several times before, so seeing him now drinking with Liu Taoyao on a Painted Boat inevitably made her suspicious.","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"I didn’t want to.\"","\"Tonight I was investigating the fire at the East Market Grain Warehouse, but who would have thought I’d run into Liu Taoyao here?\"","Fang Hongxiu’s expression changed slightly. \"Are you saying Liu Taoyao ordered someone to burn down the East Market Grain Warehouse?\"","\"If I said it was him, would you dare to investigate?\"","\"If it really was him, I would definitely bring him to justice!\"","Chen Yi paused and shook his head. \"Then I’m afraid I have to disappoint you. He had nothing to do with it.\"","He knew very well that with the Imprisonment Department’s power, they were no match for Liu Hong and Liu Taoyao.","Rather than telling Fang Hongxiu the truth, it was better to give her some clues to attract the attention of those people.","After all, he still needed some time.","Fang Hongxiu shot him a displeased glare. \"Then why did you ask me to meet you here?\"","\"To give you some clues, of course.\"","\"Speak.\"","\"King Landu. You’ve heard of him, right?\"","\"Of course I know him. He’s the leader of the Peacock Thief, who run rampant on the borders of our Wei Dynasty. He commands over ten thousand horse bandits and is incredibly powerful.\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"I’ve discovered that the Black Magic Master from Poshisu Country who rescued the barbarian slaves is one of King Landu’s men.\"","Hearing this, Fang Hongxiu’s brow furrowed. \"Is this true?\"","\"Hundred Households Fang, on this matter, our goals are aligned. Of all people, I wouldn’t lie to you.\"","\"If that’s the case... then things are bad...\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"With your status as a Hundred Households of the Imprisonment Department, you’re afraid of King Landu?\"","Fang Hongxiu ignored his teasing and looked down in thought. \"You don’t understand.\"","\"Although King Landu is a horse bandit, he also values rules greatly.\"","\"Ever since he rose to power, merchants on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road have had no fear for their lives, as long as they pay the fee.\"","\"If his people rescued those barbarian slaves, I’m afraid this matter will have to be dropped.\"","Chen Yi stroked his chin. \"So you’re saying we should thank King Landu for following the rules?\"","\"I don’t have to consider these things, but the Imprisonment Department and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office cannot ignore them.\"","\"Are you worried that people in the Government Office won’t approve of your investigation?\"","\"Looks like I chose the wrong partner.\"","Fang Hongxiu shot him an exasperated look, a rare hint of girlishness in her expression.","\"I will report this matter to Lord Thousand Households separately. Whether he agrees or not, I will find that man from Poshisu Country and the barbarian slaves.\"","\"That’s all I needed to hear.\"","With that, Chen Yi cupped his hands in a farewell gesture and left.","\"I wish Hundred Households Fang a swift success. I will come find you again.\"","Fang Hongxiu watched him disappear into the curtain of rain, then, after a moment of thought, she also departed quickly.","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi quietly returned to his residence on Chuansi Street and ordered Zhang Dabao to prepare a brush and ink for him."]},{"number":381,"title":"Chapter 381 - 246: Leaving Him Powerless to Recover","paragraphs":["Then, without a moment’s rest, he sketched portraits of Lv Jiunan, Ge Muxiao, and the young barbarian slave, Asutai.","To avoid any ambiguity caused by the ink-wash painting style, he also made sure to write down descriptions of their features.","Once Chen Yi finished the drawings and confirmed they were accurate, he handed them to Zhang Dabao and said, \"Tomorrow, use these to find them.\"","Zhang Dabao took them, glanced over them, and said with a smile, \"I will be sure to find them for you, milord.\"","He hadn’t been confident before, but it was a different story now that he had portraits.","Those hooligans and ruffians who loitered on the streets year-round weren’t good for much else, but finding people was an easy task for them.","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and instructed, \"Remember, once you find them, don’t act rashly. And don’t get too close, or you’ll be discovered.\"","He paused, then continued his orders, \"Go straight to the Imprisonment Department and inform Hundred Households Fang Hongxiu.\"","\"The Imprisonment Department?\"","\"Yes. Just do as I’ve instructed.\"","\"Yes...\"","Chen Yi gave a few more instructions, then removed his disguise and returned to the Xiao Family estate.","Only after changing his clothes did he let out a long breath, his mind finally relaxing.","His excursion tonight had been quite fruitful.","Not only had he found the mastermind who forced him to flee his own wedding, but he had also uncovered clues about Liu Hong’s collusion with the Barbarian Race and Poshisu Country.","The latter discovery was even more exhilarating to him than the former.","As Chen Yi pondered these things, he placed two pieces on the game board in his mind.","One piece was, of course, Fang Hongxiu. The other was Elder Master Xiao.","After the pieces were placed, the white stones formed a position of strength in one corner, surrounding several black stones.","Chen Yi’s mind was immersed in the game board as he thought to himself:","’No matter how wily that old fox Liu Hong is, this time he’ll be powerless to turn the tide.’","Just then, a golden light flashed. Chen Yi glanced at the screen of light:","[Daily Intel - Profound-rank Lower Grade: At 11:15 PM, Hidden Guard Simurgh Phoenix will have a nocturnal meeting with Hidden Guard General at a tailor shop in the West Market. A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","’Simurgh Phoenix, Cui Qingwu?’","Chen Yi checked the time, then glanced at the sky outside before sitting cross-legged on his bed to begin his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","With only fifteen minutes left, it was already too late for him to get there.","So he decided to ignore it.","「An unknown amount of time passed.」","[Opportunity +8.]","[Evaluation: Cui Qingwu and General parted on bad terms.]","[You did not arrive, heard no sound, and witnessed no scene. An Opportunity fell from the heavens, yet you did not take it. You are a lazy person by nature.]","...","「Meanwhile, at the Liu Family estate in Shu State.」","Amidst the sound of the falling rain, crashing sounds echoed throughout the mansion.","It was rather noisy.","But Liu Lang had no mind to pay attention to the surrounding rain. He was lying on a rooftop, staring at the study in the rear courtyard.","He had already gone to bed.","Who would have known that shortly after 11 PM, he would hear two people approaching.","Their footsteps and their conversation with Liu Hong both sounded rather urgent, as if something major had happened.","After listening for a while, Liu Lang confirmed that the visitor was Liu Hong’s eldest son, Liu Taoyao.","’That old fox Liu Hong really treats his two sons differently.’","’He’s always beating or cursing the second son, but he’s so patient with this older one.’","Just as he was thinking this, he heard Liu Hong’s grim voice from inside the study:","\"In that situation, how could you let him leave?!\"","\"Even if that person didn’t hear your conversation with Lv Jiunan, you should have found a way to keep him there!\"","Liu Taoyao’s tone was hesitant as he said, \"Father, it’s not that I didn’t want to.\"","\"It’s just that the man’s strength was truly formidable. I’m afraid that even Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao together wouldn’t have been able to take him down.\"","He paused, and seeing that Liu Hong didn’t speak, he continued, \"I’ve already tasked Lv Jiunan with investigating the man’s identity. I imagine he should be able to find something.\"","Liu Hong snorted coldly. \"Investigate?\"","\"As long as that man isn’t a fool, he won’t just sit around and wait for death.\"","\"What’s more, you announced your own identity right in front of Lv Jiunan and the others! You... you’re a muddle-headed fool!\"","\"Just a few days ago, I told Fang’er to learn from you. Is this the example you set?\"","He violently smashed a teacup at his side. CRASH! \"Do you have any idea how much trouble this will bring me—bring the Liu Family—if word gets out?!\"","\"I...\"","Before Liu Taoyao could explain, Zhao Shichang, who was standing by, spoke up first:","\"Master, now is not the time to blame the Young Master.\"","\"We await your clear instructions on what we should do.\"","A moment of silence.","Liu Hong seemed to have calmed down. He said in a low tone, \"Tomorrow, you will send someone to inform Lv Jiunan and have them leave Shu State as soon as possible.\"","\"And as for those barbarian slaves...\"","\"Shichang, find a body double for Asutai. Kill the double along with the other barbarian slaves and send the bodies to the Imprisonment Department.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Yao’er, remember this: neither of us has a path of retreat now. We cannot afford the slightest bit of carelessness.\"","\"Yes...\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang couldn’t help but raise his eyebrows. ’That old fox is truly ruthless.’","After some thought, he concealed himself again, watching the rain fall from the sky.","’The boss should be very interested in this news...’"]},{"number":382,"title":"Chapter 382 - 247: The Leopard Cat Switches the Crown Prince","paragraphs":["「The next morning.」","The rain had lessened, but a fine drizzle still fell from beneath a shroud of gray, overcast clouds.","The soft pitter-patter was everywhere.","Occasionally, a larger droplet would fall, making a crisp DRIP-DROP as it struck a puddle or a leaf.","On days like this, Xiaodie was always the busiest.","Before dawn, she had helped Xiao Wuge wash up and get dressed, then saw him off as he followed Wang Lixing to the Martial Arts Arena.","After that, she didn’t have a moment to spare.","Washing clothes, hanging them to dry, cleaning, and so on.","She bustled about for a full two hours before the Spring Lotus Garden finally looked refreshed in the gloomy, rainy weather.","It was clean and natural, like a courtyard in a Jiangnan water village.","Xiaodie looked at the tidy courtyard, wiped the sweat from her forehead, and broke into a satisfied smile.","’Time to wake the Young Master.’","But just as she put the broom away, she heard the jingling of bells from outside.","Pei Guanli came skipping over. \"Sister Xiaodie, I’m back.\"","Xiaodie turned to look and exclaimed, \"Your clothes...\"","Pei Guanli was no longer wearing her previous attire, the distinctive clothing of the Mountain Race.","Instead, she had changed into a sea-blue long dress with a band of pink embroidered flowers at the waist.","The neckline was a bit low, and pressed down by a silver bell, the pale white cleavage was faintly visible.","However, she was still barefoot, her fair, delicate feet leaving faint wet prints on the damp bluestone slabs.","A grin spread across Pei Guanli’s round face. She spun around twice like a flower and asked, \"Isn’t it pretty?\"","Xiaodie nodded repeatedly. \"Very pretty.\"","She couldn’t help but feel a little envious.","Although she didn’t lack for food or clothing in the Marquis’s Mansion, she usually went without makeup and wore the specific uniform of a servant.","She rarely got to dress up deliberately like Pei Guanli.","After a few more pleasantries, Pei Guanli glanced at the wooden building and asked, \"Is Brother-in-law not up yet?\"","Xiaodie nodded. \"I was just about to go wake the Young Master.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli’s eyes darted around. She playfully pushed Xiaodie toward the gate, saying with a giggle, \"Sister Xiaodie, you go prepare breakfast. I’ll go wake Brother-in-law.\"","\"You? No, that won’t do. You’re a guest. How could I let you do such things?\"","\"Don’t worry, it’s just bringing Brother-in-law some hot water and a towel, right? Leave it to me, leave it to me...\"","Xiaodie couldn’t win against her, so after a few words of instruction, she took an oil-paper umbrella and went to the back kitchen to prepare breakfast.","Seeing her walk away, Pei Guanli let out a couple of mischievous giggles.","She then fetched the hot water and a towel and went to Chen Yi’s door.","\"Bro... Young Master, it’s time for you to get up.\"","Pei Guanli put on a high-pitched voice, imitating Xiaodie, and gently pushed the door open to peek inside.","Once she saw Chen Yi lying on the bed, she tiptoed into the room, carefully set down the hot water, and dipped the towel in it.","As she made her preparations, she kept glancing back, afraid that Chen Yi would wake up at any moment.","After wringing the towel dry, she beamed again, her eyes curving into beautiful crescents.","But just as Pei Guanli turned around, she saw Chen Yi standing right in front of her. She yelped in fright and stumbled backward.","\"Ah!\"","\"Brother-in-law, help, help...\"","\"What sort of mischief were you planning?\" Chen Yi said, even as his hand shot out, grabbing the towel to pull her back.","Pei Guanli, still shaken, patted the bells on her chest and said with a flushed face, \"You wretched Brother-in-law! You were awake this whole time, weren’t you?\"","Chen Yi looked at her with amusement. \"Trying to turn the tables, are we? You were the one trying to scare me first.\"","Pei Guanli pouted, handing him the towel while muttering things like \"no fun at all.\"","Chen Yi took the towel and wiped his face. Knowing she had a childish nature, he didn’t tease her further and instead changed the subject, \"Have you gotten your brother and the others settled?\"","Pei Guanli’s expression immediately brightened. She hugged his arm and said, \"Brother-in-law, do you know where my brother and the others are staying?\"","\"Kangning Street?\"","\"Yep, yep, not far from Guiyun Academy.\"","’That makes sense.’","Pei Guanli didn’t know much about Shu State Prefecture City. Besides the Xiao Family estate, the only other place she was familiar with was the academy.","After all, she had almost died there.","\"That’s a good spot. When the people from the Five Poison Sect arrive, they’ll likely stay in that area too.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli blinked. \"Is that so?\"","\"Brother-in-law, do you know where they are?\"","Chen Yi helplessly patted her hand away and explained as he got dressed,","\"I ran into them over there before.\"","That night, after he killed Yan Fusha, he hadn’t told Pei Guanli about Liu Zhaoxue.","He didn’t want Pei Guanli to learn the truth and go blustering over to the Liu Family, which would interfere with his plans.","Pei Guanli clearly wasn’t concerned about that. \"So, that means I did the right thing by having my brother and the others stay there.\"","\"Yes, yes, you did...\"","Once fully dressed, Chen Yi led her downstairs to the living room to wait for Xiaodie’s return.","Pei Guanli then began to animatedly recount interesting stories about her brother and the others.","For example, her youngest sister, Lan Yanni, was a young girl who had just turned fifteen.","Although her Cultivation had already surpassed Pei Guanli’s, reaching the Upper Seventh Grade, she was like a country bumpkin, finding everything in the city new and fascinating.","Then there was the woman she called Aunt Chu, whose name was Zhu Fangling. For the past two days, she had been clamoring to go back to the mountains.","And her \"Uncle Li,\" Li Yunjun, who looked honest on the surface but was actually full of mischief.","As soon as they got to the city, he had snuck off to Yanhua Lane, only to be discovered by Zhu Fangling and given a sound beating.","There was also her third granduncle, Pei Ze, a Fourth Grade Realm Poison Master who had clashed with people from the Five Poison Sect many years ago.","\"Brother-in-law, this time, Ah Ma had my brother bring people over. We’re fully prepared. I guarantee those from the Five Poison Sect will find it a one-way trip.\"","\"Your Ah Ma isn’t making a move herself?\"","\"Don’t underestimate my brother. He made a special trip into the mountains a while back and got a few treasures from Granny Shan.\"","\"Granny Shan?\"","\"Yep, yep, from Wumeng Mountain.\""]},{"number":383,"title":"Chapter 383 - 247: A Leopard Cat for a Prince (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"You mean the treasure your brother found in the mountains?\"","Pei Guanli shook her head and explained that it was Wumeng Mountain. She added that the Mountain Race called it \"Granny Shan.\"","\"Brother-in-law, Granny Shan is very powerful. When I was little, whenever I was in danger on the mountain, I would just call out her name, and I’d be safe.\"","\"She also has two emissaries. One is a mountain beast, a tiger, that’s this big.\"","Pei Guanli drew a large circle in front of her. \"It’s a full ten feet long and very powerful.\"","\"The other is a tree so massive it would take more than ten people to wrap their arms around it.\"","\"Whenever our race faced a great disaster, Ah Ma would go under that tree and consult Granny Shan.\"","\"But Ah Ma never let anyone follow her, so I don’t know what she asked.\"","Chen Yi was skeptical, but he found it intriguing.","\"Can the treasure your brother brought really deal with the Five Poison Sect?\"","Pei Guanli tapped the bell, making it jingle. \"What my Ah Ma says is never wrong.\"","\"Besides, if my brother can’t do it, we still have my Third Grand-Uncle and Uncle Li. They’re the strongest in our race. They’ll definitely annihilate the Five Poison Sect, leaving no one alive.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and didn’t press the matter.","For him, as long as the Mountain Race could provide some assistance, he was confident he could take care of Liu Zhaoxue and the others.","A short while later, Xiaodie brought in breakfast.","The three of them sat together, chatting and laughing as they ate.","As they were eating, Chen Yi’s ear twitched. He heard footsteps outside the door and knew someone had arrived.","He put down his chopsticks, wiped his mouth, and saw Liu Si’er appear outside the wooden house with Wang Ji.","\"Sir, Shopkeeper Wang from Hundred Herbs Hall is here to see you.\"","Chen Yi nodded, exchanged a few pleasantries to dismiss Liu Si’er, and then led Wang Ji to the study.","He had just seen Wang Ji last night and given him all necessary instructions. ’For him to come now, something must have happened.’","And just as he expected.","As soon as they entered the study, Wang Ji respectfully took a letter from his robes and handed it to him. \"Guard Liu delivered this early this morning.\"","Chen Yi’s expression flickered as he took the letter and began to read.","[The old man and his eldest have decided to eliminate those barbarian slaves. Except for one named Asutai, for whom they’ll find a barbarian impostor, the bodies of the other barbarian slaves are to be handed over to the Government Office.]","[He also said to make Lv Jiunan of Poshisu Country leave as soon as possible.]","[I’ve already located the barbarian slaves—Number 4, Yiding, Pingyao Lane, near the East Market.]","[I haven’t found the person from Poshisu Country yet, but they should be somewhere near the West Market... ]","Reaching the end, Chen Yi asked without looking up, \"How long was Guard Liu at Hundred Herbs Hall this morning?\"","Wang Ji thought for a moment before replying, \"He left as soon as he finished writing. He didn’t linger at all.\"","\"Is Dabao around?\"","\"Him? He left the shop early this morning.\"","Chen Yi grunted, lit an oil lamp, and burned the letter to ash, his mind racing.","Although the message from Liu Lang was vague, he could already deduce the gist of what Liu Hong and Liu Taoyao had discussed last night.","’It must have been my appearance on the Painted Boat last night that alerted that old bastard Liu Hong.’","’That’s why he’s trying to erase all the clues.’","’Asutai is the Left King’s son. Liu Hong wouldn’t dare kill him, nor could he. Finding an impostor is a clever idea.’","’And then there’s Lv Jiunan...’","Thinking of this, Chen Yi instructed Wang Ji, \"Find a way to get a message to Zhang Dabao. Tell him the person is near the West Market.\"","He paused, then added, \"After that, have him wait on Chuansi Street.\"","Wang Ji acknowledged with a \"Yes.\" \"I’ll go at once.\"","\"Wait.\" Chen Yi blew out the oil lamp. \"I’ll go with you.\"","’Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao could wait. The most important thing right now was to find those barbarian slaves.’","’If the opportunity presented itself, he might just have to intervene.’","But when Chen Yi and Wang Ji walked out of the study, they found Pei Guanli standing outside, grinning, a look on her face that said, ’I heard everything.’","\"Brother-in-law, are you going out to have some fun?\"","\"Can I come with you?\"","Chen Yi was about to refuse when a thought occurred to him. He made a gesture for her to be quiet. \"I’ll take you if you behave.\"","Pei Guanli nodded vigorously, promising not to say a single word.","Wang Ji just gave her a curious glance before leading the way out of the wooden house.","’The boss has spoken. As a subordinate, it’s not my place to say anything.’","Chen Yi gave Xiaodie a few instructions, then left Spring Lotus Garden with Pei Guanli and Wang Ji.","Just then, Xiao Wan’er arrived from outside with Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun.","\"Brother-in-law, Shopkeeper Wang, where are you all off to?\"","Chen Yi smiled and offered a brief explanation, saying he was just taking Tiger Girl to drop by Hundred Herbs Hall and pick up some tea.","Xiao Wan’er didn’t suspect a thing and went on to say that the Old Master had agreed to their plan.","Chen Yi smiled. \"That’s wonderful news.\"","\"In the next day or two, you can start sending out letters to some Medical Saint Hands, inviting them to Shu State.\"","This was precisely the plan he had proposed: to use the Old Master’s name to invite Medical Saint Hands from all over to Shu State.","This would serve as a pretext for Xiao Wan’er to select a suitable candidate for the position of dean of the Medical Dao Academy.","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er nodded, her smile blooming like a flower.","\"I just went to see Third Grandfather and asked him to help look into which Medical Saint Hands are out there.\"","\"He has a wide network and knows many people.\"","Then, she gestured to Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang. \"We’ve also sent a letter to the Celestial Sect to ask about famous Divine Doctors in the Jianghu. We should hear back soon.\"","\"And as for Tonglin...\"","She went on about various matters, all related to the Medical Dao Academy.","After listening and offering a few words of praise, Chen Yi took his leave.","Xiao Wan’er worked quickly. In the half-day since returning from Tonglin, she had already arranged everything."]},{"number":384,"title":"Chapter 384 - 247: The Leopard Cat for Prince Swap (Part 3)","paragraphs":["All he had to do now was follow the plan. He was confident the Medical Dao Academy could officially hang its plaque in less than two months.","Not long after, Chen Yi had Wang Ji detour to Chuansi Street, where he brought Pei Guanli to the house.","Pei Guanli curiously sized up the house, looking it over inside and out several times.","She knew Chen Yi was the man behind Hundred Herbs Hall, but she wasn’t clear on his other activities.","But coming here now, she didn’t have to be a genius to guess that Chen Yi had made preparations long in advance.","\"Brother-in-law, did you buy this?\"","Chen Yi hummed in affirmation. He went into the main room, sat down, and waited for Zhang Dabao to arrive.","Seeing that he wasn’t going to say more, Pei Guanli pulled over a Grandmaster’s Chair, sat down beside him, and stared at him with wide, unblinking eyes.","Her stare made Chen Yi squirm. \"Just ask whatever you want to ask.\"","\"Brother-in-law, when you find something fun to do, do you just do it secretly by yourself and not include me?\"","\"Fun?\"","Chen Yi reached out and flicked her on the forehead. \"If I brought you along,\" he said irritably, \"now *that’s* when it would get fun.\"","’It really wouldn’t have been wise to bring Pei Guanli along for his past endeavors.’","’Take the time he burned the Three Towns’ summer grain supply. If he hadn’t been completely out of options, there was no way he would have let this Tiger Girl deliver a message to Xiao Jinghong.’","Pei Guanli rubbed her forehead and pouted. \"I knew it. Brother-in-law doesn’t want to have fun with me. You’re a meanie.\"","Chen Yi shot her a look. \"You want to go home, then?\"","Pei Guanli froze for a second, then leaned in closer and asked excitedly, \"I knew you wouldn’t forget about me, Brother-in-law!\"","\"Quick, tell me! What do you need me to do?\"","\"Why aren’t you calling me a meanie anymore?\"","\"I wasn’t...\"","After a bit more teasing, Chen Yi glanced at the sky and told her to take out the various vials and jars she had on her.","\"I need to concoct a few poisons. Let’s see if you have anything I can use.\"","’His previous encounter with Yan Fusha had taught him that while poisons like Immortal Drunk and Qingfeng Drunk were fine for dealing with ordinary Jianghu People, they weren’t quite potent enough for members of the Evil Demonic Dao, who worked with poisons year-round.’","’And Black Magic Masters like Lv Jiunan were exactly that type of foe.’","’So, Chen Yi planned to snag some of the Mountain Race’s \"local specialties\" from Pei Guanli and see if he could create a more powerful poison.’","After examining all the poisons Pei Guanli carried, he couldn’t help but marvel. It was no wonder the Mountain Race was so feared by the Jianghu People of Shu State.","The sheer variety of poisons and Gu Insects she carried was enough to leave even him astounded.","After picking through them, he selected three vials and had Pei Guanli put the rest away for a rainy day.","\"Brother-in-law, you brought me here... just for this?\"","Seeing the Tiger Girl’s slight disappointment, Chen Yi could only smile and say, \"Of course not. In a little while, you’re coming with me to do something big.\"","\"Alright!\"","About an hour later, Zhang Dabao returned in a hurry.","Before he could say much, Chen Yi instructed him to apply his disguise.","\"Did you find the two of them?\"","\"Yes, sir. They’re in Heiyu Lane, deep within the West Market. It’s the same place General Jinghong raided before.\"","\"And Liu Lang?\"","\"He’s still there watching them. I’ve already told him to keep his distance.\"","Chen Yi nodded and said no more.","Once his disguise was complete, before Pei Guanli could ask anything, he had her change into a black robe and put on a bronze mask. Then, with Zhang Dabao driving the carriage, they headed for the East Market.","Along the way, Pei Guanli asked a single question at the start, but spent the rest of the journey visibly thrilled.","By the time they reached Pingyao Lane in the East Market, she could barely contain her laughter.","\"Brother-in-law, this is the first time I’ve ever done something so fun! Disguises, fake identities... Do you think I should come up with a cool-sounding title for myself?\"","\"Fairy Pei? Or Pei Xingdao, for ’delivering justice on heaven’s behalf’...\"","But when she noticed the look in Chen Yi’s eyes, her expression immediately turned serious.","\"Okay, okay, I get it. Serious business first.\"","Chen Yi paid her no mind. He listened intently for a moment, his gaze landing on a nearby residence.","Just as he was about to go and investigate, he faintly heard a pleading voice with a strange accent coming from inside:","\"...Please, I... I beg you, don’t kill...\"","\"If you have to kill someone, kill me...\"","\"My apologies, but in today’s little drama, ’The Wildcat for the Prince,’ you are the star. You can’t die...\""]},{"number":385,"title":"Chapter 385 - 248: Strike the Mountain to Frighten the Tiger","paragraphs":["\"Switching the crown prince for a wildcat?\"","A flicker of disdain crossed Chen Yi’s eyes behind the black iron mask.","\"That’s not the right phrase to use.\"","\"’The golden cicada shedding its shell’ is more like it.\"","\"But it’s a shame I’m here. This ’golden cicada,’ Asutai, won’t be shedding its shell today.\"","It’s not about being early, it’s about being on time.","Now that he had stumbled upon this, he couldn’t possibly let Liu Hong get what he wanted.","Chen Yi then focused his senses, scanning his surroundings while keeping his attention fixed on the situation inside the residence.","After a muffled shout in the barbarian tongue, the only sound left in the residence was Asutai’s irrepressible, guttural sobbing.","\"I... I won’t... let you... get away with this...\"","\"I’ll... kill you... kill...\"","\"Targos, Lu Liyi, Bach... I, Asutai, swear by the Barbarian God that I will kill you!\"","The man who had spoken earlier replied, his tone as contemptuous as ever.","\"Your Highness Asutai, your father, the Left King, personally led his grand army, only to be crushed at Mengshui Pass. What are your odds of success if you wait to inherit his title and stage a comeback?\"","\"Besides, you are merely the Left King’s youngest son, not *the* Barbarian Left King.\"","\"It won’t be too late to say such things to me on the day you actually become the Barbarian Left King.\"","\"ARGH—I’ll kill you!\"","It sounded as if someone had covered Asutai’s mouth, and he could only manage a muffled roar.","But it was quickly drowned out by the laughter of the man who had spoken before.","\"My apologies, Your Highness Asutai. You’ll just have to bear with staying here alone for a while.\"","\"But rest assured, I will instruct them to prepare the strongest spirits and the most delicious venison for you, ensuring you have an unforgettable time here in Shu State.\"","\"Haha...\"","Listening to the arrogant laughter, Chen Yi paid it little mind, his expression turning thoughtful.","He had seen plenty of arrogant people in his time.","But it wasn’t every day he met someone as brazen as this speaker.","Especially since the target of his ridicule was the youngest son of the Barbarian Left King—a man Liu Hong was risking his own head to protect.","After a moment of thought.","Chen Yi arrived at two conclusions.","First, Liu Hong’s plan to return Asutai to the Barbarian Race wasn’t a task entrusted to him by the Left King. Rather, he was eagerly currying favor in exchange for some kind of benefit.","Second, Liu Hong and the Left King had a deeper level of cooperation, and the two considered each other equals.","Otherwise, it was impossible for Liu Hong’s confidant to have such an attitude toward Asutai.","If it were him, Chen Yi could think of countless ways to return Asutai to the Barbarian Race without the man ever being the wiser.","He certainly wouldn’t orchestrate it like this, forcing Asutai to witness his clansmen die tragically because of him.","Of course, there was a third possibility—Asutai was not valued by the Left King within the Barbarian Race.","But that seemed unlikely.","Chen Yi gazed thoughtfully at the residence, subconsciously tapping a finger on the carriage window frame.","’If it’s the second possibility, then Liu Hong’s dealings with the Barbarian Race might have been going on for a very long time.’","’A year, two years... or perhaps even before the Barbarian Left King Mu Hage attacked Mengshui Pass?’","Chen Yi couldn’t know for sure. He only knew that this Liu Hong was not only incredibly ambitious but also audacious enough to defy heaven itself.","Throughout history, many have been obsessed with power, but most limit themselves to forming factions for personal gain and wooing the great Noble Families.","But those like Liu Hong, who secretly colluded with foreign enemies, were exceedingly rare—and utterly ruthless.","No wonder that after discovering Liu Taofang’s affair with Lin Huai’an, he was determined to eliminate the latter, disregarding his status with the Ji State Trading Company.","No wonder that upon learning of Liu Taoyao’s encounter last night, which threatened to expose his dealings with Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race, his first move was to deal with the barbarian slave, Lv Jiunan, and the others.","’If a man like Liu Hong isn’t dealt with in a single, decisive blow, he will only become a massive problem later.’","With these thoughts, Chen Yi made his decision.","He lowered the curtain, rose to his feet, and headed out.","Pei Guanli saw him move and was about to follow, but then she heard Chen Yi speak.","\"You stay here. Keep an eye on our surroundings.\"","\"If anyone approaches, use this to knock them out.\"","Chen Yi tossed her a bottle of Immortal Drunk, pulled his cloak tighter around himself, and moved silently toward the residence.","Pei Guanli glanced at the bottle in her hand, then peered out at Chen Yi through a crack in the carriage wall. Beneath her mask, her lips formed a pout.","’Didn’t you say you were bringing me here to watch a show?’","’What show?’","Her Cultivation was too low. Even when she infused her ears with True Essence, it was nearly impossible to hear the conversation between Asutai and the others over the din of the rain and through the sound-proofed room inside the residence.","It wasn’t Chen Yi’s fault, really.","Chen Yi, of course, paid no mind to the Tiger Girl’s mutterings as he arrived silently at the residence.","Once he had confirmed the locations of everyone inside, he executed the Meteor Butterfly Step without hesitation.","His Great Success Martial Arts·Step drew upon the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, pushing the speed of his Body Technique to its absolute limit.","Barely more than a blurred afterimage, he first swept past the Guards stationed around the perimeter.","Before they could react, Chen Yi landed a lightning-fast knife-hand strike precisely on the back of each of their necks.","Next, Chen Yi took out a bottle of Immortal Drunk, uncorked it, and held it under each of their noses for a moment.","Once he was certain the eight gray-clad men on the perimeter were deeply unconscious, he sauntered into the main hall of the inner residence.","He made a beeline for the western side-room.","The two Martial Artists guarding the door were startled to see him suddenly appear, and both froze for an instant.","\"Who... who are you?!\"","\"Boss, we have an intruder!\"","The two shouted their questions while alerting the people in the chamber below, then drew their blades and charged.","With a slight flicker of his body, Chen Yi was already moving to meet them.","He swept past them like a gentle breeze.","The two Seventh-Grade Martial Artists collapsed to the floor.","Using his Qi Observation Skill, Chen Yi had already ascertained their Cultivation levels. Most of them were in the Lower Three Grades Realm.","They were no cause for concern.","But as his gaze fell upon the entrance to the quiet chamber within, a hint of surprise flashed in his eyes.","’Lower Fifth Grade?’","To think Liu Hong had an expert of this caliber in his service."]},{"number":386,"title":"Chapter 386 - 248: Strike the Mountain to Frighten the Tiger","paragraphs":["He waited a moment.","Seeing that the people below weren’t moving, even Asutai, who had been roaring incessantly before, had gone silent, Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle.","\"Not coming out?\"","With that, he held the Immortal Drunk under the nose of the person lying on the ground, as was his custom, before tossing it directly into the quiet room.","CRASH.","The medicine vial shattered.","The man who had spoken earlier cried out, \"Careful, it’s poison!\" and reminded those around him to cover their noses and mouths.","However, Immortal Drunk was not something that ordinary Martial Artists like them could resist.","After waiting for about ten breaths, when there was no longer any movement inside, Chen Yi finally slipped in.","Inside the small, wooden quiet room, the bodies of several barbarian slaves lay scattered about.","There were also three masked Martial Artists in gray clothes.","One of them was guarding the stairwell. Judging by his aura, he was likely the Fifth Grade Realm expert who had spoken earlier.","The other two lay beside a young barbarian boy.","Chen Yi scanned the room, his gaze falling on the corpses of the barbarian slaves. He confirmed they were the ones who had attacked the East Market Grain Store’s warehouse earlier.","Without hesitation, he moved forward, hoisted the young barbarian slave onto his shoulder, and started to walk out.","But when he reached the stairwell, he thought for a moment and decided to take the Fifth Grade Realm Martial Artist with him as well.","’A man of his cultivation level acting so arrogantly... he probably knows a few things about Liu Hong. He might have some value after all.’","Chen Yi went outside the residence. After confirming that no one was watching, he returned to the carriage and stuffed the two men inside.","Pei Guanli looked suspiciously from one to the other. \"Bro— *cough cough*, Milord, who are these two?\"","\"Bargaining chips.\"","Chen Yi said as he settled into the carriage, clapping Zhang Dabao on the shoulder and giving an order:","\"I recall we found another residence near the East Market?\"","\"Let’s go there first.\"","Zhang Dabao acknowledged the order and drove the carriage along the quiet alley, turning onto the bustling Chuandong Street.","Inside the carriage.","Pei Guanli asked, confused, \"Brother-in-law, what bargaining chips?\"","Chen Yi lifted a corner of the curtain and looked out the window, replying casually, \"The kind of bargaining chips that can make someone very uncomfortable.\"","He had already decided to throw the situation in Shu State into chaos, so he could get a clearer picture of Liu Hong, the Ji State Trading Company, and the others.","Who would have thought that before he could even make a move to manipulate the grain prices, Liu Hong would deliver such a grand gift right to him.","This way, he could advance his plans.","And the results would be better and faster than he had originally anticipated.","Seeing how vague he was being, Pei Guanli didn’t get annoyed. Instead, she just poked the young barbarian slave beside her intermittently.","\"How can one barbarian make someone uncomfortable?\"","Chen Yi smiled but didn’t explain further. He only said, \"Don’t worry. I’ll make sure you enjoy this show.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Brother-in-law, I knew you were the best to me.\"","\"Once my cultivation has a breakthrough, I’ll definitely be able to help you.\"","\"You? It would be enough if you just didn’t cause me any trouble.\"","\"Hey, Brother-in-law, how can you say that...\"","Despite his words, Pei Guanli was still delighted inside.","Ever since the Mid-Autumn Poetry Festival, she had decided she would follow Chen Yi for the rest of her life.","That was why she had been cultivating so diligently these days.","She hoped that one day, she would be able to help Chen Yi, instead of just hiding and watching from a distance like that night, completely useless.","「Not long after.」","The carriage pulled into a residence in the northern part of the East Market.","It wasn’t large, just a two-courtyard residence.","However, being located on the eastern bank of Quchi, the scenery was quite pleasant.","Chen Yi stepped out of the carriage, surveying the residence’s layout while listening intently for any sounds from the surroundings.","Once he was certain the neighbors hadn’t noticed anything, he carried the two captives from the carriage into the main hall.","As he walked, he instructed Zhang Dabao, \"Later, have Wang Ji buy some Iron Yin Wood and send it to the residence on Chuansi Street. Set up a quiet room there.\"","\"Remember, this is not something to be left to others. How about... letting those Guards from the Celestial Sect handle it?\"","Zhang Dabao understood and replied, \"The Shopkeeper has mentioned a few of them over the past few days. He said they’ve been quite dedicated since arriving at Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"Then let them do it.\"","\"As for who will guard this place...\"","Hearing Chen Yi, Pei Guanli, who was standing nearby, immediately raised her hand. \"Me! Me! I can guard this place!\"","Chen Yi looked at her with some surprise. \"Are you sure?\"","Pei Guanli grinned. \"Don’t worry, I promise there won’t be any problems.\"","Seeing her puff out her chest and guarantee it, Chen Yi thought for a moment, then nodded and warned her:","\"You can stay here and guard them, but you absolutely cannot be careless and let them escape.\"","\"Mhm, mhm.\"","\"And you can’t let them die, either.\"","\"Mhm, mhm.\"","\"You... Never mind.\"","The Tiger Girl’s past \"achievements\" were too stunning for Chen Yi to feel at ease.","So, he took matters into his own hands, directly shattering the Fifth Grade Realm Martial Artist’s three Seas of Qi.","He then used the \"Controlling Needle with Qi\" technique to shred all the meridians in the man’s body, crippling his cultivation.","But Chen Yi still didn’t feel it was secure enough. Finally, under Pei Guanli’s astonished gaze, he broke the man’s four limbs.","After doing all this, he didn’t forget to explain to Pei Guanli, \"This man’s cultivation is at the Fifth Grade. He’s very strong.\"","Pei Guanli wanted to say that she had treasures on her to help, but seeing that Chen Yi had already crippled the man, she could only nod and say with a pout:","\"Milord, are you at ease now?\"","Chen Yi paused, then said teasingly, \"Still not at ease.\"","\"Hey, you...\"","After a bit of banter, Chen Yi had Zhang Dabao find some rope and tie the two men up. He then instructed Pei Guanli:","\"You watch them here. I’ll have Dabao send over some food and drink.\"","\"Just leave it to me, I promise there won’t be any problems at all.\"","Pei Guanli nodded repeatedly, making the bell on her neck jingle."]},{"number":387,"title":"Chapter 387 - 248: Beating the Mountain to Frighten the Tiger","paragraphs":["At this point, Chen Yi had no choice but to trust her this one time.","After a few words of instruction, he had Zhang Dabao drive him to the Imprisonment Department on South Street.","He sat upright in the carriage and took off the black iron mask, a smile touching his lips as he watched the light rain outside.","’This move—knocking on the mountain to scare the tiger—I hope Lord Liu is satisfied...’","...","「An hour later.」","Fang Hongxiu received a letter and hurriedly led her people to a residence in Pingyao Lane in the East Market.","She looked at the unconscious Martial Artists inside and the dead barbarian slave in the secluded room, a thoughtful expression on her face.","She then summoned an Imprisonment Officer and asked, \"Did you get a clear look at the person who delivered the letter?\"","The Imprisonment Officer shook his head. \"Forgive me, Lord Hundred Households. I only saw the letter, not who delivered it.\"","Fang Hongxiu was a little disappointed.","Although she knew it was the work of \"Liu Wu,\" and that the two of them were currently cooperating, she still wanted to find out his true identity.","Unfortunately, Liu Wu was far too cautious.","With this in mind, Fang Hongxiu commanded, \"Take them all back to the Imprisonment Department’s Inner Prison.\"","\"Also, find some Physicians. Have them woken up as soon as possible. I will interrogate them myself.\"","\"Yes!\"","「Meanwhile, at the Governor’s Office.」","Dressed in a red Official Robe, Liu Hong sat at his desk, writing a memorial to the throne.","As his brush moved, the characters in Wei Qing’s Style were upright and orderly, each stroke penetrating the paper with force.","The summer grain tax for Shu State totals 3.3 million shi and will soon be dispatched to the Capital Prefecture; with the Annual Examination approaching, the scholars throughout the state...","As he was writing, a man hurried in from outside. \"My Lord!\"","Liu Hong furrowed his brow slightly and looked at the newcomer. \"Shichang, what has you so flustered?\"","The man was Zhao Shichang. Without hesitation, he leaned closer and whispered, \"My Lord, something has happened!\"","\"The residence in Pingyao Lane... the Imprisonment Department found it somehow.\"","\"If they found it, they found it. They were meant to be sent to the Government Office anyway...\"","Before he could finish, Liu Hong froze. He turned to face him, his tone serious. \"What about our ’distinguished guest’?\"","Zhao Shichang replied in a low voice, \"He... is gone.\"","\"And... and not only did the men from the Imprisonment Department find the bodies of the barbarian slaves, they also... also...\"","\"Also what?\"","\"They also captured our men.\"","After a pause, he hastily added, \"Fortunately, for some reason, they’re all unconscious, so the Imprisonment Department can’t interrogate them for now.\"","Upon hearing this, Liu Hong’s expression changed dramatically, his eyes flickering with uncertainty.","Scared into silence, Zhao Shichang took a few steps back, not daring to even breathe.","A long silence fell.","Liu Hong put down his brush, leaned back in his chair, and rubbed the bridge of his nose. He asked:","\"The Imprisonment Department captured them, so they should have been taken straight to the Inner Prison.\"","\"Find a way to silence them permanently.\"","Zhao Shichang bowed and replied, \"My Lord, before I came, I had already instructed our people to find an opportunity to act, but... but...\"","\"What else is there?!\"","Liu Hong’s voice was seething with rage.","A bitter smile appeared on Zhao Shichang’s face as he continued, \"Besides Asutai, Zeng Zhifeng is... is also missing.\"","Liu Hong could no longer contain his anger. He slammed his hand on the table and demanded in a low, dangerous voice, \"Are you saying he betrayed me?!\"","\"It’s... it’s not impossible.\"","\"According to the Imprisonment Department, aside from the corpses of the barbarian slaves, all the other Guards were just poisoned and unconscious.\"","\"Good. Very good!\"","\"You, go and inform the boss at once! Have him tell those two—I want them found, dead or alive!\"","Zhao Shichang naturally understood he was talking about Lv Jiunan and Ge Muxiao.","After a moment’s hesitation, he bowed and departed quickly.","Long after he had gone, Liu Hong sat in silence before finally letting out a long breath.","He stared at the memorial on his desk, his eyes as cold as ice.","’Someone definitely betrayed me, but it wasn’t necessarily Zeng Zhifeng. It could be someone else...’","’No matter who it is, anyone who dares to ruin my plans will meet the same end!’","’Death!’"]},{"number":388,"title":"Chapter 388 - 249: You are Lv Jiunan?","paragraphs":["Chen Yi had a good idea of how Liu Hong would react.","If he were in Liu Hong’s shoes and learned that Asutai had vanished, he too would do everything he could to find him.","He might even turn the entire Shu State Prefecture City upside down.","And yet, this was exactly what Chen Yi hoped to see.","The more chaotic the situation became, the clearer he could see, and in turn, seize benefits for the Xiao Family.","As for Liu Hong’s Fifth Grade Realm subordinate, Chen Yi hadn’t given him much thought. He couldn’t be bothered to plant false clues to make Liu Hong suspect his own men of betrayal.","’Strike the mountain to startle the tiger, and in doing so, probe for the truth.’","’Only by staying hidden in the shadows can I find the evidence of Liu Hong’s treason.’","While Chen Yi mulled this over, he arrived at the West Market.","To avoid drawing attention, he didn’t make an appearance at Hundred Herbs Hall.","He simply had Zhang Dabao switch to a more ordinary carriage and drive him through the West Market, straight toward Heiyu Lane in its deeper recesses.","The sky was dim, and the rain was starting to fall harder.","Rain lashed down, drumming a ceaseless PATTER against the roof tiles and flagstone roads.","Yet the West Market was still bustling with pedestrians.","Shop attendants stood under the eaves on both sides of the street, calling out greetings and respectfully welcoming customers.","Inside, a handful of customers browsed, pausing to inspect the wares and occasionally ask a question.","Hundred Herbs Hall and Yunqing Building, located near the entrance of the West Market, were doing even better business than usual.","The crowd was a mix of wealthy gentry, rich merchants, young masters and ladies from noble families, and common folk, their chatter and laughter rising and falling in waves.","No one was sure who thought of it first.","Yunqing Building, which had only recently opened, had also started selling tea drinks from Hundred Herbs Hall.","Almost every other day, the Yunqing Building’s steward would purchase ten cartloads of tea from Hundred Herbs Hall.","While they didn’t get the fifty percent profit share that the Xiao Family Medicine Hall did, even selling the tea at cost helped draw customers to Yunqing Building.","At the very least, it saved people the time they would have spent waiting in line outside Hundred Herbs Hall.","It proved to be just as much of a draw for customers as Yunqing Building’s signature Lang Wine.","This was something even Chen Yi hadn’t anticipated.","He had originally planned to wait until Hundred Herbs Hall was established across Shu State, then absorb other medicine halls before opening new sales channels in restaurants, Qin Buildings, and the like.","He never expected Cui Qingwu to figure it out on her own and implement the idea first.","Watching the bustling scene at Yunqing Building from his window and hearing Huan’er’s calls from within, the corners of Chen Yi’s mouth curled up slightly.","He could imagine other restaurants in the Prefecture City following suit in the future.","It was a pleasant surprise.","After the carriage had traveled a bit further, he lifted the curtain on the other side, his gaze sweeping over a tailor shop.","Aside from the shopkeeper, whom he had confirmed to be an Iron Banner Officer of the Hidden Guard, he focused more on a slightly older attendant.","The attendant had plain features and a tall, thin frame. Dressed in simple linen, he didn’t stand out at first glance as he welcomed and saw off customers like the others.","But upon closer inspection, Chen Yi could easily spot something off about him.","His deep-set eyes were mostly scanning the passing pedestrians and carriages, and though his movements were nimble, he was sometimes out of sync with the other attendants.","Clearly, the man’s mind wasn’t on the business of tailoring.","Chen Yi studied him for a moment, and the light of his Qi Observation Skill flickered.","Once he got a clear look at the man’s aura, he calmly closed the curtain, a flicker of apprehension on his face.","’A General... Upper Three Grades Cultivation...’","’His aura is even more potent than Xiao Jinghong’s. He’s at least at the Upper Third Grade.’","Chen Yi recalled eavesdropping on the conversation between the General and Lou Yuxue at A Wonton Shop a few days prior, and a thin sheen of sweat broke out on his back.","Fortunately, he had the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, bolstered by his Martial Arts·Body at the Great Success Realm.","Otherwise, at such a close distance, the General would have surely detected him.","Just then, the General, clad in his linen clothes, glanced at Chen Yi’s carriage for a moment before looking away.","A mere Fifth Grade Realm Martial Artist wasn’t worth his attention.","After observing for a moment, the General looked toward Yunqing Building. His expression was unchanged, but a hint of displeasure flashed in his eyes.","He was clearly thinking about his meeting the previous night with the Simurgh Phoenix, Cui Qingwu.","He had originally arranged the meeting with Cui Qingwu to discern the young lady’s purpose for coming to Shu State.","He also meant to use the opportunity to issue a warning.","But to his surprise, Cui Qingwu had the temper of a spoiled aristocrat and showed him, a Golden Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard, absolutely no respect.","Her every other word was dripping with sarcasm, and she nearly drove him mad with anger.","If she hadn’t come from the Qinghe Cui Family—with its Patriarch, Cui Mao, being one of the Nine Ministers of the Great Wei Dynasty—the General would have already given her a personal lesson on the rules of the White Tiger Guard.","’Hmph. I’d like to see what you’re really up to in Shu State.’","’If you dare interfere with the Pavilion Master’s plans, I’ll make sure you never leave this place alive, even if Cui Mao himself is protecting you!’","With these thoughts, the General retracted his gaze. He scanned the area once more, then leaned over to the Shopkeeper and whispered:","\"Any word from the Lady Tiger?\"","\"Not yet.\"","\"Send word for her to speed things up.\"","\"I don’t have much time left in Shu State. The Guangyuan Fu Family has been making moves lately; I suspect they intend to help the Xiao Family.\"","\"Yes...\"","...","「Deep in the West Market, Heiyu Lane.」","The place lived up to its name—the word ’black’ seemed to define the houses and roads.","Dilapidated black courtyard walls were choked with vines. Rain washed over the muddy roads, yet it was still difficult to see the flagstones beneath.","It looked like an old alley abandoned for a century; everything the eye could see was a scene of ruin.","Even the people who lived here were mostly dressed in black, some in coarse linen, others in fine brocade.","The only difference was in the newness of their clothes.","Those in tattered garments were mostly gaunt beggars, young and old alike, each clutching a broken bowl as they huddled under the eaves, staring blankly at passersby."]},{"number":389,"title":"Chapter 389 - 249: You’re Lv Jiunan?","paragraphs":["Those with newer clothes were mostly brawny Wandering Martial Artists.","They wore bamboo hats and carried weapons at their waists. Their expressions, as they glanced around, were grim and cruel, completely blank, or fixed in humorless smiles.","The looks varied, but all of them exuded a savage aura.","Yet Liu Lang blended in among them without looking out of place in the slightest.","On the contrary, he seemed to be in his element, squatting on the wall of a dilapidated posthouse with a smile, sizing up the passersby.","Whenever he made eye contact with someone who caught his fancy, he would grin and call out a greeting.","Of course, it wasn’t idle pleasantries like, \"Have you eaten?\" but rather phrases from the Jianghu’s secret vernacular.","For instance, upon seeing beggars, he would ask, \"Struck any gold today?\" which meant, \"Did you get anything valuable or have a full meal?\"","Or when he saw other Wandering Martial Artists, he would ask, \"Mountain, deity, or demon?\" to determine their allegiance.","Bandits occupied mountains as their strongholds, deities upheld justice, and demons were utterly vicious.","Those who roamed the Jianghu could generally be divided into these three categories.","It was a piece of slang that could be used just about anywhere.","This was all thanks to the Bright Moon Building.","If not for the Bright Moon Building’s years of influence, the various characters of the Jianghu would likely still be using the old ways.","Of course, Liu Lang was only doing this as a smokescreen.","Whether he was walking and talking or looking up at the overcast, rainy sky, his entire focus was on the residence three li away.","After getting the news from Liu Hong last night, he had switched targets and followed Liu Taoyao as she wandered through the city.","The night before, after learning from Chen Yi about his attitude toward Liu Hong, Liu Lang naturally understood that the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall was very concerned with Liu Hong’s movements.","Therefore, this time, without needing to be told, he had followed Liu Taoyao here.","He tailed her until he saw her enter that very residence.","Fortunately, in the meantime, he had stopped by Hundred Herbs Hall to send a message to his boss and learned from Zhang Dabao about the people from Poshisu Country, which was why he hadn’t gone any closer to the residence.","’The Black Magic Masters of Poshisu Country... their Martial Arts Cultivation and Techniques are similar to the Witchcraft and Gu Dao of the Mountain Race.’","’Their elusive Black Magic, in particular, allows a Black Magic Master to investigate their surroundings from a great distance. I must be on guard.’","Liu Lang had roamed the Jianghu for years and met all sorts of Wandering Martial Artists. Naturally, he had also encountered Black Magic Masters from Poshisu Country.","Furthermore, back when he followed his master, Sword Ghost, he had heard many strange tales from Jianghu seniors. He knew far more about the Jianghu People of Poshisu Country than Chen Yi did.","He knew exactly how to handle them.","At this moment, however, Liu Lang didn’t know the level of Lv Jiunan’s Cultivation inside that residence.","To be cautious, he was monitoring from three li away to avoid being detected by the Black Magic Master.","Liu Lang tilted up his bamboo hat slightly, watching the falling rain. ’I wonder if the boss has gotten my message yet.’","’Considering the time, he should have by now.’","Just as Liu Lang was thinking this, the sound of carriage wheels reached his ears.","He followed the sound with his eyes and saw a black carriage speeding over from the distance, heading straight for the residence.","He hesitated for a moment, wondering, ’Who could this be?’ and involuntarily moved a little closer.","But just as he got within about a hundred meters, he froze, his gaze shifting toward a nearby haystack.","There, beneath the rain-soaked haystack, a dilapidated black Wooden Man was staring at him silently.","Its gemstone-inlaid eyes glowed with an eerie red light in the gloomy weather.","Liu Lang cursed under his breath as his hand gripped the hilt of his blade. ’I’ve been discovered!’","He had been so careful, so exceedingly careful.","He never imagined that just by getting a hundred meters closer, he would be detected by the Black Magic set by that Lv Jiunan from Poshisu Country.","Before he could think any further, a sound like a baby’s cry reached his ears.","Then he saw the Wooden Man, only a foot tall, suddenly charge toward him.","Its limbs looked crude, but its speed was anything but slow.","As it charged, it flung several Silver Needles from its hands.","Seeing this, Liu Lang sneered. ’A mere wooden Black Magic puppet thinks it can kill me?’","With this thought, he advanced instead of retreating.","The long blade at his waist flew from its scabbard, slashing straight at the Wooden Man.","SHING—","Where the flash of the blade fell, there was a crisp sound, and the Wooden Man was sliced in two.","But before he could dodge away, the two halves of the Wooden Man exploded in a cloud of black mist.","He didn’t know what the mist was, but as soon as it spread, it began to corrode everything around it.","Amidst wisps of acrid green smoke, the crumbling walls, the haystack, and everything else were corroded into nothing.","Liu Lang cursed under his breath again, frowning as he retreated several zhang to avoid touching the mist.","’Master was right,’ he thought. ’This Black Magic has a strange name, but at its core, it’s just the Cultivation Technique and methods of the Evil Demonic Dao.’","’You can just think of them as a lesser form of Witchcraft practitioners or Poison Masters.’","Liu Lang looked toward the residence three li away. Seeing that the carriage had already driven inside, he thought for a moment and then moved closer.","Since he’d already been discovered by the people there, not going to say hello was against his nature.","He had only closed the distance by half a li when a furious roar echoed in his ears.","It was accompanied by a fierce gale that shot toward him from behind and to the side.","\"Die!\"","Hearing this word, Liu Lang scoffed as his Great Success Sword Intent erupted from his body.","The Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism surged toward him like a tide, instantly suppressing his opponent’s ferocious Fist Intent.","Only then did he slash his blade backward.","A dazzling light cut through the gloom.","CLANG!","This time, however, it wasn’t as smooth as before. His blade was blocked by immense force.","Liu Lang planted his feet and turned his head to look.","He saw a tall figure in a black robe, holding a short axe in each hand, crossed to block his blade.","The man wore no bamboo hat. He had short, slightly curly brown hair, red eyes, and a scar on the tip of his nose.","Combined with his vicious expression, his whole face looked even more ferocious.","It was none other than Ge Muxiao, from Poshisu Country, Under the Peacock Banner.","Liu Lang, of course, didn’t recognize him. \"Someone from Poshisu Country?\" he asked.","\"Just a Boxer, and your Fist Intent has only reached Minor Success. You dare to block my path?\"","Ge Muxiao glared at him and growled in a stiff tone, \"And who are you? How dare you spy on us?!\"","Liu Lang gave him a half-smile. \"This is Shu State of Great Wei, not your Poshisu Country. What’s wrong with me being here?\"","With a slight exertion of force, he used his long blade to push Ge Muxiao back completely.","Then, without hesitation, he lunged forward. \"You, on the other hand... who gave you the guts to ambush me?\"","As he spoke, Liu Lang had already unleashed two slashes.","One a downward chop, the other a horizontal sweep.","There was nothing fancy about them—it was pure overwhelming force.","But in Ge Muxiao’s eyes, it was an onslaught of blinding light from the blade.","Even though he defended with all his might, spinning his two short axes so fast that not even a drop of water could get through, he still couldn’t block it.","When he parried the first slash, one of his short axes was sent flying, embedding itself in a nearby courtyard wall with a THWACK.","After the second slash, a wound so deep the bone was visible appeared on his waist.","But as searing pain shot through him, Ge Muxiao only became more ferocious.","He recklessly lunged at Liu Lang, gripping his remaining short axe with both hands and swinging it wildly.","At the same time, he didn’t forget to roar to someone in the distance in the Poshisu language, \"Big Brother, be careful! This person is strong!\"","While dodging his attacks, Liu Lang kept an eye on the activity at the residence.","When he saw the carriage that had entered earlier quickly driving out, he lost the desire to play around.","He poured True Essence into his hands and, empowered by his tyrannical Sword Intent, executed an upward diagonal slash that shone like a bolt of silk.","It gave Ge Muxiao no chance to react, splitting the short axe in two.","The blade’s light continued unimpeded, carving another gash in his body.","Blood sprayed out, dyeing half of Ge Muxiao’s body red.","Just as Liu Lang was about to speak, he detected a piercing sonic boom coming from the distance.","He frowned slightly and instinctively leaped sideways.","THUNK!","After the sharp sound, a foot-long dagger was seen embedded in the wall behind him.","\"You’re courting death!\" a sinister voice followed.","Liu Lang turned his head and saw another person from Poshisu Country standing on the roof of the distant residence, watching him from afar.","’He’s not weak at all.’","’To have this much power from two li away... his Cultivation must be a bit higher than mine.’","Thinking this, Liu Lang shouldered his long blade and asked with a smile, \"You must be Lv Jiunan? The Black Magic Master from Poshisu Country?\"","\"That Wooden Man that ambushed me earlier was yours, right?\"","Lv Jiunan snorted coldly. \"Who are you?\"","\"Since you know my name, you should know the consequences of provoking me!\"","\"Oh? Do tell. What consequences will I face?\""]},{"number":390,"title":"Chapter 390 - 250: Liu Lang, Don’t Be Reckless","paragraphs":["Liu Lang raised an eyebrow slightly. \"What is it?\"","\"Am I supposed to be honored that you know my name?\"","\"Or do you have some special status in Poshisu Country that makes everyone bow down to you?\"","He scoffed as soon as the words left his mouth. \"I am the ’Sword Madman.’ I wander the Jianghu relying on the long blade in my hand, not some fancy title that’s supposed to scare me.\"","Lv Jiunan’s furious expression froze. He sized Liu Lang up and down before suddenly asking:","\"Last night... that wasn’t you?\"","Even Ge Muxiao, bleeding profusely from two blade wounds, recalled for a moment before clutching his injuries and saying through gritted teeth:","\"Big Brother, the person in the Spring Rain Building last night... it wasn’t him!\"","\"That ’Sword Madman’s’ Saber Dao was far sharper!\"","Liu Lang paused, looking back and forth at their expressions. The name Spring Rain Building echoed in his mind.","He suddenly realized what was happening. He guessed that his boss must have run into them last night.","He immediately stabbed his blade into the ground and grinned. \"You must be talking about Liu Lang, the ’Northern Desert Sword Madman,’ right?\"","\"I am the ’Shu State Sword Madman.’\"","Hearing this, Lv Jiunan’s eyes turned sinister.","He naturally didn’t believe such a clumsy and transparent lie.","If the person at the Spring Rain Building last night wasn’t the \"Sword Madman\" Liu Lang, then there was only one other possibility.","—Liu Wu!","But when Lv Jiunan considered this, his heart grew even heavier.","He suddenly realized that if the person at the Spring Rain Building was really Liu Wu, then this Liu Wu was terrifying.","’A young Wandering Martial Artist who has reached the Perfection Realm in Spear Dao and Great Success in Saber Dao... his talent alone is the greatest threat.’","’What’s more, he followed Ge Muxiao and me from the Spring Rain Building to Quchi. He must have overheard my conversation with Liu Taoyao and the others.’","At this thought, Lv Jiunan’s expression became even more sinister and cold.","He looked at Liu Lang and said, \"No wonder you’re here. Did he send you to watch us?\"","Liu Lang continued to play dumb. \"He? Who’s he?\"","\"I, the ’Shu State Sword Madman,’ have no idea what you’re talking about.\"","\"Hmph! Your denials are useless!\"","\"That Liu Wu’s appearance last night was suspicious, and he almost fooled us. After I deal with you, I’ll go find him myself!\"","After speaking, Lv Jiunan no longer hesitated and leaped into the air.","On the other side, Ge Muxiao seized the opportunity to pick up his short axe and charged at Liu Lang as well.","A surge of Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism instantly blew away the surrounding rain.","Seeing this, Liu Lang gave a wry, silent laugh.","’Boss, oh Boss, you used my identity to meet them last night, why didn’t you give me a heads-up?’","’Well, great. The cat’s out of the bag.’","He was surprisingly nonchalant.","Facing the combined attack of Lv Jiunan, whose Cultivation was a major Realm above his own, and the injured Ge Muxiao, he wasn’t flustered at all. Instead, he was worried about messing up Chen Yi’s plans.","’It’s come to this... I hope this doesn’t affect the boss.’","Liu Lang took a deep breath, his eyes fixed on the approaching Lv Jiunan, a hint of an excited smile on his face.","He remained motionless, then unleashed a horizontal slash.","The Sword Intent, sharp as the wind, directly intercepted Ge Muxiao, halting his attack.","The wind from the blade flew past, carving a ten-foot-long gash into the stone-paved road.","\"You’re too weak. Just stand there and watch, unless you want me to kill you with a single strike.\"","Before his voice had even faded, Liu Lang didn’t even glance at Ge Muxiao, heading straight for Lv Jiunan.","\"A Black Magic Master from Poshisu Country... This is my first time meeting one. Don’t disappoint me!\"","Ge Muxiao stared at his back, his face flushing red and pale with rage. He roared and charged forward heedlessly.","\"You... Wei Dog! You’re courting death!\"","Liu Lang glanced sideways, a mocking sneer flashing across his face.","\"All bark and no bite.\"","As he spoke, he pivoted, his long blade tracing a semicircle before he slashed out again.","This time, he didn’t hold back.","After the slash, his body flickered, and he closed in on Ge Muxiao at an even faster speed.","He gripped the hilt with both hands—one in a forward grip, one in a reverse—and before Ge Muxiao could even dodge, he unleashed another heavy, powerful slash.","Perhaps provoked by his earlier words, Ge Muxiao advanced instead of retreating, meeting the attack head-on with his short axe, using all his strength.","A silver-white, cold light instantly gleamed on the axe’s edge.","The next moment.","CLANG!","The axe and the long blade met with a deafening roar.","A flash of light from the blade erupted. It shattered the axe’s edge and, at the same time, sliced diagonally across Ge Muxiao’s shoulder, severing his left arm completely.","CLATTER.","The short axe fell to the ground, still clutched in the severed arm. Ge Muxiao’s eyes widened in fury, and he looked ready to go berserk.","\"How dare you—\"","Liu Lang curled his lip slightly, as if dissatisfied with his strike.","\"The fact that strike didn’t kill you means you have some skill after all.\"","\"But...\"","Before he could finish, Lv Jiunan flew over. He completely ignored the severely injured Ge Muxiao; his eyes were fixed only on Liu Lang.","The moment he got close, he flung two daggers from each hand.","WHOOSH! They cut through the air.","Liu Lang immediately abandoned Ge Muxiao, sidestepping two of the daggers and batting the other two away with his long blade.","\"Nice one!\"","Liu Lang shouted at Lv Jiunan, who was a hundred feet away, and charged forward with his blade raised.","He poured his True Essence into his hands.","He drew upon Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, gathering it around his body and infusing it into his long blade.","A radiant glow appeared, so intense it vaporized the surrounding rain into steam.","Seeing this, Lv Jiunan’s expression remained unchanged. With a flick of his wrists, several Wooden Men fell from his sleeves.","Before they even hit the ground, the Wooden Men charged at Liu Lang.","Behind the Wooden Men, Lv Jiunan’s hands kept moving. He flicked his fingers, sending several cloth dolls flying out.","—They were stitched together from burlap, and one could faintly see the dry straw inside, along with the Silver Needles pinned to their foreheads.","The moment the dolls appeared, they exploded, transforming into life-sized scarecrows propped up straight on wooden sticks.","Only then did Lv Jiunan press his palms together.","CLAP."]},{"number":391,"title":"Chapter 391 - 250: Liu Lang, Don’t Make Waves","paragraphs":["Dozens, even hundreds, of fine threads erupted from the arms of several straw men. They shot past the Wooden Men and coiled toward Liu Lang.","The ceaseless whistling of them tearing through the air filled his ears.","Just as Liu Lang was about to sever the threads, a foul stench suddenly assaulted his nostrils.","’Not good,’ he thought, his body flashing backward in a sudden retreat.","As he passed Ge Muxiao, he didn’t hesitate to kick him flying to block the attack.","\"You!?\"","Ge Muxiao had no time to curse. A look of terror spread across his face as he watched the hair-thin threads rush toward him.","\"No, Brother, you, you...\"","But Lv Jiunan’s cold gaze remained fixed on Liu Lang, showing no intention of stopping.","In the blink of an eye, the threads pierced through Ge Muxiao’s body.","The terror on Ge Muxiao’s face froze. He stared blankly at Lv Jiunan.","\"Brother...\"","Before the word left his lips, his body was torn to pieces, collapsing in a heap on the ground. The rain washed his blood across the alley, staining it red.","Not only that, but wisps of black smoke began to rise from the chunks of flesh.","They dissolved into a pool of pus at a speed visible to the naked eye.","Liu Lang glanced over and couldn’t help but curse, \"Dammit! You even kill your own men. Are you even human?\"","Cursing was one thing, but he didn’t dare slow his feet for a second.","If the threads were merely sharp, he could have handled them with his Swordsmanship.","But that Black Magic Master from Poshisu Country had coated them with something lethal.","The potency of the poison was clear from Ge Muxiao’s fate.","Lv Jiunan, however, was unmoved. His clasped hands flicked rapidly, sending the threads spiraling toward Liu Lang with even greater speed.","\"You cost my Peacock Banner a Golden Lion. Your life will serve as repayment!\"","Liu Lang slashed out with his Blade, deflecting the nearest threads. \"He clearly died at your hands,\" he grumbled.","As he spoke, he scanned his surroundings, searching for a way to deal with Lv Jiunan.","But this Heiyu Lane offered no advantageous terrain, nor was there anyone who dared to step forward and help him.","Even though many Wandering Martial Artists who fancied themselves quite strong were watching nearby, their own Cultivation levels kept them from daring to make a move against Lv Jiunan.","’Boss, if you don’t get here soon, I... I’ll have to run for it.’","Liu Lang knew he was no match for Lv Jiunan, but he was confident he could escape.","Still, he was unwilling to accept it.","Leaving like this would be too humiliating.","He hadn’t even managed to land a single strike on Lv Jiunan, yet he was already tied down by those Wooden Men and straw men. It was a disgrace to his title, \"Sword Madman.\"","Lv Jiunan saw through his intentions and said coldly, \"The Sword Madman? You’re nothing special.\"","\"Are you waiting for that Liu Wu to arrive?\"","\"Don’t bother. Just tell me where he is.\"","\"After I kill you, I’ll go find him myself.\"","Liu Lang grinned, his words sharp. \"Tell you where my boss is, so you can run off and get yourself killed?\"","He was indeed no match for Lv Jiunan.","But he didn’t believe for a second that Lv Jiunan would be a match for Chen Yi.","After all, besides his Martial Arts, Chen Yi was also a Medical Saint Hand.","Even an Elder from the Five Poison Sect couldn’t kill him, so what chance did this second-rate Black Magic from Poshisu Country stand in the Jianghu of the Wei Dynasty?","\"Hmph!\"","Lv Jiunan snorted coldly. \"Then you can die first!\"","In truth, he was in a greater hurry than Liu Lang.","He wasn’t one of the Jianghu People of the Wei Dynasty; he was a horse bandit from Poshisu Country.","Fighting here was inherently risky. It could attract the attention of the City Guard Army, the Imprisonment Department, and even those so-called righteous Jianghu People from the Prefecture City.","Moreover, he was involved with the likes of Liu Hong and Lin Huai’an. If he were exposed, it would ruin the cooperation between the Peacock Banner and their partners in Shu State.","That was a consequence he was desperate to avoid.","With that thought, Lv Jiunan surged forward, bringing the straw men at his side with him.","He and the Wooden Men, along with the deadly threads, charged at Liu Lang.","For a moment, a ceaseless cacophony of whistling and roaring filled the air, reducing the already dilapidated Heiyu Lane to rubble.","The Wandering Martial Artists hiding and watching from nearby didn’t hesitate to retreat further.","\"Isn’t that the ’Sword Madman’?\"","\"I heard he went with Elder Black Tooth to the three military towns a while back. I can’t believe he’s still alive.\"","\"Maybe he’s the one who betrayed Bright Moon Building. Otherwise, with Black Tooth’s caution, how could he have fallen for Xiao Jinghong’s ambush?\"","\"Whether Liu Lang broke the rules or not is irrelevant. His opponent right now is from Poshisu Country.\"","\"If we just stand here and watch, we’ll become a laughingstock.\"","\"So what? Didn’t you see?\"","\"Even Liu Lang is no match for that Black Magic Master. What good would a bunch of stragglers like us be?\"","\"Well...\"","As the crowd murmured amongst themselves, a horse-drawn carriage appeared in the distance.","The carriage didn’t proceed far, however, stopping at the entrance to Heiyu Lane.","The driver kept his head low, his face obscured, but one could see he was old and gaunt.","Inside the carriage, Zhao Shichang, who had just departed, watched the distant battle with a slightly gloomy expression.","\"Young Master, that’s the ’Sword Madman,’ Liu Lang.\"","Liu Taoyao, who was beside him, let out a soft \"oh.\" \"Last night, didn’t that Spearman, Liu Wu, say he and Liu Lang were inseparable friends?\"","\"That is correct.\"","\"If possible, tell Lv Jiunan to spare his life.\"","Zhao Shichang looked troubled. \"Young Master, I’m afraid that’s not wise.\"","\"Lv Jiunan and Liu Lang are fighting openly. Regardless of the outcome, it will attract attention.\"","\"If you were to show yourself now, I fear...\"","Liu Taoyao understood his meaning. He thought for a moment, then shook his head. \"Then let it be.\"","He watched the distant flashes of steel and sighed in admiration.","\"The people of the Jianghu, with their powerful Martial Arts Cultivation... it’s truly something to be envied.\"","Liu Taoyao was a scholar whose experience with Martial Arts was limited to physical fitness. Seeing the display put on by Liu Lang and Lv Jiunan, he was naturally filled with envy."]},{"number":392,"title":"Chapter 392 - 250: Liu Lang, Don’t Be Reckless","paragraphs":["If his Cultivation were also in the Middle Three Grades, he would be far more accomplished than he is now.","Zhao Shichang sighed to himself upon hearing this. Thankfully, he had dissuaded the young master. If he had ruined the Master’s plans, the trouble would have been even greater.","\"Young Master, it’s best we get Lv Jiunan to leave as soon as possible.\"","\"The longer he stays here, the greater the trouble.\"","After a pause, he continued, \"Asutai and Zeng Zhifeng’s whereabouts are currently unknown. We still need Lv Jiunan to find them.\"","Liu Taoyao hummed in acknowledgment. \"Get it done.\"","Zhao Shichang breathed a sigh of relief and patted the coachman at the front, whispering, \"We’ll have to trouble you, Uncle Tianming.\"","The coachman nodded slightly, then climbed down from the carriage. Using the dim light of the overcast sky for cover, he quickly approached Liu Lang and Lv Jiunan.","As he advanced, he periodically flicked several Silver Needles from his hand.","Following a series of barely audible pops, the Wandering Martial Artists, their attention completely fixed on the battle between Liu Lang and Lv Jiunan, dropped to the ground.","Even a few beggars spying from the corners couldn’t escape the fatal Silver Needles.","In the blink of an eye, several people were dead.","Seeing this from the carriage, Zhao Shichang said in a low voice, \"Young Master, with Uncle Tianming making his move, I’m sure Lv Jiunan will be able to withdraw quickly.\"","Liu Taoyao nodded, his gaze sweeping over the fallen Wandering Martial Artists as he sighed.","\"It’s a pity Liu Tianming is so advanced in years. He’ll never be able to break through to the Third Grade Realm in this lifetime.\"","At this, he thought of Liu Wu, whom he had met the previous night, and a look of regret crossed his face.","’If Liu Wu and Liu Lang were in my service, how could my grand ambitions possibly fail?’","Zhao Shichang naturally knew what his master was thinking and chimed in, \"Them... It is indeed a pity...\"","But whether it was a pity or not was no longer important.","As long as Uncle Liu cleared away the onlookers and ensured Lv Jiunan could retreat safely, their grand plan would not be affected.","Soon, the Liu Tianming they spoke of had slain dozens of people, clearing out nearly all the bystanders.","The only one left was a Wandering Martial Artist in a black robe and bamboo hat, standing closest to Liu Lang and Lv Jiunan.","Liu Tianming tried the same trick again, flicking out two Silver Needles.","SWISH! SWISH!","Two faint whistles cut through the air in quick succession.","But to Liu Tianming’s surprise, the two Silver Needles failed to pierce the black-robed man’s body as they had the others.","Instead, the man had caught them between two fingers.","Liu Tianming sized him up, his voice low. \"You’re not weak.\"","\"But this is not a place for you to linger. If you don’t want trouble, I suggest you leave at once.\"","’He knew the commotion here had already alerted many people. The longer this dragged on, the more attention it would attract.’","That was why he didn’t want to waste time on a fight.","The black-robed man glanced sideways at him. Beneath the bamboo hat, his black iron mask gleamed faintly.","\"You’re right. It is time to leave.\"","\"You...\"","Before Liu Tianming could urge him on, the black-robed man turned his head and called out to Liu Lang and Lv Jiunan, who were fighting in the distance.","\"Sword Madman, your Blade is as dull as rust. And you had the nerve to ask me for a sparring match?\"","Liu Lang was startled by the voice and was nearly struck by the threads.","After a clumsy dodge, he looked over at the black-robed man and shouted in exasperation:","\"Boss, not only is this Black Magic Master’s Cultivation higher than mine, but he’s also covered in poison. He’s a real handful.\"","The black-robed man was none other than Chen Yi.","Hearing this, he chided with a laugh, \"If you’re weak, you’re weak. Why make excuses?\"","Liu Lang instantly gritted his teeth. He stopped dodging and turned to charge at the pursuing Lv Jiunan.","\"You said it!\"","\"If I’m unfortunate enough to fall for one of his tricks, I’ll be counting on you to save me.\"","But before he could clash with the threads, a black shadow suddenly appeared before him in a flash.","\"There’s no time for you to show off.\"","\"You go deal with that old-timer over there. This one’s mine.\"","Seeing Chen Yi step in, Liu Lang pouted. ’Could’ve said so earlier,’ he muttered, then turned and charged toward Liu Tianming.","Lv Jiunan looked at Chen Yi, his expression turning grave. His voice was heavy as he asked:","\"Who in the world are you?\"","\"Last night, you appeared at the Spring Rain Building and ruined my plans. Then you followed me. What are you after?\"","Chen Yi glanced at the threads swirling around Lv Jiunan’s body and said with a smile,","\"Why is everyone so curious about my identity?\"","\"And what difference would it make if you knew?\"","After a pause, he looked at Lv Jiunan. \"Would it help you escape with your life?\""]},{"number":393,"title":"Chapter 393 - 251: How Dare You Kill Me?","paragraphs":["In truth, Chen Yi had arrived here long ago.","It was just that when he arrived, he happened to run into Zhao Shichang, who had come to inform Lv Jiunan of something.","He’d overheard a message delivered by Zhao Shichang:","\"My lord instructed me to inform you that you must find Asutai, dead or alive.\"","However, before Lv Jiunan could reply, the Wooden Man detected Liu Lang in the distance, setting off an alarm.","Chen Yi couldn’t help but feel a bit of regret over this.","While Liu Hong was, just as he’d deduced, furious over Asutai’s disappearance, Chen Yi had wanted to hear what further arrangements Liu Hong and Lv Jiunan would make, only to be interrupted by Liu Lang.","There was nothing to be done.","Chen Yi had no choice but to first get Zhang Dabao settled, then rush back to watch the battle between Liu Lang and Lv Jiunan.","And that was what led to the current situation.","At this moment, after hearing Chen Yi’s words and glancing at Liu Lang confronting Liu Tianming, Lv Jiunan spoke in an ice-cold tone:","\"I don’t care who you are. The next time we meet, I will take your life!\"","The moment he saw Chen Yi appear, he knew he couldn’t stay here any longer.","Putting aside his own identity and his cooperation with Liu Hong and Lin Huai’an, Chen Yi’s strength alone was enough of a threat.","It didn’t matter that his own Cultivation was a major Realm higher than Chen Yi’s, or that he had cultivated his Black Magic to the Great Success Realm.","When fighting a Spearman at the Perfection Realm, such a small gap could easily be erased by the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","Lv Jiunan was keenly aware of this fact.","So, before the words had even left his mouth, he flicked his wrist, sending the Wooden Man charging toward Chen Yi.","The scarecrows, brandishing their silk threads, also gathered before him to block Chen Yi’s path.","He then turned and fled.","Watching him go, Chen Yi shook his head and chuckled. \"Thinking of leaving now? Don’t you think it’s a little late?\"","As he spoke, he reached out with his right hand and drew the Five-section Spear from his left arm.","With a light flick, the sections of the spear snapped together as one.","The moment the Long Spear was in his hand, the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism surged toward him like a tidal wave.","A terrifying power erupted from Chen Yi, blasting out in all directions.","It sent the attacking Wooden Men flying and blew the scarecrows and their silk threads into a tangled mess before him.","Feeling the immense pressure from behind, a chill shot down Lv Jiunan’s spine, and the hairs on his body stood on end.","He glanced back over his shoulder, his expression growing even more grim.","For some reason, as he looked back at Chen Yi, who still hadn’t moved from his spot, a sense of dread washed over him.","’I’ve already used my full strength to flee for a great distance,’ he thought.","’But I still feel like the moment that figure moves, I’ll be—’","’Dead!’","Lv Jiunan swallowed subconsciously. Snapping out of his daze, he gritted his teeth and pulled several items from his robes.","He threw them out indiscriminately.","With a series of CRASHES and POPS,","wisps of black smoke rose into the air within a hundred-yard radius.","The acrid smoke instantly corroded the surrounding buildings, eating pockmarks into them.","It ate through brick, tile, and metal alike.","Even so, Lv Jiunan was still terrified.","As he fled, he roared, \"Liu Wu, I’m warning you, don’t push it!\"","\"Do you have any idea who I really am?!\"","Chen Yi stared at him without blinking, completely ignoring the poisonous fog.","His Spear Dao drew upon the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism, locking firmly onto Lv Jiunan’s position.","\"Your identity? A horse bandit from Poshisu Country? Or some little Peacock under the Peacock King?\"","As he spoke, he took a single, effortless step forward.","BOOM!","Thunder cracked through the dark clouds above.","Lightning flashed.","It snaked down from the clouds in a bizarre arc, striking right where Lv Jiunan was.","Lv Jiunan seemed to sense something. He looked up, his face a mask of pure horror.","\"You... How could you...\"","Chen Yi, who had been miles away just a moment ago, had seemingly ridden the lightning bolt to appear directly in front of him.","Chen Yi regarded him with a faint, unreadable smile, ignoring his shock. He just gave his Long Spear a light swing.","——Dragon-Falling Spear: Soaring Dragon Slash!","KREEE!","A clear dragon’s cry echoed in all directions.","Along with it, a golden dragon soared from the tip of the spear, merging with the lightning in the sky.","Instantly, a dragon of gold and silver light circled twice above Chen Yi’s head before shooting straight for Lv Jiunan.","Its surging, tyrannical might completely suppressed him.","Lv Jiunan felt the pressure crushing down on him. Even with all his strength, he couldn’t move a single step. A deep chill filled his heart.","His eyes nearly bursting from their sockets, he stared at the dragon and roared, \"I am the blood brother of King Landu! A Grand General under the Peacock King! How dare you kill me?!\"","But these words only made the smile in Chen Yi’s eyes grow wider.","\"King Landu’s brother, you say? That’s even better!\"","Before he’d even finished speaking, the shimmering gold-and-silver dragon whistled through Lv Jiunan’s body.","The dragon’s phantom head turned to look back at him, its tail just emerging from his back, making it seem for an instant as if it had grown from his very body.","Then, with a deafening BOOM, it exploded.","Countless streaks of golden spear light and silver lightning shot out in all directions.","The look of fear on Lv Jiunan’s face froze. He tremblingly raised a finger to point at Chen Yi, his heart filled with the ashes of despair as he spoke:","\"You... you... will surely... die...\"","\"I... I’ll be waiting... for you... in the afterlife...\"","The moment the words left his lips, he fell backward, his breathing as faint as a silk thread.","Chen Yi flashed forward to catch his body, then glanced over at Liu Lang and Liu Tianming.","He saw that they hadn’t even started fighting yet.","Liu Lang and Liu Tianming faced each other from a distance, but both were staring in his direction.","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. Holding Lv Jiunan with one arm, he waved to Liu Lang with the other.","\"Since you’re feeling so charitable, why don’t you go ahead and retreat?\"","Liu Lang snapped out of his trance. \"Oh, right,\" he muttered, sheathing his long blade and running over.","Liu Tianming didn’t dare try to stop him. His aged face was a mask of astonishment as he stared blankly at Chen Yi."]},{"number":394,"title":"Chapter 394 - 251: How Dare You Kill Me?","paragraphs":["\"Th-this is the Perfection Realm of Martial Arts?\"","Lv Jiunan, a Fourth Grade Realm expert, couldn’t even take a single blow. Truly terrifying.","No wonder the Jianghu saying goes that while Cultivation can be improved through diligent practice, advancing in the Realm of Martial Arts Techniques depends solely on talent and comprehension.","Those without high talent would find it difficult to enter the Dao, even if they practiced until death.","It was an undeniably tyrannical principle.","Chen Yi glanced at him, then his gaze fell upon the distant carriage, a meaningful look flashing in his eyes.","He then took the arriving Liu Lang and sped away, heading out of the West City Gate.","Liu Lang suppressed the shock in his heart. Looking at the body of Lv Jiunan in Chen Yi’s grasp, he asked in bewilderment, \"Boss, why did you...\"","Chen Yi raised a hand to cut him off. \"He may be a dead man, but he was still a significant figure. We should dig a hole and bury him.\"","\"This...\"","A strange look appeared on Liu Lang’s face as he muttered, \"Since when were you so kind-hearted?\"","Chen Yi obviously heard him. He glanced sideways at Liu Lang. \"I haven’t even settled my score with you yet, and you’re already giving me grief.\"","\"I wouldn’t dare, I wouldn’t dare...\"","After a few more words of idle chatter, Chen Yi and Liu Lang charged straight past the West City Wall and vanished into the rainy night.","In the carriage.","Liu Taoyao watched all this in astonishment. He was stunned for a long time before finally turning his head to look at Zhao Shichang.","\"Lv Jiunan is dead?\"","\"What... what do we do now?\"","Zhao Shichang gave a bitter smile and shook his head. \"Young Master, I... I don’t know either.\"","After a pause, he looked at Liu Tianming, who had already returned, and continued:","\"The commotion here was too big. It’s already alerted everyone in the city.\"","\"Young Master, we should hurry back and report this to your father.\"","Liu Taoyao snapped back to his senses and nodded hastily. \"Yes, yes, we must let Father know.\"","Hearing this, Liu Tianming cracked the whip, and the carriage drove away from Heiyu Lane.","The downpour was torrential.","The RUMBLE of the carriage wheels carried far into the distance.","Liu Taoyao sat dazedly in the carriage, a panicked look on his face.","He could already imagine Liu Hong’s furious reaction upon learning of this.","He was even more worried about the news reaching Poshisu Country, reaching the ears of King Landu.","’That Lv Jiunan was King Landu’s own younger brother. For him to die here... I fear, I fear...’","’I’m afraid even Father won’t be able to explain this.’","Zhao Shichang naturally knew what the consequences would be, but it was not his place to say anything.","He had never expected that a situation that had been proceeding so smoothly would suddenly be fraught with complications.","First, Asutai had been abducted, and it was suspected to be an inside job.","Then, Lv Jiunan had been killed.","It had all caught him completely off guard.","’Right now, we can only hope the Master can resolve this matter.’","However, in Zhao Shichang’s estimation, even Liu Hong would likely be unable to give King Landu a satisfactory explanation.","If things went poorly, this incident could directly affect the cooperation between Liu Hong and King Landu.","「Not long after.」","Outside Heiyu Lane, a group of people galloped over on horseback.","The man in the lead wore black brocade robes, with a goldfish embroidered in gold thread on his chest and a long, sheathed blade at his waist.","At his side were Fang Hongxiu and a handsome young man.","It was none other than the Imprisonment Department from Shu State Prefecture City.","And behind them, a number of variously dressed Jianghu People followed along.","\"That display of power just now was truly shocking. I never thought a spearman of such strength existed here in Shu State, so far from the Central Plains.\"","\"Who could it have been?\"","\"Could it be Xiao Jinghong, the so-called ’Spear and Sword Dual Mastery’?\"","\"It wasn’t her.\"","\"I heard she left the Prefecture City before the Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","\"That’s right. General Jinghong is outside building something called the Wu Mountain Mutual Market with the Mountain Race. She shouldn’t be in the Prefecture City right now.\"","\"Then who was it?\"","\"With such astonishing spear force, he can’t possibly be a nobody in the Jianghu.\"","\"I think the man who just died shouted his name.\"","\"Liu Wu?\"","\"Who’s Liu Wu?\"","\"Probably a fake name...\"","As the various Wandering Martial Artists discussed among themselves, none could figure out the man’s identity. They could only follow the group ahead toward Heiyu Lane.","General, who had changed into a set of common linen clothes, blended into the crowd, silently observing his surroundings.","Listening to the chatter, he couldn’t help but wonder.","’Liu Wu?’","’That must be the mysterious spearman who went to Iron Wall Town with Liu Lang before.’","’But why would he kill Lv Jiunan?’","General knew Lv Jiunan. He knew that he was King Landu’s full-blooded younger brother.","Furthermore, he also knew that Liu Lang and Lv Jiunan had visited the Spring Rain Building together last night.","Lou Yuxue had reported all of this to him first thing in the morning.","But no matter how he thought about it, General couldn’t figure out a reason for \"Liu Wu\" to kill Lv Jiunan.","’Previously, Liu Wu’s actions seemed to be aimed at helping the Xiao Family. This time... could it also be because of the Xiao Family?’","After a moment of thought, General shook his head, dismissing the idea.","’Although King Landu of Poshisu Country is at odds with the Great Wei Dynasty, his attention right now is entirely on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road and the Pirate Alliance.’","’In the short term, there’s no way King Landu could meddle with the Wei Dynasty’s borders, so he has no reason to move against the Xiao Family.’","’It’s just that now, Lv Jiunan is dead, and Ge Muxiao is dead too.’","’Although there are still some horse bandits in Shu State who can contact King Landu, sending messages back and forth will inevitably waste time.’","’Furthermore, Lv Jiunan was King Landu’s brother, born of the same mother. His death here will likely cause some unpredictable changes to the situation in Shu State.’","’My fear is that King Landu, in his fury, will destroy the order that was so painstakingly established.’","’The Ancient Tea-Horse Road, the border between the Wei Dynasty and Poshisu Country, and... the Barbarian Race.’","’If King Landu sides with the Barbarian Race because of this, it would be unequivocally bad news.’","At this thought, General’s brow furrowed unconsciously.","He hadn’t expected this. After managing operations in Shu State for so many years, just as the matter entrusted to him by the Pavilion Master was about to bear fruit, something like this had to happen.","It truly displeased him.","At the same time, General was very clear about one thing: Shu State could fall into chaos, but that chaos absolutely could not be caused by the Barbarian Race."]},{"number":395,"title":"Chapter 395 - 251: How Dare You Kill Me?","paragraphs":["’If that’s the case, the Xiao Family... will have a chance to rise...’","Considering the worst-case scenario gave even the ever-confident General a headache.","\"How dare Liu Wu... interfere with the White Tiger Guard’s affairs. Hmph!\"","Not far from the General, Xiao Jing, dressed in a green robe with a bamboo hat, also followed the crowd.","He, too, had guessed that the mysterious spearman was the one who had helped the Xiao Family before.","However, he was unaware of Liu Wu’s true strength.","Now that he knew the man possessed Spear Dao at the Perfection Realm, he couldn’t help but feel a surge of secret joy.","Even without knowing the man’s true identity, he was filled with joy.","’If the Master finds out that such an expert is helping the Xiao Family, he’ll surely be very happy too.’","Lost in their own thoughts, the crowd soon reached Heiyu Lane.","Fang Hongxiu frowned as she looked at the bodies littering the ground, her gaze lingering on the emaciated beggars.","’Did Liu Wu kill all these people?’","However, after a quick scan of the area, her expression relaxed slightly.","’These people were likely killed by silver needles. This probably wasn’t Liu Wu’s doing.’","Fang Hongxiu certainly had her grievances with Liu Wu, but they had also just recently worked together.","She really didn’t want him to be such a cruel and ruthless person.","Just then, the middle-aged man in the black, fish-patterned robe standing before her spoke.","\"Hundred Households Fang, take your people and see if there are any survivors left around.\"","\"Yes, Lord Thousand Households.\"","Fang Hongxiu waved her hand and led several Imprisonment Officers to quickly investigate the surroundings.","Her heart leaped in shock when she saw the collapsed ruins in the distance.","’This is the result of Liu Wu using his full power?’","At that moment, the last trace of resentment Fang Hongxiu held for the humiliation she’d suffered at Chen Yi’s hands completely vanished.","For a powerful Wandering Martial Artist like him, just toying with them with some poison was nothing. If he had actually wanted to kill them, it probably would have taken only a single move.","At this thought, Fang Hongxiu’s gaze fell upon the distant West City Wall.","’Liu Wu... what exactly are you trying to do?’","’Are the people from Poshisu Country the problem, or is it those barbarian slaves...?’","Fang Hongxiu had no way of knowing. She only felt that Liu Wu was shrouded in a fog of mystery, impossible to see through.","While the Imprisonment Officers were investigating the area, the General, Xiao Jing, and the crowd of Wandering Martial Artists who had followed them also got a clear look at the situation.","Most of them drew in a sharp breath.","\"Seeing it from a distance already scared the hell out of me. Now that I’m seeing it up close, it’s really... it’s...\"","\"Terrifying!\"","\"Still, it’s a good thing.\"","\"Ever since the Barbarian Race army attacked Mengshui Pass five years ago, killing all the old masters in our Shu State, we haven’t produced any decent experts.\"","\"Exactly. The appearance of a Spearman at the Perfection Realm now will definitely bring some stability to the Jianghu in Shu State.\"","\"Right. The Mountain Race is strong, to be sure, but that old matriarch of theirs hardly ever gets involved in the affairs of the Jianghu.\"","The Jianghu and the Imperial Court are different.","Strength reigns supreme.","If there are no renowned masters with profound Cultivation and high Technique Realms to keep things in check, all sorts of monsters will inevitably crawl out of the woodwork.","The General listened and watched. After a moment’s thought, he silently slipped away, heading out of West City.","He was intensely curious about Liu Wu’s identity. He wouldn’t be able to eat or sleep in peace until he found out.","...","「Meanwhile.」","After leaving through the West City Gate with Liu Lang, Chen Yi took a long, roundabout path before slipping back into the city through the north gate.","However, he didn’t head for the residence on Chuansi Street. Instead, he snuck directly into the place where Liu Zhaoxue and Liu Wen had been staying.","After finding an empty room, Chen Yi ordered Liu Lang to stand guard at the door.","He, in turn, laid Lv Jiunan down flat and took several silver needles from his person.","Liu Lang glanced over, his face a mask of astonishment.","\"Boss, you, you, what are you doing?\"","\"Isn’t it obvious? I’m saving him.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi used his Controlling Needle with Qi technique, inserting the silver needles into the vital acupoints on Lv Jiunan’s body.","\"I know that, of course, but—but why would you save him after you just killed him?\"","\"Killing him was an act for others to see.\"","\"And saving him... that’s for...\""]},{"number":396,"title":"Chapter 396 - 252: The Chess Player? Just a Pawn","paragraphs":["Chen Yi continued speaking as he inserted needles into Lv Jiunan:","\"I’m saving him so he can help me put on a good show.\"","Liu Lang was not satisfied with this ambiguous answer.","He leaned against the wooden door, glanced at the barely breathing Lv Jiunan, and said with a slight pout:","\"Boss, are you plotting against someone again?\"","\"Liu Hong?\"","\"It has to be him.\"","\"You’re saving Lv Jiunan because you want to get evidence from him that Liu Hong is involved with those horse bandits from Poshisu Country, right?\"","But when Chen Yi didn’t respond, Liu Lang lost confidence in his own guess.","\"No? That makes sense, I guess.\"","\"After all, you already ’killed’ Lv Jiunan in front of everyone.\"","\"Even if he showed up again to accuse Liu Hong, that old fox could just deny everything.\"","Without looking up, Chen Yi said, \"Stop guessing. With your brain, you could guess until next year and still not figure it out.\"","\"...\"","Liu Lang wanted to argue.","But thinking about his recent experiences, he had to admit that intelligence, much like one’s Martial Arts Realm, was a matter of innate talent, not knowledge or experience.","After a moment of silence, he asked, unwilling to give up, \"Well, you can at least tell me about you going to the Spring Rain Building last night, right?\"","\"Just now, uh... this guy said someone went to the Spring Rain Building last night using my name. I immediately guessed it was you.\"","\"If I hadn’t reacted quickly, I almost would have blown our cover.\"","Chen Yi glanced up at him, then lowered his head again to treat Lv Jiunan, saying casually, \"Didn’t you already blow it?\"","Liu Lang gave a sheepish laugh. \"Ah, so you already know?\"","\"You can’t blame me for that. I’d already given my name before I heard from him that you’d been to the Spring Rain Building. It was too late to take it back.\"","\"Th-this... this won’t affect your plans, will it?\"","Chen Yi shook his head slightly. \"It won’t.\"","Now that Ge Muxiao was dead and Lv Jiunan was half-crippled, the only person who knew he had gone to the Spring Rain Building last night was Lou Yuxue.","Even Liu Taoyao and Zhao Shichang were unaware.","Besides, even if Lou Yuxue revealed it to the White Tiger Guard, or if Liu Taoyao and the others had just overheard Liu Lang, it wouldn’t affect his plans.","At most, he would just have to meet with Liu Lang less often from now on and make sure not to let him in on too much.","That way, the fool wouldn’t run his mouth and leak anything.","With this in mind, Chen Yi instructed, \"From now on, you don’t need to go back to the Liu Mansion. Just return to Hundred Herbs Hall and wait.\"","\"If I need you, I’ll have Zhang Dabao and Wang Ji contact you.\"","Liu Lang paused, stunned, then asked suspiciously, \"That old fox is bound to make a lot of moves soon. Isn’t it a bad idea not to keep an eye on him?\"","Chen Yi said flatly, \"There’s nothing to worry about.\"","\"I already know what that old fox is thinking. Whether we follow him or not won’t affect the big picture.\"","\"Besides, his next reactions and actions are all predictable. It’s not hard to guess.\"","More importantly, Chen Yi now held the people who could seal Liu Hong’s fate—Asutai and Lv Jiunan.","So he wasn’t worried at all.","Liu Hong was the one who should be panicking.","Liu Lang, of course, knew none of this. He scratched his head, turned to look out the window, and muttered to himself:","’Not hard to guess?’","’Why can’t I figure it out?’","Chen Yi ignored him, his hands moving swiftly as he inserted twelve silver needles into Lv Jiunan’s body.","Then, he circulated his True Essence, using the silver needles to repair Lv Jiunan’s heart-vein, Gate of Life, and other major meridian points.","He even mended his internal organs, which had been shattered into pieces.","After an hour of intense work, he finally pulled Lv Jiunan back from the brink of death.","Chen Yi let out a small breath and then removed the silver needles.","Hearing the movement, Liu Lang turned back and asked, \"Boss, are you done?\"","\"No.\"","Then, under Liu Lang’s curious gaze, Chen Yi inserted three more silver needles into Lv Jiunan’s three major Sea of Qi acupoints: the Yintang, the chest, and the Dantian.","He circulated his True Essence and gave the needles a slight twist.","Lv Jiunan’s eyes shot open, and he began to scream in agony.","\"Nngh, AAAAAH!\"","With a calm expression, Chen Yi inserted a fourth silver needle into a vital point on Lv Jiunan’s throat, forcibly silencing his screams.","Lv Jiunan’s mouth was wide open, but he couldn’t make a sound.","The intense pain twisted his features. His body arched and writhed as if desperately trying to escape.","About fifteen minutes later, Chen Yi used his Qi Observation Skill to confirm that the True Essence in Lv Jiunan’s body was completely drained, and only then did he remove the needles from the Sea of Qi points.","\"Done.\"","But Lv Jiunan clearly didn’t feel \"done.\" He continued to struggle frantically, letting out silent screams.","Only when the excruciating pain in his body began to subside did he slowly calm down.","Liu Lang grimaced at the sight. \"He’s crippled.\"","With his three major Seas of Qi destroyed, he would never be able to practice Martial Arts again, unless a legendary Medical Master intervened.","Chen Yi, of course, knew this. He casually removed the last silver needle and sat down in a chair to slowly recover his depleted True Essence.","Lv Jiunan lay limply on the square table, turning his head to look at him and asking in a hoarse voice:","\"Why... why didn’t you kill me?\"","He already knew he was a cripple.","Not only were his Seas of Qi destroyed and his cultivation lost, but the meridians and vital points in his body were also severely damaged.","Anyone would break down in such a situation, let alone a vicious and ruthless man like him.","\"Answer me!\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and raised a finger to his lips. \"Shh.\"","\"Quiet down. Don’t attract the people outside.\"","Lv Jiunan was in no state to care. He glared at him, his eyes bloodshot, and ground out the words through clenched teeth:","\"Why didn’t you kill me!?\"","Chen Yi let out a soft chuckle. \"What would be the point of killing you?\"","\"You’re King Landu’s blood brother. If a Grandmaster of his stature found out I killed you, wouldn’t that just bring me a world of trouble?\""]},{"number":397,"title":"Chapter 397 - 252: The Player? Just a Pawn","paragraphs":["He paused, then continued, \"Besides, I have other uses for your life. It would be a shame for you to die.\"","Hearing this, Lv Jiunan glared at him with venomous eyes. \"You... what are you planning?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"Forgive me, but I can’t tell you what I’m planning just yet.\"","\"You won’t get away with this!\"","\"Liu Wu, I’m telling you, whatever you’re planning, you won’t succeed!\"","Lv Jiunan struggled to get up, only to find that he couldn’t feel anything below his neck.","He could only crane his neck, hissing viciously, \"My big brother knows I’m here! He knows!\"","\"If he finds out I’m here and learns what you’ve done, he’ll lead the Peacock Banner and crush Shu State!\"","Chen Yi chuckled, unconcerned. \"If that’s true, I might actually develop some admiration for King Landu.\"","\"A horse bandit chieftain from Poshisu Country, willing to go to such lengths for his brother... I suppose you could call that loyalty.\"","As he spoke, he glanced sideways at Lv Jiunan, a smirk on his face. \"Unfortunately, even if he does come to Shu State, you won’t be around to see it.\"","\"You!?\"","\"I’ll kill you!\"","\"I’ll kill you!\"","Lv Jiunan roared frantically, but his voice grew fainter and fainter.","For some reason, the sight of Chen Yi’s all-knowing gaze, as if he had everything under control, filled Lv Jiunan’s heart with a profound terror.","It was a fear far greater than what he’d felt when the spear had pierced his body.","He didn’t know what the man before him was planning, but he was certain he was plotting against their Peacock King Banner.","Even his big brother, King Landu, might be drawn into it.","Yet now, he could do nothing but watch helplessly as his enemy orchestrated it all.","’I can’t accept this!’","At this thought, Lv Jiunan stopped roaring. The ferocious expression on his face slowly faded.","His face ashen, he stared at Chen Yi. \"Tell me... what... what exactly are you planning?\"","\"I... I don’t want to die not knowing why.\"","Chen Yi let out a short laugh. \"I don’t care to answer the same question twice.\"","\"But I can tell you this: your life is very important. Important enough to change the entire situation in Shu State.\"","\"You... You...\"","Before Lv Jiunan could say more, Chen Yi reached out and tapped him on the neck.","\"Enough with the ’you-ing.’ Save your strength and get some rest.\"","\"It was a lot of trouble to save your life. I can’t have you dying on me now.\"","Lv Jiunan refused to give up, still trying to ask something, but his eyelids grew heavier and heavier.","Soon, he fell unconscious once more.","Once he fell silent, Liu Lang couldn’t help but ask, \"Boss, are you sure you’re not deliberately torturing him?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, asking with some surprise, \"What makes you think that?\"","Liu Lang said helplessly, \"With your incredible Medical Skill, you could have obviously knocked him out without him even realizing it.\"","’My mind might not be the sharpest, but I’m not an idiot.’","Chen Yi smiled and looked at Lv Jiunan. \"Let’s just say I’m settling a score.\"","’If Lv Jiunan hadn’t manipulated my predecessor into fleeing his marriage and then killed him, none of this would have happened.’","’Emotionally and logically, I had to avenge both myself and him.’","Liu Lang sighed in relief upon hearing this. \"Oh, it’s a grudge. That’s good, that’s good...\"","He had come to deeply admire everything Chen Yi had done recently.","He really didn’t want to think of Chen Yi as some kind of sadist from the Evil Demonic Dao who enjoyed torturing people.","Chen Yi more or less guessed what he was thinking but didn’t say anything more.","’Many times, things change too quickly to be altered by one’s personal will.’","’Even I can’t escape it.’","’That’s why he had helped the Xiao Family—to completely free himself from these endless troubles.’","As Chen Yi mulled this over, his gaze drifted out the window.","By now, the rain had begun to let up.","The residence where Liu Zhaoxue lived was silent, save for the patter of a light drizzle.","From farther away on Kangning Street, the faint din of conversation could be heard, carrying snippets of discussion.","\"Did you hear? There was just a murder over in the West Market.\"","\"Some powerful Wandering Martial Artist killed two people from Poshisu Country.\"","\"People from Poshisu Country? Good riddance!\"","\"They’re from a barbaric land. Letting them live is just asking for trouble.\"","\"Exactly. For years, our merchants passing through the Ancient Tea-Horse Road have been constantly attacked, mostly by those horse bandits from Poshisu Country.\"","\"Old Marquis Xiao should have slaughtered every last one of them back in the day...\"","These scholars were clearly more concerned with court affairs and couldn’t care less about a few dead men from Poshisu Country.","The Wandering Martial Artists, however, were only interested in his identity.","\"...When did a Spearman like that appear in Shu State?\"","\"The Spear Dao at the Perfection Realm... Truly enviable.\"","\"Why have I never heard of someone like that? He’s probably not from around here, not one of our own Jianghu People from Shu State.\"","\"That’s possible.\"","\"We’ll have to wait and see.\"","\"Regardless of whether he killed men from Poshisu Country or not, it happened on Shu State soil, after all.\"","\"The Government Office and the Imprisonment Department will surely do everything they can to uncover his identity. We’ll know who he is then.\"","\"That’s true...\"","Just as Chen Yi, having heard enough, was about to rise and signal for Liu Lang to leave, his ears twitched. He turned his head to look northeast.","’This aura... It’s familiar...’","\"Huh?\"","’The Golden Banner Officer of the White Tiger Guard... Jiang Xing?’","Chen Yi’s brow furrowed. He quickly activated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, suppressing his aura.","Liu Lang noticed his expression. \"Is someone coming?\"","Chen Yi raised a hand, signaling him to be quiet. He mouthed the words, \"An expert of the Upper Three Grades.\"","Liu Lang smacked his lips but obediently said no more.","However...","’In my heart,’ he thought, ’Upper Three Grades, Middle Three Grades... none of it is as shocking as Chen Yi.’","’I thought I had a complete grasp of Chen Yi’s power.’","’But after seeing him in action today, I realize what I saw before was just the tip of the iceberg.’","Liu Lang thought about his upcoming duel with Chen Yi in a few days and couldn’t help but grumble to himself.","’I have to make sure the boss only uses his Saber Dao.’","’His Spear Dao Realm is too high, and the power of his techniques is terrifying. If he uses his spear in our duel... I’d be better off just picking a fight with Xiao Jinghong...’","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea what Liu Lang was thinking. After concealing his aura, he silently monitored the activity outside.","He knew Jiang Xing must have gone to Heiyu Lane first, then followed their trail here.","Fortunately, he had been cautious enough not to return directly to his own residence on Chuansi Street, choosing Liu Zhaoxue’s home instead. Otherwise, Jiang Xing might have actually discovered his identity.","But even though he’d guessed this much, he still hadn’t figured out a way to escape.","’I can only hope Jiang Xing doesn’t find this place.’","’Otherwise...’","’I’ll have to make a move here again.’","...","「A little over a mile from Chen Yi’s location.」","Jiang Xing kept his bamboo hat low, appearing to scan the pedestrians on Kangning Street, but in reality, he was searching for a faint fluctuation within the Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","This was a unique Magic Gate of the White Tiger Guard, specialized for hunting and tracking fugitives.","At first, everything had gone smoothly.","But when he reached Kangning Street, the sheer number of people, combined with the fluctuations from the Martial Arts Realms of various Wandering Martial Artists, had completely disrupted the local Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism.","Combined with the fact that nearly an hour had passed, the search became exceedingly difficult.","「About a quarter of an hour later.」","Jiang Xing spotted a faint, intermittent trail of aura to the southwest. He let out a small sigh of relief and began to walk slowly in that direction.","「Before long.」","He arrived just outside the residence where Chen Yi was hiding, stopping less than half a mile away.","’It vanished?’","Jiang Xing studied the modest residence before him. ’Are they... in here?’","After a moment’s thought, he walked up to the main gate and looked at the plaque above it: Liu Mansion.","’Liu?’","’Is this Liu Hong’s place?’","Just as Jiang Xing was pondering this, he heard the rumbling of carriage wheels. With a slight frown, he quickly ducked out of sight.","Soon, an ornate, canopied carriage came rolling slowly down Kangning Street.","Jiang Xing focused his gaze and saw that the carriage also bore the character for \"Liu.\"","Beside it flew a small banner: a red field with white clouds, emblazoned with the head of a wild wolf.","’The Jing State Liu Family... Then it’s not Liu Hong’s.’","As he was thinking this, Jiang Xing saw the carriage stop at the entrance to the mansion.","Two graceful female figures descended from it.","One was dressed as a Maid, while the other, wearing a pure white gown, was sheltered by an umbrella held by the Maid as she stepped down.","After a quick glance, Jiang Xing had a sudden realization. ’Liu Zhaoxue. It’s her?’","Suddenly, a shocking thought struck him—’Could that Liu Wu be one of her people?!’"]},{"number":398,"title":"Chapter 398 - 253: A Hero’s Weakness for a Beauty","paragraphs":["It was no wonder the General thought this way.","He had previously heard reports from \"Hawk\" Ge the Third and \"Lady Tiger\" Lou Yuxue:","\"The man, Liu Wu, claimed to be one of Liu Zhaoxue’s people from the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"He said he killed Liu Wen to clear the way for Liu Zhaoxue, allowing her to have a smooth path in the main branch of the Liu Family.\"","\"However, judging from the burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain, the Xiao Family actually benefited the most.\"","The General watched Liu Zhaoxue walk into the residence, a contemplative look on his face.","’What if, at that time, Liu Wu was telling the truth?’","’What if he really was one of Liu Zhaoxue’s people?’","’If all that were true, then the truth would be—’","Liu Wu gave those 300,000 silver to the Xiao Family through Xiao Dongchen, seemingly solving their urgent crisis.","’But what was the reality?’","’In reality, he did it to deceive everyone, making the Jing State Liu Family think that Liu Wen was killed by the Xiao Family.’","’That way, no one would ever suspect that the true mastermind was Liu Zhaoxue.’","The General let out a soft breath and mouthed the words, \"What is false, make real. What is real, make false.\"","\"This Liu Wu... his mind is incredibly meticulous!\"","Although the General had never actually met this Liu Wu, the information he had gathered painted a picture of a man whose talent in the Martial Arts, intellect, and temperament were unlike any he had ever encountered.","This was especially true regarding the \"burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain.\"","It seemed that his White Tiger Guard had gained some advantages and achieved certain objectives, but the biggest beneficiary was none other than \"Liu Wu.\"","Even the Xiao Family, who had successfully avoided damage to the Three Towns’ summer grain, were losers to a certain extent.","Only this \"Liu Wu\" had managed it all. First, he deceived the Bright Moon Building to get the chance to go to Iron Wall Town.","Then, he used Liu Wen’s name to lure Xiao Dongchen into a trap, ultimately leading to his death.","Finally, he killed Liu Wen in Iron Wall Town and framed the Xiao Family for it.","One by one, Liu Wu had pulled off these schemes, almost perfectly erasing all his tracks.","If not for the involvement of several Silver Banner Officers from the White Tiger Guard who had contact with Liu Wu, it’s likely no one would have ever known the full extent of what he had done.","\"No wonder the Pavilion Master said that internal strife has already begun in the Liu Family.\"","\"With ’Liu Wu’ helping her, how could Liu Zhaoxue possibly fail to gain power in the main branch of the Liu Family?\"","Among the current heirs of the Jing State Liu Family’s main branch, the eldest son, Liu Yong, certainly had the best chance.","The second son, Liu Wen, also had a chance to become the Liu Family Patriarch because of his mother, but he died in Shu State.","The third miss, Liu Zhaoxue, was known as the number one beauty of Jing State and was greatly favored by her father.","The fourth son, Liu Wu, was a disciple of Jing State’s Langyue Mountain. His talent in the Martial Arts was exceptional, and his Cultivation had already reached the Fourth Grade Realm.","The other heirs mostly stood no chance.","As the General thought of this, he glanced once more at the two words, \"Liu Mansion,\" on the residence, then turned and vanished into the gloomy rain.","He didn’t know why that \"Liu Wu\" was helping Liu Zhaoxue.","’Could it be... that even a hero cannot resist a beautiful woman?’","’It wasn’t impossible.’","Liu Zhaoxue, of course, could not have known she was being watched by the General.","After returning to the residence, her lovely face, which could look charming whether in joy or anger, took on its usual cool expression.","\"Shu State, I’ve returned.\"","Although it had only been twenty days since she had left for Jing State, standing here again truly felt like a lifetime had passed.","This was especially true when she thought about her experiences in Jing State over the past few days, making her cherish this hard-won opportunity even more.","Liu Zhaoxue looked at the Maids and Household Servants kneeling inside the residence, and her father’s warning surfaced in her mind.","\"As your father, I know you are unwilling, but you were born into the Liu Family. Some things cannot be decided by your own whims.\"","\"This time, I will only give you half a year. Whether you succeed or fail, you must return to Jing State.\"","’Half a year.’","Liu Zhaoxue sighed and waved her hand gently. \"All of you, rise and go about your duties.\"","\"Yes, Third Miss.\"","After the Maids and servants had left, Liu Zhaoxue looked to the side at a steward dressed in cotton clothes and gave an order:","\"Uncle Fu, go and invite the shopkeepers to come here. We will hold a meeting in an hour.\"","The steward, who was about fifty years old, nodded and bowed. \"Miss, should I also summon the accountants?\"","\"Have them come as well. Remember to bring the account books from the Medicine Halls for the past few days.\"","\"Yes...\"","Liu Zhaoxue watched him walk away before leading several Attendants to the main hall of the West Mansion.","Three Cyan-clothed Guards stood watch at the door.","Two Maids stood silently behind her.","After a moment of silence, one of the Maids looked up, surveyed her surroundings, and suddenly spoke:","\"Miss Zhaoxue, this place is not bad.\"","Liu Zhaoxue paused. She ordered the other Maid to go prepare tea before saying calmly:","\"My third uncle, Liu Hong, found it. How could it be bad?\"","Although the Maid wore a short, orange-colored outfit, her oval face held no warmth. Instead, there was a hint of cunning in her eyes.","\"It’s near Quchi and the North City Gate, making it convenient for an escape.\"","\"It’s also close to Kangning Street, which is frequented by scholars, most of whom are descendants of Shu State’s Noble Families. Information flows freely there.\"","She paused, looked at Liu Zhaoxue, and chuckled before continuing, \"What do you think?\"","\"As long as you’re satisfied.\"","\"Miss Zhaoxue, that sounds a bit distant.\"","\"Ling’er is your Maid now. Of course, everything revolves around you.\"","The Maid named Ling’er blinked her lively eyes and asked, feigning ignorance:","\"Besides, my Five Poison Sect has already lost an Elder for your sake. Why are you still so guarded?\"","Liu Zhaoxue turned her head to look at her, studying her for a moment before saying, \"You should know the reason very well.\"","\"My goals, you are clear about.\"","\"But as for your goals, no one has ever told me.\"","\"Even the previous Elder, Yan Fusha, only said one thing—that you want to make use of Xinglin Hall.\"","Liu Zhaoxue paused, as if observing Ling’er’s reaction. Seeing her expression remained unchanged, she continued to ask:"]},{"number":399,"title":"Chapter 399 - 253: A Hero’s Weakness for a Beauty","paragraphs":["\"So, Miss Ling’er, would you care to elaborate?\"","Ling’er looked at her with a half-smile. \"Miss Zhaoxue, please rest assured. No matter what my Five Poison Sect does, you will not be implicated.\"","Liu Zhaoxue turned her head away, no longer looking at her.","\"Not necessarily.\"","\"Last time, Elder Yan Fusha abducted Pei Guanli of the Mountain Race. Now that you’ve returned in force, do you really think you won’t attract the Mountain Race’s attention?\"","Ling’er’s smile froze, and she pouted at the back of Liu Zhaoxue’s head.","\"We will.\"","\"That’s why this time, besides me, a Great Elder has also come, along with several Altar Masters.\"","\"Then where are they now?\"","\"Miss Zhaoxue, don’t be so anxious. Right now, your most important task is to successfully expand Xinglin Hall. I will report everything else to the Great Elder myself.\"","Hearing this, Liu Zhaoxue said softly, \"It had better be that way.\"","She was well aware of her own situation.","If her father hadn’t helped her, she would have never been able to return to Shu State this time.","She had even been on the verge of being sent to the Capital Prefecture by her second brother Liu Wen’s birth mother, in league with several family elders, to be some man’s bed warmer.","Thus, Liu Zhaoxue cherished this opportunity.","Even though she knew the situation in Shu State was perilous, she would not give up.","For some reason, the image of Chen Yi surfaced in Liu Zhaoxue’s mind. She thought to herself,","’If only I had someone like Mr. Qingzhou to help me, how could I possibly fail to achieve my goals?’","She still remembered what she had seen before leaving Jing State—a Spearman at the Perfection Realm, along with Liu Lang, had rescued Chen Yi and Pei Guanli.","As she saw it, those two must have helped the Xiao Family because of their connection to Chen Yi.","Liu Zhaoxue thought with a sigh, ’What a pity...’","Alas, she had no one like that by her side.","Otherwise, she would have never cooperated with the Five Poison Sect.","Just then, Ling’er heard footsteps from outside in the distance. Her eyes darted around for a moment before she stepped forward and bowed.","\"Miss Zhaoxue, I’ve just arrived in Shu State and would like to go out for a walk. I hope you’ll grant me permission.\"","Liu Zhaoxue glanced at her and nodded slightly. \"Feel free, Miss Ling’er.\"","\"Alrighty then.\"","After she left, it just so happened that several shopkeepers arrived at the West Mansion with their respective accountants.","Liu Zhaoxue composed herself and rose to greet them.","\"Greetings, Third Miss.\"","\"There’s no need for such formalities, Uncles. Please, come in...\"","Amidst the pleasantries, in the East Mansion just a wall away...","Chen Yi and Liu Lang exchanged a look and then waited a while longer.","\"Boss, Liu Zhaoxue is back.\"","\"Mm, she was bound to come back sooner or later.\"","A smile touched Chen Yi’s lips as he thought about what had happened that day.","Honestly, Liu Zhaoxue’s timing was perfect.","If the General saw her, it might even mislead his judgment.","Seeing his smile, Liu Lang shuddered instinctively and asked in a low voice,","\"So when are we leaving?\"","\"No rush. It won’t be too late to leave after we hear what Miss Zhaoxue plans to do next.\"","That was what he said, anyway. But Chen Yi was more concerned with avoiding the General and any potential pursuers who might have followed them from the West Market.","After all, he didn’t care about Xinglin Hall expanding its business in Shu State.","What he cared about was the extent of Liu Zhaoxue’s ambition and the Five Poison Sect’s purpose for coming to Shu State.","’From what Liu Zhaoxue just said, the Five Poison Sect wants to use Xinglin Hall to achieve some goal. That’s a bit strange.’","Chen Yi had originally thought the Five Poison Sect came to Shu State to seek revenge on the Mountain Race.","But now it seemed their target had never been the Mountain Race at all.","Thinking about it carefully, it made sense.","The men Elder Yan Fusha brought last time had some strength, but going up against the Mountain Race would have been like throwing an egg against a rock.","With so few people, forget about taking revenge on the Mountain Race.","They only managed to abduct Pei Guanli because they had the element of surprise, attacking an unsuspecting target.","If they had actually run into Granny Shan, their fate would have been even more miserable.","In contrast, from what Ling’er said this time, it seemed the Five Poison Sect had sent some powerful people.","’A Great Elder, Altar Masters... I wonder what level of strength these people from the Five Poison Sect possess.’","Chen Yi pondered for a moment, then shook his head to himself and stopped overthinking it.","Regardless of their Cultivation, he couldn’t let the Five Poison Sect become the main focus.","Right now, Liu Hong was the person he truly had to deal with.","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi listened carefully to the conversation in the West Mansion, gaining a deeper understanding of Xinglin Hall.","He had to admit, Xinglin Hall had survived in Jing State for a hundred years for a reason; it had its unique strengths.","Even without a few Medical Saint Hands presiding over it, its internal regulations and the quality of its personnel alone were far superior to other Medicine Halls.","Needless to say, it was leagues ahead of the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, which was a newcomer to the business.","It could be said that Xinglin Hall had already developed a complete system that could be replicated from scratch in other State Capitals.","From purchasing medicinal herbs and arranging for armed escorts for transportation, to methods for developing and expanding the Medicine Hall, every aspect was covered.","Every single detail was covered by specific requirements.","The regulations even specified the duties of every person in each Medicine Hall and the abilities they needed to possess.","It was nothing short of meticulous.","Liu Lang, at his side, had also heard everything, but he didn’t have as many thoughts on the matter.","He peeked outside through a crack in the door and asked in a low voice,","\"Boss, why doesn’t Liu Zhaoxue move into this mansion?\"","\"The east is considered more honorable, but she’s always stayed in the West Mansion. Liu Wen is already dead now.\"","Chen Yi smiled at his words and replied, \"That’s what makes Liu Zhaoxue clever.\"","\"She has ambition and brains, but what she lacks is a significant contribution to her name.\"","\"Until she has one, she has to restrain her ambitions and not overstep her bounds. Only then can she quietly win people over to her side.\"","\"I see...\"","Of course, there was more to it. Chen Yi knew very well the situation of someone with low status within a family.","Just like him, the \"son-in-law who married into the family.\"","It was only because he was in the Xiao Family, where Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Jinghong, and even Old Master Xiao Yuan treated him well.","If he had been in a place like the Liu Family, he probably would have been beaten with clubs and driven out of the Liu Family back when he tried to flee the marriage.","One could only imagine the difficulties and criticism Liu Zhaoxue had to face to achieve her goals.","That was why Chen Yi could understand Liu Zhaoxue’s decision to join forces with the Five Poison Sect.","The only thing that displeased him was that Liu Zhaoxue had targeted Xiao Wan’er and, worse, allowed the Five Poison Sect to make a move against him and Pei Guanli.","For those two reasons alone, he could never let Liu Zhaoxue succeed.","After waiting a little longer, when the shopkeepers and accountants from Xinglin Hall were about to leave, Chen Yi finally hoisted Lv Jiunan onto his shoulder and signaled for Liu Lang to go.","\"Boss, where are we going?\"","\"Back to the house on Chuansi Street for now.\"","Although Chen Yi didn’t know the whereabouts of the General and his men, Kangning Street was crowded and full of prying eyes, so he could only head east or north.","Returning to Chuansi Street was the most suitable option.","Before long, Chen Yi and Liu Lang arrived at the house on Chuansi Street without alerting anyone.","They listened for a moment, and only after confirming that Zhang Dabao was the only one inside did they slip in quietly.","When Zhang Dabao saw them, he hurriedly bowed and said, \"Sir.\"","Chen Yi nodded, set Lv Jiunan aside, and glanced around, raising an eyebrow as he asked, \"Is the quiet room set up?\"","\"Reporting to you, Sir. This afternoon, the Shopkeeper personally brought several disciples from the Celestial Sect to set it up.\"","\"It only took them a couple of hours to install soundproofing panels on the doors, windows, walls, and ceiling.\"","\"The Shopkeeper also said that he’ll order those Guards to come back tomorrow to continue reinforcing it.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand. \"Tell him they don’t need to come.\"","Now that Lv Jiunan was here, the fewer people who knew, the better.","Besides, he also planned to have Pei Guanli hide here with Asutai, making it even more crucial that this place remained undiscovered.","After a few more words of idle chat, Chen Yi had Zhang Dabao disguise Liu Lang, then sent him off to Hundred Herbs Hall ahead of him.","After Zhang Dabao removed his own disguise, Chen Yi instructed,","\"Try not to go out for the next few days. Guard this place well.\"","He pointed to the quiet room and ordered, \"Just give the person inside some food and water every day.\"","\"If he shouts or screams, gag him to prevent anyone from discovering the situation here.\"","Zhang Dabao glanced toward the quiet room and nodded. \"Rest assured, Sir. I will guard this place well.\"","Chen Yi smiled and patted his shoulder. \"I’ll have to trouble you for now. Once everything in Shu State has settled down, I’ll grant you one request.\"","\"Sir, I couldn’t...\"","\"Don’t refuse. Consider it compensation for you not achieving the title ’Two Fingers’.\"","\"Thank you, Sir!\"","Chen Yi smiled, nodded, and then left the house with his Oil Paper Umbrella, heading straight for the Xiao Family residence.","By now, it was late in the evening.","But since the rain had stopped, the dusky yellow sky was wreathed in colorful clouds, a truly beautiful sight.","The pedestrians on the road were no longer rushing; most of them, finished with their busy day, were strolling leisurely.","Chen Yi was no different.","But when he arrived outside the Xiao Family gate and saw Xiaodie waiting anxiously at the entrance from a distance, he couldn’t help but quicken his pace.","The moment Xiaodie saw him, the anxiety vanished from her face. She patted her chest and said,","\"Young Master, you’re finally back.\"","Chen Yi pretended to look at the sky. \"It’s not even dark yet.\"","\"It’s not about it being dark! It’s—it’s that the Young Miss was worried about you.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Earlier, news came from the West Market that some villains were attacking and killing people in the street. The Miss and I were both so worried about you...\""]},{"number":400,"title":"Chapter 400 - 254: Dragon Spear","paragraphs":["No news is small news in Shu State.","By midday, the events that took place in West Market’s Heiyu Lane had spread like wildfire.","One rumor claimed that some reckless fools from Poshisu Country had been indiscriminately killing innocents in Heiyu Lane, angering the spearman who then killed them with a single thrust of his spear.","Another said the spearman had accepted a bounty from Bright Moon Building to kill the men from Poshisu Country for a reward.","Yet another claimed the man from Poshisu was a horse bandit, one of the horse bandits under the Peacock Banner led by King Landu.","This version said the spearman had hunted him down for revenge because the bandit had killed his friends or family on the Ancient Tea-Horse Road.","The theories were endless, with every sort of story being told.","Some busybodies even gave the spearman the title \"Dragon Spear.\"","Such a resounding title was well-received by the people of the Jianghu.","Most considered him one of the most remarkable rising stars in the Shu State Jianghu in recent years.","But upon hearing all this, Chen Yi just curled his lip in disdain.","\"Dragon Spear? What kind of name is that?\"","\"It should at least be ’Cyan Dragon Crescent Blade Spear’ or ’Coiling Dragon Spear.’ Even ’Snow Gall Silver Spear’ would be acceptable.\"","’They really don’t have a shred of culture.’","Xiaodie earnestly agreed, \"Master Chen is right.\"","\"’Dragon Spear’ sounds awful. They’re uncultured.\"","Chen Yi nodded in satisfaction. This girl, Xiaodie, was certainly worth having around; she knew how to keep people happy.","Joking and laughing, the two of them returned to Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wuge had already returned from the Martial Arts Arena and was currently in the pavilion, practicing his Stand Form.","In the afterglow of the setting sun, his small frame stood ramrod straight, his long shadow stretching over the pond and stirring the Golden Carp into a frenzy of splashing.","Chen Yi watched for a moment before gesturing to Xiaodie, signaling for her to go report back to Xiao Wan’er so she wouldn’t worry.","Xiaodie nodded and tiptoed toward Jiaxing Garden.","As he watched her go, Chen Yi sat down quietly to the side, observing Xiao Wuge with great interest, a faint light glittering in his eyes.","Using his Qi Observation Skill, Chen Yi could clearly see a faint aura being generated from deep within Xiao Wuge’s body, strengthening his muscles, bones, and skin.","The process was slow, but for a boy not yet six years old, the effects of this Pile Skill were already outstanding.","’It seems the grade of the \"Little Yellow Court\" Pile Skill is quite high.’","’To have this kind of strength-enhancing effect without anyone using True Essence to clear Wuge’s meridians... it must be a much higher grade than the Big Spear Pile Skill.’","’This is good, too.’","Chen Yi had already planned to teach Xiao Wuge the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique before he left for Jinling. The better his Foundation Establishment, the better.","That way, he would be sure to meet the threshold for cultivating that particular Pile Skill.","’With the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to mask his progress, outsiders won’t be able to perceive Wuge’s cultivation level.’","’And with old Mr. Sun Fu’s help, I believe Wuge will be able to spend ten comfortable years in Jinling.’","Just as Chen Yi was lost in these thoughts, a Golden Carp leaped out of the pond, slapped its tail twice, and splashed water all over him.","He had just wiped himself dry when several more Golden Carp thrashed to the surface.","They \"bombarded\" him one after another.","Chen Yi feigned a strike, and the Golden Carp, as if understanding him, went SPLASH SPLASH and dove to the bottom of the pond.","He couldn’t help but curse them with a private chuckle. ’Just you wait. After Wuge goes to Jinling, I’ll definitely catch every last one of you to be fried, boiled, and roasted.’","At that moment, Xiao Wuge seemed to notice the commotion. He slowly concluded his practice and exhaled.","\"HOOO.\"","He stood up straight, tilted his head slightly to see Chen Yi, and a smile spread across his small face. \"Brother-in-law, when did you get back?\"","\"Big Sister was just worried about you. She sent Xiaodie to the gate to wait for you.\"","Chen Yi patted his head and said with a smile, \"I just got back. I already told Xiaodie to report to Big Sister.\"","After a brief explanation, he asked, \"How did you do at the Martial Arts Arena today?\"","Xiao Wuge chuckled, a hint of pride in his voice. \"I still think I have a long way to go.\"","\"But Second Uncle said my talent is excellent and that my Pile Skill training is very solid.\"","\"He also said he’ll teach me how to use a spear tomorrow, to lay the foundation for cultivating our Xiao Family’s Spear Technique in the future.\"","Chen Yi smiled and said, \"The spear is the king of a hundred weapons. It can be used both on horseback and on foot.\"","Having achieved Spear Dao Perfection, he naturally held the Long Spear in high regard.","Of course, if Xiao Wuge were to cultivate the Saber Dao or the Fist Dao, he would support that as well.","\"That’s what Second Uncle said, too.\"","\"He even had someone demonstrate a few Spear Techniques for me. Like this, and this, and this...\"","As he spoke, Xiao Wuge mimicked the spear movements with his empty hands.","He actually looked quite the part.","As they were chatting, Xiaodie ran over and said, \"Young Master, Master Chen, the Eldest Miss has prepared a banquet for this evening and asks you to come over.\"","Chen Yi nodded and led Xiao Wuge toward Jiaxing Garden.","\"Brother-in-law, where is Sister Guanli?\"","\"She went out with the visitors from the Mountain Race.\"","\"Oh. I wanted to ask her for some advice about Martial Arts.\"","\"There’s no rush...\"","The three of them chatted idly as they arrived at Jiaxing Garden, where the dining table in the main hall was already laden with dishes.","Four small dishes, four large dishes, plus a soup.","After taking his seat, Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wan’er and asked, \"Big Sister, what’s the special occasion? This is quite a feast.\"","While instructing Cui’er to serve the two of them soup and rice, Xiao Wan’er replied with a smile,","\"Nun Jingci from Wumeng Mountain wrote back.\"","\"I don’t have to go there to recuperate this year.\"","Chen Yi suddenly understood. He remembered Xiao Wan’er mentioning this after they returned from Tonglin Town last time.","At the time, Xiao Wan’er had still been hesitant.","He hadn’t expected that in just three to five days, she would have already made her decision and sent a letter.","\"How is the search for the Medical Saint Hands going?\"","\"I’ve just finished writing the letters. You can look them over for me later, Brother-in-law.\"","\"Alright...\"","Since the Old Master had already agreed to widely distribute the \"Divine Doctor invitations,\" Xiao Wan’er wasted no time.","She had also commissioned a blueprint for a Medical Dao Academy and asked the butler to hire a hundred laborers.","She planned to have them head to Tonglin Town first thing tomorrow morning to begin construction."]}]);
